    // FILE: mod_legends\afterHooks\contracts\templates\intro_templates.nut
    // context: ::Const.Contracts.IntroNobleHouseNeutral[0].Text
    {
        // corrige base: «Las direcciones a la casa» calca «directions»; en castellano son «indicaciones para llegar».
        // corrige base: «Al leer la nota revela que» no tiene sujeto; pasa a «Al leer la nota descubres que».
        // corrige base: «aparentemente» traduce «apparently» abriendo la oración; según el criterio fijado es «por lo visto».
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]{A man surprises you by sliding into your shoulder. You just about draw your sword when he quickly explains that a %person_employer% by the name of %employer% has sought your acquaintance. Sheathing your weapon, you tell the stranger to take you to %them_employer% - if %they_employer%'s got business, %they_employer% should tell you %themselves_employer%. The messenger nods and leads the way to a nobleman's house. | A messenger - a young lad about as tall as a longsword - sprints by you, throwing a scroll into the air as he swings past. You catch it, but by the time you can look for the kid he's already gone. Shrugging, you open the scroll and find the name of %employer%. %They_employer% appears to be in need of your services. Directions to a nobleman's house tag the bottom of the scroll. | While walking about %townname%, a messenger eases up next to you. A glance at him has the poor guy throwing a scroll into your hands before running off. You open up to see that a local nobleman has requested your audience. | %townname% seems peaceful enough, but something must be going wrong because a messenger comes to you with a notice from a local nobleman. And where there's riches, there's trouble... | A messenger greets you. He names himself as someone forgettable, because you instantly forget his name. However, his information is quite important: a local nobleman has requested your audience. | A bird flies to your shoulder and plants itself there. It coos at you, then gestures towards its feet where a notice has been rolled up. The second you take the message, the bird is off, no friend of anything but its own delivery services. Reading the note reveals that a local nobleman, and presumed friend of the aviary critters, has requested your audience. | A leashed dog runs up to you with a whole lotta barking. The man at the end of the leash nods toward the canine. You see a scroll hooked to its collar, the beast some sort of messenger mongrel. That or someone is having a bit of a laugh.\n\n Taking the note, you read that a local nobleman has requested your services. Maybe it's not a joke after all. The dog simply barks again and wags its tail, sitting dutifully and looking rather accomplished. | A straight-backed man walks toward you. He's got a scroll in a lifted arm, approaching you like a message board on stilts. He says nothing, merely extends his arm and you merely take the message as you're gestured to do. It reads that a local nobleman is looking for you and presumably your services. You thank the messenger, but he says nothing, simply turning and stilting his way down the road. | While walking down %townname%'s road, a few men cry out from a local tavern, howling with laughter as they wave you over. Snickering and doubling over, they can barely spit out their news: apparently some nobleman has been looking for a sellsword. Interesting, but you can't help but ask why they were laughing. The men go silent for a moment and one shrugs while another coughs out an answer.%SPEECH_ON%Because we're drunk?%SPEECH_OFF%The men keep a strained set of straight faces for but a second longer before bursting into laughter once more. | A servant of a local noble asks you to follow him on his master's behest. He leads you into the wealthier part of %townname%, where the buildings get taller and the people streets don't reek of horse manure. Eventually you reach a manor that looks as if it used to be a temple. Fake owls dot the eaves, staring you down as you walk by. A depressed-looking cat idles on the front steps. You enter through a front door that squalls with opulence, its hinges and wide swing echoing into the foyer. Your mouth drops open as you hardly even know the words to describe the grandeur inside.}"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]{Un hombre te sorprende chocando contra tu hombro. Estás a punto de desenvainar tu espada cuando rápidamente explica que %un_employer% %hombre_employer% llamad%o_employer% %employer% ha solicitado tu presencia. Envainando tu arma, le dices al desconocido que te lleve con %el_employer%: si tiene negocios, debería decírtelos personalmente. El mensajero asiente y guía el camino hacia la casa de un noble. | Un mensajero, un muchacho tan alto como una espada larga, pasa corriendo junto a ti, lanzando un pergamino al aire mientras gira. Lo atrapas, pero cuando puedes buscarlo ya se ha ido. Encogiéndote de hombros, abres el pergamino y encuentras el nombre de %employer%. Parece necesitar tus servicios. Al pie del pergamino figuran indicaciones para llegar a la casa de un noble. | Mientras caminas por %townname%, un mensajero se acerca sigilosamente. Una mirada hacia él hace que el pobre tipo te lance un pergamino a las manos antes de salir corriendo. Lo abres y ves que un noble local ha solicitado tu audiencia. | %townname% parece bastante pacífico, pero algo debe andar mal porque un mensajero viene hacia ti con un aviso de un noble local. Y donde hay riquezas, hay problemas... | Un mensajero te saluda. Se presenta como alguien olvidable, porque instantáneamente olvidas su nombre. Sin embargo, su información es bastante importante: un noble local ha solicitado tu audiencia. | Un pájaro vuela hacia tu hombro y se posa allí. Te arrulla, luego gesticula hacia sus patas donde hay un aviso enrollado. En cuanto tomas el mensaje, el pájaro se va, amigo de nada salvo de sus propios servicios de entrega. Al leer la nota descubres que un noble local, y presunto amigo de las criaturas aviares, ha solicitado tu audiencia. | Un perro con correa corre hacia ti ladrando muchísimo. El hombre al final de la correa asiente hacia el canino. Ves un pergamino enganchado a su collar, la bestia algún tipo de chucho mensajero. Eso o alguien se está burlando bastante.\n\n Tomando la nota, lees que un noble local ha solicitado tus servicios. Quizás no sea una broma después de todo. El perro simplemente ladra de nuevo y menea la cola, sentándose obedientemente y luciendo bastante orgulloso. | Un hombre de espalda recta camina hacia ti. Tiene un pergamino en un brazo levantado, acercándose como un tablón de anuncios sobre zancos. No dice nada, simplemente extiende su brazo y tú simplemente tomas el mensaje como te indica. Dice que un noble local te está buscando y presumiblemente tus servicios. Agradeces al mensajero, pero no dice nada, simplemente se gira y se aleja sobre sus zancos por el camino. | Mientras caminas por el camino de %townname%, unos hombres gritan desde una taberna local, aullando de risa mientras te hacen señas. Riendo y doblándose, apenas pueden escupir sus noticias: por lo visto, algún noble ha estado buscando un mercenario. Interesante, pero no puedes evitar preguntar por qué se reían. Los hombres guardan silencio por un momento y uno se encoge de hombros mientras otro tose una respuesta.%SPEECH_ON%¿Porque estamos borrachos?%SPEECH_OFF%Los hombres mantienen un conjunto tenso de caras serias solo un segundo más antes de estallar en carcajadas una vez más. | Un sirviente de un noble local te pide que lo sigas bajo órdenes de su amo. Te conduce a la parte más adinerada de %townname%, donde los edificios se vuelven más altos y las calles no apestan a estiércol de caballo. Al final llegas a una mansión que parece haber sido un templo. Búhos falsos salpican los aleros, mirándote fijamente mientras pasas. Un gato de aspecto deprimido holgazanea en los escalones frontales. Entras por una puerta frontal que chilla con opulencia, sus bisagras y amplio giro resonando en el vestíbulo. Tu boca se abre mientras apenas conoces las palabras para describir la grandeza interior.}"
    }
    // context: ::Const.Contracts.IntroNobleHouseFriendly[0].Text
    {
        // corrige base: «si te interesa más negocios» no concuerda; pasa a «si te interesan más negocios».
        // corrige base: «te lanza una {col | cebolla | patata | tomate}» da «una tomate»; el artículo entra en cada variante: «{una col | una cebolla | una patata | un tomate}».
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]{A few peasants walk up to you and one even offers a hug. You decline.%SPEECH_ON%It's good to see you again, sellsword. %employer%'s been looking for you.%SPEECH_OFF% | A woman offers you a flower when you walk into town. This is against the usual response which is shutter the windows and hide the kids. You take the flower and she sways her skirt a little before prancing away. A man comes up to you.%SPEECH_ON%Sorry for that bother, sir, the townsfolk seemed to have taken a liking to you. %employer% as well, seeing as how %they_employer%'s been looking for you since the moment %they_employer% heard you were in town.%SPEECH_OFF% | A pack of dogs streams down the road, a few children in chase. They scatter past you one by one, the dogs howling and huffing with joy, the children screaming out greetings. A woman walks up, a metal skillet in one hand and a wash rag in the other.%SPEECH_ON%Hey there sellsword. I probably should let one of them messenger men find and tell you this, but I got the news so I'll tell you anyhow. %employer%'s looking for you.%SPEECH_OFF%She flutters her eyes. You smile back and nod. %randombrother% smirks.%SPEECH_ON%See something you like, sir?%SPEECH_OFF%You tell the man to go fark a goat. | A couple of bleating goats are being lead down the road. They shuffle through the mud, prodding their noses through the muck and somehow finding things to chew up. Their shepherd plants his cane in the ground.%SPEECH_ON%Hey there mercenary. %employer%'s been looking for ya.%SPEECH_OFF% | A man sitting on his porch leans forward at the very sight of you. He points a finger.%SPEECH_ON%Well if it ain't the sellsword everyone been talking of.%SPEECH_OFF%You look around before nodding. He grins and hoots and hollers.%SPEECH_ON%Hell, it's damned nice seeing you around again! And it'd be short of me not to tell you that %employer%'s been tryin' to find ya. Go and see him. Tell %them_employer% I sent ya, maybe %they_employer%'ll send me a reward. Probably just a bunch of flowers, that bastard. Or a cat. Who wants a cat? Why did %they_employer% ever send me a cat? I told %them_employer% I hate cats...%SPEECH_OFF%As the man rambles on, you quietly make your leave. | A woman runs up to you. She brings her children with, not exactly taking precautions with a sellsword. One of the kids swings their arms around your leg.%SPEECH_ON%He's back!%SPEECH_OFF%You look down and grin, subtly trying to shake the bastard off although he just takes it for play. The mother retrieves the spawn before pointing up the road.%SPEECH_ON%%employer%'s been lookin' for ya. Tell %them_employer% I fetched ya, maybe %they_employer%'ll come and fix our well once %they_employer% knows I done a favor.%SPEECH_OFF%She looks world weary, dragged to the hells by the cheeriness of her children. | You walk into %townname% and a man beckons you into his garden. He's tending the plants, using a steady hand to clip the vegetables or fruit or whatever it is, you're not a gardener.%SPEECH_ON%How are you doing, sellsword? If you're wondering, %employer% been talking of you. Suppose %they_employer%'s been wanting to see you, too, if yer interested in some more business. Here, catch.%SPEECH_OFF%He turns and tosses a {cabbage | onion | potato | tomato} at you.%SPEECH_ON%Nice catch.%SPEECH_OFF%You take a bite and nod back.%SPEECH_ON%Doesn't taste half bad.%SPEECH_OFF% | An old shopkeep waves at you.%SPEECH_ON%It's good seeing you again, sellsword. How often do you hear that?%SPEECH_OFF%He thumbs down the road.%SPEECH_ON%If you'd like to do some more of that good work, then %employer% been looking for you.%SPEECH_OFF% | A man fleecing a sheep looks over to you, the runt wriggling around.%SPEECH_ON%I should just eat this lil' bastard. Look at her go. Quit it, would ya?%SPEECH_OFF%He elbows the beast and it bleats, cursing back with as much sapience as a sheep can muster. The man looks up at you again.%SPEECH_ON%Say, yer that sellsword everyone's been talking about. I should probably tell you, and I guess I will, heh, that, uh, %employer% been looking for you.%SPEECH_OFF%The sheep jumps in an attempted escape, but the man slams her down.%SPEECH_ON%You little git, I'mma milk yer tits dry if you try that again!%SPEECH_OFF%}"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]{Unos campesinos se acercan a ti y uno incluso te ofrece un abrazo. Declinas.%SPEECH_ON%Es bueno verte de nuevo, mercenario. %employer% te ha estado buscando.%SPEECH_OFF% | Una mujer te ofrece una flor cuando entras al pueblo. Esto va contra la respuesta usual que es cerrar las ventanas y esconder a los niños. Tomas la flor y ella menea su falda un poco antes de alejarse bailando. Un hombre se acerca a ti.%SPEECH_ON%Disculpa esa molestia, señor, los lugareños parecen haberte tomado cariño. %employer% también, viendo que te ha estado buscando desde el momento en que oyó que estabas en el pueblo.%SPEECH_OFF% | Una manada de perros corre por el camino, unos niños persiguiéndolos. Pasan junto a ti uno por uno, los perros aullando y resoplando con alegría, los niños gritando saludos. Una mujer se acerca, una sartén de metal en una mano y un trapo de lavar en la otra.%SPEECH_ON%Hola, mercenario. Probablemente debería dejar que uno de esos mensajeros te encuentre y te diga esto, pero tengo las noticias así que te las diré de todos modos. %employer% te está buscando.%SPEECH_OFF%Pestañea coquetamente. Sonríes y asientes. %randombrother% sonríe burlonamente.%SPEECH_ON%¿Ves algo que te guste, señor?%SPEECH_OFF%Le dices al hombre que vaya a tirarse a una cabra. | Un par de cabras balando son conducidas por el camino. Se arrastran por el barro, hurgando sus narices por el fango y de alguna manera encontrando cosas para masticar. Su pastor clava su bastón en el suelo.%SPEECH_ON%Hola, mercenario. %employer% te ha estado buscando.%SPEECH_OFF% | Un hombre sentado en su porche se inclina hacia adelante a la sola vista de ti. Señala con un dedo.%SPEECH_ON%Vaya si no es el mercenario del que todos han estado hablando.%SPEECH_OFF%Miras alrededor antes de asentir. Sonríe y grita y aúlla.%SPEECH_ON%¡Demonios, es malditamente agradable verte por aquí de nuevo! ¡Y sería descortés de mi parte no decirte que %employer% ha estado intentando encontrarte! Ve a ver%lo_employer%. Dile que te envié, tal vez me envíe una recompensa. Probablemente solo un montón de flores, %ese_employer% bastard%o_employer%. O un gato. ¿Quién quiere un gato? ¿Por qué me envió un gato? Le dije que odio los gatos...%SPEECH_OFF%Mientras el hombre divaga, te retiras silenciosamente. | Una mujer corre hacia ti. Trae a sus hijos, sin tomar precauciones con un mercenario. Uno de los niños abraza tus piernas.%SPEECH_ON%¡Ha vuelto!%SPEECH_OFF%Miras hacia abajo y sonríes, tratando sutilmente de sacudirte al bastardo aunque él solo lo toma como juego. La madre recupera al engendro antes de señalar el camino.%SPEECH_ON%%employer% te ha estado buscando. Dile que te encontré, tal vez venga y arregle nuestro pozo una vez sepa que hice un favor.%SPEECH_OFF%Luce agotada por el mundo, arrastrada a los infiernos por la alegría de sus hijos. | Entras a %townname% y un hombre te hace señas hacia su jardín. Está cuidando las plantas, usando una mano firme para cortar las verduras o frutas o lo que sea, no eres jardinero.%SPEECH_ON%¿Cómo estás, mercenario? Si te lo preguntas, %employer% ha estado hablando de ti. Supongo que ha querido verte también, si te interesan más negocios. Aquí, atrapa.%SPEECH_OFF%Se gira y te lanza {una col | una cebolla | una patata | un tomate}.%SPEECH_ON%Buena atrapada.%SPEECH_OFF%Das un mordisco y asientes.%SPEECH_ON%No sabe nada mal.%SPEECH_OFF% | Un viejo tendero te saluda.%SPEECH_ON%Es bueno verte de nuevo, mercenario. ¿Cuán seguido escuchas eso?%SPEECH_OFF%Señala con el pulgar el camino.%SPEECH_ON%Si quieres hacer más de ese buen trabajo, entonces %employer% te ha estado buscando.%SPEECH_OFF% | Un hombre esquilando una oveja te mira, la cría retorciéndose.%SPEECH_ON%Debería simplemente comerme a esta pequeña bastarda. Mírala moverse. Quieta, ¿quieres?%SPEECH_OFF%Le da un codazo a la bestia y bala, maldiciendo con tanta sapiencia como una oveja puede reunir. El hombre te mira de nuevo.%SPEECH_ON%Oye, eres ese mercenario del que todos han estado hablando. Probablemente debería decirte, y supongo que lo haré, je, que, eh, %employer% te ha estado buscando.%SPEECH_OFF%La oveja salta en un intento de escape, pero el hombre la aplasta.%SPEECH_ON%¡Pequeña imbécil, voy a ordeñarte las tetas hasta secarlas si intentas eso de nuevo!%SPEECH_OFF%}"
    }
    // context: ::Const.Contracts.IntroNobleHouseCold[0].Text
    {
        // corrige base: «una capa bien amueblada» calca «well furnished»; una capa no se amuebla. Pasa a «una capa de buena hechura».
        // corrige base: «tú retaliadas» no existe; pasa a «respondes con una mirada amenazante».
        // corrige base: «déjalos festejear» no existe; pasa a «déjalos darse un festín».
        // corrige base: «Adelante y ve a %employer%» pierde el «see» («Go ahead and see»); pasa a «Anda, ve a ver a %employer%».
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]{You cautiously enter the home of one of %employer%'s liaisons. He's sitting next to a fire, a scroll in one hand and a goblet in the other.%SPEECH_ON%Don't bother sitting, sellsword. Wouldn't want to bring a chill to my comforts now would we? If you're looking for %employer%, then I'll send word. %They_employer%'s not happy with you, but business is business, or so we like to say.%SPEECH_OFF%He smiles and tips his goblet toward you. | A few of %employer%'s personal bodyguards stand before you, arms crossed.%SPEECH_ON%What was it we were supposed to do with him again?%SPEECH_OFF%You clutch your sword's handle. One of them laughs.%SPEECH_ON%Send him on through. That's what. %employer% wants further business with him, dunno why, the way I see it we should just run him through here and now.%SPEECH_OFF%They let you on through, but you keep a good eye on your surroundings. | You can't quite put your finger on it, but %townname% seems rather hostile lately. Windows shutter when you walk past, as though your steps carry the wind with them. While doors slam shut and peasants scurry away, a militiaman approaches.%SPEECH_ON%%employer% wishes to have your audience, though you may want to keep on your best behavior. %They_employer% is not in the happiest of moods right now.%SPEECH_OFF% | A few militiaman whistle and hoot as you walk by.%SPEECH_ON%Some nuts on that man coming through here again. Hey sellsword! If you want more business, %employer% is open to some more talks. Just, you know, don't fark it up this time!%SPEECH_OFF% | A man grips the leashes on some war dogs, the hounds snapping their jaws right before they can glom onto one of your legs. Their handler looks at you and for a second he almost seems ready to loosen the harnesses.%SPEECH_ON%Oh, it's you. Well, %employer%'s been looking for you.%SPEECH_OFF% | You pass by a few militiamen. They spit and rattle their scabbards, but you pay it no mind. A man in a well furnished cloak comes to you.%SPEECH_ON%If it is business you seek, then come with me. %employer% would like to speak with you.%SPEECH_OFF% | You pass by a woman who throws a rotten vegetable your way. It sails wide, but you retaliate with a mean, mugging look. She snaps at you.%SPEECH_ON%I say you deserved truer aim!%SPEECH_OFF%You rattle your scabbard and she scurries off. A man approaches, chuckling as he had seen the whole affair.%SPEECH_ON%You are not the most popular person in this town, sellsword. Please, come with me so that you may speak with %employer%.%SPEECH_OFF% | A few militiamen running sword over a grindstone glance at you.%SPEECH_ON%Isn't there a price on his head?%SPEECH_OFF%Another man slugs him in the shoulder.%SPEECH_ON%Aren't you saying that a bit farkin' too loud? Why hey there, sellsword! %employer% would most like to speak with you!%SPEECH_OFF%Uh, yeah, of course. | You approach a man who has a number of warhounds on leashes. They're sitting upright and under command, not a single tongue aloll. Their handler stares at you, the ropes of their bindings in one unclenched hand.%SPEECH_ON%You know, %employer% told me to sic these mutts on you at first sight. And then he said, no, I'd better not. So it went, back and forth, let 'em feast, let the man live.%SPEECH_OFF%You ask the houndmaster which it is now. He turns and spits.%SPEECH_ON%Go up and see %employer%. %They_employer% just wants to talk.%SPEECH_OFF% | You pass a rope swinging from a tree. A man calls out from your side.%SPEECH_ON%Look out, dead man a-walkin'!%SPEECH_OFF%When you turn to him he laughs aloud.%SPEECH_ON%Don't worry, I think they just put that up for practice. Ain't no reason to use it, yet. Go ahead and see %employer%.%SPEECH_OFF% | You walk past a man looking at a wanted poster. He stares at it, then at you, then at the poster, then at you again.%SPEECH_ON%Damn. So close. Hey there, mercenary! I hear %employer% would like to talk to ya!%SPEECH_OFF%}"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]{Entras cautelosamente en la casa de uno de los enlaces de %employer%. Está sentado junto al fuego, un pergamino en una mano y una copa en la otra.%SPEECH_ON%No te molestes en sentarte, mercenario. No querríamos traer un escalofrío a mis comodidades, ¿verdad? Si buscas a %employer%, entonces enviaré aviso. No está content%o_employer% contigo, pero los negocios son negocios, o eso nos gusta decir.%SPEECH_OFF%Sonríe e inclina su copa hacia ti. | Unos guardaespaldas personales de %employer% están frente a ti, brazos cruzados.%SPEECH_ON%¿Qué se suponía que debíamos hacer con él otra vez?%SPEECH_OFF%Agarras el mango de tu espada. Uno de ellos ríe.%SPEECH_ON%Déjenlo pasar. Eso es todo. %employer% quiere más negocios con él, no sé por qué, tal como yo lo veo deberíamos atravesarlo aquí y ahora.%SPEECH_OFF%Te dejan pasar, pero mantienes un buen ojo en tus alrededores. | No puedes precisarlo exactamente, pero %townname% parece bastante hostil últimamente. Las ventanas se cierran cuando pasas, como si tus pasos llevaran el viento con ellos. Mientras las puertas se cierran de golpe y los campesinos se escabullen, un miliciano se acerca.%SPEECH_ON%%employer% desea tu audiencia, aunque querrás comportarte lo mejor posible. No está del mejor humor ahora mismo.%SPEECH_OFF% | Unos milicianos silban y gritan mientras pasas.%SPEECH_ON%Hay que tener agallas para volver por aquí de nuevo. ¡Oye mercenario! Si quieres más negocios, %employer% está abierto a más conversaciones. ¡Solo, ya sabes, no la cagues esta vez!%SPEECH_OFF% | Un hombre agarra las correas de unos perros de guerra, los sabuesos chasqueando sus mandíbulas justo antes de poder agarrarse a una de tus piernas. Su cuidador te mira y por un segundo casi parece listo para soltar los arneses.%SPEECH_ON%Oh, eres tú. Bueno, %employer% te ha estado buscando.%SPEECH_OFF% | Pasas junto a unos milicianos. Escupen y sacuden sus vainas, pero no le prestas atención. Un hombre con una capa de buena hechura viene hacia ti.%SPEECH_ON%Si buscas negocios, entonces ven conmigo. %employer% quisiera hablar contigo.%SPEECH_OFF% | Pasas junto a una mujer que te lanza un vegetal podrido. Pasa de largo, pero tú respondes con una mirada amenazante. Ella te grita.%SPEECH_ON%¡Digo que merecías mejor puntería!%SPEECH_OFF%Sacudes tu vaina y ella se escabulle. Un hombre se acerca, riendo pues había visto todo el asunto.%SPEECH_ON%No eres la persona más popular en este pueblo, mercenario. Por favor, ven conmigo para que puedas hablar con %employer%.%SPEECH_OFF% | Unos milicianos pasando espada sobre una piedra de afilar te miran.%SPEECH_ON%¿No hay un precio por su cabeza?%SPEECH_OFF%Otro hombre le golpea el hombro.%SPEECH_ON%¿No estás diciendo eso demasiado jodidamente alto? ¡Pero hola, mercenario! ¡A %employer% le gustaría mucho hablar contigo!%SPEECH_OFF%Eh, sí, por supuesto. | Te acercas a un hombre que tiene varios mastines de guerra con correa. Están sentados erguidos y bajo mando, ni una sola lengua colgando. Su cuidador te mira fijamente, las cuerdas de sus ataduras en una mano sin apretar.%SPEECH_ON%Sabes, %employer% me dijo que azuzara estos chuchos contra ti a primera vista. Y luego dijo, no, mejor no. Así fue, ida y vuelta, déjalos darse un festín, deja vivir al hombre.%SPEECH_OFF%Le preguntas al maestro de sabuesos cuál es ahora. Se gira y escupe.%SPEECH_ON%Ve a ver a %employer%. Solo quiere hablar.%SPEECH_OFF% | Pasas una cuerda colgando de un árbol. Un hombre grita desde tu lado.%SPEECH_ON%¡Cuidado, hombre muerto caminando!%SPEECH_OFF%Cuando te giras hacia él ríe en voz alta.%SPEECH_ON%No te preocupes, creo que solo la pusieron para practicar. No hay razón para usarla, todavía. Anda, ve a ver a %employer%.%SPEECH_OFF% | Pasas junto a un hombre mirando un cartel de recompensa. Lo mira fijamente, luego a ti, luego al cartel, luego a ti de nuevo.%SPEECH_ON%Maldición. Tan cerca. ¡Hola, mercenario! ¡Oigo que %employer% quisiera hablar contigo!%SPEECH_OFF%}"
    }
    // context: ::Const.Contracts.IntroSettlementNeutral[0].Text
    {
        // corrige base: «una brisa rígida» calca «stiff breeze»; en castellano es «una brisa fuerte».
        // corrige base: «hay direcciones escritas en él» calca «directions»; pasa a «indicaciones».
        // corrige base: «Alcanzas tu daga» calca «reach for»; pasa a «Llevas la mano a tu daga».
        // corrige base: «él es el hombre a quien ir» no es gramatical; pasa a «a quien acudir».
        // corrige base: «desea tener tu oído» calca «wishes to have your ear»; pasa a «desea hablar contigo».
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]{A cowl-shaded man hisses at you, his teeth and nose winking momentarily from the dark of his hood. You've no time for lepers or jokers and demand the man to get out of your way. Instead, he starts talking.%SPEECH_ON%My master requires your services, %they_employer%'s heard of your exploits. Follow me and I shall take you to him.%SPEECH_OFF%You rest your hands on the handle of your sword and nod. | You sit alone, studying a map as a stiff breeze tries to take off with it. As you struggle to keep the sheet on the table, %randombrother%, one of your men, approaches and slams a mug on the paper's corner. You look up to see %they_randombrother%'s a bit slackjawed with drink on %their_randombrother% breath. %They_randombrother% explains that %they_randombrother% shared stories with a local by the name of %employer% who has a proposal for you. The maps and the lands they detail aren't going anywhere, so you agree to meet with %them_employer% and hear %them_employer% out. | You enter %townname% and a man immediately approaches, trundling through the mud to get to you. He announces himself as someone in the employ of %employer%, a %person_employer% of some power in this town and %they_employer%, along with the thoughts and monies of others, have decided to seek your services. | A man walks up to you and holds a scroll halfway between he and you.%SPEECH_ON%My name is %randomname%, representative of %employer% and speaking on behalf of the good people of %townname%. We seek your services, mercenary.%SPEECH_OFF% | A man approaches from the side of the road. He's dressed in a peasant's garb, yet is guarded by two well-armed men. He announces himself as a councilman in the employ of %employer%, a local leader of %townname%. You are asked to take audience with the man. | A hooded man gestures you to follow him. Nervously looking over his shoulder, he leads you to the backroom of a local tavern. Before addressing you, he takes his time to peek out the windows - probably looking for anyone eavesdropping.%SPEECH_ON%A figurehead by the name of %employer% wishes to see you. %They_employer%'s a %person_employer% of some repute in this town, so you understand my discretion.%SPEECH_OFF%He slides a paper toward you - there are directions written on it. | A drunken woman throws herself at you. She practically drools licentious horrors into your ear and you beat her off with a stick. One onlooker rushes to your side, yanking the wench away.%SPEECH_ON%Begone, whore! How many times must I tell you?%SPEECH_OFF%The lady saunters off, clambering from one man to another like an animal between tree branches. Your 'rescuer' offers his hand.%SPEECH_ON%I am %randomname%. A man of some import, %employer%, has been looking for you. Please, follow me and I shall bring you to him.%SPEECH_OFF% | While your men venture around town, you go to a pub and take a seat. As soon as you do, a strange man joins you.%SPEECH_ON%You with the %companyname%?%SPEECH_OFF%You nod. The man nods back then reaches into his pocket. You reach for your dagger. The stranger puts his hand out.%SPEECH_ON%Easy there. I'm wearing a sword. If I wanted to kill ya, taking a seat probably wouldn't be the best route.%SPEECH_OFF%The man lifts the sheath and it bumps the underside of the table. He cocks his head as if to say, 'see?' You nod and the man continues with his move, taking out a note and passing it to you.%SPEECH_ON%A local councilman by the name of %employer% wishes to see you.%SPEECH_OFF% | You walk around %townname% before stopping a man and asking him if there's anything interesting around. He balances a smelly and dripping pitchfork on his shoulder as he thinks.%SPEECH_ON%Well. There's the hoo-ores, mmhmm.%SPEECH_OFF%The man grins, mostly to himself on that one.%SPEECH_ON%They alright. There's also %employer%. Wait, are you that sellsword feller?%SPEECH_OFF%The stranger squints at you then quickly continues.%SPEECH_ON%Ah shit, of course. Yeah, %employer% talked about you. %They_employer% said... '%randomname%, go and clear out the shit in the horse stalls. And if you see that mercenary people are talking of, fetch 'im for me.'%SPEECH_OFF%He stops and points down the road toward a building.%SPEECH_ON%So, yeah, if ya want some money then that fella in there wants to pay ya. I don't think %they_employer% needs another man slingin' shit, if you was worried about that. I got that shit under lock!%SPEECH_OFF% | You enter a tavern and garner a few looks for your arrival. Men whisper to one another, the women ogle as they tend to do. The bartender fists a cloth into a mug then calls you over.%SPEECH_ON%You're that mercenary people been wonderin' about.%SPEECH_OFF%Curious, you ask how could he know, being that you aren't the only man walking around with a sword. He laughs.%SPEECH_ON%The eyes. That's where I can see it. You're a man who hunts a most dangerous sort of prey. A life of taking lives is a world in and of itself, but you seek out those whose lives have gained such odd values that their death would be but a monetary appreciation for others. A purchase is placed, so thus you become the means to a transaction. It is so, isn't it? You're a bone collector, my friend. A gravedigger paid in advance.%SPEECH_OFF%You nod, understanding. Suddenly, a man comes up to you and explains that a local figurehead by the name of %employer% wishes to have your ear. When you turn back, the bartender is gone. | You come across a man leaning against a porch post. He hails you down.%SPEECH_ON%%employer%'s been looking for you, sellsword. %They_employer%'s down yonder in the village communal.%SPEECH_OFF%The stranger nods towards a large building a little ways along the road.%SPEECH_ON%I hope you do good, mercenary. The people of %townname% are wary of your sort, but that don't mean their hearts can't be won over.%SPEECH_OFF% | A man strums a stringed instrument as you walk by. He slashes an ear-piercing chord and you turn to find him laughing.%SPEECH_ON%Heh, I thought that mind fetch your attention. %employer% said we should keep a lookout for a man of your... vocation. If you're looking for work, %they_employer%'s the %person_employer% to go to.%SPEECH_OFF%You ask if this figurehead pays well. The man nods.%SPEECH_ON%Yup. %They_employer% gave me this here lute as payment once. Now I'm just waiting for the old devils to come down and challenge me to a tune. %employer% said if you best one in a game of songs, then they'll give ya golden lute. Now that's what I call good payment, wouldn't you agree?%SPEECH_OFF%The man turns back to the instrument, drawing a mewling tune out from the strings. In the distance, dogs begin to howl. | As you take stock of your inventory, a rather well-to-do man spots you and heads your way. He announces himself as being in the employ of %employer%, an influential person in %townname% that wishes to talk business. You hand your duties over to %randombrother% and let the man lead the way. | %randombrother% comes along with a small boy racing at his side. When they get to you, the pair talk at the same time, stop, and then start again. You hold your hand up, and then point to the little boy who immediately says that %employer% wishes to see you. You then point to the battle brother who says a local bitch has birthed puppies and maybe the %companyname% could take one. Pursing your lips, you tell the boy to take you to his master who is found already waiting for you.}"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]{Un hombre con capucha te sisea, sus dientes y nariz destellando momentáneamente desde la oscuridad de su capucha. No tienes tiempo para leprosos o bromistas y exiges al hombre que se aparte de tu camino. En su lugar, comienza a hablar.%SPEECH_ON%Mi am%o_employer% requiere tus servicios, ha oído de tus hazañas. Sígueme y te llevaré con %el_employer%.%SPEECH_OFF%Apoyas tus manos en el mango de tu espada y asientes. | Te sientas solo, estudiando un mapa mientras una brisa fuerte intenta llevárselo. Mientras luchas por mantener la hoja sobre la mesa, %randombrother%, uno de los tuyos, se acerca y golpea una jarra en la esquina del papel. Miras hacia arriba para ver que está algo boquiabiert%o_randombrother% con aliento a bebida. Explica que compartió historias con %un_employer% lugareñ%o_employer% llamad%o_employer% %employer% que tiene una propuesta para ti. Los mapas y las tierras que detallan no van a ninguna parte, así que aceptas reunirte con %el_employer% y escuchar%lo_employer%. | Entras a %townname% y un hombre se acerca inmediatamente, caminando pesadamente por el barro para llegar a ti. Se presenta como alguien al servicio de %employer%, %un_employer% %hombre_employer% de cierto poder en este pueblo que, junto con los pensamientos y dineros de otros, ha decidido buscar tus servicios. | Un hombre camina hacia ti y sostiene un pergamino a medio camino entre él y tú.%SPEECH_ON%Mi nombre es %randomname%, representante de %employer% y hablando en nombre de la buena gente de %townname%. Buscamos tus servicios, mercenario.%SPEECH_OFF% | Un hombre se acerca desde el lado del camino. Está vestido con atuendo campesino, pero custodiado por dos hombres bien armados. Se presenta como concejal al servicio de %employer%, %un_employer% líder local de %townname%. Se te pide que tengas audiencia con el hombre. | Un hombre encapuchado te hace señas para que lo sigas. Mirando nerviosamente sobre su hombro, te conduce al cuarto trasero de una taberna local. Antes de dirigirse a ti, se toma su tiempo para asomarse por las ventanas, probablemente buscando a cualquiera escuchando a escondidas.%SPEECH_ON%Una figura llamada %employer% desea verte. Es %un_employer% %hombre_employer% de cierta reputación en este pueblo, así que entiendes mi discreción.%SPEECH_OFF%Desliza un papel hacia ti: hay indicaciones escritas en él. | Una mujer borracha se te lanza encima. Prácticamente babea horrores lascivos en tu oído y la ahuyentas con un palo. Un espectador corre a tu lado, arrancando a la desgraciada.%SPEECH_ON%¡Fuera, puta! ¿Cuántas veces debo decírtelo?%SPEECH_OFF%La dama se aleja contoneándose, agarrándose de un hombre a otro como un animal entre ramas de árbol. Tu 'rescatador' ofrece su mano.%SPEECH_ON%Soy %randomname%. %Un_employer% %hombre_employer% de cierta importancia, %employer%, te ha estado buscando. Por favor, sígueme y te llevaré con %el_employer%.%SPEECH_OFF% | Mientras tus hombres se aventuran por el pueblo, vas a un bar y tomas asiento. Tan pronto lo haces, un hombre extraño se te une.%SPEECH_ON%¿Eres de la %companyname%?%SPEECH_OFF%Asientes. El hombre asiente de vuelta luego mete la mano en su bolsillo. Llevas la mano a tu daga. El extraño levanta su mano.%SPEECH_ON%Tranquilo. Llevo una espada. Si quisiera matarte, sentarme probablemente no sería la mejor ruta.%SPEECH_OFF%El hombre levanta la vaina y golpea el lado inferior de la mesa. Inclina la cabeza como diciendo '¿ves?' Asientes y el hombre continúa con su movimiento, sacando una nota y pasándotela.%SPEECH_ON%%Un_employer% concejal local llamad%o_employer% %employer% desea verte.%SPEECH_OFF% | Caminas por %townname% antes de detener a un hombre y preguntarle si hay algo interesante por aquí. Balancea una horca maloliente y goteante en su hombro mientras piensa.%SPEECH_ON%Bueno. Están las pu-utas, mmhmm.%SPEECH_OFF%El hombre sonríe, sobre todo para sus adentros con ese chiste.%SPEECH_ON%Están bien. También está %employer%. Espera, ¿eres ese tipo mercenario?%SPEECH_OFF%El extraño entrecierra los ojos hacia ti luego continúa rápidamente.%SPEECH_ON%Ah mierda, por supuesto. Sí, %employer% habló de ti. Dijo... '%randomname%, ve y limpia la mierda en los establos de caballos. Y si ves a ese mercenario del que la gente habla, tráemelo.'%SPEECH_OFF%Se detiene y señala el camino hacia un edificio.%SPEECH_ON%Así que, sí, si quieres algo de dinero, quien está ahí dentro quiere pagarte. No creo que necesite otro hombre lanzando mierda, si te preocupaba eso. ¡Tengo esa mierda bajo llave!%SPEECH_OFF% | Entras a una taberna y recibes algunas miradas por tu llegada. Los hombres susurran entre ellos, las mujeres te miran como suelen hacer. El cantinero mete un trapo en una jarra luego te llama.%SPEECH_ON%Eres ese mercenario del que la gente se ha estado preguntando.%SPEECH_OFF%Curioso, preguntas cómo pudo saber, siendo que no eres el único hombre caminando con una espada. Ríe.%SPEECH_ON%Los ojos. Ahí es donde puedo verlo. Eres un hombre que caza una clase muy peligrosa de presa. Una vida tomando vidas es un mundo en sí mismo, pero buscas a aquellos cuyas vidas han ganado valores tan extraños que su muerte sería solo una apreciación monetaria para otros. Se hace una compra, así te conviertes en el medio para una transacción. Es así, ¿no? Eres un coleccionista de huesos, amigo mío. Un sepulturero pagado por adelantado.%SPEECH_OFF%Asientes, entendiendo. De repente, un hombre se acerca a ti y explica que una figura local llamada %employer% desea hablar contigo. Cuando te giras, el cantinero se ha ido. | Te encuentras con un hombre apoyado contra un poste del porche. Te saluda.%SPEECH_ON%%employer% te ha estado buscando, mercenario. Está allá abajo en el comunal del pueblo.%SPEECH_OFF%El extraño asiente hacia un gran edificio un poco más adelante en el camino.%SPEECH_ON%Espero que hagas el bien, mercenario. La gente de %townname% desconfía de tu clase, pero eso no significa que sus corazones no puedan ser ganados.%SPEECH_OFF% | Un hombre rasguea un instrumento de cuerda mientras pasas. Corta un acorde desgarrador y te giras para encontrarlo riendo.%SPEECH_ON%Je, pensé que eso captaría tu atención. %employer% dijo que deberíamos estar atentos a un hombre de tu... vocación. Si buscas trabajo, es %art_employer% %hombre_employer% a quien acudir.%SPEECH_OFF%Preguntas si esta figura paga bien. El hombre asiente.%SPEECH_ON%Sip. Me dio este laúd como pago una vez. Ahora solo estoy esperando que los viejos demonios bajen y me desafíen a una melodía. %employer% dijo que si vences a uno en un juego de canciones, entonces te darán un laúd dorado. Ahora eso es lo que llamo buen pago, ¿no estarías de acuerdo?%SPEECH_OFF%El hombre se gira de vuelta al instrumento, extrayendo una melodía llorosa de las cuerdas. A la distancia, los perros comienzan a aullar. | Mientras haces inventario, un hombre bastante acomodado te ve y se dirige hacia ti. Se presenta como al servicio de %employer%, una persona influyente en %townname% que desea hablar de negocios. Entregas tus deberes a %randombrother% y dejas que el hombre guíe el camino. | %randombrother% viene junto con un niño pequeño corriendo a su lado. Cuando llegan a ti, el par habla al mismo tiempo, se detiene, y luego comienza de nuevo. Levantas la mano, luego señalas al niño pequeño que inmediatamente dice que %employer% desea verte. Luego señalas al hermano de batalla que dice que una perra local ha parido cachorros y tal vez la %companyname% podría tomar uno. Frunciendo los labios, le dices al niño que te lleve con su am%o_employer%, que ya te está esperando.}"
    }
    // en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]\x7bA few peasants walk up to you and one even offers a hug. You decline.%SPEECH_ON%It's good to see you again, sellsword. %employer%'s been looking for you.%SPEECH_OFF% | A woman offers you a flower when you walk into town. This is against the usual response which is shutter the windows and hide the kids. You take the flower and she sways her skirt a little before prancing away. A man comes up to you.%SPEECH_ON%Sorry for that bother, sir, the townsfolk seemed to have taken a liking to you. %employer% as well, seeing as how he's been looking for you since the moment he heard you were in town.%SPEECH_OFF% | A pack of dogs streams down the road, a few children in chase. They scatter past you one by one, the dogs howling and huffing with joy, the children screaming out greetings. A woman walks up, a metal skillet in one hand and a wash rag in the other.%SPEECH_ON%Hey there sellsword. I probably should let one of them messenger men find and tell you this, but I got the news so I'll tell you anyhow. %employer%'s looking for you.%SPEECH_OFF%She flutters her eyes. You smile back and nod. %randombrother% smirks.%SPEECH_ON%See something you like, sir?%SPEECH_OFF%You tell the man to go fark a goat. | A couple of bleating goats are being lead down the road. They shuffle through the mud, prodding their noses through the muck and somehow finding things to chew up. Their shepherd plants his cane in the ground.%SPEECH_ON%Hey there mercenary. %employer%'s been looking for ya.%SPEECH_OFF% | A man sitting on his porch leans forward at the very sight of you. He points a finger.%SPEECH_ON%Well if it ain't the sellsword everyone been talking of.%SPEECH_OFF%You look around before nodding. He grins and hoots and hollers.%SPEECH_ON%Hell, it's damned nice seeing you around again! And it'd be short of me not to tell you that %employer%'s been tryin' to find ya. Go and see him. Tell him I sent ya, maybe he'll send me a reward. Probably just a bunch of flowers, that bastard. Or a cat. Who wants a cat? Why did he ever send me a cat? I told him I hate cats...%SPEECH_OFF%As the man rambles on, you quietly make your leave. | A woman runs up to you. She brings her children with, not exactly taking precautions with a sellsword. One of the kids swings their arms around your leg.%SPEECH_ON%He's back!%SPEECH_OFF%You look down and grin, subtly trying to shake the bastard off although he just takes it for play. The mother retrieves the spawn before pointing up the road.%SPEECH_ON%%employer%'s been lookin' for ya. Tell him I fetched ya, maybe he'll come and fix our well once he knows I done a favor.%SPEECH_OFF%She looks world weary, dragged to the hells by the cheeriness of her children. | You walk into %townname% and a man beckons you into his garden. He's tending the plants, using a steady hand to clip the vegetables or fruit or whatever it is, you're not a gardener.%SPEECH_ON%How are you doing, sellsword? If you're wondering, %employer% been talking of you. Suppose he's been wanting to see you, too, if yer interested in some more business. Here, catch.%SPEECH_OFF%He turns and tosses a \x7bcabbage | onion | potato | tomato\x7d at you.%SPEECH_ON%Nice catch.%SPEECH_OFF%You take a bite and nod back.%SPEECH_ON%Doesn't taste half bad.%SPEECH_OFF% | An old shopkeep waves at you.%SPEECH_ON%It's good seeing you again, sellsword. How often do you hear that?%SPEECH_OFF%He thumbs down the road.%SPEECH_ON%If you'd like to do some more of that good work, then %employer% been looking for you.%SPEECH_OFF% | A man fleecing a sheep looks over to you, the runt wriggling around.%SPEECH_ON%I should just eat this lil' bastard. Look at her go. Quit it, would ya?%SPEECH_OFF%He elbows the beast and it bleats, cursing back with as much sapience as a sheep can muster. The man looks up at you again.%SPEECH_ON%Say, yer that sellsword everyone's been talking about. I should probably tell you, and I guess I will, heh, that, uh, %employer% been looking for you.%SPEECH_OFF%The sheep jumps in an attempted escape, but the man slams her down.%SPEECH_ON%You little git, I'mma milk yer tits dry if you try that again!%SPEECH_OFF%\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // context: ::Const.Contracts.IntroSettlementCold[0].Text
    {
        // corrige base: «armas laterales» calca «sidearms»; pasa a «armas de cinto».
        // corrige base: «Parte de la milicia [...] te miran de reojo» no concuerda; pasa a «te mira de reojo».
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]{An old man's sitting out on a hovel's porch when you enter the town. He spits at the very sight of you.%SPEECH_ON%Some balls on you showing your face around these parts, sellsword.%SPEECH_OFF%He wipes his mouth on his sleeve.%SPEECH_ON%But I won't lie and say we don't need you, though I hate to all the hells that I have to admit it. Come on then, you know who to see if it's money yer after. %employer% be where %they_employer% always be.%SPEECH_OFF% | You enter %townname% and a man barks out at you.%SPEECH_ON%Well shit, if it ain't the %companyname% and the snake in the grass it calls a leader.%SPEECH_OFF%You raise an eyebrow, and put a hand to your sword. The man laughs.%SPEECH_ON%We don't care for you, sellsword, but we do need ya. Come on, slither this way so we can talk business. That's what you really care about, right? %employer% is the man you want to be seeing.%SPEECH_OFF% | %townname%'s denizens duck out of sight as you enter. Many a shutter slam close, and children are hushed and hurried away. A man's standing in the middle of the road, his hands on his hips.%SPEECH_ON%Well, it's you.%SPEECH_OFF%You look around, making sure some ambush isn't about to fall down on your damn head. The man laughs.%SPEECH_ON%We ain't gonna kill ya, sellsword. I'm out here to broker a deal, that's all. If you're interested, come see %employer%.%SPEECH_OFF%He spits, turns, and walks off. You spend a second longer looking out for that ambush. | Frightened women and children run from the sight of you. A few men linger, clutching their pitchforks or sidearms as you pass. An elder steps forward, eyeing you up and down.%SPEECH_ON%%employer%'s been looking for ya. I don't know why after all that you've done, but I won't get between %them_employer% and his business.%SPEECH_OFF% | Some of %townname%'s ragged militia give you the side-eye as you enter the town. One spits and yells out.%SPEECH_ON%%employer%'s looking for you, sellsword.%SPEECH_OFF%His voice trails off into what you thought sounded like obscenities. | A woman hurries across the road to pick up her child. She twirls the kid around, a protective hand clutching the back of its head.%SPEECH_ON%I don't know what you're doing here again, sellsword, but %employer%'s been looking for you anyhow.%SPEECH_OFF%She runs off, though occasionally looking behind her with furtive glances. | Kids cycle around your feet as you walk down the road. Their parents come out screaming, telling the kids to get away from you. A mother ushers her daughter away while mean mugging you.%SPEECH_ON%Don't ever touch my child. And if it's business you want, then go see %employer%.%SPEECH_OFF% | A man's repairing the roof of his home when he sees you.%SPEECH_ON%Ah hell, you again?%SPEECH_OFF%You look around then turn back to the man. He laughs.%SPEECH_ON%Most folks don't take kindly to yer being here. I suppose I'm neutral on the matter, but then again it's easy to be on the fence when yer ten feet up in the air.%SPEECH_OFF%He grins, but his foot kicks out and he almost slides off his roof. He clutches onto the thatching.%SPEECH_ON%Whoa! Well, uh, anyway %employer%'s looking for you. Don't mind the hate of the people. It's what comes natural to them.%SPEECH_OFF% | People scurry from the sight of the %companyname%. One man yells out from his window.%SPEECH_ON%'Ey mercenary! %employer% been wanting to see you!%SPEECH_OFF%He quickly shutters his windows before you can respond.}"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_20.png[/img]{Un anciano está sentado en el porche de un cuchitril cuando entras al pueblo. Escupe a la sola vista de ti.%SPEECH_ON%Hay que tener agallas para mostrar tu cara por estos lados, mercenario.%SPEECH_OFF%Se limpia la boca con su manga.%SPEECH_ON%Pero no mentiré y diré que no te necesitamos, aunque odio hasta los infiernos tener que admitirlo. Vamos entonces, sabes a quién ver si es dinero lo que buscas. %employer% está donde siempre está.%SPEECH_OFF% | Entras a %townname% y un hombre te ladra.%SPEECH_ON%Vaya mierda, si no es la %companyname% y la serpiente en la hierba que llama líder.%SPEECH_OFF%Levantas una ceja y pones una mano en tu espada. El hombre ríe.%SPEECH_ON%No nos agradas, mercenario, pero sí te necesitamos. Vamos, repta por aquí para que podamos hablar de negocios. Eso es lo que realmente te importa, ¿verdad? %employer% es %art_employer% %hombre_employer% a quien quieres ver.%SPEECH_OFF% | Los habitantes de %townname% se esconden de la vista cuando entras. Muchas ventanas se cierran de golpe, y los niños son callados y apurados. Un hombre está parado en medio del camino, sus manos en sus caderas.%SPEECH_ON%Bueno, eres tú.%SPEECH_OFF%Miras alrededor, asegurándote de que alguna emboscada no esté a punto de caer sobre tu maldita cabeza. El hombre ríe.%SPEECH_ON%No vamos a matarte, mercenario. Estoy aquí para negociar un trato, eso es todo. Si te interesa, ven a ver a %employer%.%SPEECH_OFF%Escupe, se gira y se va. Pasas un segundo más buscando esa emboscada. | Mujeres y niños asustados huyen a tu vista. Unos hombres permanecen, agarrando sus horcas o armas de cinto mientras pasas. Un anciano da un paso adelante, mirándote de arriba abajo.%SPEECH_ON%%employer% te ha estado buscando. No sé por qué después de todo lo que has hecho, pero no me interpondré entre %el_employer% y sus negocios.%SPEECH_OFF% | Parte de la milicia andrajosa de %townname% te mira de reojo cuando entras al pueblo. Uno escupe y grita.%SPEECH_ON%%employer% te está buscando, mercenario.%SPEECH_OFF%Su voz se apaga en lo que pensaste sonaban como obscenidades. | Una mujer se apresura a cruzar el camino para recoger a su hijo. Gira al niño, una mano protectora agarrando la parte trasera de su cabeza.%SPEECH_ON%No sé qué estás haciendo aquí de nuevo, mercenario, pero %employer% te ha estado buscando de todos modos.%SPEECH_OFF%Huye, aunque ocasionalmente mirando detrás con miradas furtivas. | Los niños circulan alrededor de tus pies mientras caminas por el camino. Sus padres salen gritando, diciéndoles a los niños que se alejen de ti. Una madre lleva a su hija mientras te mira amenazadoramente.%SPEECH_ON%Nunca toques a mi hija. Y si es negocios lo que quieres, entonces ve a ver a %employer%.%SPEECH_OFF% | Un hombre está reparando el techo de su casa cuando te ve.%SPEECH_ON%Ah demonios, ¿tú otra vez?%SPEECH_OFF%Miras alrededor luego te giras de vuelta al hombre. Ríe.%SPEECH_ON%A la mayoría de la gente no le agrada que estés aquí. Supongo que soy neutral en el asunto, pero entonces de nuevo es fácil estar en la cerca cuando estás diez pies arriba en el aire.%SPEECH_OFF%Sonríe, pero su pie patea y casi se desliza de su techo. Se agarra del techo de paja.%SPEECH_ON%¡Guau! Bueno, eh, de todos modos %employer% te está buscando. No te importe el odio de la gente. Es lo que les viene natural.%SPEECH_OFF% | La gente se escabulle a la vista de la %companyname%. Un hombre grita desde su ventana.%SPEECH_ON%¡Ey mercenario! ¡%employer% ha querido verte!%SPEECH_OFF%Cierra rápidamente sus ventanas antes de que puedas responder.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\afterHooks\contracts\templates\negotiation_templates.nut
    // en = "Get <n:int> crowns on completion"
    // en base_es
    // context: ::Const.Contracts.Overview[0].start.Text
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_04.png[/img]{%SPEECH_START%I refuse to pay any more for this.%SPEECH_OFF%  | %SPEECH_START%Be reasonable.%SPEECH_OFF%  | %SPEECH_START%No, no and no.%SPEECH_OFF%  | %SPEECH_START%Who do you think you are? I tell you how much you're getting paid!%SPEECH_OFF%  | %They_employer% looks at you sternly and shakes %their_employer% head. | %SPEECH_START%No, you are already getting more than you're worth.%SPEECH_OFF%  | %SPEECH_START%No. Don't not push me too far!%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%This isn't worth that much to me.%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%I don't think you quite understand how this works. We need to come to terms if you want to be paid for this. My offer still stands.%SPEECH_OFF% }"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_04.png[/img]{%SPEECH_START%Me niego a pagar más por esto.%SPEECH_OFF%  | %SPEECH_START%Sé razonable.%SPEECH_OFF%  | %SPEECH_START%No, no y no.%SPEECH_OFF%  | %SPEECH_START%¿Quién te crees que eres? ¡Soy yo quien dice cuánto se te paga!%SPEECH_OFF%  | Te mira con severidad y niega con la cabeza. | %SPEECH_START%No, ya estás cobrando más de lo que vales.%SPEECH_OFF%  | %SPEECH_START%No. ¡No me presiones demasiado!%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%Esto no vale tanto para mí.%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%Creo que no entiendes del todo cómo funciona esto. Tenemos que llegar a un acuerdo si quieres cobrar por esto. Mi oferta sigue en pie.%SPEECH_OFF% }"
    }
    // en = "We need to be paid more for this."
    // en base_es
    // en = "Forget it, this isn't worth it."
    // en base_es
    // context: ::Const.Contracts.NegotiationDefault[0].start.Text
    {
        // corrige base: «¿Esto es entonces?» no es idiomático; «This is it then?» es «¿Así que esto es todo?».
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_04.png[/img]{%SPEECH_START%This is it then?  | %They_employer% takes a deep breath.%SPEECH_ON% | %They_employer% sighs.%SPEECH_ON% | %SPEECH_START%Fair enough.  | %SPEECH_START%Fine, fine.  | %SPEECH_START%If it must be.  | %SPEECH_START%Fine. How about this?  | %SPEECH_START%Sure, sure, I understand.  | %SPEECH_START%Reasonable.  | %SPEECH_START%Interesting. I think this would be more appropiate then.  | %SPEECH_START%Would you take this instead?  | %SPEECH_START%Let me make the following offer.  | %SPEECH_ON%Fair. Would you accept this instead?  | %SPEECH_START%Very well. Given your demands I offer you this.  | %SPEECH_START%Let's get this over with quickly. Here is my new offer.  | %SPEECH_START%We're all friends here, aren't we? Let's see... }"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_04.png[/img]{%SPEECH_START%¿Así que esto es todo?  | Respira profundamente.%SPEECH_ON% | Suspira.%SPEECH_ON% | %SPEECH_START%Es justo.  | %SPEECH_START%Bien, bien.  | %SPEECH_START%Si es necesario.  | %SPEECH_START%Bien. ¿Qué tal esto?  | %SPEECH_START%Claro, claro, lo entiendo.  | %SPEECH_START%Razonable.  | %SPEECH_START%Interesante. Creo que esto sería más apropiado entonces.  | %SPEECH_START%¿Aceptarías esto en su lugar?  | %SPEECH_START%Permíteme hacerte la siguiente oferta.  | %SPEECH_ON%Aceptable. ¿Aceptarías esto en su lugar?  | %SPEECH_START%Muy bien. Ante tus exigencias te ofrezco esto.  | %SPEECH_START%Terminemos con esto rápidamente. Aquí está mi nueva oferta.  | %SPEECH_START%Todos somos amigos aquí, ¿no? Vamos a ver... }"
    }
    // en = "We need to be paid per head we return with."
    // en base_es
    // en = "We need to be paid more per head we return with."
    // en base_es
    // context: ::Const.Contracts.NegotiationPerHead[0].start.Text
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_04.png[/img]{%They_employer% nods.%SPEECH_ON%Yes. Good. I was thinking about payment for your task earlier. | %They_employer% smiles.%SPEECH_ON%This will make you rich, my friend. | %They_employer% takes a deep breath.%SPEECH_ON%Very well, this is what I'm prepared to offer you. | %They_employer% puts %their_employer% hand on your shoulder, smiling reaffirmingly.%SPEECH_ON%I think I know an adequate compensation for your services. | %They_employer% gesticulates with %their_employer% hands, pointing at %their_employer% fingers as if counting something, but it means nothing to you.%SPEECH_ON%Judging from experience, this is good payment for the task. | %They_employer% nods. %SPEECH_ON%You look able, so I am willing to pay quite a bit. | %They_employer% jingles with a bag of coins.%SPEECH_ON%This will be yours if you help me out on this. | %They_employer% opens the palm of %their_employer% hands.%SPEECH_ON%I'm tight on crowns, so before you ask, this is all I have right now. | %SPEECH_ON%Rest assured that what I'm offering you now is a fine prize for your work.} "
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_04.png[/img]{Asiente.%SPEECH_ON%Sí. Bien. Hace un rato estaba pensando en el pago por tu tarea. | Sonríe.%SPEECH_ON%Esto te hará rico, amigo mío. | Respira profundamente.%SPEECH_ON%Muy bien, esto es lo que estoy dispuest%o_employer% a ofrecerte. | Te pone la mano en el hombro con una sonrisa tranquilizadora.%SPEECH_ON%Creo que sé cuál sería una compensación adecuada por tus servicios. | Gesticula con las manos y se señala los dedos como si contara algo, pero para ti no significa nada.%SPEECH_ON%Por experiencia, esta es una buena paga por la tarea. | Asiente. %SPEECH_ON%Pareces capaz, así que estoy dispuest%o_employer% a pagar bastante. | Hace tintinear una bolsa de monedas.%SPEECH_ON%Será tuya si me ayudas con esto. | Abre las palmas de las manos.%SPEECH_ON%Ando cort%o_employer% de coronas, así que, antes de que lo preguntes, esto es todo lo que tengo ahora mismo. | %SPEECH_ON%Ten por seguro que lo que te ofrezco ahora es una buena recompensa por tu trabajo.} "
    }
    // en = "\x7bYou'll get | You are to receive | You'll be paid | It's\x7d %reward_count% crowns per head you bring back, \x7bfor up to %maxcount% heads | and I'll pay for up to %maxcount% heads | %maxcount% heads at most\x7d.%SPEECH_OFF%"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bYou'll get | You are to receive | You'll be paid | It's\x7d %reward_advance% crowns in advance, and another %reward_count% crowns per head you bring back, \x7bfor up to %maxcount% heads | and I'll pay for up to %maxcount% heads | %maxcount% heads at most\x7d.%SPEECH_OFF%"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bYou'll get | You are to receive | You'll be paid | It's\x7d %reward_count% crowns per head you return with, \x7bfor up to %maxcount% heads | and I'll pay for up to %maxcount% heads | %maxcount% heads at most\x7d, and another %reward_completion% when the job is done.%SPEECH_OFF%"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bYou'll get | You are to receive | You'll be paid | It's\x7d %reward_advance% crowns in advance, %reward_count% crowns per head you bring, \x7bfor up to %maxcount% heads | and I'll pay for up to %maxcount% heads | %maxcount% heads at most\x7d, and another %reward_completion% when the job is done.%SPEECH_OFF%"
    // en base_es
    // context: ::Const.Contracts.NegotiationPerHead[1].Text
    {
        // corrige base: «You act as if you were the only ones» va en plural; «Actúas como si fueras el único» pasa a «Actúan como si fueran los únicos».
        // corrige base: «I can only be pushed so far» no es «solo puedo dejarme llevar»; pasa a «mi paciencia tiene un límite».
        // corrige base: «I'll take my leave» es «Me retiro»; «Largo» añade una grosería que el inglés no tiene.
        // corrige base: «until you learned some reason» es «hasta que hayas entrado en razón», no «sin algún motivo».
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_74.png[/img]{%SPEECH_START%You act as if you were the only ones to hold a sword for coin. I think I'll look elsewhere for the men I need. Good day.%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%My patience has limits, too, and I think I'm wasting my time here.%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%I've had enough of this! I'm sure I'll find someone else to do the job!%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%Do not insult my intelligence! Forget about this contract. We're done.%SPEECH_OFF% | %Their_employer% face turns red with anger.%SPEECH_ON%Get out of here, I'm not in the habit of making deals with greedy devils!%SPEECH_OFF% | %They_employer% sighs. %SPEECH_ON%Just... forget it. I shouldn't have trusted you in the first place. Leave me so I can look for other, more sensible men.%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%I really thought we had a good relationship here. But know that I can only be pushed so far. I don't think this is working out. I'll take my leave.%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%This has been an utter waste of time for me. Don't bother coming back until you learned some reason.%SPEECH_OFF%}"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_74.png[/img]{%SPEECH_START%Actúan como si fueran los únicos que empuñan una espada a cambio de monedas. Creo que buscaré en otra parte a los hombres que necesito. Buen día.%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%Mi paciencia también tiene límites y creo que estoy perdiendo el tiempo aquí.%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%¡Ya tuve suficiente de esto! ¡Estoy segur%o_employer% de que encontraré a alguien más que haga el trabajo!%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%¡No insultes mi inteligencia! Olvídate de este contrato. Hemos terminado.%SPEECH_OFF% | Su cara se pone roja de ira.%SPEECH_ON%¡Fuera de aquí, no tengo la costumbre de hacer tratos con demonios codiciosos!%SPEECH_OFF% | Suspira. %SPEECH_ON%Solo... olvídalo. En primer lugar, no debería haber confiado en ti. Déjame para buscar otros hombres más sensatos.%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%Realmente pensé que teníamos una buena relación aquí. Pero debes saber que mi paciencia tiene un límite. No creo que esto esté funcionando. Me retiro.%SPEECH_OFF% | %SPEECH_START%Esto ha sido una total pérdida de tiempo para mí. No te molestes en volver hasta que hayas entrado en razón.%SPEECH_OFF%}"
    }
    // en = "Get <per:int> crowns per head you arrive with, up to <max:int> total"
    // en base_es
    // en = "We need to be paid per head we arrive with."
    // en base_es
    // en = "We need to be paid more per head we arrive with."
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bYou'll get | You are to receive | You'll be paid | It's\x7d %reward_count% crowns per head you arrive with, \x7bfor up to %maxcount% heads | and I'll pay for up to %maxcount% heads | %maxcount% heads at most\x7d.%SPEECH_OFF%"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bYou'll get | You are to receive | You'll be paid | It's\x7d %reward_advance% crowns in advance, and another %reward_count% crowns per head you arrive with, \x7bfor up to %maxcount% heads | and I'll pay for up to %maxcount% heads | %maxcount% heads at most\x7d.%SPEECH_OFF%"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bYou'll get | You are to receive | You'll be paid | It's\x7d %reward_count% crowns per head you arrive with, \x7bfor up to %maxcount% heads | and I'll pay for up to %maxcount% heads | %maxcount% heads at most\x7d, and another %reward_completion% when the job is done.%SPEECH_OFF%"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bYou'll get | You are to receive | You'll be paid | It's\x7d %reward_advance% crowns in advance, %reward_count% crowns per head you arrive with, \x7bfor up to %maxcount% heads | and I'll pay for up to %maxcount% heads | %maxcount% heads at most\x7d, and another %reward_completion% when the job is done.%SPEECH_OFF%"
    // en base_es
