    // en = "the Gelding"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bWhen %name% was just a boy, a local clergymen castrated him so that his voice could carry a higher pitch in the local choir. | When raiders invaded his village, %name% fought back only for his cock and balls to be cut from his body as punishment. | Accused of a heinous crime in the bed of an unwanting woman, %name% had the option of death or living life as a eunuch. You don't need physical evidence to know which one he chose. | Once a monk in training, it is said that %name% bedded a woman of another faith. He was kicked out of the faith and, in an attempt to regain their sympathies, the man removed the offending 'equipment.' It appears the faithful did not welcome him back. | As a child, %name%'s drunkard \x7bmother | father | elder sister | elder brother\x7d took a \x7bhot pan | jagged knife\x7d \x7bto his cock while he slept | to his cock as a form of vicious torture\x7d. | When %name% was traversing the forests not far from %townname%, he was attacked by a wild \x7bboar | bear | dog | hawk\x7d which tore great strands of flesh from his body. Surviving, he eventually realized the beast had castrated him, too. | %name% hails from the whorehouses of %randomtown% where mutilation of his body was made to satisfy a particular customer's requests.\x7d \x7bThe man was adrift when you ran across him. Now, it just seems like he wants to get away from the world, even if it means joining \x7bsellswords | mercenaries\x7d. Though his plight is not one you would wish upon anyone, he is a rather calm fellow. | You found the man being bullied by kids when you found him. Seeing your sword, he politely asked to join your band of men where one's past, or physical deformities, do not matter. He is already used to life's struggles, perhaps in a way most men can't speak to. | Surprisingly, the man stands straighter than most. He looks rather calm and collected for man who has had something so dear to him removed. | While the horrors of the man's past raise your hairs, and lower your nether regions into nearly being tucked, the eunuch seems unbothered by what has happened to him. He is a calm, almost passive figure. | The man has more stoicism in his movements than most monks you've seen. He seems at peace with his calamitous past. | No longer able to satiate his carnal desires, the man seems rather pacified and calm. Resolute, even, and seeing more in the world than what its physical appearances might initially offer.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\eunuch_southern_background.nut
    // en = "\x7bWhen desert raiders invaded his village, %name% fought back only for his cock and balls to be cut from his body as punishment. | Accused of a heinous crime in the bed of an unwanting woman, %name% had the option of death or living life as a eunuch. You don't need physical evidence to know which one he chose. | As a child, %name%'s drunkard \x7bmother | father | elder sister | elder brother\x7d took a \x7bhot pan | jagged knife\x7d \x7bto his cock while he slept | to his cock as a form of vicious torture\x7d. | When %name% was traversing the endless deserts, he was attacked by a wild hyena which tore great strands of flesh from his body. Surviving, he eventually realized the beast had castrated him, too. | %name% hails from the whorehouses of %randomcitystate% where mutilation of his body was made to satisfy a particular customer's requests.\x7d \x7bThe man was adrift when you ran across him. Now, it just seems like he wants to get away from the world, even if it means joining \x7bsellswords | mercenaries\x7d. Though his plight is not one you would wish upon anyone, he is a rather calm fellow. | You found the man being bullied by kids when you found him. Seeing your sword, he politely asked to join your band of men where one's past, or physical deformities, do not matter. He is already used to life's struggles, perhaps in a way most men can't speak to. | Surprisingly, the man stands straighter than most. He looks rather calm and collected for man who has had something so dear to him removed. | While the horrors of the man's past raise your hairs, and lower your nether regions into nearly being tucked, the eunuch seems unbothered by what has happened to him. He is a calm, almost passive figure. | The man has more stoicism in his movements than most monks you've seen. He seems at peace with his calamitous past. | No longer able to satiate his carnal desires, the man seems rather pacified and calm. Resolute, even, and seeing more in the world than what its physical appearances might initially offer.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\executioner_background.nut
    // en = "Executioners are dour and used to violence, although they have little experience in true warfare."
    // en base_es
    // context: executioner_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "%name% eventually retired from the company and once again found %themselves% plying the executioner's trade. %Their% considerable decapitation skills only honed further by sellswording, the %person% has apparently gained such notoriety in %their% field that the local nobility frequently get into feuds over who may keep %them% on retainer."
        es = "Con el tiempo, %name% se retiró de la compañía y volvió a ejercer el oficio de verdugo. Con su considerable destreza para decapitar aún más afilada tras sus años de mercenari%o%, por lo visto se ha ganado tal fama en su oficio que los nobles de la zona se enzarzan a menudo en disputas por ver quién %lo% mantiene a su servicio."
    }
    // context: executioner_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "%Their% skill with the headsman's blade sharpened further by combat, %name% left the company and resumed work as an executioner. The townsfolk found little spectacle in %their% efficiency, however, and %they% was soon replaced with a more crowd-pleasing amateur. Left destitute, it wasn't long before the %person% was found hanging from a tree outside of town."
        es = "Con su destreza con la espada del verdugo aún más afilada por el combate, %name% dejó la compañía y volvió a trabajar como verdugo. Sin embargo, a los lugareños su eficacia les ofrecía poco espectáculo, y pronto %lo% sustituyeron por un aficionado que entretenía más al público. En la miseria, no pasó mucho tiempo antes de que %lo% encontraran colgad%o% de un árbol a las afueras del pueblo."
    }
    // en = "Headtaker"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Neckrender"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Axe"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Judicator"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Headsman"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Hangman"
    // en base_es
    // context: executioner_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{As with many men, %name%'s direction in life was dictated by the family business: executing criminals for the burgomeister of %randomtown%. | As a %child%, %name% dreamed of becoming a knight clad in shining armor. As a %person%, %they% became an executioner clad in a dark hood. | %name%'s whole family was slain in a bandit raid. Unable to join the manhunt himself, %they% became an apprentice to the local executioner in the hopes of one day meting out revenge in %their% own way. | Once a brigand %themselves%, %name% had a change of heart and turned %themselves% in. The local guard offered %them% a pardon if %they% agreed to execute any criminals they captured, and %they're% been in the trade ever since. | With the distant stare of one who has seen much death, and the worn blade of one who has dealt it, it's obvious that %name% is an executioner. | An executioner, %name% is about as cheerful as the gallows %they% operates.} {Though content with %their% profession, it made %them% unpopular. After carrying out the beheading of {a local youth sentenced for stealing from a noble | a beloved whore who slept with the wrong lord | a respected craftsman accused of embezzling}, %they% was ostracized by the townsfolk. | %They% always viewed %themselves% as a necessary, if grisly, part of law for the common folk. But when %they% learned {%their% employer was making backroom deals with brigands | the local lord was ordering the deaths of the innocent | a man %they% executed was innocent | of the horrible things the local lord did with the heads of the condemned}, %they% resigned %their% post in disgust. | One day %they% was tasked with killing a strange cultist from distant lands. After %they% broke a third blade halfway through the strangely cheerful man's neck, %they% decided it was time to find a new profession. | But one day %they% woke up and found %they% could no longer stomach the idea of slaying a man who couldn't fight back. | But eventually %they% grew unhappy with %their% role, finding little satisfaction in slaying men after they'd already performed their evil works.} {With few other careers available to %them%, %name% decided mercenary work seemed the best fit for %their% talents. | While not a warrior, %name% knows how to handle a blade, and so sellswording was the obvious career change. | With a skillset predominantly based around necklines, %name% decided %they% could either become a mercenary or a tailor. The former seemed like it paid better, and now here %they% is. | In need of a new career but with few other skills, %name% decided that mercenary work was sort of like executing with more steps.} {The %person% stands silently before you, staring wide-eyed and expectant but not saying a word. Ok then. | Less confident in conversation than in killing, %they% mumbles out a nervous greeting to you and asks about pay. | Not much for words, %they% grunts expectantly at you. As long as %they% can kill, you suppose you don't mind the quiet. | %They% approaches and barks something at you that %their% heavy hood muffles beyond comprehension. After a few moments of silence %they% follows up with '...please?' and you realize %they're% asking to join the company. Oh.}"
        es = "{Como a tantos otros, a %name% el rumbo de la vida se lo marcó el negocio familiar: ejecutar criminales para el burgomaestre de %randomtown%. | De niñ%o%, %name% soñaba con ser caballero de reluciente armadura. De mayor, acabó siendo verdugo de oscura capucha. | Toda la familia de %name% murió en un ataque de bandidos. Sin poder unirse a la cacería de los culpables, entró como aprendiz del verdugo local con la esperanza de vengarse algún día a su manera. | Antes bandid%o%, %name% cambió de parecer y se entregó. La guardia local le ofreció el perdón si aceptaba ejecutar a cualquier criminal que capturaran, y desde entonces se dedica al oficio. | Con la mirada perdida de quien ha visto mucha muerte, y la hoja gastada de quien la ha repartido, es evidente que %name% es verdugo. | Verdugo de oficio, %name% es tan alegre como el patíbulo que maneja.} {Aunque estaba content%o% con su oficio, este le granjeaba antipatías. Tras decapitar {a un joven del lugar condenado por robar a un noble | a una puta muy querida que se acostó con el señor equivocado | a un respetado artesano acusado de malversación}, los lugareños le dieron la espalda. | Siempre se había visto como una parte necesaria, aunque macabra, de la ley para la gente común. Pero cuando descubrió {que su patrón hacía tratos a escondidas con bandidos | que el señor local ordenaba la muerte de inocentes | que un hombre al que había ejecutado era inocente | las cosas horribles que el señor local hacía con las cabezas de los condenados}, renunció a su puesto, asquead%o%. | Un día le encargaron matar a un extraño cultista de tierras lejanas. Después de romper una tercera hoja a medio cuello de aquel hombre extrañamente alegre, decidió que era hora de buscarse otro oficio. | Pero un día se despertó y descubrió que ya no soportaba la idea de matar a un hombre que no podía defenderse. | Pero con el tiempo empezó a disgustarle su papel, pues encontraba poca satisfacción en matar a hombres que ya habían cometido sus maldades.} {Con pocas salidas a su alcance, %name% decidió que el trabajo de mercenario era lo que mejor encajaba con sus talentos. | Aunque no es guerrer%o%, %name% sabe manejar una hoja, así que hacerse mercenari%o% era el cambio de oficio más obvio. | Con unas destrezas centradas sobre todo en los cuellos, %name% decidió que podía hacerse mercenari%o% o sastre. Lo primero parecía estar mejor pagado, y aquí %lo% tienes. | Necesitaba un oficio nuevo y no sabía hacer gran cosa más, así que %name% decidió que el trabajo de mercenario era algo así como ejecutar, pero con más pasos.} {Se queda de pie en silencio ante ti, con los ojos muy abiertos y expectantes, sin decir palabra. Muy bien, entonces. | Menos segur%o% conversando que matando, masculla un saludo nervioso y te pregunta por la paga. | Poco dad%o% a las palabras, te gruñe con expectación. Mientras sepa matar, supones que no te importa el silencio. | Se acerca y te ladra algo que su pesada capucha ahoga hasta hacerlo incomprensible. Tras unos instantes de silencio, añade un '...¿por favor?' y te das cuenta de que te está pidiendo unirse a la compañía. Ah.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\executioner_southern_background.nut
    // context: executioner_southern_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{Once an executioner in the many nomad tribes of the South, %name% was banished {for a beheading gone horribly wrong | when it was discovered %they%'d slain the wrong man | after %they% faked the death of a friend}. Aimless, %they% drifted into %randomcitystate% and resumed %their% trade in service of the viziers. | An executioner, %name% was tasked with beheading, hanging, quartering, and all the other punishments conveyed upon those criminals deemed unworthy of repaying their debts to the Gilder in life, and those who had been given the chance and failed. | %name% worked for %randomvizier% as an executioner, meting out grisly justice to the criminals of the South. | From %their% distinctive hood, it's clear %name% is an executioner. From %their% grim affect, it's clear %they're% been in the trade for some time.} {In the city states, however, even criminals are more valuable alive than dead, and soon %they% found %themselves% running out of work and out of crowns. | One day %they% was charged with severing the neck of another headsman who had 'ruined' an execution by allowing the condemned to predict the killing blow and scream. %name% carried out %their% own task in silence, then decided it was time to find a new line of work. | For many years %they% was content with %their% work, but one day %they% was tasked with {hanging a young boy who had stolen food from the market | beheading a beautiful concubine who had displeased her master | drowning an old man too feeble even to stand}. %They% performed %their% duty, but found %they% no longer had a taste for the profession after that. | Though happy enough in %their% role, %they% learned that all of %their% predecessors had eventually been indebted or executed themselves after displeasing %their% employer. Seeing the writing on the wall, %they% began looking for a new line of work.} {Unsure what else to do, %name% decided mercenary work was a good fit for %their% skillset. | Figuring %they%'d be no less respected as a Crownling, but better paid, %name% now pursues a sellsword's career. | Accustomed to blood and blades alike, mercenary work is an obvious next step for %name%. | %name% tried %their% hand at a few occupations before deciding that %their% particular talents were best suited for the bloody, and well-paid, work of a sellsword.}"
        es = "{Antes verdugo en las numerosas tribus nómadas del Sur, %name% fue desterrad%o% {por una decapitación que salió terriblemente mal | cuando se descubrió que había matado al hombre equivocado | después de fingir la muerte de un amigo}. Sin rumbo, acabó en %randomcitystate% y retomó su oficio al servicio de los visires. | Como verdugo, a %name% le encargaban decapitar, ahorcar, descuartizar y aplicar todos los demás castigos reservados a los criminales considerados indignos de saldar en vida sus deudas con el Dorado, y a quienes tuvieron la oportunidad y fracasaron. | %name% trabajó como verdugo para %randomvizier%, impartiendo una justicia macabra a los criminales del Sur. | Por su característica capucha, está claro que %name% es verdugo. Por su semblante sombrío, está claro que lleva un tiempo en el oficio.} {Sin embargo, en las ciudades-estado hasta los criminales valen más vivos que muertos, y pronto se quedó sin trabajo y sin coronas. | Un día le encargaron cortarle el cuello a otro verdugo que había 'arruinado' una ejecución al dejar que el condenado adivinara el golpe mortal y gritara. %name% cumplió su propia tarea en silencio y luego decidió que era hora de buscarse otro oficio. | Durante muchos años estuvo content%o% con su trabajo, pero un día le encargaron {ahorcar a un muchacho que había robado comida en el mercado | decapitar a una hermosa concubina que había disgustado a su amo | ahogar a un anciano demasiado débil incluso para tenerse en pie}. Cumplió con su deber, pero después de aquello descubrió que el oficio ya no le agradaba. | Aunque estaba bastante a gusto en su puesto, se enteró de que todos sus predecesores habían acabado endeudados o ejecutados tras disgustar a quien los empleaba. Viendo lo que se avecinaba, empezó a buscarse otro oficio.} {Sin saber qué otra cosa hacer, %name% decidió que el trabajo de mercenario encajaba bien con sus destrezas. | Pensando que como cuentacoronas no %lo% respetarían menos, pero cobraría más, %name% busca ahora hacer carrera como mercenari%o%. | Habituad%o% tanto a la sangre como al acero, %name% ve en el trabajo de mercenario el siguiente paso obvio. | %name% probó suerte en unos cuantos oficios antes de decidir que sus talentos particulares eran ideales para el trabajo sangriento, y bien pagado, de mercenario.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\farmhand_background.nut
    // en = "Farmhands are used to hard physical labor."
    // en base_es
    // en = "The former farmhand, %name%, retired from the %companyname%. The money he made was put toward purchasing a bit of land. He spends the rest of his days happily farming and starting a family with way too many children."
    // en base_es
    // en = "The former farmhand, %name%, soon left the %companyname%. He purchased a bit of land out \x7bsouth | north | east | west\x7d and was doing quite well for himself - until noble soldiers hanged him from a tree for refusing to hand over all his crops."
    // en base_es
    // context: farmhand_background.o.setGender.m.Name
    {
        en = "Milkmaid"
        es = "Lechera"
    }
    // context: farmhand_background.o.setGender.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "Milkmaids are used to physical labor."
        es = "Las lecheras están acostumbradas al trabajo físico."
    }
    // context: farmhand_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: la 1.0 añade al final "Extrañarás ese acento campechano suyo. No sus chistes sobre vacas, no.", que el en no tiene.
        en = "The former farmhand, %name%, retired from the %companyname%. The money she made was put toward purchasing a bit of land. she spends the rest of her days happily farming and starting a family with way too many children."
        es = "La antigua peona de granja, %name%, se retiró de %companyname%. El dinero que ganó lo destinó a comprar un pedazo de tierra. Pasa el resto de sus días cultivando feliz y formando una familia con demasiados hijos."
    }
    // context: farmhand_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "The former farmhand, %name%, soon left the %companyname%. She purchased a bit of land out {south | north | east | west} and was doing quite well for herself - until noble soldiers hanged her from a tree for refusing to hand over all her crops."
        es = "La antigua peona de granja, %name%, pronto dejó %companyname%. Compró un pedazo de tierra al {sur | norte | este | oeste} y le iba bastante bien, hasta que unos soldados de un noble la colgaron de un árbol por negarse a entregar todas sus cosechas."
    }
    // context: farmhand_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{Tilling the soil is hard work, requiring the blood and sweat of sturdier women. | Every farm in the land needs a stable of hardy folk to work the fields.  | A woman puts her sweat into the earth to feed herself, and she feeds herself to put her sweat into the Earth another day. | No matter the weather, a farm needs working. | Pigsties, stables, and ungated pens, these are the dreams and nightmares of farming women. | While some women earn their keep by killing, others look below their own two feet, wondering what crops the soil may hold. | A special breed of women comes out of ranchers and farmers. Sturdy, resolute, hard-working. | With food so needed, there's little wonder why farmers are the most common sort of woman in all the land. | A farm wife hates to see her land fertilized in blood, but that's becoming more and more common these days. | In war, farms are hotspots for armies. Not just to feed themselves, but to recruit from the stable of strong women who work those lands. | As cities grow and distance themselves from the hinterland, citizens often forget to whom their full bellies owe gratitude.} %name% {is a burly, sweat-sculpted farmhand. | hails from the outskirts of %randomtown% where she drove ploughs and broke horses. | knows a couple kinds of hoes, all of which the farmhand can swing with ease. | grew up on one of the land's many farms. | spent many years harvesting the crops that feed everyone in the land. | worked as a farmhand for a simple homestead. | fell into farming after her father's boating business went under. | became a farmhand to help feed her dozen kids and layabout husband. | took up farming as a means to a belly-filled end. | carries the stocky frame best used for planting, harvesting, and surviving winters.} {Unfortunately, it didn't take war and turmoil long to find her farm. | But poor harvests have driven her from the farms. | Sadly, her farm was one of the first to be attacked during these trying times. | Word of coming violence, however, drove her from the peaceful vocation of farming. | Droughts, poorly-timed as ever, have now driven the woman from her work. | Unpaid for her labor, she eventually abandoned the farm life. | With more crowns than ever in the killing businesses, the woman was easily drawn away from her motley crops. | One day, she realized her strong body had more value chopping heads than milking cows. | After raiders pillaged her crops, she'd had enough, leaving the farm life for good. | After the weather soured her harvest, the farmer decided to choose a vocation not wholly based on the whims of Mother Nature. | Word has it she really did sleep with the farmer's son. What a surprise she's no longer on the farm.} {Cornfed and barnbred, %name% stands before you as fit a woman you've ever seen. | She misses the cows, true, but %name% should take to the mercenary's tough life with ease. | Growing up on a farm gives a woman all the nutrients she'd ever need, and %name% certainly took advantage. | %name% once took a mule kick to the face. Its foot broken, they had to put the animal down. | If women were trees, %name% would never fall down. Or something gracious like that. | Don't let her simple past fool you, %name% could fit right in with any wrestler or fighter. | %name% shares a lot in common with draught animals. Just point her the right way. | Judging by her size, there must have been a lot of meat in that corn %name% spent all her life eating. | %name% is big enough to wring a guy's neck like it was a cow's udder.}"
        es = "{Labrar la tierra es un trabajo duro que exige la sangre y el sudor de mujeres recias. | Toda granja del reino necesita una cuadrilla de gente curtida para trabajar los campos. | Una mujer riega la tierra con su sudor para alimentarse, y se alimenta para regarla con su sudor un día más. | Haga el tiempo que haga, la granja hay que trabajarla. | Pocilgas, establos y corrales sin cerca: esos son los sueños y las pesadillas de las campesinas. | Mientras algunas mujeres se ganan el sustento matando, otras miran bajo sus pies preguntándose qué cosechas guardará la tierra. | De entre ganaderos y granjeros sale una raza especial de mujeres. Recias, resueltas, trabajadoras. | Con lo necesaria que es la comida, no es de extrañar que las campesinas sean el tipo de mujer más común en todo el reino. | A una granjera no le gusta ver su tierra abonada con sangre, pero hoy en día es cada vez más habitual. | En la guerra, las granjas son lugares codiciados por los ejércitos. No solo para alimentarse, sino para reclutar entre las mujeres fuertes que trabajan esas tierras. | A medida que las ciudades crecen y se alejan del campo, sus habitantes suelen olvidar a quién deben agradecer tener la barriga llena.} %name% {es una peona fornida, esculpida a base de sudor. | viene de las afueras de %randomtown%, donde guiaba arados y domaba caballos. | conoce un par de tipos de azada, y las maneja todas con soltura. | se crio en una de las muchas granjas del reino. | pasó muchos años recogiendo las cosechas que alimentan a todo el reino. | trabajó como peona en una humilde granja. | acabó en el campo después de que quebrara el negocio de barcas de su padre. | se hizo peona para ayudar a alimentar a su docena de hijos y a su holgazán marido. | se dedicó al campo como medio para llenar la barriga. | tiene la complexión robusta que mejor sirve para sembrar, cosechar y sobrevivir a los inviernos.} {Por desgracia, la guerra y el caos no tardaron en llegar a su granja. | Pero las malas cosechas la han echado del campo. | Lamentablemente, su granja fue de las primeras en ser atacadas en estos tiempos difíciles. | Sin embargo, los rumores de la violencia que se avecinaba la apartaron del pacífico oficio de la labranza. | Las sequías, tan inoportunas como siempre, han apartado ahora a la mujer de su trabajo. | Como no le pagaban por su trabajo, acabó por abandonar la vida en la granja. | Con más coronas que nunca en el negocio de matar, a la mujer no le costó dejar atrás sus variopintos cultivos. | Un día se dio cuenta de que su fuerte cuerpo valía más cortando cabezas que ordeñando vacas. | Después de que unos saqueadores arrasaran sus cultivos, se hartó y dejó la vida de granja para siempre. | Después de que el tiempo le estropeara la cosecha, la granjera decidió elegir un oficio que no dependiera por completo de los caprichos de la Madre Naturaleza. | Dicen que de verdad se acostó con el hijo del granjero. Qué sorpresa que ya no esté en la granja.} {Criada a base de maíz y en un granero, %name% es la mujer más en forma que has visto nunca. | Echa de menos a las vacas, es cierto, pero %name% debería adaptarse sin problemas a la dura vida de mercenaria. | Criarse en una granja le da a una mujer todos los nutrientes que pueda necesitar, y %name% sin duda los aprovechó. | Una vez, a %name% le dieron una coz de mula en la cara. Con la pata rota, tuvieron que sacrificar al animal. | Si las mujeres fueran árboles, %name% nunca caería. O algo así de elegante. | Que no te engañe su pasado sencillo: %name% no desentonaría al lado de cualquier luchador o púgil. | %name% tiene mucho en común con los animales de tiro. Basta con apuntarla en la dirección correcta. | A juzgar por su tamaño, ese maíz que %name% se pasó la vida comiendo debía de llevar mucha carne. | %name% es lo bastante grande para retorcerle el cuello a un tipo como si fuera la ubre de una vaca.}"
    }
    // en = "\x7bTilling the soil is hard work, requiring the blood and sweat of sturdier men. | Every farm in the land needs a stable of hardy men to work the fields.  | Man puts his sweat into the earth to feed himself, and he feeds himself to put his sweat into the Earth another day. | No matter the weather, a farm needs working. | Pigsties, stables, and ungated pens, these are the dreams and nightmares of farming men. | While some men earn their keep by killing, others look below their own two feet, wondering what crops the soil may hold. | A special breed of men comes out of ranchers and farmers. Sturdy, resolute, hard-working. | With food so needed, there's little wonder why farmers are the most common sort of man in all the land. | A farmer hates to see his land fertilized in blood, but that's becoming more and more common these days. | In war, farms are hotspots for armies. Not just to feed themselves, but to recruit from the stable of strong men who work those lands. | As cities grow and distance themselves from the hinterland, citizens often forget to whom their full bellies owe gratitude.\x7d %name% \x7bis a burly, sweat-sculpted farmhand. | hails from the outskirts of %randomtown% where he drove ploughs and broke horses. | knows a couple kinds of hoes, all of which the farmhand can swing with ease. | grew up on one of the land's many farms. | spent many years harvesting the crops that feed everyone in the land. | worked as a farmhand for a simple homestead. | fell into farming after his boating business went under. | became a farmhand to help feed his dozen kids and two wives. | took up farming as a means to a belly-filled end. | carries the stocky frame best used for planting, harvesting, and surviving winters.\x7d \x7bUnfortunately, it didn't take war and turmoil long to find his farm. | But poor harvests have driven him from the farms. | Sadly, his farm was one of the first to be attacked during these trying times. | Word of coming violence, however, drove him from the peaceful vocation of farming. | Droughts, poorly-timed as ever, have now driven the man from his work. | Unpaid for his labor, he eventually abandoned the farm life. | With more crowns than ever in the killing businesses, the man was easily drawn away from his motley crops. | One day, he realized his strong body had more value chopping heads than milking cows. | After raiders pillaged his crops, he'd had enough, leaving the farm life for good. | After the weather soured his harvest, the farmer decided to choose a vocation not wholly based on the whims of Mother Nature. | Word has it he really did sleep with the farmer's daughter. What a surprise he's no longer on the farm.\x7d \x7bCornfed and barnbred, %name% stands before you as fit a man you've ever seen. | He misses the cows, true, but %name% should take to the mercenary's tough life with ease. | Growing up on a farm gives a man all the nutrients he'd ever need, and %name% certainly took advantage. | %name% once took a mule kick to the face. Its foot broken, they had to put the animal down. | If men were trees, %name% would never fall down. Or something gracious like that. | Don't let his simple past fool you, %name% could fit right in with any wrestler or fighter. | %name% shares a lot in common with draught animals. Just point him the right way. | Judging by his size, there must have been a lot of meat in that corn %name% spent all his life eating. | %name% is big enough to wring a guy's neck like it was a cow's udder.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\fisherman_background.nut
    // en = "Fishermen are used to physical labor."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% retired from fighting and returned to his fishing ventures. A huge storm ran up the shores, destroying every skiff and drifter - except that wily fisherman's! The only boat afloat, %name%'s business boomed. He lives a comfortable life waking up to a nice beachfront view every morning."
    // en base_es
    // en = "With the fighting career going so poorly, %name% decided to retire from the field and return to fishing. He went missing at sea after an enormous storm wrecked the shorelines."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Fisherman"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Fisher"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7b%name% loved the sea and the serenity of fishing alone on the water | Ironically, %name% always hated the water, but became a fisherman after his father and his father's father | %name% was a strong and able fisherman | %name% was content with being a fisherman | %name% always had a lucky hand in finding the best fishing grounds and catching the fattest fish\x7d. As long as there was no storm, he was out there, fishing, day in and out. \x7bSadly, his fishing cabin burned to the ground while he was out at sea. | But disaster struck as he lost his best friend at sea when a storm suddenly came up, leaving him with a badly damaged boat and no one to sail out with. | But disaster struck when his wife died during childbirth, shattering all what he held dear. | After being unable pay his debts for some time, however, his boat was taken from him by a merciless loan shark. | It was after he strangled his wife in a fit of rage that he lost all interest in the fishing trade. | Much to his dismay, for almost a whole summer most of the fish he caught was already dead and rotten inside. | It was after a priest of the gods told %name% that the life of a fisherman was not what they desired of him, but that they wished for him to spill blood in their name, that he would set his eyes on another trade.\x7d Visiting the tavern one evening, a new opportunity presented itself with the promise of coin for dangerous work."
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\flagellant_background.nut
    // en = "Flagellant"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Flagellants have a high resolve in what they do, and a high tolerance for pain, but their work has often left their bodies scarred for life."
    // en base_es
    // en = "One of the more disturbing members of the group, %name% the flagellant at least put aside the whip long enough to bring blades to your enemies. Although he was a capable if not unsettlingly diligent mercenary, it became increasingly obvious that his habits would be the end of him. After another night of harsh personal repudiation, the company found the man unconscious and nearly bleeding out yet again. Hoping to save %name% from himself, they dropped the flagellant off at a monastery where he eventually woke to painful confusion. A kind monk nursed him to health and taught him the ways of peaceful religiosity. To this day, %name% walks the cloisters, giving tempered talks to the young and sparing them from notions of savage spirituality."
    // en base_es
    // en = "With the company rapidly declining, many mercenaries turned to desperate measures. %name% the flagellant was one such measure. Due to chaos and confusion, some men came to believe %name% could lead them to honor and salvation. A handful of survivors broke off from the %companyname% and went mad, joining his cult of savage spirituality. A howling %name% at their helm, the converts wander aimlessly, sulking half-bent across the earth, rinds of raw hides for backs."
    // en base_es
    // context: flagellant_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{The gods pity men, spurring many, not unlike %name%, to seek their favor. | Illiterate and born to poverty, %name% found refuge in tales of the gods. | Always one to devour books, it wasn't long until %name% discovered texts of the gods. | Some say the gods speak to us and, if true, they definitely spoke to %name%. | With new cults springing up in the wilds, %name% returned to the familiarity of the gods. | Raised by %their% firebrand father, %name% spent much of %their% early years nursing wounds from good floggings. The gods would approve.} {When war came to the land, the gods told %them% to take part for greater justice. | As cultists spread their vile word like disease on a rat, %name% saw fit to take up arms and battle the heresy. | Straying from %their% faith, %they% committed a horrific crime in %randomtown%. While flagellating %themselves% nightly, %they% seeks redemption. | Hearing but a mere rumor of a holy place, the pilgrim took up staff and supplies to seek it out. | Now that war has returned to the land, the gods devotee wished to find out why, through prayer and corporeal means. | A night spent in a cave revealed to the believer that the gods demanded blood. %name% was not one to refuse their beckoning. | After raiders looted the coffers of their church, %name%'s quest was to refill the pure purses.} {As the laws of the universe bend to a world-consuming war, a thaumaturge like %name% might be useful to have around. | %They% carries a whip with glass-barbed leather. This is not for your enemies, %they% states, but for purity. Interesting. | %They% professes to hate evil, but for a few crowns %name% can be persuaded to make anything 'evil'. | This chosen one seeks the difficult road, no doubt why %they% saw fit to join a mercenary band. | If %name% had the power, you believe %they%'d purge the entire world. | Talks of the gods might be a tad irksome, but %name%'s fiery passion lends itself well to the battlefield. | So enamored with the world of the gods, it's not much of a surprise that the pilgrim sees the real one filled with enemies.}"
        es = "{Los dioses se apiadan de los hombres y empujan a muchos, no muy distintos de %name%, a buscar su favor. | Analfabet%o% y nacid%o% en la pobreza, %name% halló refugio en los relatos de los dioses. | Siempre devorando libros, %name% no tardó en descubrir los textos de los dioses. | Algunos dicen que los dioses nos hablan y, si es cierto, desde luego le hablaron a %name%. | Con nuevos cultos brotando en las tierras salvajes, %name% regresó a la familiaridad de los dioses. | Criad%o% por un padre fanático, %name% pasó buena parte de sus primeros años curándose las heridas de buenas azotainas. Los dioses lo aprobarían.} {Cuando la guerra llegó a estas tierras, los dioses le ordenaron tomar parte en ella en nombre de una justicia mayor. | Mientras los cultistas propagaban su vil palabra como la enfermedad en una rata, %name% creyó oportuno tomar las armas y combatir la herejía. | Tras apartarse de su fe, cometió un crimen horrible en %randomtown%. Ahora se flagela cada noche en busca de redención. | Con solo oír un rumor sobre un lugar sagrado, %art% peregrin%o% tomó bastón y provisiones para ir en su busca. | Ahora que la guerra ha vuelto a estas tierras, %art% devot%o% de los dioses quiso averiguar por qué, mediante la oración y los medios corporales. | Una noche pasada en una cueva le reveló %al% creyente que los dioses exigían sangre. %name% no era de los que desoyen su llamada. | Después de que unos saqueadores vaciaran las arcas de su iglesia, la misión de %name% pasó a ser volver a llenar las puras bolsas.} {Mientras las leyes del universo se doblegan ante una guerra que devora el mundo, puede ser útil tener cerca a %un% taumaturg%o% como %name%. | Lleva un látigo de cuero con púas de vidrio. No es para tus enemigos, afirma, sino para la pureza. Interesante. | Dice odiar el mal, pero por unas pocas coronas se puede convencer a %name% de tachar de 'malvada' cualquier cosa. | %Ese% elegid%o% busca el camino difícil; sin duda por eso creyó oportuno unirse a una banda de mercenarios. | Crees que, si tuviera el poder, %name% purgaría el mundo entero. | Sus charlas sobre los dioses pueden resultar algo irritantes, pero la pasión ardiente de %name% se presta bien al campo de batalla. | Tan prendad%o% del mundo de los dioses, no sorprende mucho que %art% peregrin%o% vea el mundo real lleno de enemigos.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\gambler_background.nut
    // en = "Gambler"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Gamblers tend to have quick reflexes and a higher resolve than their opponents at the card table."
    // en base_es
    // context: gambler_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: la 1.0 añade entre llaves una variante que el inglés no tiene (el juego de cartas 'Went', guiño a Gwent), con lo que descuadra llaves, barras y %name% frente al en; aquí se omite porque la fusión exige las mismas llaves que el en. Decidir en la 1.0 si se conserva como guiño
        en = "It was perhaps a risk to take a gambler like %name% into your ranks. Now, many days later it's obvious you made the right choice. Last you heard, %they% was still with the company and uses %their% earnings to enrich %their% habits. Rumor has it that, through all %their% winnings, %they%'s secretly become one of the richest men in all the land. You think it's a bunch of hogwash, but a surprising number of mayors have become suddenly lax on gaming..."
        es = "Quizás fue un riesgo incorporar a tus filas a alguien que vive del juego, como %name%. Ahora, muchos días después, es obvio que tomaste la decisión correcta. Lo último que supiste es que seguía en la compañía y que usa sus ganancias para alimentar sus hábitos. Se rumorea que, con todas sus ganancias, se ha convertido en secreto en una de las personas más ricas de todo el país. Crees que no son más que patrañas, pero un número sorprendente de alcaldes se ha vuelto de repente muy permisivo con el juego..."
    }
    // context: gambler_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "%name% the gambler retired from the declining company and returned to %their% gambling ways. %They% quickly acquired great debts %they% could not pay. You saw %them% begging on a street corner with one of %their% hands missing and gaps in %their% teeth. You dropped a few crowns into %their% tin and said a few words, but %they% did not recognize you."
        es = "%name% se retiró de la compañía en decadencia y volvió a su vida de apuestas. Enseguida contrajo grandes deudas que no podía pagar. %Lo% viste mendigando en una esquina, con una mano de menos y huecos en los dientes. Dejaste caer unas cuantas coronas en su lata y le dijiste unas palabras, pero no te reconoció."
    }
    // en = "Deuces"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Wild Card"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Luck Maker"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Lucky"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Cardsharper"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Gambler"
    // en base_es
    // context: gambler_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{They say luck is the devil, so just how long can a gambler like %name% play with it? | Everyone gambles, so %name% figured why not do it for money? | Dice, cards, marbles - there are a lot of ways to take a man's money, and %name% knows all of them. | %name%'s got the eyes of a desert snake - and shaping cards is %their% rattle. | In a world of life or death, taking risks is %name%'s game. | A %person% like %name% sees everything coming, especially the next card in the deck.} {%They% supported %themselves% by playing cards from town to town, only leaving after %they%'d cleaned out their pockets. | But it is a mystery as to how a %person% decides to take up cards as a lifestyle. | The constant coming and going of mercenaries made for easy targets - until one sore loser ran %them% off with a bastard sword. | Orphaned by %their% own birth, %they%'s always scrounged up a living by gambling with others. | When %they% was a kid, a trickster's cup-game showed %them% the value in hustling. | When %their% father fell into gambling debts, %they% figured the best way to pay them back was to become an even better hustler %themselves%. | After taking all their crowns, towns across the land banned %name% from hustling in a fit of so-called 'religious revival.'} {Now, the gambler seeks to throw %their% dice into the wind - as well as the mud, taking rank with any outfit that pays. | One has to wonder what a cardplayer is doing not playing cards. Then again, maybe it's good that %they% sees your group as a smart gamble. | Perhaps years of scamming mercenaries has given %them% the notion that %they% could just as easily be one. | Clever and quick-thinking, the cardshaper survives by moving before anyone else does, a skill as useful as any other in this world. | Ironically, a bad play put %them% into enormous debt with a baron. Now %they% has to find another way to pay it back. | Wars have sapped most of the fish from %their% cards games. Instead of waiting around %they% figured %they%'d just go ahead and follow them.}"
        es = "{Dicen que la suerte es el diablo, así que ¿cuánto tiempo podrá seguir jugando con ella alguien que vive de apostar, como %name%? | Todo el mundo apuesta, así que %name% pensó: ¿por qué no hacerlo por dinero? | Dados, cartas, canicas... hay muchas formas de quitarle el dinero a un hombre, y %name% las conoce todas. | %name% tiene los ojos de una serpiente del desierto, y trucar cartas es su cascabel. | En un mundo de vida o muerte, arriesgarse es el juego de %name%. | %Un% %hombre% como %name% lo ve venir todo, sobre todo la siguiente carta del mazo.} {Se ganaba la vida jugando a las cartas de pueblo en pueblo, y solo se marchaba después de vaciarles los bolsillos a todos. | Pero sigue siendo un misterio cómo %un% %hombre% decide hacer de las cartas su forma de vida. | El constante ir y venir de mercenarios le ofrecía presas fáciles, hasta que un mal perdedor %lo% echó a punta de espada bastarda. | Huérfan%o% desde el día en que nació, siempre se ha buscado la vida apostando con otros. | De niñ%o%, el juego de los cubiletes de un embaucador le enseñó lo que vale un buen engaño. | Cuando su padre cayó en deudas de juego, pensó que la mejor forma de saldarlas era volverse aún más hábil en el engaño. | Después de que les quitara todas sus coronas, pueblos de todo el país le prohibieron a %name% sus trampas, en un arrebato de supuesto 'renacer religioso'.} {Ahora quiere lanzar sus dados al viento, y también al barro, alistándose en cualquier grupo que pague. | Uno se pregunta qué hace alguien que vive de las cartas sin jugar a las cartas. Aunque quizá sea bueno que vea a tu grupo como una apuesta sensata. | Quizá años estafando a mercenarios le hayan hecho pensar que podría serlo con la misma facilidad. | List%o% y rápid%o% de mente, sobrevive moviéndose antes que nadie, una habilidad tan útil como cualquier otra en este mundo. | Irónicamente, una mala jugada %lo% dejó con una deuda enorme con un barón. Ahora tiene que encontrar otra forma de saldarla. | Las guerras han dejado sus partidas de cartas casi sin incautos. En vez de quedarse esperando, decidió ir tras ellos.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\gladiator_background.nut
    // en = "Gladiator"
    // en base_es
    // context: gladiator_background.o.create.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "Gladiators are expensive, but a life in the arena has forged them into skilled fighters. Always a show off, gladiators fight better if there are no allies nearby."
        es = "Los gladiadores son caros, pero una vida en la arena los ha forjado como luchadores hábiles. Siempre fanfarrones, los gladiadores luchan mejor si no hay aliados cerca."
    }
    // context: gladiator_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "You thought that %name% the gladiator would return to the arenas as you thought %they% might. However, news from the south speaks of an uprising of indebted and gladiators alike. Unlike previous revolts, this one has viziers swinging from rooftops and slavers being lynched in the streets. The general upheaval is apparently about to sit the once-ringfighter as a legitimate powerbroker in the region."
        es = "Creías que %name% volvería a las arenas de gladiadores, como sospechabas que haría. Sin embargo, las noticias del sur hablan de un levantamiento de endeudados y gladiadores por igual. A diferencia de revueltas anteriores, en esta hay visires colgando de los tejados y esclavistas linchados en las calles. Por lo visto, la agitación general está a punto de encumbrar a quien antes luchaba en la arena como un poder legítimo en la región."
    }
    // context: gladiator_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        // corrige base: errata "a los arenas" por "a las arenas"; "mortally slain" es que murió, no "fue mortalmente herido"; "pitchfork" es una horca, no un rastrillo
        en = "The call of the crowd was too loud for the gladiator %name%. After your quick retirement from the unsuccessful %companyname%, the fighter returned to the southern kingdoms' fighting arenas. Unfortunately, the wear and tear of %their% time with mercenaries slowed %them% a step and %they% was mortally slain by a half-starved slave wielding a pitchfork and a net."
        es = "El llamado de la multitud fue demasiado fuerte para %name%, que venía de las arenas de gladiadores. Después de tu rápido retiro de la fracasada %companyname%, volvió a las arenas de combate de los reinos del sur. Por desgracia, el desgaste de su tiempo con los mercenarios %lo% había vuelto un paso más lent%o%, y murió a manos de un esclavo medio muerto de hambre que empuñaba una horca y una red."
    }
    // context: gladiator_background.o.getTooltip.ret.push().text
    {
        en = "[color=%positive%]10%[/color] damage increase"
        es = "[color=%positive%]10%[/color] de aumento del daño"
    }
    // context: gladiator_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{The South is littered with slaves of all sorts, called the indebted for their debt to the Gilder. While most find themselves in the fields, a select few are taken to the fighting pits to battle it out. | While northerners do partake in combat tournaments, nothing gets close to the violence and gore of a southern gladiatorial pit. | In the South, rich and poor alike enjoy cheering on the gladiators of the fighting pits. | Southern gladiatorial pits are filled with indebted and voluntary killers alike. | A bloody house of combat and betting, a gladiatorial pit is the one place in the South one may find rich and poor crowded together.} {It was from these ranks %name% came. %They% rapidly grew through the ranks and managed to buy %their% way out of the pits and into whatever 'freedom' one could find after such a life. | A crowd-favorite, %name%'s time as a gladiator ended after a 'pardon' by %their% wealthy sponsors. But in early retirement %they% found %their% life unfulfilled. | Successful killers such as %name% can buy their way to freedom, though the bloodlust has yet to leave the %person%. | %name% was involved in a 'diving' incident and received a year long ban from the pits. | But gladiators like %name% are not just popular with the public, but particularly with lusty folk. A raunchy tryst with a noble led to the fighter being spirited away under the cover of night lest %they% be mutilated. | A pit's most popular fighter is usually a blend of murderous handsomeness, and a %person% such as %name% was only the former. Dispirited by the lack of fame %they% thought %they% had earned, %they% purchased %their% freedom and departed the blood sport.} {Gladiators usually cross from fighting pit to fighting pit, so a sturdy, well skilled fighter such as %name% is rare to find in the wild. Yet here %they% stands, albeit with enough scars to make a flagellant blush. | You've met many a warrior, but rarely one with the particular skillsets of a pit fighter such as %name%. All the clashing in the arenas has made %them% a clever warrior indeed, and also one with many a scar and injury to match %their% time there. | There's many pairings in this world, and a gladiator with an untouched body is not one of them. %name% is a skilled fighter, but %they% earned those experiences with %their% own blood and body. | An impressive gladiatorial resume such as the one %name% brings hints at a %person% well versed in killing. The many scars, however, flatly state that %their% time in the pits came with an irreversible price of their own. | Gladiators such as %name% could be the most skilled fighters in all the land, but the fighting pits are full of games and are designed to bring harm to all who partake. The %person% is a talented warrior, but %they% wears the scars and wounds of a career in the arena.}"
        es = "{El Sur está plagado de esclavos de toda clase, llamados endeudados por su deuda con el Dorado. Mientras la mayoría acaba en los campos, unos pocos elegidos son llevados a los fosos de combate para pelear a muerte. | Aunque los norteños participan en torneos de combate, nada se acerca a la violencia y la sangre de un foso de gladiadores del sur. | En el Sur, ricos y pobres por igual disfrutan animando a los gladiadores de los fosos de combate. | Los fosos de gladiadores del sur están llenos tanto de endeudados como de asesinos que están allí por voluntad propia. | Casa sangrienta de combates y apuestas, el foso de gladiadores es el único lugar del Sur donde ricos y pobres se apiñan juntos.} {De esas filas salió %name%. Ascendió con rapidez y logró comprar su salida de los fosos hacia la 'libertad' que uno pueda encontrar después de una vida así. | %name% era favorit%o% del público, y su etapa en la arena terminó con un 'indulto' de sus ricos patrocinadores. Pero, en su temprano retiro, sintió que su vida no %lo% llenaba. | Los asesinos de éxito como %name% pueden comprar su libertad, aunque la sed de sangre aún no ha abandonado a %ese% %hombre%. | %name% se vio envuelt%o% en un asunto de combates 'amañados' y le prohibieron pisar los fosos durante un año. | Pero los gladiadores como %name% no solo son populares entre el público, sino sobre todo entre la gente lujuriosa. Un encuentro subido de tono con un noble hizo que %lo% sacaran a escondidas al amparo de la noche para que no %lo% mutilaran. | El luchador más popular de un foso suele ser una mezcla de instinto asesino y buena planta, y %un% %hombre% como %name% solo tenía lo primero. Desanimad%o% por la falta de la fama que creía haberse ganado, compró su libertad y abandonó el deporte sangriento.} {Los gladiadores suelen ir de foso en foso, así que es raro encontrar por ahí a alguien tan robust%o% y hábil en la lucha como %name%. Y sin embargo aquí está, aunque con suficientes cicatrices para hacer sonrojar a un flagelante. | Has conocido a muchos guerreros, pero rara vez a uno con las aptitudes particulares de quien ha luchado en los fosos, como %name%. Tantos choques en las arenas %lo% han convertido en %un% guerrer%o% astut%o%, y también en un%o% con tantas cicatrices y heridas como tiempo pasó allí. | En este mundo hay muchas cosas que van de la mano, y un gladiador con el cuerpo intacto no es una de ellas. %name% lucha con destreza, pero se ganó esa experiencia con su propia sangre y su propio cuerpo. | Una trayectoria de gladiador tan impresionante como la que trae %name% apunta a %un% %hombre% muy versad%o% en matar. Sus muchas cicatrices, sin embargo, dejan claro que su paso por los fosos tuvo un precio irreversible. | Gladiadores como %name% podrían ser los luchadores más hábiles de todo el país, pero los fosos de combate están llenos de trampas y pensados para dañar a todo el que participa. %Ese% %hombre% es %un% guerrer%o% talentos%o%, pero lleva las cicatrices y las heridas de toda una carrera en la arena.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\gravedigger_background.nut
    // en = "Gravediggers are used to physical labor and handling the dead."
    // en base_es
    // en = "With the great successes of the %companyname%, %name% the gravedigger got continued practice in his trade. As the crowns began to stack, he eventually left the company and returned to the graveyards. Last you heard, he had retired to digging holes again and was happily raising a family of sextons."
    // en base_es
    // en = "The way you heard things, %name% the gravedigger was one of the last men to leave the %companyname%. With hardly a crown to his name, he slipped hard into drinking and last you heard his body was found in a muddied gully."
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7b%name% got his start as a gravedigger by burying his baby brother. | Putting a sword to his drunken father's neck, %name%'s start in gravedigging was a nasty one. First he buried the crime, and then he buried the lawmen who came around asking questions. | After disease swept through %townname%, %name% was the last man standing. He had to abandon his trade to take up the only thing left: gravedigging.\x7d There's a look in the dead, they say. But there's also a look in those who have seen the dead. %name% has now spent a life and a half \x7bstaring at corpses | putting bodies in the ground | digging graves, big ones and small\x7d. To the gravedigger, \x7bdeath is now but a science | the dead have been better company than the living | earning gold for burying the dead is no new task\x7d. \x7bEmployed by a wagon-train, %name% traveled the land and dug it up, too. But one day his burial was suddenly undone. Not by the buzzards or rats, but by the dead itself. Seeing such a sight, and having to bury the same man twice, no doubt compels a swift career change. | Every gravedigger is eyed with suspicion. It wasn't long until his patrons became accusers and the notion of a horrific crime of undead passion drove him from his work. The claims are absurd, but you can't get a read on his pale face. It's like playing cards with the moon. | By now, the man looks as if he could use a change of scenery. Just don't ask him to bury the casualties.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\graverobber_background.nut
    // en = "Graverobber"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Graverobbers are not faint of heart."
    // en base_es
    // en = "Graverobbers like %name% aren't exactly the most well liked men in this world, but all you needed from him was to be a great mercenary and he came through in spades. After you left the business, you learned that the graverobber stayed for the long haul. From what you know, he's now the company's trainer, helping green recruits get up to speed."
    // en base_es
    // en = "A man like %name% the graverobber came to the company to help escape from his most unlawful and immoral errors, and what better way to do that than killing people for money? Unfortunately, the %companyname% slowly began to fall apart. You learned that %name% eventually left the company and joined with a similar, competing outfit. You're not sure where he is now, and you're not sure whether to be insulted by his betrayal or understand the reasoning behind it. Business is only business, after all."
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bWhat compels a man to disturb those who have passed away? | With rumors of the dead rising again, perhaps it is but forward thinking to go around digging up graves. | An enemy to moral standards and sensibilities, men who take spades to fresh graves find few allies. | A coward attacks a man when he's down, a graverobber attacks a man when he's really down. | It is trivial how easily a man abrogated by death can be acquired by mere graverobbing. | When it comes to death, worms take the flesh, and time the bones, but graverobbers get the jewels.\x7d \x7bRaised by an abusive mother, %name% found happier coordinance with the dead than the living. | After many lonely nights in hermitry, %name% is said to have taken up dancing with the dead. | %name% romanced beneath the stars, but pale and cold describes more than just the night sky. | For entertainment in a boring life, %name% is known to visit the murky gastines of graveyards. | Swindled by a salesman, %name% found himself digging up graves for loot. So the story goes, anyway. | Once a fine jeweler, dementia drove %name% into crafting a very different style of attire. A toothy necklace chatters at you as he explains.\x7d \x7bThe deviancies of such a man may know no bounds, but his for-now warm body could be of use. | He's not right in the head, but maybe he's right with a sword in hand. Maybe. | Disturbing as he might be, desperate times call for desperate recruits. | He wears a plain necklace with a subtle offwhite color best described as 'bone'. | Driven away by an especially mad mob, %name% is one of many outcasts to venture into the world of mercenaries. | The man is quiet, but you can't shut him up around a graveyard. | Hopefully he likes putting cold bodies into graves as much as he likes digging them up.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\hedge_knight_background.nut
    // en = "Hedge Knight"
    // en base_es
    // context: hedge_knight_background.o.create.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "Hedge Knights are competitive individuals that excel in fighting man against man with brute strength and heavy armor, but less so in cooperating with others or in swiftness. Hedge Knights strike with such strength that they might cleave a secondary enemy."
        es = "Los caballeros errantes son individuos competitivos que destacan en la lucha hombre contra hombre con fuerza bruta y armadura pesada, pero menos en cooperación con otros o en rapidez. Los caballeros errantes golpean con tanta fuerza que su tajo puede alcanzar también a un segundo enemigo."
    }
    // context: hedge_knight_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "A %person% like %name% would always find a way. The hedge knight eventually, if not inevitably, left the company and set out on %their% own. Unlike many other mercenaries, %they% did not spend %their% crowns on land or ladders with which to climb the noble life. Instead, %they% bought %themselves% the finest war horses and the talents of armorers. The behemoth of a %person% rode from one jousting tournament to the next, winning them all with ease. %They're% still at it to this day, and you think %they% won't stop until %they're% dead. The hedge knight simply knows no other life."
        es = "%Un% %hombre% como %name% siempre encontraría la manera. Al final, como era inevitable, dejó la compañía y siguió su propio camino. A diferencia de muchos otros mercenarios, no gastó sus coronas en tierras ni en escaleras con las que trepar hasta la vida noble. En su lugar, se compró los mejores caballos de guerra y los servicios de los mejores armeros. Aquella mole de %hombre% cabalgó de un torneo de justas al siguiente y los ganó todos con facilidad. Todavía hoy sigue en ello, y crees que no parará hasta el día de su muerte. Sencillamente, no conoce otra vida."
    }
    // context: hedge_knight_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        // corrige base: la 1.0 añade "con su lanza 'amañada'", un juego de palabras que el inglés no tiene; "throw a match" es dejarse ganar, no amañar sin más
        en = "%name% the hedge knight eventually left the company. %They% traveled the lands, returning to %their% favorite pastime of jousting, which was really a cover for %their% real favorite pastime of lancing men off horses in a shower of splinters and glory. At some point, %they% was ordered to 'throw' a match against a pitiful and gangly prince to earn the nobleman some prestige. Instead, the hedge knight drove %their% lance through the man's skull. Furious, the lord of the land ordered the hedge knight killed. They say over a hundred soldiers took to %their% home and only half returned alive."
        es = "%name% acabó dejando la compañía. Recorrió estas tierras y volvió a su pasatiempo favorito, las justas, que en realidad eran una tapadera para su verdadero pasatiempo favorito: derribar hombres de sus caballos a lanzazos entre una lluvia de astillas y gloria. En cierto momento, le ordenaron 'dejarse ganar' en un combate contra un príncipe lamentable y desgarbado para que el noble se ganara algo de prestigio. En cambio, le atravesó el cráneo con la lanza. Furioso, el señor de aquellas tierras ordenó su muerte. Dicen que más de cien soldados fueron a buscar%lo% a su casa y que solo la mitad regresó con vida."
    }
    // en = "the Wolf"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Hound"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Jouster"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Giant"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Mountain"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Strongface"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Defiler"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Knightslayer"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Hedge Knight"
    // en base_es
    // context: hedge_knight_background.o.getTooltip.ret.push().text
    {
        en = "Once per turn upon killing an enemy execute an attack of opportunity on an enemy on an adjacent tile for [color=%negative%]50%[/color] damage"
        es = "Una vez por turno, al matar a un enemigo, realiza un ataque de oportunidad contra un enemigo en una casilla adyacente que inflige un [color=%negative%]50%[/color] del daño"
    }
    // context: hedge_knight_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{Some people are born to be feared. Well over six feet tall, %name%'s stature alone is a threatening one. | %name%'s shadow casts over smaller men - and they seem to only further shrink when %they% walks by. | Standing amongst men like a bear in a suit of armor, %name% earns plenty of double-takes. | Years of brutal combat with %their% equally huge brothers left %name% a scarred and scary figure.} {The hedge knight has spent many seasons taking %their% prized horse to jousting tournaments. Unfortunately, a polearm crowned %their% mount, leaving %them% without a ride. | A mercenary in the company of %themselves%, the hedge knight wandered for years, doing battle for those who offered the most crowns. | When %they% cleaved five men with one swing, three of which were on %their% side, the hedge knight was banned from service in every army in the land. | Ordered to kill a lord's enemies, the hedge knight kicked in the door of a family and slaughtered them all with %their% bare hands. When the lord refused to pay, %name% killed him, too. | The hedge knight has spent many nights sleeping peacefully beneath a pale moon - and just as many days killing ruthlessly beneath a shining sun.} {Always on the hunt for more crowns, the company of sellswords seemed like a good fit. | Too terrifying to be employed for long, %name% seeks the company of men who will not piss themselves when %they% grabs a weapon. | Tired of killing jousters and lords, as well as women and children, %name% sees mercenary work as something of a vacation. | War has apparently gotten in the way of %name%'s jousting career. %They% seeks to amend that problem.}"
        es = "{Hay gente que nace para inspirar miedo. Con bastante más de seis pies de altura, la estatura de %name% ya resulta amenazante por sí sola. | La sombra de %name% se cierne sobre los hombres más bajos, y estos parecen encogerse aún más cuando pasa a su lado. | Como un oso con armadura entre los hombres, %name% hace que más de uno se gire a mirar dos veces. | Años de combates brutales junto a sus hermanos, igual de enormes, han dejado a %name% convertid%o% en una figura temible y llena de cicatrices.} {Pasó muchas temporadas llevando su preciado caballo a torneos de justas. Por desgracia, un arma de asta le partió la cabeza a su montura y %lo% dejó a pie. | Mercenari%o% sin más compañía que la suya propia, vagó durante años luchando para quien ofreciera más coronas. | Cuando partió a cinco hombres de un solo tajo, tres de ellos de su propio bando, le prohibieron servir en todos los ejércitos del país. | Cuando le ordenaron matar a los enemigos de un señor, derribó a patadas la puerta de una familia y los masacró a todos con sus propias manos. Cuando el señor se negó a pagar, %name% también lo mató. | Ha pasado muchas noches durmiendo en paz bajo una luna pálida, y otros tantos días matando sin piedad bajo un sol radiante.} {Siempre en busca de más coronas, una compañía de mercenarios parecía encajar bien. | Como da demasiado miedo para que nadie %lo% contrate mucho tiempo, %name% busca la compañía de hombres que no se meen encima cuando empuña un arma. | Cansad%o% de matar a justadores y señores, y también a mujeres y niños, %name% ve el trabajo de mercenario como una especie de vacaciones. | Al parecer, la guerra se ha interpuesto en la carrera de justas de %name%. Pretende ponerle remedio.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\historian_background.nut
    // en = "Historian"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Historians are studious individuals with vast amounts of knowledge, none of it any use on the battlefield."
    // en base_es
    // en = "You did not expect the historian, %name%, to stay in the company forever. He eventually left and it is said he took with him a large trove of scrolls. As it turns out, he was compiling a list of the %companyname%'s achievements. He created a codex of all its accomplishments, enshrining the name of all the mercenaries into the history books for future generations to see. You hope they learn something from your doings."
    // en base_es
    // en = "The %companyname% continued its decline and many non-fighters such as %name% the historian saw this as a good time to leave. You tried to keep up with these men, but the historian was particularly easy to find: he left a paper trail. You sought the man out, asking scribes if they had heard of him. They said he was a mere little man writing a tome about how dark, violent, and pointless the life of a sellsword is."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Owl"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Studious"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Historian"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bAlways a voracious reader, %name%'s early life consisted of long nights in %randomcity%'s library. | Bullied by his stronger peers, a young %name% retreated into the world of books. | Looking for where man's past truly lies, %name% read books and studied human nature. | With so many changes in the world, %name% decided to help record them. | A quick-learner with a penchant for a good read, %name% sought to envision the world on paper for others. | A scholar of %randomcity%'s small college, %name% records the histories of the world for future generations. | Chilled by dark events in the world, %name% stopped studying plants and began recording human history.\x7d \x7bA proper historian seeks the closest sources he can get, which has brought the man to the company of mercenaries. | After brigands ruined his written works, the man strapped on his boots to carve out new research - personally. | When his professor said his research was rubbish, the historian went out into the world to prove him wrong. | Accused of plagiarism, the historian was kicked out of academia. He seeks redemption in the world of what he studied: war. | Using his position in academia to bed women, eventual scandals and controversies drove the historian from his field, and left him penniless and ready to take on any job. | Bored with reading about adventurers, the historian figured he'd suit up to fashion himself a closer look at the real thing. | With so many mercenary bands floating around, the historian sought to attach himself for some real-life studying.\x7d \x7b%name% has little in common with actual soldiers, but his imaginative mind fancies a good battle nonetheless. | While %name% spent all his life writing, he spent exactly none of it fighting. Until now. | %name% has the itch to record your outfit's travels. He can help by grabbing a sword and suiting up. | A bag of books is hefted over %name%'s shoulder. You suggest a flail as replacement. It's similar, but pointier and stabbier. | %name% is frequently found scribbling notes as he still sees the world with a researcher's eye. | %name% comes with a pocketful of quill pens. The feathers would make for some pretty good arrows. | You can place good faith in %name%'s earnest want to research, but maybe not so much faith in his ability to swing a sword. | %name%'s time with the outfit is to develop a theory, but can he survive the experiments? | You promise %name% that, shall he perish, you will find a way to record his life. He thanks you and hands over his will. It's written in a language foreign to you and you can read absolutely none of it. You smile back anyway.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\historian_southern_background.nut
    // en = "\x7bAlways a voracious reader, %name%'s early life consisted of long nights in the many libraries of %randomcitystate%. | Bullied by his stronger peers, a young %name% retreated into the world of books. | Looking for where man's past truly lies, %name% read books and studied human nature. | With so many changes in the world, %name% decided to help record them. | A quick-learner with a penchant for a good read, %name% sought to envision the world on paper for others. | A scholar of %randomcitystate%'s college, %name% records the histories of the world for future generations. | Chilled by dark events in the world, %name% stopped studying plants and began recording human history.\x7d \x7bA proper historian seeks the closest sources he can get, which has brought the man to the company of mercenaries. | After desert raiders ruined his written works, the man strapped on his boots to carve out new research - personally. | When his professor said his research was rubbish, the historian went out into the world to prove him wrong. | Accused of plagiarism, the historian was kicked out of academia. He seeks redemption in the world of what he studied: war. | Using his position in academia to bed women, eventual scandals and controversies drove the historian from his field, and left him penniless and ready to take on any job. | Bored with reading about adventurers, the historian figured he'd suit up to fashion himself a closer look at the real thing. | With so many mercenary bands floating around, the historian sought to attach himself for some real-life studying.\x7d \x7b%name% has little in common with actual soldiers, but his imaginative mind fancies a good battle nonetheless. | While %name% spent all his life writing, he spent exactly none of it fighting. Until now. | %name% has the itch to record your outfit's travels. He can help by grabbing a sword and suiting up. | A bag of books is hefted over %name%'s shoulder. You suggest a flail as replacement. It's similar, but pointier and stabbier. | %name% is frequently found scribbling notes as he still sees the world with a researcher's eye. | %name% comes with a pocketful of quill pens. The feathers would make for some pretty good arrows. | You can place good faith in %name%'s earnest want to research, but maybe not so much faith in his ability to swing a sword. | %name%'s time with the outfit is to develop a theory, but can he survive the experiments? | You promise %name% that, shall he perish, you will find a way to record his life. He thanks you and hands over his will. It's written in a language foreign to you and you can read absolutely none of it. You smile back anyway.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\houndmaster_background.nut
    // en = "Houndmaster"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Houndmasters are used to handle dogs of war."
    // en base_es
    // en = "Dogs were not simply 'hounds' to %name%, despite his title as 'houndmaster.' To him, they were the most loyal friends of his life. After leaving the company, he discovered an ingenious way to breed the animals specifically tailored to the desires of the nobility. Wanted a brutish beast for a guard dog? He could do it. Wanted something small and cuddly for the children? He could do that, too. The former mercenary now earns an incredible earning doing what he loves - working with dogs."
    // en base_es
    // en = "What's merely a hound to one man is a loyal beast to %name%. After leaving the company, the houndmaster went out to work for the nobility. Unfortunately, he refused to let hundreds of his dogs be used as a battle vanguard to be thrown away for some short-lived tactical advantage. He was hanged for his 'traitorous ideals'."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Houndmaster"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Kennelmaster"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Dogkeeper"
    // en base_es
    // context: houndmaster_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "Dogs were not simply 'hounds' to %name%, despite her title as 'houndmaster.' To her, they were the most loyal friends of her life. After leaving the company, she discovered an ingenious way to breed the animals specifically tailored to the desires of the nobility. Wanted a brutish beast for a guard dog? She could do it. Wanted something small and cuddly for the children? She could do that, too. The former mercenary now earns an incredible earning doing what she loves - working with dogs."
        es = "Los perros no eran simplemente 'sabuesos' para %name%, a pesar de su título de 'maestra de sabuesos'. Para ella, eran los amigos más leales de su vida. Después de dejar la compañía, descubrió una forma ingeniosa de criar animales adaptados específicamente a los deseos de la nobleza. ¿Querían una bestia brutal como perro guardián? Podía hacerlo. ¿Querían algo pequeño y tierno para los niños? También podía hacerlo. La antigua mercenaria ahora gana una fortuna increíble haciendo lo que ama: trabajar con perros."
    }
    // context: houndmaster_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "What's merely a hound to some folks is a loyal beast to %name%. After leaving the company, the houndmaster went out to work for the nobility. Unfortunately, she refused to let hundreds of her dogs be used as a battle vanguard to be thrown away for some short-lived tactical advantage. She was hanged for her 'traitorous ideals'."
        es = "Lo que para algunos es simplemente un sabueso, para %name% es una bestia leal. Después de dejar la compañía, la maestra de sabuesos se puso a trabajar para la nobleza. Por desgracia, se negó a permitir que cientos de sus perros se usaran como vanguardia en la batalla, para ser sacrificados a cambio de alguna efímera ventaja táctica. La ahorcaron por sus 'ideales traidores'."
    }
    // en = "Wardogs unleashed by this character will start at confident morale"
    // en base_es
    // context: houndmaster_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: "El maestro de perros" por "El maestro de sabuesos", el nombre que usa la 1.0 en el resto del texto; "probar suerte como hoja a sueldo por sí mismo": sellsword es "mercenario" y "por sí mismo" no está en el inglés
        en = "{%name%'s fondness for dogs started after her father won a pup in a shooting contest. | When a dog saved her from a bear, %name% dedicated her life to the canine lot. | Seeing a dog stave off a would-be robber, %name%'s fondness for the mutts only grew. | A young, bird-hunting %name% quickly saw the honor, loyalty, and workmanship of a dog. | Once bitten by a wild dog, %name% confronted her fear of canines by learning to train them.} {The houndmaster spent many years working for a local lord. She gave up the post after the liege struck a dog down just for sport. | Quick with training her mongrels, the houndmaster put her dogs into a lucrative traveling tradeshow. | The woman made a great deal of money on the dog-fighting circuits, her mutts renowned for their easily commanded - and unleashed - ferocity. | Employed by lawmen, the houndmaster used her strong-nosed dogs to hunt down many a criminal element. | Used by a local lord, many of the houndmaster's dogs found their way onto the battlefield. | For many years, the houndmaster used her dogs to help lift the spirits of orphaned children and the crippled.} {Now, though, %name% seeks a change of vocation. | When she heard word of a mercenary's pay, %name% decided to try her hand at being a sellsword. | Approached by a sellsword to buy one of her dogs, %name% became more interested in the prospect of she, herself, becoming a mercenary. | Tired of training dogs for this purpose or that, %name% seeks to train herself for... well, this purpose or that. | An interesting prospect, you can only hope %name% is as loyal as the dogs she once commanded.}"
        es = "{El cariño de %name% por los perros comenzó después de que su padre ganara un cachorro en un concurso de tiro. | Cuando un perro la salvó de un oso, %name% dedicó su vida al mundo canino. | Al ver a un perro ahuyentar a un ladrón en potencia, el afecto de %name% por los mestizos no hizo más que crecer. | De joven, cazando aves, %name% vio enseguida el honor, la lealtad y la destreza de un perro. | Tras ser mordida una vez por un perro salvaje, %name% se enfrentó a su miedo a los caninos aprendiendo a adiestrarlos.} {La maestra de sabuesos pasó muchos años trabajando para un señor local. Renunció al cargo después de que su señor matara a un perro solo por diversión. | Rápida en el adiestramiento de sus mestizos, la maestra de sabuesos llevó a sus perros a un lucrativo espectáculo itinerante. | La mujer ganó mucho dinero en los circuitos de peleas de perros, con unos mestizos famosos por su ferocidad, fácil de controlar... y de desatar. | Empleada por los agentes de la ley, la maestra de sabuesos usó a sus perros de buen olfato para dar caza a numerosos criminales. | Utilizados por un señor local, muchos de los perros de la maestra de sabuesos acabaron en el campo de batalla. | Durante muchos años, la maestra de sabuesos usó a sus perros para levantar el ánimo de niños huérfanos y lisiados.} {Ahora, sin embargo, %name% busca un cambio de vocación. | Cuando oyó cuánto cobra un mercenario, %name% decidió probar suerte en el oficio. | Cuando un mercenario la abordó para comprarle uno de sus perros, a %name% le interesó más la posibilidad de convertirse ella misma en mercenaria. | Cansada de adiestrar perros para este propósito o aquel, %name% busca adiestrarse a sí misma para... bueno, este propósito o aquel. | Una perspectiva interesante; solo cabe esperar que %name% sea tan leal como los perros que antes comandaba.}"
    }
    // en = "\x7b%name%'s fondness for dogs started after his father won a pup in a shooting contest. | When a dog saved him from a bear, %name% dedicated his life to the canine lot. | Seeing a dog stave off a would-be robber, %name%'s fondness for the mutts only grew. | A young, bird-hunting %name% quickly saw the honor, loyalty, and workmanship of a dog. | Once bitten by a wild dog, %name% confronted his fear of canines by learning to train them.\x7d \x7bThe houndmaster spent many years working for a local lord. He gave up the post after the liege struck a dog down just for sport. | Quick with training his mongrels, the houndmaster put his dogs into a lucrative traveling tradeshow. | The man made a great deal of money on the dog-fighting circuits, his mutts renowned for their easily commanded - and unleashed - ferocity. | Employed by lawmen, the houndmaster used his strong-nosed dogs to hunt down many a criminal element. | Used by a local lord, many of the houndmaster's dogs found their way onto the battlefield. | For many years, the houndmaster used his dogs to help lift the spirits of orphaned children and the crippled.\x7d \x7bNow, though, %name% seeks a change of vocation. | When he heard word of a mercenary's pay, %name% decided to try his hand at being a sellsword. | Approached by a sellsword to buy one of his dogs, %name% became more interested in the prospect of he, himself, becoming a mercenary. | Tired of training dogs for this purpose or that, %name% seeks to train himself for... well, this purpose or that. | An interesting prospect, you can only hope %name% is as loyal as the dogs he once commanded.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\hunter_background.nut
    // en = "Hunters are used to expertly hunt animals with bow and arrow, and traverse the woods on their own."
    // en base_es
    // context: hunter_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "While the %companyname% continued on with great success, %name% the hunter eventually saw fit to leave it all behind. %They% returned to the forests and fields, hunting deer and small game. %They% rarely showed the grim reality of hunting humans, but you have to imagine %they%'d just rather stop doing it. As far as you know, %they're% doing well for %themselves% these days. %They% purchased a bit of land and helps guide nobles on pricy hunting trips."
        es = "Mientras %companyname% seguía cosechando grandes éxitos, %name% acabó por dejarlo todo atrás. Volvió a los bosques y los campos para cazar ciervos y piezas menores. Rara vez dejaba ver lo sombrío que era cazar humanos, pero te imaginas que, sencillamente, prefería dejar de hacerlo. Por lo que sabes, hoy en día le va bien. Compró un pedazo de tierra y hace de guía para nobles en costosas partidas de caza."
    }
    // context: hunter_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        // corrige base: "shot by the nobleman and his guard" es que pasó como una flecha junto a ellos, no que les disparara; "evidentemente obvio" es redundante
        en = "With the decline of the %companyname% readily obvious, %name% the hunter departed from the company and returned to game hunting. Unfortunately, a hunting trip with a nobleman went awry when the lord was gored through both cheeks by a boar. The hunter, feeling %they%'d be blamed, shot by the nobleman and his guard and fled through the forests on %their% own. %They% has not been seen since."
        es = "Con el declive de %companyname% ya bien evidente, %name% dejó la compañía y volvió a la caza de animales. Por desgracia, una partida de caza con un noble se torció cuando un jabalí le atravesó al señor ambas mejillas con los colmillos. Temiendo que le echaran la culpa, pasó como una exhalación junto al noble y su guardia y huyó a solas por los bosques. No se le ha vuelto a ver desde entonces."
    }
    // en = "the Deerhunter"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Woodsman"
    // en base_es
    // en = "True-Shot"
    // en base_es
    // en = "One Shot"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Eagle Eye"
    // en base_es
    // context: hunter_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{Without %their% father around, %name%'s mother taught %them% how to shoot a bow, and how to feed the rest of %their% family. | Born in the hinterlands of %randomtown%, %name% has spent much of %their% life stalking the beasts amongst the trees. | %name% once took a bet to shoot an apple off a pig's head. %They% missed. With a belly full of bacon, %they% became determined to never miss again - unless it meant more bacon, of course. | Early in %their% life, %name% liked to traipse about the forests. When a rabid fox attacked %them%, %they% learned to take a bow. When a devilish eagle clawed %their% face, %they% learned to shoot it.} {Once employed by local royalty, a disastrous boar hunt ended with a gored baron and all the blame - and blood - on %name%'s hands. | The hunter hid the thought well, but for the longest time %they% wondered what it would be like to hunt the ultimate game: man. | Sadly, a bad game of peasant-roulette forced the deer hunter into seeking other means of income. | Unfortunately, %they% is not nearly as good at cooking deer as %they% is at shooting them. A dinner consisting of undercooked meats poisoned his entire family. %their% desperation for a new life is understandable. | After an arduous trip to town to sell meats and leathers, %they% followed the call of mercenary work. | War drove the game out of the forests, and the hunt out of %name%. Now %they% seeks another line of work. | When %their% %partner% fell ill, %they% could not heal her with hunted meat. Needing to earn crowns to pay for treatment, %they% took up the vocation of sellswords - or sellbows, as it were.} {Any outfit could use a deadeye such as this %person%. | Not entirely without faults, %name% is a professional bowman nonetheless. | A quick demonstration is offered: %name% shoots one arrow high into the sky, and with another %they% knocks it out. Impressive. | %name% looks like %they% has something to prove - just make sure %they% does it at range. When first given a sword, %they% grabbed it at the wrong end. Yes, that end. | The hunter wields %their% bow like another limb, and shoots %their% arrows like a preacher does words.}"
        es = "{Sin un padre cerca, la madre de %name% le enseñó a tirar con arco y a alimentar al resto de la familia. | Nacid%o% en los confines de %randomtown%, %name% ha pasado buena parte de su vida acechando a las bestias entre los árboles. | %name% aceptó una vez la apuesta de acertarle a una manzana sobre la cabeza de un cerdo. Falló. Con la panza llena de tocino, se propuso no volver a fallar nunca, salvo que eso significara más tocino, claro. | De joven, a %name% le gustaba vagar por los bosques. Cuando un zorro rabioso %lo% atacó, aprendió a empuñar un arco. Cuando un águila endiablada le arañó la cara, aprendió a dispararlo.} {Al servicio de la realeza local, una desastrosa cacería de jabalíes terminó con un barón destripado y toda la culpa, y la sangre, en las manos de %name%. | Lo disimulaba bien, pero durante muchísimo tiempo se preguntó cómo sería cazar la presa definitiva: el hombre. | Por desgracia, una mala partida de 'ruleta campesina' %lo% obligó a buscar otras fuentes de ingresos. | Por desgracia, no se le da ni de lejos tan bien cocinar ciervos como abatirlos. Una cena de carne mal cocinada envenenó a toda su familia. Es comprensible su desesperación por empezar una vida nueva. | Tras un arduo viaje al pueblo para vender carnes y pieles, siguió la llamada del oficio de mercenario. | La guerra ahuyentó las presas de los bosques y le quitó a %name% las ganas de cazar. Ahora busca otro oficio. | Cuando su %partner% enfermó, no pudo curarla con carne de caza. Como necesitaba ganar coronas para pagar el tratamiento, abrazó el oficio de las espadas a sueldo, o más bien de los arcos a sueldo.} {A cualquier grupo le vendría bien alguien con tan buena puntería como %ese% %hombre%. | No del todo libre de defectos, %name% es aun así %un% arquer%o% profesional. | %name% ofrece una rápida demostración: dispara una flecha bien alto hacia el cielo y la derriba con otra. Impresionante. | %name% parece tener algo que demostrar; solo asegúrate de que lo haga a distancia. La primera vez que le dieron una espada, la agarró por el lado equivocado. Sí, por ese lado. | Maneja el arco como si fuera una extremidad más, y dispara sus flechas como un predicador suelta palabras.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\juggler_background.nut
    // en = "Jugglers need to have good reflexes and hand-eye-coordination for their profession."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% the juggler took all his mercenary money and started a traveling troupe of performers. Last you heard, he started an entire theater and puts on a new play a month!"
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% the juggler retired from fighting. He was performing for a gaudy nobleman in the \x7bsouth | north | east | west\x7d when an act went horribly wrong. Word has it he was thrown off a tower for his mistake, but you prefer to not believe that."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Juggler"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Jester"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Fool"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Higher Chance To Hit Head"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bTaught by his step-brother, %name% took up juggling like a sailor to his oars. | Although sneered at by his peers, %name% always loved juggling. | Visited by a troupe of jesters, %name% was most enamored - and eventually taught - by one particularly interesting man: a juggler. | Son to a local lord, %name%'s embarrassing obsession with juggling and entertaining had him exiled from the family line. | %name% didn't juggle just for the sake of it, but to earn the laughter and applause of an audience.\x7d \x7bUnfortunately, there's not many folks to entertain when war is ravaging the land. | But crowds and crowns are sparse in a land of misery and suffering. | But a juggling accident involving adzes and a royal infant had the entertainer running for his life. | So good at flipping swords and daggers, it wasn't long until he was accused of sorcery and driven from his passion. | Sadly, %name%'s skill in juggling led to much jealousy amongst his fellow jesters. They conspired against him - and his poor wrists. | When an assassin killed the lord he was entertaining, the juggler was the first to be accused. He barely escaped with his life.\x7d \x7bNow, %name% seeks a new path, even if death itself has become his audience. | Now, %name% finds respite in the company of equally down-on-their-luck men. | With fast hands and quick reactions, %name% should have no problem hitting his targets. | Juggling knives with his eyes closed, %name% knows exactly where to throw each blade. | There is far more coin in killing than juggling, a sad reality %name% has come to accept.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\juggler_southern_background.nut
    // context: juggler_southern_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{Natural talent is rare, and %name% had it in ample supply. A quick and easy career awaited them as a juggler and performer at the most illustrious street corners. Eventually climbing to a position within the Vizir's court, one vicious mockery of a steward's nose ended badly. %name% had a choice — be thrown into the arena for the insult, or self imposed exile. | %name% is a mercurial character and very different to the performers you have seen before. Other performers swear they have not seen or heard of them before, yet they have a reputation among their own craft. When asked about their routine and history, %name% casually waves off the question and laughs. Their startling obsession with anything pointed and throwable is not all that unusual — but what you can't shake is the feeling that you have seen them before. | While not as dangerous as mercenary work, %name% found themselves in recent trouble concerning some knives, a target and a young street girl. When pushed for answers all they can grumble is “I did not hit her” and “It's not true”, normally followed by “I did not”. Even for a performer their behaviour is bizarre and often erratic, going on at length about the ideas they have for new stage plays, sometimes for hours. | Jaded by a life of performance, %name% retired from physical acts and instead devoted their time to writing for others. They had dreamt about this moment for years but when the time came to writing their audience informed them that they were, quite frankly, terrible. A long deep spiral of despair awaited %name% until the day their writing had them cast out of their home by a mob. | Slathered in a musk of arrogance, %name% strides around like everyone should know their name — throwing veiled insults as they go. Overly critical and thin skinned themselves, %name% managed to get on the bad side of almost everyone they met, somehow without realising they were doing so at all. The day another performer rejected their “help” was the last straw. In just a few moments they destroyed all their work and set out to work in another profession, much to the relief of their fellow performers. | Natural talent in the juggling arts is rare, but %name% claims to be a renowned master. Other performers swear they have never seen or heard of them before, so you take this with a pinch of salt. While juggling is not as dangerous as mercenary work, they recently found themselves in trouble after witnessing a common back-alley robbery. Eager to be a hero, %name% applied their natural talent in a new, unexpectedly violent way, much to the distress of all present. With the local Muhtasib seeking answers for the unexplained deaths, %name% wisely decided it was time for a change of profession.}"
        es = "{El talento natural escasea, y a %name% le sobraba. Le esperaba una carrera rápida y fácil como malabarista y artista en las esquinas más ilustres. Llegó a hacerse un hueco en la corte del visir, pero una burla despiadada sobre la nariz de un mayordomo acabó mal. %name% tuvo que elegir: acabar en la arena por el insulto o exiliarse por voluntad propia. | %name% tiene un carácter voluble y no se parece en nada a los artistas que has visto antes. Otros artistas juran no haber visto ni oído hablar nunca de esta persona, y aun así tiene fama en su propio oficio. Cuando le preguntas por su número y su historia, %name% esquiva la pregunta con un gesto despreocupado y se ríe. Su sorprendente obsesión por todo lo que sea puntiagudo y arrojadizo no es tan rara, pero lo que no consigues quitarte de encima es la sensación de que ya se conocen de antes. | Su oficio no es tan peligroso como el de mercenario, pero hace poco %name% se metió en problemas por unos cuchillos, una diana y una muchacha de la calle. Cuando se le insiste, solo alcanza a refunfuñar “No le pegué” y “No es verdad”, normalmente seguido de “No lo hice”. Incluso para alguien de la farándula, su comportamiento es extraño y a menudo errático: se pasa horas hablando sin parar de las ideas que tiene para nuevas obras de teatro. | Con el hastío de toda una vida sobre el escenario, %name% abandonó los números físicos y dedicó su tiempo a escribir para otros. Llevaba años soñando con ese momento, pero cuando llegó la hora de escribir, su público le hizo saber que, francamente, era terrible. Una larga y profunda espiral de desesperación aguardaba a %name%, hasta el día en que sus escritos le costaron su hogar a manos de una turba. | Con un almizcle de arrogancia encima, %name% se pasea como si todo el mundo tuviera que conocer su nombre, soltando insultos velados a su paso. Con un exceso de espíritu crítico y sin soportar una sola crítica hacia sí, %name% se las arregló para caerle mal a casi todo aquel con quien se cruzó, sin darse cuenta en absoluto de que lo estaba haciendo. El día en que otro artista rechazó su “ayuda” fue la gota que colmó el vaso. En apenas unos momentos destruyó todo su trabajo y se marchó a buscarse otra profesión, para gran alivio de sus colegas de escena. | El talento natural para los malabares escasea, pero %name% asegura ser una eminencia de renombre. Otros artistas juran no haber visto ni oído hablar nunca de esta persona, así que te lo tomas con reservas. Aunque los malabares no son tan peligrosos como el trabajo de mercenario, hace poco se metió en problemas tras presenciar un robo corriente en un callejón. Con ganas de jugar a los héroes, %name% aplicó su talento natural de una forma nueva e inesperadamente violenta, para gran consternación de todos los presentes. Con el muhtasib local buscando respuestas sobre aquellas muertes sin explicar, %name% decidió sabiamente que era hora de cambiar de profesión.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\killer_on_the_run_background.nut
    // en = "Killer on the Run"
    // en base_es
    // en = "A killer on the run may kill again, and he knows where to aim."
    // en base_es
    // en = "Always a risk taker, you accepted %name% into the %companyname%'s ranks despite him being a killer on the run. It worked in your favor as he proved himself an able and brave sellsword. As far as you know, he is still with the company, thoroughly enjoying every 'business' opportunity it affords him."
    // en base_es
    // en = "While many doubted the risk of hiring a killer on the run such as %name%, the man did prove himself a very capable sellsword. Unfortunately, an old life never trails far behind and bounty hunters kidnapped him in the night. You can find his skeleton squatting in a gibbet fifty feet in the air."
    // en base_es
    // en = "Darkhearted"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Backblade"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Throatslash"
    // en base_es
    // en = "on the Run"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Wanted"
    // en base_es
    // context: killer_on_the_run_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "Always a risk taker, you accepted %name% into the %companyname%'s ranks despite her being a killer on the run. It worked in your favor as she proved herself an able and brave sellsword. As far as you know, she is still with the company, thoroughly enjoying every 'business' opportunity it affords her."
        es = "Siempre te gustó correr riesgos, así que aceptaste a %name% en las filas de %companyname% pese a que era una asesina a la fuga. Te salió bien, pues demostró ser una mercenaria capaz y valiente. Por lo que sabes, sigue en la compañía, disfrutando a fondo de cada oportunidad de 'negocio' que le brinda."
    }
    // context: killer_on_the_run_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "While many doubted the risk of hiring a killer on the run such as %name%, the woman did prove herself a very capable sellsword. Unfortunately, an old life never trails far behind and bounty hunters kidnapped her in the night. You can find her skeleton squatting in a gibbet fifty feet in the air."
        es = "Aunque muchos dudaban de que valiera la pena el riesgo de contratar a una asesina a la fuga como %name%, la mujer demostró ser una mercenaria muy capaz. Por desgracia, la vida pasada nunca queda muy atrás, y unos cazarrecompensas la secuestraron por la noche. Puedes encontrar su esqueleto acuclillado en una jaula de hierro colgada a cincuenta pies de altura."
    }
    // context: killer_on_the_run_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{%fullname% has a face that no one desires - one fit for a wanted poster. | With blood on her hands, %name% resembles a woman recently described to you by bounty hunters. | %name% looks about ready to join any outfit - or disappear into its ranks. | Upon meeting people, %name% stammers out her name as if reluctant to part with it.} {Recognizing %name% is no hard feat: this woman is a known-murderer, the blood of both her cuckolding husband and his lover on her hands. | Her eyes are dark and shifting. There is a crime behind them, but also a sense of humanity, as if she knows she has done wrong and is looking to make amends. | Mud stands up to her legs. She's been running for a long time. Her hands tremble, too, for her legs run from what her hands have done. | They say she killed her newborn daughter, having always wanted a son instead. | Some believe she struck down a man in self-defense. | Being blackmailed with scandalous information, it's hard to blame the woman for what she has done.} {Even if she has done wrong, a party of killers could use a woman such as she. But can the woman be trusted? | %name%'s eyes skirt from yours. When you ask how she is with a weapon, she mumbles about only having to hit 'the man' once. | A woman of %name%'s physique could be useful, but how much can you depend upon a woman whose former life was one of being on the run? | The woman chamfers on her fingernails like a beaver would a tree. She's jumpy, but maybe that's a good thing in this world. | Mercenary bands are just the thing for a woman like her.}"
        es = "{%fullname% tiene una cara que nadie querría tener: de las que acaban en un cartel de 'se busca'. | Con sangre en las manos, %name% se parece a una mujer que unos cazarrecompensas te describieron hace poco. | %name% parece dispuesta a unirse a cualquier grupo, o a desaparecer entre sus filas. | Al conocer a alguien, %name% balbucea su nombre como si le costara desprenderse de él.} {Reconocer a %name% no es difícil: esta mujer es una asesina conocida, con la sangre de su marido infiel y de la amante de este en las manos. | Tiene los ojos oscuros e inquietos. Hay un crimen detrás de ellos, pero también cierta humanidad, como si supiera que ha obrado mal y quisiera enmendarse. | El barro le cubre las piernas. Lleva mucho tiempo huyendo. También le tiemblan las manos, porque sus piernas huyen de lo que han hecho sus manos. | Dicen que mató a su hija recién nacida porque siempre había querido un hijo varón. | Algunos creen que mató a un hombre en defensa propia. | La estaban chantajeando con información escandalosa, así que cuesta culparla por lo que hizo.} {Aunque haya obrado mal, a una banda de asesinos le vendría bien una mujer como ella. Pero ¿se puede confiar en ella? | %name% rehúye tu mirada. Cuando le preguntas qué tal se le dan las armas, masculla que a 'aquel hombre' solo tuvo que golpearlo una vez. | Una mujer con el físico de %name% podría ser útil, pero ¿hasta qué punto puedes depender de alguien cuya vida anterior consistía en huir? | Se roe las uñas como un castor roería un árbol. Es asustadiza, pero quizá eso no sea malo en este mundo. | Las bandas de mercenarios son justo lo que necesita una mujer como ella.}"
    }
    // en = "\x7b%fullname% has a face that no one desires - one fit for a wanted poster. | With blood on his hands, %name% resembles a man recently described to you by bounty hunters. | %name% looks about ready to join any outfit - or disappear into its ranks. | Upon meeting people, %name% stammers out his name as if reluctant to part with it.\x7d \x7bRecognizing %name% is no hard feat: this man is a known-murderer, the blood of both his cuckolding wife and her lover on his hands. | His eyes are dark and shifting. There is a crime behind them, but also a sense of humanity, as if he knows he has done wrong and is looking to make amends. | Mud stands up to his legs. He's been running for a long time. His hands tremble, too, for his legs run from what his hands have done. | They say he killed his newborn daughter, having always wanted a son instead. | Some believe he struck down a man in self-defense. | Being blackmailed with scandalous information, it's hard to blame the man for what he has done.\x7d \x7bEven if he has done wrong, a party of killers could use a man such as he. But can the man be trusted? | %name%'s eyes skirt from yours. When you ask how he is with a weapon, he mumbles about only having to hit 'the man' once. | A man of %name%'s physique could be useful, but how much can you depend upon a man whose former life was one of being on the run? | The man chamfers on his fingernails like a beaver would a tree. He's jumpy, but maybe that's a good thing in this world. | Mercenary bands are just the thing for a man like him.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\kings_guard_background.nut
    // en = "King's Guard"
    // en base_es
    // en = "You thought %name% a simple peasant when you found him freezing in the wastes of the north. As it turned out, he was very much a King's Guard, not only in title but in action. He fought like a man protecting his liege from the world at large. Thankfully, for a time, that 'liege' happened to be you. Last you heard he traveled to the southern realms and is protecting an upstart nomad king trying to overthrow the local Viziers."
    // en base_es
    // en = "You never truly found out which king %name% supposedly 'guarded' in his days before joining the %companyname%, but it matters not now. After your abrupt retirement, the King's Guard took himself to the southern deserts. He served a Vizier for a time but failed to protect the royal from a concubine's poison. For punishment, %name%'s equipment was melted into a pot and poured down his throat."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Kingsguard"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\lindwurm_slayer_background.nut
    // context: lindwurm_slayer_background.o.create.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "This mercenary is a one of a kind Lindwurm hunter, descendant of Dirk the Dragonslayer."
        es = "Un caso único entre los cazadores de Lindwurms: desciende de Dirk el Cazadragones."
    }
    // context: lindwurm_slayer_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "%name% left the %companyname% and started a lucrative career as a 'dragon specialist' advisor to the nobility. As far as you can tell %they% does very little actual work, instead spending %their% days attending lavish banquets, entertaining hosts and their guests with war-stories whilst quaffing their wine."
        es = "%name% dejó %companyname% y emprendió una lucrativa carrera como 'especialista en dragones' al servicio de la nobleza. Por lo que sabes, apenas trabaja de verdad: se pasa los días asistiendo a banquetes fastuosos y entreteniendo a sus anfitriones y a los invitados con historias de guerra mientras se bebe su vino."
    }
    // context: lindwurm_slayer_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "Disillusioned with the %companyname%, %name% left to pursue a solo dragon hunting career in order to finally live-up to the legacy of %their% famous father. %They% was last seen taking odd beast hunting contracts, but news of his exploits has no spread far and you fear the worst."
        es = "Desencantad%o% con %companyname%, %name% se marchó para dedicarse a cazar dragones por su cuenta y estar por fin a la altura del legado de su famoso padre. La última vez que se supo de %el%, aceptaba algún que otro contrato de caza de bestias, pero las noticias de sus hazañas no han llegado lejos y te temes lo peor."
    }
    // context: lindwurm_slayer_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: la 1.0 añade una variante anidada "{Eyck de Denesle | Dirk}" (guiño a The Witcher) que el inglés no tiene y descuadra llaves y barras frente al en; aquí se omite porque la fusión exige las mismas llaves. Decidir en la 1.0 si se conserva como guiño
        en = "{%name% is a supposedly famous monster hunter with a particular talent for slaying lindwurms. They says %they% is the %offspring% of Dirk the Dragonslayer, the monster hunter who ostensibly slew the last living dragon.}"
        es = "{%name% es, según dicen, toda una celebridad entre los cazadores de monstruos, con un talento especial para matar Lindwurms. Afirma ser hij%o% de Dirk el Cazadragones, el cazador de monstruos que en teoría mató al último dragón vivo.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\lumberjack_background.nut
    // en = "Lumberjack"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Lumberjacks are used to hard physical labor. And axes."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% the burly lumberjack eventually left the company to return to the woods. He started a woodcutting business and operates every day of the year. Luckily, timing was on his side: the nobility have recently really gotten 'into' cabins and are paying out crowns left and right to anyone who can build them."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% the lumberjack had enough of the sellsword's life and returned to woodcutting. Last you heard, he was involved in a tree-falling accident and his body could have been rolled up like a rug the bones were so thoroughly squashed."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Sturdy"
    // en base_es
    // en = "A lumberjack, %fullname% \x7bspent most of his days in the woods, chopping down trees | earned his crowns by chopping trees for firewood | was never seen without either axe or wood on his shoulder | always was a quiet man that prefered the serenity of the woods to the company of people | was eyed by many a young woman for his good stature and strong hands | always used to day-dream he was a knight, swinging his axe not against trees but orcs and trolls\x7d. \x7bA large and sturdy man, working outside came easily to him | He loved his collection of axes, having named every single one after a woman he once knew | He worked hard every day, but it was honest work | Alone in the woods he would talk to the trees and have them tell him which ones would give the best wood | Few men could swing an axe like he did, having a tree fall just like he wanted it | With his large and sturdy build he could carry on his back what other people would be crushed by\x7d. \x7bLike most people, he took on the profession of his father. Yet over the years, it dawned on him that he wanted to see more from the world than the same woods every day. After thinking long and hard, he made up his mind to | His life collapsed on him as his beloved wife died in childbirth. With everything taken from him, he became more and more reclusive, and not even the woods could bring him peace anymore. Just wanting to get away, he decided to | Returning from the woods one day, he saw smoke from afar. His village was burning, the people slaughtered or taken. His home destroyed. Full of anger he set off and decided to | Over time, strange creatures began to appear in the woods. One villager after the other disappared, some moved away. After a long night with no sleep, he decided it was time for him to leave as well. With nothing to live off, he was desperate to | Curious to all the villagers, it seemed %name% lost his interest in the woods with time, speaking of going away every more often if he spoke at all. One fateful day, they saw him volunteer to | One fateful day a tree he fell slew a deer. %name% did not want to waste it and so took it home, only to find himself accused of poaching. Before a sentence was cast he decided to leave the village in haste and attempt to\x7d join a travelling mercenary company."
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\manhunter_background.nut
    // en = "Manhunters are used to hunting down people in the rough environment of the south."
    // en base_es
    // context: manhunter_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: "cazador de hombres" por "cazahombres", el término que fija el glosario
        en = "%name% the manhunter stuck with the %companyname% for a long while after you left it. You haven't gotten much word other than %name%'s found far more income in the world of sellswords than that of hunting down the indebted."
        es = "%name% siguió con %companyname% durante mucho tiempo después de que tú la dejaras. No has recibido muchas noticias, salvo que %name% ha encontrado muchos más ingresos en el mundo de los mercenarios que en el de la caza de endeudados."
    }
    // context: manhunter_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "Upset with how time in the company of the %companyname% has gone, %name% the manhunter deserted and returned south. It's hard to say what became of the slaver, but the business of tracking and hunting human prey carries endless dangers. The only news you haveis ancillary to the vocation: that of numerous indebted uprisings with many manhunters being buried alive or fed to a variety of desert-borne creatures."
        es = "A disgusto con cómo le había ido en %companyname%, %name% desertó y volvió al sur. Es difícil saber qué fue de quien comerciaba con esclavos, pero el negocio de rastrear y cazar presas humanas entraña peligros sin fin. Las únicas noticias que te llegan tocan el oficio solo de refilón: hablan de numerosos levantamientos de endeudados en los que muchos cazahombres fueron enterrados vivos o arrojados como alimento a toda clase de criaturas del desierto."
    }
    // en = "the Manhunter"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Mancatcher"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Ruthless"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Bounty Hunter"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Brutal"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Merciless"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Catcher"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Heartless"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Swine"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Slaver"
    // en base_es
    // context: manhunter_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: "cazador(es) de hombres" por "cazahombres", el término que fija el glosario (la misma 1.0 alterna ambos); "vizires" por "visires"; "el temor" omite el "sweat" del inglés (el sudor del miedo)
        en = "{The large population of slaves, prisoners, criminals, and indebted servants in the south has produced an economy of sellers, buyers, and, given the flighty nature of the product, hunters. | Southern city states must have enormous reserves of labor to fuel their desert-borne economies. While many are born into working tirelessly for Viziers, some must be coerced into a life of servitude. | The deserts so sparse in natural resources, it is often an ample supply of captured criminals and indebted souls which bolsters the southern economy. And the business of hunting down these eventual servants is a prosperous one. | Southern Viziers are so fearful of rebellions that an entire market of Manhunters has emerged to nip them in the bud.} {%name% entered manhunting with a vengeful attitude: their entire family was massacred in a slave uprising. | %name% was once an ordinary caravan guard but turned to manhunting nomads who kept trying to ambush their convoys. Finding more profit in the human trade, %name%'s stuck with it ever since. | %name% is a manhunter with a good nose for tracking criminals, deserters, prisoners of war, and more. You sometimes wonder if %name%'s got a keen sense of smell for fearful sweat. | Once a big game hunter, %name% grew fond of chasing the greatest game of all: man. %name% is an expert tracker with a nose for sniffing out desperation.} {For %name%, the opportunity of working for a mercenary band simply brings in more consistent work than waiting around for some pressed criminal to get antsy about his chains. | %name% is a rugged, shady individual and it is quite possibly just as flighty as those being hunted. | Hunters like %name% carry traits and skills that would be useful in a mercenary band, but to some their past may be an ever present slight. Not all manhunters are seen in good light. | Capturing humans for the purpose of labor is frowned upon by many and catching those seeking their freedom equally so. Manhunters like %name% certainly have useful skills, but may rub some the wrong way. | To no surprise, many see slavers like %name% as opportunistic slugs. If %name% can make it with the company, it may take time to change the minds of some about the past.}"
        es = "{La gran población de esclavos, prisioneros, criminales y sirvientes endeudados del sur ha dado lugar a una economía de vendedores, compradores y, dada la naturaleza escurridiza del producto, cazadores. | Las ciudades-estado del sur necesitan enormes reservas de mano de obra para alimentar sus economías nacidas del desierto. Aunque muchos nacen para trabajar sin descanso para los visires, a otros hay que obligarlos a una vida de servidumbre. | Con unos desiertos tan pobres en recursos naturales, suele ser un amplio suministro de criminales capturados y almas endeudadas lo que sostiene la economía del sur. Y el negocio de dar caza a estos futuros sirvientes es próspero. | Los visires del sur temen tanto las rebeliones que ha surgido todo un mercado de cazahombres para cortarlas de raíz.} {%name% se metió en la caza de hombres con ánimo de venganza: toda su familia fue masacrada en un levantamiento de esclavos. | %name% se ganaba la vida protegiendo caravanas, pero se dedicó a cazar a los nómadas que no dejaban de intentar emboscar sus convoyes. Al encontrar más beneficios en el comercio de personas, %name% se ha quedado en él desde entonces. | %name% es cazahombres y tiene buen olfato para rastrear criminales, desertores, prisioneros de guerra y más. A veces te preguntas si %name% tiene un olfato especial para el sudor del miedo. | Tras años cazando presas mayores, %name% le tomó el gusto a perseguir la mayor presa de todas: el hombre. %name% rastrea como nadie y tiene olfato para husmear la desesperación.} {Para %name%, la oportunidad de trabajar para una banda de mercenarios simplemente ofrece un trabajo más constante que esperar a que algún criminal desesperado se ponga nervioso con sus cadenas. | %name% es una persona ruda y turbia, y es muy posible que se escabulla con la misma facilidad que sus presas. | Cazadores como %name% tienen rasgos y habilidades que serían útiles en una banda de mercenarios, pero para algunos su pasado puede ser una ofensa siempre presente. No todos ven con buenos ojos a los cazahombres. | Muchos ven con malos ojos capturar personas para hacerlas trabajar, y lo mismo pasa con atrapar a quienes buscan su libertad. Los cazahombres como %name% tienen, sin duda, habilidades útiles, pero pueden caerle mal a más de uno. | Como era de esperar, muchos consideran a los esclavistas como %name% unas babosas oportunistas. Si %name% logra hacerse un sitio en la compañía, puede llevar tiempo que algunos cambien de opinión sobre su pasado.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\mason_background.nut
    // en = "Mason"
    // en base_es
    // en = "A good mason is used to physical labor and studying to improve his craft."
    // en base_es
    // en = "Masonry has its own call, notably a call perfectly cut stones and impossible towers that defy the eye's ability to even shape them against the skies. %name% the mason returned to his old trade and, with all the money he'd made with the %companyname%, he started a reputable business renowned for its ability to construct stone rooms that held the heat during winters and the cool during summers."
    // en base_es
    // en = "The %companyname% continued to suffer losses long after you'd left. More and more of the brothers departed the company, a good lot of them returning to old trades. %name% the mason was no different. Sadly, all the time spent fighting had destroyed any steadiness he had left. With hands that wouldn't stop shaking, he could no longer shape stones like he used to. Last you heard, he was hauling rocks as a daytaler instead of shaping them as a mason."
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bGrowing up in %townname%, %name% spent his youth poring over construction books with earnest. | Raised by a guild of tradesmen, %name%'s swift ascent through the field of masonry was of little surprise. | A student of %randomtown%'s esteemed college, %name% graduated with great expectations, and even greater things yet to build. | With a bricklayer for a father, %name%'s entrance into masonry was but the smallest of steps. | Amazed by the regal structures of church and state, %name% fell in love with masonry. | When %randomtown% was in dire need of defensive walls, %name% took to masonry like a very fortunately-timed natural.\x7d \x7bUnfortunately, his time as a mason was short-lived. A church he built collapsed and out of its ruins rose a murderous mob looking for revenge. | Five buildings built, five buildings knocked down. Endless wars made the man's vocation an impossible one. | Betrayed by a fellow architect, the mason bricked his rival inside the walls of his next project. It wasn't long until people started asking questions. | While roofing, the man took a misstep and fell. The ensuing injuries forced him out of his field. | But when a lord demanded he build a horrific dungeon, the mason refused. Now he is banished from ever laying a brick again. | A misplaced blueprint had the mason building the temple of the Davkulians and not the temple of the Davkuliads. Now he says the gods themselves are after him.\x7d \x7bPutting down his hammer and chisel for a hammer and sharpened chisel called a sword, %name% now works in the field of mercenaries. | One day, a poster for a mercenary troop caught his eye. Much like his old buildings, the rest is history. | Years of masonry made the man fit for a life of blood and mud. | %name% finds a flaw in every building he passes. Hopefully he can tune that annoying analysis to the battlefield.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\messenger_background.nut
    // en = "Messenger"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Messengers are used to long and tiring travels."
    // en base_es
    // context: messenger_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: "la ocasión ocasional" es redundante (por "de vez en cuando la ocasión"); falta la exclamación final del inglés
        en = "The oddity of having %name% the messenger in your band did not seem so strange after %they% showed %themselves% to be a killer sellsword. As far as you know, %they%'s still with the company, preferring the march of a mercenary to that of a messenger. You don't blame %them%: an errand %child% must bend the knee to every nobleman %they% comes across, but in the company of sellswords %they%'ll no doubt get the occasional chance to kill one of them bastards. Not a hard trade off to accept!"
        es = "Tener a %name%, %art% mensajer%o%, en tu banda dejó de parecer tan raro cuando demostró ser %un% mercenari%o% letal. Por lo que sabes, sigue en la compañía y prefiere la marcha de un mercenario a la de un mensajero. No se lo reprochas: %un% chic%o% de los recados tiene que hincar la rodilla ante cada noble con el que se cruza, pero en una compañía de mercenarios sin duda tendrá de vez en cuando la ocasión de matar a alguno de esos bastardos. ¡No es un trato difícil de aceptar!"
    }
    // context: messenger_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "%name% the messenger departed the %companyname% and returned to being an errand %child% for the letters of lieges. You tried to find out where the %person% had gone to and eventually tracked %them% down - or what was left of %them%. Unfortunately, 'don't shoot the messenger' is not an adage well followed in these fractured lands."
        es = "%name%, %art% mensajer%o%, dejó %companyname% y volvió a ser %un% chic%o% de los recados al servicio de las cartas de los señores. Intentaste averiguar adónde había ido y al final diste con %el%, o con lo que quedaba de %el%. Por desgracia, 'no mates al mensajero' no es un dicho que se respete mucho en estas tierras fracturadas."
    }
    // en = "the Messenger"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Courier"
    // en base_es
    // context: messenger_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{Some people are so important that they require others to carry their words. %name% is such a %person% - the latter, that is. | %name%'s shoulders are yoked with bags of mail, the receivers almost certainly dead on arrival. | To escape a life of servitude, %name% took up the vocation of a messenger. | With so many hurrying to find out the status of relatives, %name% has found ample work as a messenger. | %name% once traveled the land as a modest messenger. | The %child% of a long line of messengers, %name% took messages across the land for royalty and laymen alike. | Picking up a dead messenger's bags, %name% soon found %themselves% in the role of a would-be messenger. | Once a refugee, %name% figured %they% might as well deliver letters if %they% was already wandering the land.} {But making the rounds gets boring. The mail%person% seeks a new field of work. | Carrying love letters, the would-be adventurer wondered what the hell %they% was doing. | Claiming to be a budding hero, %name% now believes the task of delivering mail is beneath %them%. | Rain or sunshine, sure, snow or sleet, sure, but all out war? Maybe another time. | But after opening a letter that would ruin a goodhearted noble, the messenger decided to leave %their% post. | When robbers made %their% life hell, %name% figured %they%'d be better off traveling in the company of armed men. | After sleeping with a mayor's daughter, the messenger had a small army on %their% heels. %They% figured %they%'d best slip into a different outfit for %their% own safety.} {%name% has spent years memorizing messages. Now %they%'ll have to remember keeping the shield wall as arrows rain down on it. | Ironically, %name% has never written anything in %their% life. | Rolling up %their% sleeves, %name% boasts %they% has one last message to give the world. Everybody look out. | Perhaps %their% joining mercenaries suggests that, indeed, the pen is not mightier than a sword. | %name% has a tendency to repeat everything said to %them%. Old messenger habits die hard. | Ironically, the well-traveled messenger has probably seen more horrors on the road than most of the men in the outfit. | Few, if any, of %name%'s skills make %them% ready for combat. But %they% does have some sturdy legs, hopefully just not for running away.}"
        es = "{Hay gente tan importante que necesita que otros lleven sus palabras. %name% es una de esas personas; de las que las llevan, claro. | Los hombros de %name% cargan con sacas de correo cuyos destinatarios, casi con seguridad, estarán muertos cuando lleguen. | Para escapar de una vida de servidumbre, %name% abrazó el oficio de mensajero. | Con tanta gente ansiosa por saber de sus parientes, %name% ha encontrado trabajo de sobra como mensajer%o%. | %name% recorrió en su día estas tierras como humilde mensajer%o%. | Hij%o% de un largo linaje de mensajeros, %name% llevó mensajes por todo el país tanto para la realeza como para la gente llana. | Tras recoger las sacas de un mensajero muerto, %name% pronto se vio haciendo de mensajer%o% improvisad%o%. | Antes refugiad%o%, %name% pensó que, ya que vagaba por estas tierras, bien podía repartir cartas.} {Pero hacer siempre la misma ronda aburre. Ahora quien repartía el correo busca un nuevo oficio. | Mientras llevaba cartas de amor, %ese% aspirante a aventurer%o% se preguntaba qué demonios estaba haciendo. | Convencid%o% de tener madera de héroe, %name% cree ahora que repartir el correo no está a su altura. | Con lluvia o con sol, claro; con nieve o aguanieve, también. ¿Pero en plena guerra? Quizá en otra ocasión. | Pero tras abrir una carta que arruinaría a un noble de buen corazón, %art% mensajer%o% decidió abandonar su puesto. | Cuando los ladrones le hicieron la vida imposible, %name% pensó que estaría mejor viajando en compañía de hombres armados. | Tras acostarse con la hija de un alcalde, %art% mensajer%o% tenía un pequeño ejército pisándole los talones. Pensó que, por su propia seguridad, lo mejor era cambiar de ropaje y de grupo.} {%name% se ha pasado años memorizando mensajes. Ahora tendrá que acordarse de mantener el muro de escudos mientras le llueven flechas encima. | Irónicamente, %name% no ha escrito nada en su vida. | Arremangándose, %name% presume de tener un último mensaje que darle al mundo. Todo el mundo, cuidado. | Quizá que se haya unido a unos mercenarios demuestre que, en efecto, la pluma no es más poderosa que la espada. | %name% tiende a repetir todo lo que se le dice. Las viejas costumbres de mensajero son difíciles de perder. | Irónicamente, %ese% mensajer%o% tan viajad%o% probablemente haya visto más horrores en los caminos que la mayoría de los hombres del grupo. | Pocas habilidades de %name%, si es que hay alguna, %lo% preparan para el combate. Pero sí tiene unas piernas robustas; esperemos que no las use para huir.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\militia_background.nut
    // en = "Anyone that's been in the militia will have received at least some basic training in matters of combat."
    // en base_es
    // context: militia_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "A former militia recruit such as %name% eventually left the %companyname%. Traveling the lands, visiting villages and helping them establish credible militias with which to defend themselves. Finding success in an increasingly dangerous world, %name% eventually came to be a known name, called upon as a sort of 'fixer' to come and ensure these villages would remain safe. Last you heard, %name% had purchased a plot of land and was raising a family far from the strife of the world."
        es = "Con el tiempo, %name%, que venía de las filas de la milicia, dejó %companyname%. Recorrió estas tierras visitando aldeas y ayudándolas a formar milicias capaces con las que defenderse. Con éxito en un mundo cada vez más peligroso, %name% acabó siendo un nombre conocido, al que recurrían como una especie de 'apagafuegos' para asegurarse de que esas aldeas siguieran a salvo. Lo último que supiste es que %name% había comprado un terreno y estaba criando una familia lejos de las luchas del mundo."
    }
    // context: militia_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        // corrige base: añade una frase que el inglés no tiene ("Sin embargo, gracias a su sacrificio, la aldea se salvó.") y el adjetivo "heroico", además mal acentuado ("heróico"); "playfighting" es jugar a pelear, no solo jugar; "mataba a través de" es un calco
        en = "%name% left the collapsing company and returned to the village. Back in the militia, it wasn't long until {greenskins | raiders} attacked and the militia was called to action. It's said that %name% stood tall, rallying the defense while slaying through countless enemies before succumbing to mortal wounds. When you visited the village, you found children playfighting beneath a statue made in the %name%'s image."
        es = "%name% dejó la compañía en pleno derrumbe y regresó a la aldea. De vuelta en la milicia, no pasó mucho tiempo antes de que {pieles verdes | saqueadores} atacaran y se llamara a la milicia a la acción. Se dice que %name% se mantuvo firme, alentando la defensa mientras se abría paso entre incontables enemigos, hasta sucumbir a heridas mortales. Cuando visitaste la aldea, encontraste niños jugando a pelear al pie de una estatua hecha a imagen de %name%."
    }
    // context: militia_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{A militia recruit like %name% is only raised in times of need. | Broke and without work, %name% joined the local militia. | Caught stealing an apple, %name% was pressed into the militia as a form of punishment. | Although a member of the peasantry, %name% was always willing to join the militia and protect the homestead. | War is a hungry beast - militia conscripts like %name% are what feed it.} {While %name% got proper training, there was rarely enough food to go around for the 'second-rate soldiers'. | %name% fought just as hard as the professionals, but was unable to garner any sort of respect for the work. | Being the bottom rung of soldiering, quickly makes it clear that your life is expendable. | %name%'s weapons were rusted and the armor nonexistent. Unfortunately, enemies were not so kindly under-equipped.} {After a year of traipsing around with shoddy gear, %name% decided to look for something a bit more welcoming: sellswords. | Years in an outfit where %name% couldn't depend on the solider beside, drove %name% to find something better. Perhaps not the best soldier you've ever seen, but earnest. | When the local militia was disbanded, %name% returned home to find the town had been burned to the ground. One foot already in the door, it only made sense to join one of the numerous mercenary bands roaming the land. | %name%'s modest military garb belies one who has seen their fair share of training and combat.}"
        es = "{A reclutas de la milicia como %name% solo se les llama en tiempos de necesidad. | Sin blanca y sin trabajo, %name% se unió a la milicia local. | %name% acabó en la milicia a la fuerza, como castigo por robar una manzana. | Aunque procede del campesinado, %name% siempre tuvo voluntad de unirse a la milicia y proteger su hogar. | La guerra es una bestia hambrienta, y reclutas de la milicia como %name% son lo que la alimenta.} {Aunque %name% recibió un entrenamiento adecuado, rara vez había comida suficiente para todos los 'soldados de segunda'. | %name% luchó con tanto empeño como los profesionales, pero nunca consiguió que se le respetara por ello. | Ser el último escalón de la tropa deja claro enseguida que tu vida es prescindible. | Las armas de %name% estaban oxidadas y la armadura brillaba por su ausencia. Por desgracia, los enemigos no tenían la amabilidad de ir igual de mal equipados.} {Tras un año de dar tumbos con un equipo de pacotilla, %name% decidió buscar algo un poco más acogedor: los mercenarios. | Años en una tropa donde %name% no podía fiarse del soldado de al lado empujaron a %name% a buscar algo mejor. Quizá no sea lo mejor que has visto en el campo de batalla, pero pone empeño. | Cuando la milicia local se disolvió, %name% volvió a casa y encontró el pueblo reducido a cenizas. Con un pie ya en el oficio, lo lógico era unirse a una de las numerosas bandas de mercenarios que recorren estas tierras. | El modesto atuendo militar de %name% oculta a alguien que ha tenido su buena ración de entrenamiento y combate.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\miller_background.nut
    // en = "A miller is used to physical labor."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% the once-miller stayed with the %companyname% for a time, collecting enough crowns to start his own bakery. Last you heard, his sword-shaped desserts have been a hit with the nobility and he makes more money selling to them than he ever did with the company."
    // en base_es
    // en = "As the %companyname% fell on hard times, %name% the miller saw fit to go ahead and leave while he could still walk. He helped a nobleman test out a new way of grinding grains with mules and waterwheels working in tandem. Unfortunately, by 'helping' he managed to fall into the contraption and was brutally crushed to death."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Miller"
    // en base_es
    // context: miller_background.o.setGender.m.Name
    {
        en = "Baker"
        es = "Panadero"
    }
    // context: miller_background.o.setGender.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "A baker is used to working the oven and kneading bread."
        es = "Una panadera está acostumbrada a trabajar el horno y a amasar pan."
    }
    // context: miller_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: "vendiéndolos a ellos" → "vendiéndoles a ellos": "them" es la nobleza, complemento indirecto, no los postres.
        en = "%name% the once-miller stayed with the %companyname% for a time, collecting enough crowns to start his own bakery. Last you heard, her  sword-shaped desserts have been a hit with the nobility and she makes more money selling to them than she ever did with the company."
        es = "%name%, la antigua molinera, se quedó con %companyname% durante un tiempo, reuniendo suficientes coronas para abrir su propia panadería. Lo último que supiste es que sus postres en forma de espada han sido un éxito entre la nobleza y gana más dinero vendiéndoles a ellos que el que jamás ganó con la compañía."
    }
    // context: miller_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "As the %companyname% fell on hard times, %name% the miller saw fit to go ahead and leave while she could still walk. She helped a nobleman test out a new way of grinding grains with mules and waterwheels working in tandem. Unfortunately, by 'helping' she managed to fall into the contraption and was brutally crushed to death."
        es = "A medida que %companyname% pasaba por tiempos difíciles, %name%, la molinera, consideró apropiado marcharse mientras aún podía caminar. Ayudó a un noble a probar una nueva forma de moler grano con mulas y ruedas hidráulicas trabajando en tándem. Desafortunadamente, al 'ayudar', logró caer en la maquinaria y murió brutalmente aplastada."
    }
    // context: miller_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: "%name% no le importaba" → "a %name% no le importaba" (falta la preposición).
        // corrige base: "un granizo de golpes" es calco de "hail of blows" → "una lluvia de golpes".
        // corrige base: "capítan mercenario" (errata) traduce "mercenary recruiter" → "reclutador de mercenarios".
        en = "{The life as a miller had always been lacking something for %name%, yet the hard work kept her from making any big plans. | Continuing the family tradition, %name% learned the millers trade from her father. | Although just a simple miller, %name% always dreamed about wandering out into the world and bring home tales and pockets full of crowns. | Being a simple lass, %name% did not mind working hard in the mill every day. | %name% always was more ambitious than other people. While her brother was content with running their family's mill, she could not shake the feeling that she was destined for more.} {One night he was awoken by a loud thunderstorm. Rushing outside, %name% realised that her mill had been ignited by a lightning strike. | When she caught her promised husband in bed with another woman, she was furious, battering both of them with a hail of blows. Her fists were bruised, people were shouting at her, but the only thing she felt was emptyness where once was her heart. As if in a dream she quickly packed her belongings and set out, never to return. | When her husband was found dead, torn apart by wild beasts in the woods, she did not say a word. Silently she packed her belongings and set out into the world, to start a new life somewhere far away. | After hearing wild tales from a hedge knight in the tavern of %townname%, her imagination was running wild with all the possibilities out there in the world waiting for her. | A drought meant business was running slow for her. When %name% was not able to pay his debts any more her life was threatened by ruthless money collectors. She had to disappear.} {Remembering her cousin, %randomname%, who has made a decent living in the mercenary business, %name% decided to do the same. | While looking for opportunities she met a mercenary recruiter who promised her fame and fortune. | Although she does not know the next thing about fighting, %name% is eager to sign up with a mercenary company hooked by the promise of adventure. | Whether by lack of alternatives or by her free will, %name% stands before you now, ready to swear fealty.}"
        es = "{En su vida como molinera, a %name% siempre le había faltado algo, pero el duro trabajo le impedía hacer grandes planes. | Continuando la tradición familiar, %name% aprendió de su padre el oficio de molinera. | Aunque solo era una simple molinera, %name% siempre soñaba con recorrer el mundo y volver a casa con historias y los bolsillos llenos de coronas. | Siendo una muchacha sencilla, a %name% no le importaba trabajar duro en el molino todos los días. | %name% siempre fue más ambiciosa que los demás. Mientras su hermano se contentaba con dirigir el molino familiar, ella no podía sacudirse la sensación de que estaba destinada a algo más.} {Una noche la despertó una fuerte tormenta eléctrica. Al salir corriendo, %name% se dio cuenta de que un rayo había prendido fuego a su molino. | Cuando descubrió a su prometido en la cama con otra mujer, se enfureció y les descargó a ambos una lluvia de golpes. Tenía los puños magullados y la gente le gritaba, pero lo único que sentía era el vacío donde antes estaba su corazón. Como en un sueño, recogió rápidamente sus pertenencias y partió para no volver jamás. | Cuando encontraron muerto a su esposo, despedazado por bestias salvajes en el bosque, no dijo una palabra. En silencio, recogió sus pertenencias y partió hacia el mundo, para empezar una nueva vida en algún lugar lejano. | Después de escuchar historias increíbles de un caballero errante en la taberna de %townname%, su imaginación se desbocó con todas las posibilidades que el mundo le tenía reservadas. | Una sequía hizo que su negocio fuera cada vez peor. Cuando %name% ya no pudo pagar sus deudas, unos implacables cobradores amenazaron su vida. Tuvo que desaparecer.} {Recordando a su primo, %randomname%, que se ha ganado bien la vida en el negocio de los mercenarios, %name% decidió hacer lo mismo. | Mientras buscaba oportunidades, conoció a un reclutador de mercenarios que le prometió fama y fortuna. | Aunque no sabe lo más mínimo de pelear, %name% está ansiosa por unirse a una compañía de mercenarios, atraída por la promesa de aventura. | Ya sea por falta de alternativas o por su libre albedrío, %name% está frente a ti ahora, lista para prestar juramento de lealtad.}"
    }
    // en = "\x7bThe life as a miller had always been lacking something for %name%, yet the hard work kept him from making any big plans. | Continuing the family tradition, %name% learned the millers trade from his father. | Although just a simple miller, %name% always dreamed about wandering out into the world and bring home tales and pockets full of crowns. | Being a simple fellow, %name% did not mind working hard in the mill every day. | %name% always was more ambitious than other people. While his brother was content with running their family's mill, he could not shake the feeling that he was destined for more.\x7d \x7bOne night he was awoken by a loud thunderstorm. Rushing outside, %name% realised that his mill had been ignited by a lightning strike. | When he caught his promised wife in bed with another man, he was furious, battering both of them with a hail of blows. His fists were bruised, people were shouting at him, but the only thing he felt was emptyness where once was his heart. As if in a dream he quickly packed his belongings and set out, never to return. | When his young and lovely wife was found dead, torn apart by wild beasts in the woods, he did not say a word. Silently he packed his belongings and set out into the world, to start a new life somewhere far away. | After hearing wild tales from a hedge knight in the tavern of %townname%, his imagination was running wild with all the possibilities out there in the world waiting for him. | A drought meant business was running slow for him. When %name% was not able to pay his debts any more his life was threatened by ruthless money collectors. He had to disappear.\x7d \x7bRemembering his cousin, %randomname%, who has made a decent living in the mercenary business, %name% decided to do the same. | While looking for opportunities he met a mercenary recruiter who promised him fame and fortune. | Although he does not know the next thing about fighting, %name% is eager to sign up with a mercenary company hooked by the promise of adventure. | Whether by lack of alternatives or by his free will, %name% stands before you now, ready to swear fealty.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\miner_background.nut
    // en = "A miner will be used to physical labor, but breathing in the dusty air of the mines may have taken a toll on his health over the years."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% the miner never did return to the mines, thankfully. If there's one life that could be worse than that of fighting for a living, it very well may be digging into mountains for a living! Apparently, the miner built a home by the sea, spending the rest of his days peacefully fishing for dinner and enjoying sunrises or some such sappy shite."
    // en base_es
    // en = "If there's one life that's more rough than that of being a sellsword, it is that of being a miner. Sadly, %name% returned to that life, going back into the mines to dig out metals and ores to fill some rich man's pockets. A recent earthquake collapsed many such mines. You're not sure if the ol' brother survived, but it's looking pretty grim."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Miner"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Crawler"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Earthside"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bTo support a fatherless family, %name% went into the mines at a very young age. | An orphan, the only work %name% could find was working the mines of the earth. | Mining is tough work, the sort of job men like %name% flock to. | Even though his father died in the mines, %name% felt compelled to work in them himself, like most men do where he grew up. | %name% worked in the mines as a family tradition spanning many generations. | Whenever wars start up, miners like %name% are more needed than ever, lest an army wishes to go without steel to wield. | A hardhelm and a pickaxe, the tools %name% has been taking deep into the earth for years.\x7d \x7bBut, as always, a mine doesn't last forever, and the miner barely escaped the last collapse. | Sadly, he proved to be the only survivor of a shaft collapse, and there's no way he's digging back in there by himself. | After a tragic mine collapse, the sight of dozens of widows moved the man to think of a different field of work. | Surviving yet another collapse, the man's wife demanded he seek a new line of work no matter what it was. | Bending over and scuttling about in the dark gets old, though, and so the man sought a different vocation. | Working in environments far too dark, the man accidentally killed a coworker. The tragedy pushed him from the field. | After his own son lost his life in the mines, the man left the job forever. | But suffering from relentless coughs, the man felt maybe a career in fresh air would better serve him.\x7d \x7b%name% has the stocky frame of a miner. Unfortunately, he has the lungs of one, too. | He's tough alright, but %name%'s wheezing sounds like rusted blades grinding together.  | You have to wonder if %name%'s lungs have enough metal dust in them to fashion a blade or two. | %name%'s breath could probably ink a chunk of coal. | %name% spent years earning keep for a company store. Now he wants to earn some real coin. | %name% looks forward to pocketing some of that gold he spent years plucking out of the earth. | Annoyingly, %name% points at half your gear - the metal stuff, mostly - and reminds everyone who's responsible for it being there. | %name% has almost catlike vision in the dark. He would have made for a good assassin if it weren't for his damned wheezing. | %name% has cheated death a few times, so why not try it a few times more as mercenary? | %name%'s already had the earth itself out for his head so a few things above the soil don't scare him much. | If darkness truly is death's ambassador, %name%'s already been talking to it for years. | Stupidly brave souls like %name% can definitely find a good register in an outfit such as this. | %name% proudly boasts that, once upon a time, he could play cards in the dark. You don't doubt it. | If %name% can swing a sword as well as a pickaxe, then all is well.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\minstrel_background.nut
    // en = "A good minstrel will sing a saga to inspire the men, play the flute to calm them, or entertain them with poetry around the camp fire. A lute is not a weapon, however, and minstrels are often not used to physical labor or bloodshed."
    // en base_es
    // en = "Ah, %name%. What an addition to the %companyname%! The minstrel not only became an excellent fighter, but was crucial in keeping the men's spirits high in the toughest of times. A poet and actor at heart, he eventually retired from the company and started up a theater company. He current performs plays for both the nobility and laymen. The minstrel does not yet realize it, but his playful wit and sharp commentary are slowly bringing the classes together."
    // en base_es
    // en = "Never a fighter at heart, %name% the minstrel quickly left the declining %companyname%. He and a group of musicians and jesters spend their evenings performing for drunken noblemen. You managed to see one of these performances for yourself. %name% spent much of the time being berated by the inebriated and having half-eaten chicken bones thrown at him. One of the nobles even thought it'd be funny to set a dog loose on one of the jesters. You could see the minstrel's dreams dying in his eyes, but the show went on."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Minstrel"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Skjald"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Poet"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Songbird"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Troubadour"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Chorine"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Lover"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Bard"
    // en base_es
    // context: minstrel_background.o.setGender.m.Name
    {
        en = "Troubadour"
        es = "Trovador"
    }
    // context: minstrel_background.o.setGender.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "A good troubadour will give a speech to inspire the company, act out a scene to calm them, or entertain them with dancing around the camp fire. The actors tumbles and moves may be repurposed for the real battle, if their nerve holds steady"
        es = "Una buena trovadora dará un discurso para inspirar a la compañía, representará una escena para calmarla o la entretendrá bailando alrededor de la hoguera del campamento. Las volteretas y los movimientos de una actriz pueden aprovecharse en la batalla de verdad, si sus nervios se mantienen firmes"
    }
    // context: minstrel_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "Ah, %name%. What an addition to the %companyname%! The minstrel not only became an excellent fighter, but was crucial in keeping the men's spirits high in the toughest of times. A poet and actor at heart, she eventually retired from the company and started up a theater company. She currently performs plays for both the nobility and laymen. The minstrel does not yet realize it, but her playful wit and sharp commentary are slowly bringing the classes together."
        es = "¡Ah, %name%! ¡Qué incorporación a %companyname%! La juglaresa no solo se convirtió en una excelente luchadora, sino que fue crucial para mantener alto el ánimo de los hombres en los momentos más difíciles. Poeta y actriz de corazón, acabó retirándose de la compañía y fundó una compañía de teatro. Actualmente representa obras tanto para la nobleza como para el pueblo llano. La juglaresa aún no se da cuenta, pero su ingenio juguetón y sus agudos comentarios están acercando poco a poco a las clases sociales."
    }
    // context: minstrel_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        // corrige base: falta "declining": %name% deja la compañía cuando está en declive.
        en = "Never a fighter at heart, %name% the minstrel quickly left the declining %companyname%. She and a group of musicians and jesters spend their evenings performing for drunken noblemen. You managed to see one of these performances for yourself. %name% spent much of the time being berated by the inebriated and having half-eaten chicken bones thrown at her. One of the nobles even thought it'd be funny to set a dog loose on one of the jesters. You could see the minstrel's dreams dying in her eyes, but the show went on."
        es = "Como nunca fue una luchadora de corazón, %name%, la juglaresa, abandonó rápidamente %companyname%, que estaba en declive. Ella y un grupo de músicos y bufones pasan las noches actuando para nobles borrachos. Lograste ver una de esas actuaciones por ti mismo. %name% pasó gran parte del tiempo soportando los insultos de los ebrios y esquivando los huesos de pollo a medio comer que le lanzaban. Uno de los nobles incluso pensó que sería gracioso soltar un perro contra uno de los bufones. Podías ver los sueños de la juglaresa muriendo en sus ojos, pero el espectáculo continuó."
    }
    // context: minstrel_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "'{I can swing a sword and cleave an axe, | One might ask of me a task, | Right with god, but in the left a flask,} {and I say, 'You question a woman who wears no mask?'. | and so I have to move quick, but not quite fast.} {Stare down the stuffed bears I did, | Into my frayed pantaloons I bid, | Along the muddy roads my boots skid,} {and so of many things I am rid. | truth! My shameful talent is to - ferociously! - knit.} {So take me along your adventure, | Bring me with your men who clatter and clamber, | Hand me your shield and that thing shaped like a member,} {and let us go and bid fear a farewell to remember! | and let's - oh, ow! I have a splinter! | and may we come, one and all, to a healthy next-winter!}'. {The woman speaks gibberish. | It rhymes!}"
        es = "'{Sé blandir la espada y el hacha descargar, | Alguien una tarea me podría encargar, | En paz con dios, y en la izquierda un frasco que apurar,} {y digo: '¿A una mujer sin máscara pretendes interrogar?'. | y por eso he de ir ligera, pero sin acelerar.} {A osos disecados con la mirada he vencido, | En mis raídos calzones me he metido, | Por caminos de barro mis botas se han escurrido,} {y así de muchas cosas me he desprendido. | ¡lo juro! Mi vergonzoso talento es el - ¡feroz! - tejido.} {Así que llévame en tu aventura, | Llévame con tus hombres de ruidosa armadura, | Dame tu escudo y esa cosa de fálica hechura,} {¡y vamos a darle al miedo un adiós de inolvidable factura! | y vamos a - ¡ay, uy! ¡Una astilla en la cintura! | ¡y que todos, uno a uno, lleguemos al invierno con salud y holgura!}'. {La mujer dice disparates. | ¡Rima!}"
    }
    // context: minstrel_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{I can swing a sword and cleave an axe, | One might ask of me a task, | Right with god, but in the left a flask,} {and I say, 'You question a man who wears no mask?'. | and so I have to move quick, but not quite fast.} {Stare down the stuffed bears I did, | Into my frayed pantaloons I bid, | Along the muddy roads my boots skid,} {and so of many things I am rid. | truth! My shameful talent is to - ferociously! - knit.} {So take me along your adventure, | Bring me with your men who clatter and clamber, | Hand me your shield and that thing shaped like my member,} {and let us go and bid fear a farewell to remember! | and let's - oh, ow! I have a splinter! | and may we come, one and all, to a healthy next-winter!}. {The man speaks gibberish. | It rhymes!}"
        es = "{Sé blandir la espada y el hacha descargar, | Alguien una tarea me podría encargar, | En paz con dios, y en la izquierda un frasco que apurar,} {y digo: '¿A un hombre sin máscara pretendes interrogar?'. | y por eso he de ir ligero, pero sin acelerar.} {A osos disecados con la mirada he vencido, | En mis raídos calzones me he metido, | Por caminos de barro mis botas se han escurrido,} {y así de muchas cosas me he desprendido. | ¡lo juro! Mi vergonzoso talento es el - ¡feroz! - tejido.} {Así que llévame en tu aventura, | Llévame con tus hombres de ruidosa armadura, | Dame tu escudo y esa cosa que de mi miembro tiene la hechura,} {¡y vamos a darle al miedo un adiós de inolvidable factura! | y vamos a - ¡ay, uy! ¡Una astilla en la cintura! | ¡y que todos, uno a uno, lleguemos al invierno con salud y holgura!}. {El hombre dice disparates. | ¡Rima!}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\monk_background.nut
    // en = "Monks tend to have a high resolve in what they do, but are not used to hard physical labor or warfare."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% the monk retired back into calmer spiritual duties. He is currently out in a mountain monastery, enjoying the quiet while reflecting on his time in the mercenary company. The other monks hate him for fighting and killing, but he's penning a world-changing tome on the balance between peace and violence."
    // en base_es
    // en = "After having a spiritual breakdown, %name% retired from fighting and found home in a monastery. All his fellow brothers and abbots ostracized him for taking part in such a violent venture. Word has it he was eventually exiled when a sexton caught him stealing an offertory."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Pious"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Scholar"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Preacher"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Devoted"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Quiet"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Calm"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Monk"
    // en base_es
    // context: monk_background.o.setGender.m.Name
    {
        en = "Nun"
        es = "Monja"
    }
    // context: monk_background.o.setGender.m.Titles.push()
    {
        en = "the Nun"
        es = "la Monja"
    }
    // context: monk_background.o.setGender.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "Nuns tend to have a high resolve in what they do, but are not used to hard physical labor or warfare."
        es = "Las monjas suelen tener una gran resolución en lo que hacen, pero no están acostumbradas al trabajo físico duro ni a la guerra."
    }
    // context: monk_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "%name% the nun retired back into calmer spiritual duties. She is currently out in a mountain convent, enjoying the quiet while reflecting on her time in the mercenary company. The other nuns hate her for fighting and killing, but she's penning a world-changing tome on the balance between peace and violence."
        es = "%name%, la monja, volvió a retirarse a deberes espirituales más tranquilos. Actualmente vive en un convento de montaña, disfrutando de la calma mientras reflexiona sobre su tiempo en la compañía de mercenarios. Las demás monjas la odian por haber luchado y matado, pero ella está escribiendo sobre el equilibrio entre la paz y la violencia un tomo que cambiará el mundo."
    }
    // context: monk_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        // corrige base: "ostracizaron" no es castellano normativo → "condenaron al ostracismo" o "marginaron".
        en = "After having a spiritual breakdown, %name% retired from fighting and found home in a monastery. All her fellow sisters and abbesses ostracized her for taking part in such a violent venture. Word has it she was eventually exiled when a mother superior caught her stealing an offertory."
        es = "Después de sufrir una crisis espiritual, %name% se retiró de la lucha y encontró refugio en un monasterio. Todas sus hermanas y abadesas la condenaron al ostracismo por participar en una empresa tan violenta. Se rumorea que finalmente fue desterrada cuando una madre superiora la sorprendió robando una ofrenda."
    }
    // context: monk_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: "Abandonado por sus padre en un monasterio" tiene una errata ("sus padre") y cambia el sentido del inglés ("on the steps of a monastery") → "Abandonado en las escaleras de un monasterio".
        // corrige base: "junto con su determinación por llevar su visión a cabo" es un añadido; el inglés dice "almost scary in its determination" → "casi aterrador por su determinación".
        en = "{After raiders murdered her family, %name% retreated into the comforts of religion and became a nun at a nearby convent. | Often traveling away from her church and fellow nuns, %name% spent years preaching to peasantry in remote villages. | %name%, a quiet nun, has spent untold days worshipping the old gods in %townname%'s monastery. | One nun amongst many, %name% used to wander the steepled temples of %randomtown%. | Abandoned on the steps of a convent, %name% grew up in the company of nuns, and soon took to their lifestyle. | Trying to find peace in a land of ruin, %name% became a nun. | Always an unruly child, %name%'s parents handed her over to the local convent where she was quickly pacified as a nun.} {Unfortunately, her abbess's liking for youth and fleshen things led to a terrible scandal. %name% fled to preserve her life and her faith. | But her faith was irreversibly damaged as a hellacious attack by raiders left men castrated, women raped, and children skewered on spits. | Though a believer in the old gods, the nun could not stand what atrocities her head priest committed in their name. The nun eventually left to seek spirituality on her own terms. | As the world's suffering grew, %name%'s abbess requested that she go out and heal the people of the earth. | Cults of death, beasts of nightmare, and men of cruelty. %name% left the halls of her temple to purify them all. | But when a child asked her a faith-shattering question, %name% abandoned her faith, seeking out spirituality by other means. | Unfortunately, prayer did not spare her sisters from a slaughter. %name% realized that her faith was better invested in looking out for herself than muttering to some so-called god. | Always a fiery woman, %name% left the safety of the monasteries to go out and 'right' the world. | One of the few literate women around, %name% abandoned her ascetic life to learn more of the world and, hopefully, to cure that which sickened it. | But one night a man bedded her. She woke with her faith cratered in the crumpled sheets around her. Ashamed, she never returned to her monastery. | But she used her trusted position for ill-gotten gains, stealing from the temple's treasury. It didn't take long for the scandal to drive her out. | Unfortunately, a child accused her of behavior unbecoming of a nun. Nobody knows the truth behind the story, but %name% did not last much longer at the church. | One night, she discovered an awful truth in an old tome. Not long after, %name% quickly left the church, never quite saying what it was that she discovered.} {The woman hardly knows a thing about fighting, but she carries the mental fortitude of a mountain standing against a storm. | Years of solitude and prayer have left %name% out of shape, but it is her steeled mind that is of most value. | Perhaps never really content with her life, it's difficult to entirely know why someone like %name% would join a band of mercenaries. | Maybe there are too many devils in the world, or too many inside her, but you don't question why %name% wishes to join a band of sellswords. | Faith won't cleave a greenskin, but it won't have a woman like %name% running away from one, either. | %name%'s stated desire to rid the world of 'the unfaithful' is almost scary in its determination. | While %name%'s spirituality is to be commended, the constant mutterings to the old gods are a bit annoying. | While %name%'s hands are better clasped in prayer than around the handle of a sword, few mercenaries have the sense of resolve that she does. | A holy book practically anchored to her wrist, %name% has sought the company of sellswords. | The holy book she carries is thick enough to be used as a shield, but %name% looks absolutely horrified when you say as much out loud. | Perhaps with a romantic view of mercenaries in need of a good spiritual cleansing, %name% seeks to accompany sellswords. | Once having read of warrior priestesses, %name% now wishes to emulate those brave, unwavering soldiers of faith. | You get the feeling %name% wants release from this sinful world. If that's the truth then she has come to the right place.}"
        es = "{Después de que unos asaltantes asesinaran a su familia, %name% se refugió en las comodidades de la religión y se hizo monja en un convento cercano. | Viajando a menudo lejos de su iglesia y de sus compañeras monjas, %name% pasó años predicando a los campesinos en aldeas remotas. | %name%, una monja tranquila, ha pasado incontables días adorando a los antiguos dioses en el monasterio de %townname%. | Una monja entre muchas, %name% solía vagar por los templos con campanarios de %randomtown%. | Abandonada en las escaleras de un convento, %name% creció en compañía de monjas y pronto adoptó su estilo de vida. | Tratando de encontrar la paz en una tierra en ruinas, %name% se hizo monja. | %name% siempre fue una niña rebelde, y sus padres la entregaron al convento local, donde rápidamente la apaciguaron como monja.} {Desafortunadamente, el gusto de su abadesa por la juventud y las cosas carnales desembocó en un terrible escándalo. %name% huyó para preservar su vida y su fe. | Pero su fe quedó irreversiblemente dañada cuando un infernal ataque de asaltantes dejó a hombres castrados, mujeres violadas y niños ensartados en asadores. | Aunque creía en los antiguos dioses, la monja no podía soportar las atrocidades que su sumo sacerdote cometía en su nombre. La monja acabó marchándose para buscar la espiritualidad a su manera. | A medida que crecía el sufrimiento del mundo, la abadesa de %name% le pidió que saliera a sanar a la gente de la tierra. | Cultos de muerte, bestias de pesadilla y hombres crueles. %name% abandonó los pasillos de su templo para purificarlos a todos. | Pero cuando un niño le hizo una pregunta que hizo añicos su fe, %name% la abandonó y buscó la espiritualidad por otros medios. | Desafortunadamente, la oración no libró a sus hermanas de una matanza. %name% se dio cuenta de que era mejor invertir su fe en cuidar de sí misma que en murmurarle a algún supuesto dios. | %name% siempre fue una mujer apasionada, y dejó la seguridad de los monasterios para salir a 'corregir' el mundo. | Una de las pocas mujeres alfabetizadas que hay, %name% abandonó su vida ascética para aprender más del mundo y, con suerte, curar aquello que lo enferma. | Pero una noche un hombre se acostó con ella. Despertó con la fe hecha un cráter entre las sábanas arrugadas que la rodeaban. Avergonzada, nunca regresó a su monasterio. | Pero usó su posición de confianza para obtener ganancias mal habidas, robando del tesoro del templo. El escándalo no tardó en echarla. | Desafortunadamente, un niño la acusó de un comportamiento impropio de una monja. Nadie sabe la verdad detrás de la historia, pero %name% no duró mucho más en la iglesia. | Una noche, descubrió una terrible verdad en un viejo tomo. Poco después, %name% abandonó a toda prisa la iglesia, sin llegar a decir nunca qué había descubierto.} {La mujer apenas sabe nada de lucha, pero tiene la fortaleza mental de una montaña que resiste la tormenta. | Años de soledad y oración han dejado a %name% en baja forma, pero lo más valioso es su mente de acero. | Quizás nunca estuvo satisfecha del todo con su vida, pero es difícil saber por qué alguien como %name% se uniría a una banda de mercenarios. | Tal vez haya demasiados demonios en el mundo, o demasiados dentro de ella, pero no te cuestionas por qué %name% desea unirse a una banda de mercenarios. | La fe no partirá a un piel verde, pero tampoco hará que una mujer como %name% huya de uno. | El deseo declarado de %name% de librar al mundo de 'los infieles' es casi aterrador por su determinación. | Si bien la espiritualidad de %name% es digna de elogio, los constantes murmullos a los antiguos dioses resultan un poco molestos. | Si bien las manos de %name% están mejor juntas en oración que alrededor de la empuñadura de una espada, pocos mercenarios tienen la determinación que tiene ella. | Con un libro sagrado prácticamente anclado a la muñeca, %name% ha buscado la compañía de mercenarios. | El libro sagrado que lleva es lo bastante grueso como para usarlo de escudo, pero %name% parece absolutamente horrorizada cuando lo dices en voz alta. | Quizás con una visión romántica de unos mercenarios necesitados de una buena limpieza espiritual, %name% busca acompañar a los mercenarios. | Tras haber leído sobre sacerdotisas guerreras, %name% desea ahora emular a esas valientes e inquebrantables soldados de la fe. | Tienes la sensación de que %name% quiere liberarse de este mundo pecaminoso. Si es así, ha venido al lugar correcto.}"
    }
    // en = "\x7bAfter raiders murdered his family, %name% retreated into the comforts of religion and became a monk at a nearby monastery. | Often traveling away from his church and fellow monks, %name% spent years preaching to peasantry in remote villages. | %name%, a quiet monk, has spent untold days worshipping the old gods in %townname%'s monastery. | One monk amongst many, %name% used to wander the steepled temples of %randomtown%. | Abandoned on the steps of a monastery, %name% grew up in the company of monks, and soon took to their lifestyle. | Trying to find peace in a land of ruin, %name% became a monk. | Always an unruly child, %name%'s parents handed him over to the local monastery where he was quickly pacified as a monk.\x7d \x7bUnfortunately, his abbot's liking for youth and fleshen things led to a terrible scandal. %name% fled to preserve his life and his faith. | But his faith was irreversibly damaged as a hellacious attack by raiders left men castrated, women raped, and children skewered on spits. | Though a believer in the old gods, the monk could not stand what atrocities his head priest committed in their name. The monk eventually left to seek spirituality on his own terms. | As the world's suffering grew, %name%'s abbot requested that he go out and heal the people of the earth - or kill those who did them wrong. | Cults of death, beasts of nightmare, and men of cruelty. %name% left the halls of his temple to purify them all. | But when a child asked him a faith-shattering question, %name% abandoned his faith, seeking out spirituality by other means. | Unfortunately, prayer did not spare his brothers from a slaughter. %name% realized that his faith was better invested in looking out for himself than muttering to some so-called god. | Always a fiery man, %name% left the safety of the monasteries to go out and 'right' the world. | One of the few literate men around, %name% abandoned his ascetic life to learn more of the world and, hopefully, to cure that which sickened it. | But one night a woman bedded him. He woke with his faith cratered in the crumpled sheets around him. Ashamed, he never returned to his monastery. | But he used his trusted position for ill-gotten gains, stealing from the temple's treasury. It didn't take long for the scandal to drive him out. | Unfortunately, a child accused him of behavior unbecoming of a monk. Nobody knows the truth behind the story, but %name% did not last much longer at the church. | One night, he discovered an awful truth in an old tome. Not long after, %name% quickly left the church, never quite saying what it was that he discovered.\x7d \x7bThe man hardly knows a thing about fighting, but he carries the mental fortitude of a mountain standing against a storm. | Years of solitude and prayer have left %name% out of shape, but it is his steeled mind that is of most value. | Perhaps never really content with his life, it's difficult to entirely know why someone like %name% would join a band of mercenaries. | Maybe there are too many devils in the world, or too many inside him, but you don't question why %name% wishes to join a band of sellswords. | Faith won't cleave a greenskin, but it won't have a man like %name% running away from one, either. | %name%'s stated desire to rid the world of 'the unfaithful' is almost scary in its determination. | While %name%'s spirituality is to be commended, the constant mutterings to the old gods are a bit annoying. | While %name%'s hands are better clasped in prayer than around the handle of a sword, few mercenaries have the sense of resolve that he does. | A holy book practically anchored to his wrist, %name% has sought the company of sellswords. | The holy book he carries is thick enough to be used as a shield, but %name% looks absolutely horrified when you say as much out loud. | Perhaps with a romantic view of mercenaries in need of a good spiritual cleansing, %name% seeks to accompany sellswords. | Once having read of warrior priests, %name% now wishes to emulate those brave, unwavering soldiers of faith. | You get the feeling %name% wants release from this sinful world. If that's the truth then he has come to the right place.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\monk_turned_flagellant_background.nut
    // en = "Monk turned Flagellant"
    // en base_es
    // en = "The world was too dark for %name% to continue his ways. A talk with a flagellant showed him that the old gods are not happy with man's pursuits of justice through reasonable means. Now the once-monk can be found whipping himself, bleeding righteousness into the world one strike at a time."
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\nomad_background.nut
    // en = "Any nomad that survived out in the desert will have some expertise in fighting."
    // en base_es
    // context: nomad_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "The nomad %name% left the %companyname% a few months after yourself. %they% apparently traveled south and now leads what they're calling the 'City on Legs,' a huge band of peoples that roam the deserts. It is apparently so rich and successful a society that the Viziers worry their own people will flock to it."
        es = "%Art% nómada %name% dejó %companyname% unos meses después que tú. Por lo visto, viajó hacia el sur y ahora lidera lo que llaman la 'Ciudad Errante', una enorme banda de gentes que recorre los desiertos. Al parecer, es una sociedad tan rica y próspera que los visires temen que su propio pueblo acuda en masa a ella."
    }
    // context: nomad_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "You learned that %name% the nomad departed the company with the hope of finding new plains to roam. Apparently, %they% got the idea in %their% head that %they% would travel far to the north and land cozily with the barbarians there. To %their% credit, the barbarians and nomads share a similar lifestyle, culture, language, religion, laws, struggles, conflicts, and general appearances aside. The nomad was butchered almost instantly upon entrance to a barbarian encampment and %their% remains eaten in a warrior ritual."
        es = "Te enteraste de que %name%, %art% nómada, dejó la compañía con la esperanza de encontrar nuevas llanuras por las que vagar. Por lo visto, se le metió en la cabeza la idea de viajar muy al norte y acomodarse a gusto entre los bárbaros de allí. Hay que reconocer que bárbaros y nómadas comparten un estilo de vida similar, dejando aparte la cultura, la lengua, la religión, las leyes, las penurias, los conflictos y el aspecto en general. %Art% nómada fue descuartizad%o% casi en cuanto entró en un campamento bárbaro, y sus restos fueron devorados en un ritual guerrero."
    }
    // en = "the Desert Raider"
    // en base_es
    // en = "of the Desert"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Son of the Desert"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Desert Scourge"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Nomad"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Redsands"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Free"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Waylayer"
    // en base_es
    // context: nomad_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: "un desastroso emboscada" es errata de género → "una desastrosa emboscada".
        // corrige base: "voted out" no es "desterrado" sino "expulsado por votación".
        en = "{Like many southerners, %name% is someone who grew up in the desert, roaming the dunes and waylaying caravans and lost travelers alike. | Born into one of the South's many desert tribes, %name% learned the ways of the sands before they learned anything else. | Nomads pepper the southern deserts and it is in one of these roaming bands that %name% was born. | True nomads are a rare find in the cities of the south and %name% is no different. | You rarely see a nomad outside their element in the dunes of the southern sands, but %name% stands, darkly tanned and gritting %themselves% again.} {However, nomadic politics are a mite complicated. Some event, which the nomad-turned-sellsword refuses to explain, ushered %them% into the cities looking for work. | A rule of %their% tribe is that every third son must travel out to see the world and, if they so wish, return. So, here %name% stands. | Accused of sexual impropriety with a woman not formally gifted to %them%, %name% was faced with execution or exile from the tribe. Their breathing and standing before you hints at which of the two they chose. | Having murdered one of their fellow tribesman over a gambling debt, the nomad was exiled from %their% tribe. | But a disastrous ambush, which they were responsible for planning, saw %them% voted out of their particular tribe. | But the nomad wished to see more of the world, to see %themselves% as more than what %they% could muster within the confines of their tribe, and so they left and ventured to the cities for adventurous work.} {The nomad stands before you every bit of their upbringing: darkly toned, eyes black, hands sanded down. If they's not a warrior already, they presumably could be trained into one with time. | As a man of the unbearable sands of the south, it's no surprise that the nomad is physically ready to take on the tasks of sellswording. Whether the skills are there is another matter entirely. | Men who venture the desert wastes are a hardy lot and %name% is no different. | Nomads such as %name% earn most of their combat experience ambushing caravans. It could be of use in a mercenary band, though frontline work is a fair bit different than waylaying poor merchants. | %name% is every bit of the South as you expect: worn down by the sands, yet standing with the constitution of a man ready to take on the day and all those to come. | %name% is unlikely to be a trained and skilled fighter quite yet, but as a man of the southern wastes there is little doubt that they have the heart and spirit of a warrior.}"
        es = "{Como muchos sureños, %name% creció en el desierto, vagando por las dunas y asaltando por igual caravanas y viajeros perdidos. | Nacid%o% en una de las muchas tribus del desierto del Sur, %name% aprendió los caminos de las arenas antes que cualquier otra cosa. | Los nómadas abundan en los desiertos del sur, y fue en una de estas bandas errantes donde nació %name%. | Los verdaderos nómadas son difíciles de encontrar en las ciudades del sur y %name% no es una excepción. | Rara vez se ve a un nómada fuera de su elemento, las dunas de las arenas del sur, pero aquí está %name%, con la piel muy tostada y apretando los dientes una vez más.} {Sin embargo, la política nómada es un tanto complicada. Algún suceso, que %art% nómada convertid%o% en mercenari%o% se niega a explicar, %lo% llevó a las ciudades en busca de trabajo. | Una regla de su tribu es que cada tercer hijo debe salir a ver el mundo y, si así lo desea, regresar. Así que aquí está %name%. | Acusad%o% de conducta sexual inapropiada con una mujer que no le había sido entregada formalmente, %name% tuvo que elegir entre la ejecución y el exilio de la tribu. Que siga respirando y esté ante ti insinúa cuál de las dos opciones eligió. | Después de asesinar a uno de sus compañeros de tribu por una deuda de juego, %art% nómada fue desterrad%o% de su tribu. | Pero una desastrosa emboscada, de cuya planificación era responsable, hizo que %lo% expulsaran por votación de su tribu. | Pero %art% nómada deseaba ver más del mundo, verse a sí mism%o% como algo más de lo que podía llegar a ser dentro de los límites de su tribu, así que se marchó y se aventuró en las ciudades en busca de trabajo aventurero.} {%Art% nómada que tienes ante ti refleja por completo su crianza: piel oscura, ojos negros, manos curtidas por la arena. Si aún no es guerrer%o%, presumiblemente podría llegar a serlo con el tiempo. | Como %hombre% de las insoportables arenas del sur, no es de extrañar que %art% nómada esté físicamente preparad%o% para las tareas del oficio mercenario. Si tiene la destreza necesaria es otra cuestión. | Quienes se aventuran en los yermos del desierto son gente recia y %name% no es una excepción. | Nómadas como %name% obtienen la mayor parte de su experiencia en combate asaltando caravanas. Podría ser útil en una banda de mercenarios, aunque el trabajo en primera línea es bastante distinto de asaltar a pobres mercaderes. | %name% es todo lo que esperas del Sur: desgastad%o% por las arenas, pero con la constitución de %un% %hombre% list%o% para afrontar el día y todos los que vengan. | Es poco probable que %name% tenga ya entrenamiento y destreza en combate, pero como %hombre% de los yermos del sur, no hay duda de que tiene el corazón y el espíritu de %un% guerrer%o%.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\orc_slayer_background.nut
    // en = "Orc Slayer"
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% doesn't talk much about himself. He just wants to kill orcs and goblins which, given the state of things, makes him a perfect fit for the company. If he's true to his word, he'll leave as soon as the invasion is taken care of."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Orc Slayer"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\pacified_flagellant_background.nut
    // en = "Pacified Flagellant"
    // en base_es
    // en = "After a long talk with a monk, %name% was converted to a more peaceful means of expressing his faith. Now when he picks up a weapon you can be assured it will only be pointed at someone other than himself."
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\paladin_background.nut
    // en = "Oathtaker"
    // en base_es
    // context: paladin_background.o.create.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "Oathtakers are brave warriors sworn to uphold a strict code, and are no strangers to combat. The faith in their cause might seem foolhardy for the nonbeliever, but for them it's a driving force which increases their health and initiative."
        es = "Los Juramentados son valientes guerreros que han jurado defender un código estricto, y no son ajenos al combate. La fe en su causa puede parecer temeraria a los no creyentes, pero para ellos es una fuerza motriz que aumenta su salud y su Iniciativa."
    }
    // context: paladin_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: "'debe' observar el acto" añade las comillas y "el acto", que el inglés no tiene ("insists on Young Anselm's skull watching from the corner").
        en = "%name% the Oathtaker stayed with the %companyname%, wielding Young Anselm's skull to proselytize knightly virtues unto the world. Most see %them% as something of an annoyance, but there is also some charm in a %person% who believes fully in matters of honor and pride and doing good. Last you heard, %they% singlehandedly saved a lord's princess from a gang of alley thieves. In celebration, he was wed to the damsel, though rumors abound that she is unhappy in bed, proclaiming that the Oathtaker insists on Young Anselm's skull watching from the corner. Whatever's going on, you're happy that the %person% is still doing %their% thing to the fullest."
        es = "%name%, %art% Juramentad%o%, permaneció con %companyname%, empuñando el cráneo del Joven Anselm para predicar las virtudes caballerescas al mundo. La mayoría %lo% ve como una especie de incordio, pero también tiene cierto encanto %un% %hombre% que cree plenamente en el honor, el orgullo y en hacer el bien. Lo último que supiste es que salvó sin ayuda a la princesa de un lord de una banda de ladrones callejeros. Para celebrarlo, se casó con la damisela, aunque abundan los rumores de que ella no es feliz en la cama y asegura que %art% Juramentad%o% insiste en que el cráneo del Joven Anselm mire desde el rincón. Pase lo que pase, te alegra que %ese% %hombre% siga haciendo lo suyo al máximo."
    }
    // context: paladin_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "Once an Oathtaker to the bone, %name% grew disenchanted with %their% fellow believers and one night had a dream that they were, in fact, the true heretics. %They% slew every Oathtaker in reach and then fled out, eventually joining the Oathbringers of all people. Last that was heard of %them%, %they% reclaimed Young Anselm's skull and smashed it with a hammer. Enraged, %their% new Oathbringer brethren promptly slew %them% down. %name%'s corpse was found stabbed over a hundred times, ashy skull fragments powdering a bloodied, madly grinning face."
        es = "Antaño Juramentad%o% hasta la médula, %name% se fue desencantando de sus correligionarios y una noche soñó que eran ellos, de hecho, los verdaderos herejes. Mató a todos los Juramentados que tuvo a su alcance y luego huyó, para acabar uniéndose nada menos que a los Juramentadores. Lo último que se supo de %el% es que recuperó el cráneo del Joven Anselm y lo hizo pedazos con un martillo. Enfurecidos, sus nuevos hermanos Juramentadores %lo% abatieron sin perder un instante. El cadáver de %name% apareció con más de cien puñaladas, con fragmentos de cráneo cenicientos espolvoreando un rostro ensangrentado y de sonrisa demente."
    }
    // en = "the Paladin"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Oathbound"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Oathsworn"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Virtuous"
    // en base_es
    // context: paladin_background.o.getTooltip.ret.push().text
    {
        en = "[color=%positive%]%_bonus%[/color] bonus to Hitpoints, Fatigue and Initiative from your base Resolve"
        es = "[color=%positive%]%_bonus%[/color] de bonificación a Puntos de vida, Fatiga e Iniciativa según tu Resolución base"
    }
    // context: paladin_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers. Oathbringers!\n\nOathbringers Oathbringers Oathbringers Oathbringers Oathbringers Oathbringers!!!\n\nOATHBRINGERS OATHBRINGERS OATHBRINGERS!!! | %name% is a diligent follower of the famed founder of the Oathtakers, Young Anselm. %They% believes %themselves% blessed to be in the company of likeminded warriors who, though not without fault, will try and do right in the world. | Some say %name% was an Oathtaker the moment %they% was born. It is the %person% %themselves% who says this most often, though, which leads to some speculation that %they% was almost assuredly a terrible degenerate and %they%'s just now making up for a horrific past. | When you think of an Oathtaker, %name% is about as clean as they come. Keeps %their% uniform and armor nice and tidy. Respects %their% superiors but is never mawkish. And %they%'s absolutely excellent at directing steel through an Oathbringer's face. An outstanding Oathtaker if there ever was one. | Living in a faraway land, chasing honor and bringing death to Oathbringers, %name% heard of the %companyname%'s prestigious past and just had to find it and join up. %They% is a %person% of incredible resolve and most importantly %they% does not truck with Oathbringers. | Young Anselm's spirit has brought %name% to the %companyname%. Or so %they% says. Whatever brought %them% into the company, %they% is no doubt a talented fighter and will serve the outfit well. | The majesty of Young Anselm's spirit cannot be taken for granted. At least that is what %name% believes. %they% states that %they% fights on behalf of the dead Oathtaker. Young Anselm must have been a spirited fellow indeed for this %person% is a wicked talent with any steel.  | Like many Oathtakers, %name% knows three divine elements: Young Anselm's spirit is to be cherished, Oaths are to be taken seriously, and all Oathbringers must die. Earning some coin on the side is also nice, which is why %they% has made %their% 'fourth' element fighting for outfits like the %companyname%. | It is a little peculiar for an Oathtaker to earn a sellsword's coin fighting, but %name% states that it was never forbidden by Young Anselm's teachings. Instead, it is the personal responsibility of the individual Oathtakers to maintain their oaths, which %they% can readily do cleaving enemies for the %companyname%. | %name% carries a ledger dedicated to only one kind of inventory: how many Oathbringers %they%'s killed. %They% even has a list of when and where %they% did the deed, and of course how. The \"how\" entries even get a little extra dedication, with lines and lines meticulously describing how %they% dispatched %their% hated foes. Frankly, you like the %person%'s enthusiasm. | %name%, a Oathtaker, is of such a singular mind it has you almost worried what %they%'d do without Young Anselm's directives. Now, that said, a part of you is curious how %they%'d fare dedicating %themselves% to another craft. With %their% resolve and drive, %they% could probably weave an unbelievable basket, possibly even do it underwater like those learned experts. | %name% is everything one would want in an honorable %person%: smart, fit, and quite good swinging some steel. %Their% dedication to the Oaths is only matched by %their% ability to absolutely demolish those who stand in %their% way. A perfect fit for the %companyname%, truly. | With the %companyname% gaining renown, it is becoming one of the more notable outfits in the land. Naturally, a talented and honorable %person% like %name% would seek to join up, albeit at a cost. %Their% services to Young Anselm's cause mean %their% attention is no doubt split, but even being consumed by righteousness %they% is still an indefatigable fighter worth having in the %companyname%.}"
        es = "{Juramentadores. Juramentadores. Juramentadores. Juramentadores. Juramentadores. Juramentadores. Juramentadores. Juramentadores. Juramentadores. Juramentadores. Juramentadores. ¡Juramentadores!\n\n¡¡¡Juramentadores Juramentadores Juramentadores Juramentadores Juramentadores Juramentadores!!!\n\n¡¡¡JURAMENTADORES JURAMENTADORES JURAMENTADORES!!! | %name% sigue con diligencia al célebre fundador de los Juramentados, el Joven Anselm. Se considera bendecid%o% por estar en compañía de guerreros de ideas afines que, aunque no carecen de defectos, intentarán obrar bien en el mundo. | Hay quien dice que %name% ya era Juramentad%o% desde el momento en que nació. Aunque quien más lo dice es %el% mism%o%, lo que lleva a sospechar que casi con total seguridad fue %un% degenerad%o% terrible y que ahora solo está compensando un pasado horrendo. | Si piensas en un Juramentado, %name% es de lo más pulcro que hay. Mantiene su uniforme y su armadura limpios y en orden. Respeta a sus superiores, pero nunca es empalagos%o%. Y es absolutamente excelente clavando el acero en la cara de un Juramentador. %Un% Juramentad%o% excepcional como pocos. | Viviendo en una tierra lejana, persiguiendo el honor y llevando la muerte a los Juramentadores, %name% oyó hablar del prestigioso pasado de %companyname% y no paró hasta encontrarla y unirse a ella. Es %un% %hombre% de increíble resolución y, lo más importante, no tiene tratos con Juramentadores. | El espíritu del Joven Anselm ha traído a %name% a %companyname%. O eso dice. Sea lo que sea lo que %lo% trajo a la compañía, no cabe duda de que lucha con talento y servirá bien al grupo. | La majestuosidad del espíritu del Joven Anselm no puede darse por sentada. Al menos eso cree %name%. Afirma que lucha en nombre del difunto Juramentado. El Joven Anselm debió de ser un tipo muy animoso, porque %ese% %hombre% tiene un talento endiablado con cualquier acero.  | Como muchos Juramentados, %name% conoce tres elementos divinos: el espíritu del Joven Anselm debe ser venerado, los Juramentos deben tomarse en serio y todos los Juramentadores deben morir. Ganar algo de dinero por el camino tampoco está mal, y por eso ha hecho de luchar para grupos como %companyname% su 'cuarto' elemento. | Es un poco peculiar que un Juramentado cobre como mercenario por luchar, pero %name% afirma que las enseñanzas del Joven Anselm nunca lo prohibieron. Al contrario, mantener sus juramentos es responsabilidad personal de cada Juramentado, algo que puede hacer sin problema partiendo enemigos por %companyname%. | %name% lleva un libro de cuentas dedicado a un único tipo de inventario: cuántos Juramentadores ha matado. Incluso tiene una lista de cuándo y dónde lo hizo y, por supuesto, cómo. Las entradas del \"cómo\" reciben incluso una dedicación especial, con líneas y líneas que describen meticulosamente cómo despachó a sus odiados enemigos. Francamente, te gusta el entusiasmo de %ese% %hombre%. | %name%, Juramentad%o%, tiene una mente tan obstinada que casi te preocupa qué haría sin las directrices del Joven Anselm. Dicho esto, una parte de ti siente curiosidad por saber cómo le iría si se dedicara a otro oficio. Con su determinación y su empuje, probablemente podría tejer una cesta increíble, puede que incluso bajo el agua, como esos doctos expertos. | %name% es todo lo que uno querría en %un% %hombre% de honor: list%o%, en forma y bastante hábil blandiendo el acero. Su dedicación a los Juramentos solo se ve igualada por su capacidad para demoler por completo a quienes se interponen en su camino. Encaja a la perfección en %companyname%, de verdad. | Con el renombre que está ganando, %companyname% se está convirtiendo en uno de los grupos más notables de estas tierras. Naturalmente, %un% %hombre% talentos%o% y honorable como %name% querría unirse, aunque a un precio. Sus servicios a la causa del Joven Anselm hacen que su atención esté sin duda dividida, pero incluso consumid%o% por la rectitud sigue siendo %un% combatiente infatigable que vale la pena tener en %companyname%.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\peddler_background.nut
    // en = "Peddlers are not used to hard physical labor or warfare, but they do excel at haggling for good prices."
    // en base_es
    // context: peddler_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "A lover of the sale, %name% the peddler couldn't stay fighting for long. He eventually left the %companyname% to go out and start his own business. Recently,you got word that he was selling trinkets with the company's sigil on them. You specifically told him to do whatever they wanted except just this one thing, but apparently your warning merely fostered the idea. When you went to tell him to stop, he slammed a crown-bulging satchel on a rather ornate table, saying it was your 'cut.' He sells those trinkets to this day."
        es = "Amante de las ventas, %name%, el vendedor ambulante, no pudo seguir luchando mucho tiempo. Acabó dejando %companyname% para salir a montar su propio negocio. Hace poco te llegó la noticia de que vendía baratijas con el emblema de la compañía. Le dijiste expresamente que hiciera lo que quisiera salvo eso precisamente, pero al parecer tu advertencia no hizo más que alimentar la idea. Cuando fuiste a decirle que parara, plantó de golpe una bolsa repleta de coronas sobre una mesa bastante ornamentada, diciendo que era tu 'parte'. A día de hoy sigue vendiendo esas baratijas."
    }
    // en = "With hard times hitting the %companyname%, many brothers saw fit to return to their old lives. %name% the peddler was no different. Last you heard he got the tar beaten out of him trying to sell stolen wares that 'fell off the wagon' to the very merchant which they originally belonged."
    // en base_es
    // context: peddler_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "A lover of the sale, %name% the peddler couldn't stay fighting for long. She eventually left the %companyname% to go out and start her own business. Recently, you got word that she was selling trinkets with the company's sigil on them. You specifically told her to do whatever they wanted except just this one thing, but apparently your warning merely fostered the idea. When you went to tell her to stop, she slammed a crown-bulging satchel on a rather ornate table, saying it was your 'cut.' She sells those trinkets to this day."
        es = "Amante de las ventas, %name%, la vendedora ambulante, no pudo seguir luchando mucho tiempo. Acabó dejando %companyname% para salir a montar su propio negocio. Hace poco te llegó la noticia de que vendía baratijas con el emblema de la compañía. Le dijiste expresamente que hiciera lo que quisiera salvo eso precisamente, pero al parecer tu advertencia no hizo más que alimentar la idea. Cuando fuiste a decirle que parara, plantó de golpe una bolsa repleta de coronas sobre una mesa bastante ornamentada, diciendo que era tu 'parte'. A día de hoy sigue vendiendo esas baratijas."
    }
    // context: peddler_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "With hard times hitting the %companyname%, many brothers saw fit to return to their old lives. %name% the peddler was no different. Last you heard she got the tar beaten out of her trying to sell stolen wares that 'fell off the wagon' to the very merchant which they originally belonged."
        es = "Cuando a %companyname% le llegaron tiempos difíciles, muchos hermanos consideraron oportuno volver a sus antiguas vidas. %name%, la vendedora ambulante, no fue diferente. Lo último que supiste es que le dieron una paliza tremenda cuando intentaba venderle mercancía robada que 'se cayó del carro' al mismo comerciante al que pertenecía originalmente."
    }
    // context: peddler_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{House to house, | Once a proud merchant, now | An annoyance to most, | In tough times, everyone has to scrape by somehow, hence why | Not of the trades, but instead of trade itself,} %name% is a mere peddler. {Dancing, singing, boasting or acting a king, anything to make that sale. | Pushy and unrelenting, their tenacity is admirable. | %name% will try to sell off a rusty bucket for a helm once worn by kings. This trader will sell anything. | %name% will make you crave things you never knew you wanted. No refunds, though. | %name% used to make a decent living selling {used carts | pots, pans and jars }, until fierce competition ended the business - with a broken arm.} {Self marketing is what this frail merchant does best, though few believe the pitch about having 'Great swordsmanship and resolute bravery'. | Supposedly handed out 'coupons' for 'services', whatever those are. %name% is chippy, though, and any outfit these days could use a warm body no matter its real value. | If hired, %name% promises, you'll get a special discount on a virility enhancing potion. | %name% lowers their voice and tells you they've got a great deal on rusted arrow tips, just for you. The merchant looks disappointed at your lack of interest. | This merchant knows a man who knows a man who knows a man. All three strangers potentially better at fighting than %name%. | A shame a war can't be fought with words these days. %name% would be unstoppable.}"
        es = "{De casa en casa, | Antes al frente de un orgulloso negocio, ahora | Para fastidio de casi todos, | En tiempos difíciles todo el mundo tiene que salir adelante como sea, y por eso | Sin más oficio que el propio comercio,} %name% se dedica a la venta ambulante. {Bailar, cantar, fanfarronear o hacerse pasar por rey: lo que haga falta para cerrar la venta. | Su insistencia no da tregua; esa tenacidad es admirable. | %name% intentará venderte un cubo oxidado como si fuera un yelmo que una vez llevaron reyes. Aquí se vende de todo. | %name% hará que ansíes cosas que nunca supiste que querías. Eso sí, no se admiten devoluciones. | %name% se ganaba decentemente la vida vendiendo {carros usados | ollas, sartenes y tarros }, hasta que una competencia feroz acabó con el negocio - con un brazo roto.} {Pese a su aspecto frágil, lo que mejor se le da es venderse, aunque pocos se creen eso de tener una 'gran destreza con la espada y una valentía resuelta'. | Supuestamente repartía 'vales' para 'servicios', sean lo que sean. Aun así, %name% tiene carácter, y a cualquier grupo le viene bien hoy en día alguien con pulso, sea cual sea su valía. | Si le das trabajo, promete %name%, tendrás un descuento especial en una poción para potenciar la virilidad. | %name% baja la voz y te dice que tiene una oferta estupenda en puntas de flecha oxidadas, solo para ti. Tu falta de interés le decepciona a ojos vista. | Tiene un conocido que tiene un conocido que tiene un conocido. Los tres, posiblemente, pelean mejor que %name%. | Lástima que hoy en día las guerras no se libren con palabras. %name% sería imparable.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\peddler_southern_background.nut
    // context: peddler_southern_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{House to house, | Once a proud merchant, now | An annoyance to most, | In tough times, everyone has to scrape by somehow, hence why | Not of the trades, but instead of trade itself,} %name% is a mere peddler. {dancing, singing, boasting and acting like a king, anything to make that sale. | Pushy and unrelenting, that tenacity is admirable. | %name%'ll try to sell off a rusty bucket for a helm once worn by kings. This peddler will sell anything. | This peddler will make you crave things you never knew you wanted. No refunds, though. | %name% used to make a decent living selling {used carts | pots, pans and jars}, until fierce competition drove down business - by breaking arms.} {Marketing is what this frail peddler does best, though few believe the pitch about having 'Great swordsmanship and resolute bravery'. | %name% supposedly handed out 'coupons' for services, whatever those are. %name%'s chippy, though, and any outfit these days could use a warm body no matter its real value. | If hired, %name% promises, you'll get a special discount on a virility enhancing potion. | The merchant lowers their voice and tells you the've got a great deal on rusted arrow tips, just for you. %name% looks disappointed at your lack of interest. | This merchant knows a man who knows a man who knows a man. All three strangers potentially better at fighting. | A shame a war can't be fought with words these days. %name% would be unstoppable.}"
        es = "{De casa en casa, | Antes al frente de un orgulloso negocio, ahora | Para fastidio de casi todos, | En tiempos difíciles todo el mundo tiene que salir adelante como sea, y por eso | Sin más oficio que el propio comercio,} %name% se dedica a la venta ambulante. {Baila, canta, fanfarronea y se da aires de rey: lo que haga falta para cerrar la venta. | Insistencia sin tregua: esa tenacidad es admirable. | %name% intentará venderte un cubo oxidado como si fuera un yelmo que una vez llevaron reyes. Aquí se vende de todo. | Con sus artes de venta acabarás ansiando cosas que nunca supiste que querías. Eso sí, no hay devoluciones. | %name% se ganaba decentemente la vida vendiendo {carros usados | ollas, sartenes y tarros}, hasta que una competencia feroz hundió el negocio - a base de romper brazos.} {Pese a su aspecto frágil, lo que mejor se le da es la venta, aunque pocos se creen eso de tener una 'gran destreza con la espada y una valentía resuelta'. | Supuestamente, %name% repartía 'vales' para servicios, sean lo que sean. Aun así, %name% tiene carácter, y a cualquier grupo le viene bien hoy en día alguien con pulso, sea cual sea su valía. | Si le das trabajo, promete %name%, tendrás un descuento especial en una poción para potenciar la virilidad. | Baja la voz y te dice que tiene una oferta estupenda en puntas de flecha oxidadas, solo para ti. Tu falta de interés decepciona a %name% a ojos vista. | Tiene un conocido que tiene un conocido que tiene un conocido. Los tres, posiblemente, pelean mejor. | Lástima que hoy en día las guerras no se libren con palabras. %name% sería imparable.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\pimp_background.nut
    // en = "Pimp"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\poacher_background.nut
    // en = "Poachers tend to have some skill in using bow and arrow to hunt down rabbits and the like."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name%, former poacher, eventually saved enough money to leave the %companyname%. You learned he found a bit of mountain land and works it for a local nobleman. Ironically, his job is to hunt down poachers."
    // en base_es
    // en = "No longer seeing the point in risking his life for so few crowns, %name% the former poacher put down the sellsword's life and returned to unlawfully hunting deer in the woods. A nobleman once offered you a good satchel of crowns to specifically hunt the man down. You declined the offer, but the writing was on the wall: his days are numbered."
    // en base_es
    // context: poacher_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "%name%, former poacher, eventually saved enough money to leave the %companyname%. You learned she found a bit of mountain land and works it for a local nobleman. Ironically, her job is to hunt down poachers."
        es = "%name%, antigua cazadora furtiva, acabó ahorrando suficiente dinero para dejar %companyname%. Supiste que encontró un pedazo de tierra en la montaña y lo trabaja para un noble local. Irónicamente, su trabajo consiste en perseguir a cazadores furtivos."
    }
    // context: poacher_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        // corrige base: "sus días estaban contados" → "están contados": el inglés va en presente ("his days are numbered").
        en = "No longer seeing the point in risking her life for so few crowns, %name% the former poacher put down the sellsword's life and returned to unlawfully hunting deer in the woods. A nobleman once offered you a good satchel of crowns to specifically hunt the woman down. You declined the offer, but the writing was on the wall: her days are numbered."
        es = "Al no ver ya sentido en arriesgar su vida por tan pocas coronas, %name%, la antigua cazadora furtiva, dejó la vida de mercenaria y volvió a cazar ciervos ilegalmente en el bosque. Una vez, un noble te ofreció una buena bolsa de coronas precisamente para darle caza a esa mujer. Rechazaste la oferta, pero estaba claro: sus días están contados."
    }
    // context: poacher_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{Interested in the thrill of the hunt, | Looking to support a family, | With a grumbling stomach, | After a long and hard winter without a stock of food,} %name% {set off into the woods in chase of deer | sought wildlife to which, if skittishness is any indication, the hunter may or may not have had proper claim | ate a fill of all manner of woodland creatures, a well-used bow yoked across shoulders indicating the means to the meals | took to the woods to hunt game with bow and spear}. Hailing from %townname%, %name% {was, as a poacher, the hunter and the hunted | needed to feed the children back home | sought to support oneself, one's own hide, and one's ever-growling stomach | was poaching, an act of rebellion against the order of things as much as a means to a full belly}. {Fearful these pursuits would attract bounty hunters or lawmen, decided to settle on life as a bow for hire. | Tired of working so hard just to put food on the table, buying a meal with a sellsword's pay just seemed so much easier. | After a bad hunt led to a long stay in a lord's dungeon, the poacher would rather put neck on the line as a mercenary now than in the noose as a poacher. | Years of lonely hunting wore on. Although life as a mercenary is exceedingly dangerous, it seems better to die with company than alone. | With a mother pleading for a change of ways, lest the whole family pay for the crimes. the poacher stands here now, a testament to who won the argument.}"
        es = "{Por la emoción de la caza, | Para mantener a una familia, | Con el estómago rugiendo, | Tras un invierno largo y duro sin provisiones,} %name% {se adentró en el bosque persiguiendo ciervos | buscó presas sobre las que, a juzgar por su nerviosismo, quizá no tuviera ningún derecho | se dio un atracón de toda clase de criaturas del bosque, con un arco muy usado cruzado sobre los hombros como prueba de cómo conseguía la comida | se echó al bosque para cazar con arco y lanza}. Natural de %townname%, %name% {practicaba la caza furtiva siendo a la vez quien caza y a quien cazan | necesitaba alimentar a los hijos que esperaban en casa | buscaba mantener su propio pellejo y su estómago siempre rugiente | cazaba furtivamente, como acto de rebeldía contra el orden de las cosas tanto como para llenar la barriga}. {Por miedo a que estas andanzas atrajeran a cazarrecompensas o a la ley, se decidió por la vida de arco a sueldo. | Tras tanto esfuerzo solo para poner comida en la mesa, comprar el sustento con la paga de un mercenario parecía mucho más fácil. | Después de que una mala cacería acabara en una larga estancia en la mazmorra de un señor, ahora prefiere jugarse el cuello en el oficio mercenario antes que en la horca por caza furtiva. | Los años de caza solitaria pasaron factura. Aunque la vida de mercenario es sumamente peligrosa, parece mejor morir en compañía que en soledad. | Ante las súplicas de una madre para que cambiara de vida, no fuera a ser que toda la familia pagara por sus crímenes, aquí está ahora, como testimonio de quién ganó la discusión.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\raider_background.nut
    // en = "Any raider that survived so far will have some expertise in fighting."
    // en base_es
    // context: raider_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "A former raider, %name% fit in well with the %companyname% and proved %themselves% an excellent fighter. Having saved a veritable mountain of crowns, %they% retired from the company and returned from whence %they% came. %They% was last seen sailing a riverboat toward a small village."
        es = "Antigu%o% asaltante, %name% encajó bien en %companyname% y demostró ser %un% excelente combatiente. Tras ahorrar una verdadera montaña de coronas, se retiró de la compañía y volvió al lugar de donde vino. Fue vist%o% por última vez navegando en un barco fluvial hacia un pequeño pueblo."
    }
    // context: raider_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        // corrige base: "Francamente, se lo buscó." es un añadido que el inglés no tiene; se elimina.
        en = "As the %companyname% speedily declined, %name% the raider departed from the company and went on %their% own way again. %They% returned to raiding, taking %their% greedy violence along the shorelines of river villages. You're not sure if it's true, but word has it that %they% was impaled with a pitchfork by a stable boy. Word has it that the town hoisted %their% body parts along the outer walls as a warning to future would-be raiders."
        es = "A medida que %companyname% decaía a toda velocidad, %name%, %art% asaltante, abandonó la compañía y volvió a seguir su propio camino. Regresó a los saqueos, llevando su codiciosa violencia a las orillas de las aldeas ribereñas. No estás seguro de si es cierto, pero se dice que un mozo de cuadra %lo% empaló con una horca. Se dice que el pueblo colgó partes de su cuerpo a lo largo de las murallas exteriores como advertencia para futuros aspirantes a asaltantes."
    }
    // en = "the Raider"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Marauder"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Bandit"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Fourfingers"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Ravensblack"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Defiant"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Pillager"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Menace"
    // en base_es
    // context: raider_background.o.onBuildDescription.maleOnlyOption
    {
        // local maleOnlyOption = this.getContainer().getActor().getGender() != 1 ? "| But while raping and pillaging, %name% was noticed to have a preference for the husbands over the wives. %Their% taste ostracized %them% from the rest of the warband." : "";
        en = "| But while raping and pillaging, %name% was noticed to have a preference for the husbands over the wives. %Their% taste ostracized %them% from the rest of the warband."
        es = "| Pero mientras violaba y saqueaba, se notó que %name% prefería a los maridos antes que a las esposas. Sus gustos le valieron el rechazo del resto de la banda de guerra."
    }
    // context: raider_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // return "{Living by the shore, %name%\'s life was peppered with the spice of sea raiders. As an adult, %they% joined them in the raiding. | When %their% family was slaughtered, newborn %name% was taken in by the very raiders who did it. | Born in a faraway place, %name% traveled to this land looking for towns to pillage. | A strong %person% from a remote part of the land, %name%\'s presence here has been hellacious for local residents. | A raider with a strong oar-arm and an even greater axe-arm, %name% is part of the folklore that keeps kids in bed at night. | Part warrior, part criminal, %name% has made a good life as a raider. | %name% decided many years ago to take by force from the weak and feeble whatever %they% desired, and has made %their% presence known by raiding caravans and villages ever since. | A poor and starved %child% growing up, %name% took to joining robbers and cutthroats out of desperation. For the first time in %their% life %they% didn\'t feel hunger every night, and so %they% continued to take by force from others what %they% needed. %They% learned to fight and to kill without remorse, and before long, %they% was a monster of a %person%. | Wearing a lord\'s boots and a queen\'s torn dress as a shawl, %name%\'s attire reflects %their% years of raiding well. | The threat that stirs lords in their sleep and rushes housewives beneath beds, %name% is a menacing raider. | The strong take from the weak - that is the order of things that %name% lives by.} {%They% and %their% comrades raided caravans and preyed on outlying farms, only to find themselves being attacked for spoils of war one day. A small band of orcs had spotted %name%\'s camp and washed it away like a force of nature, scattering the few survivors into every which direction. %name% ran and didn\'t look behind. | After many years of ill-gotten gains, the %person% gave up the life after a raid on an orphanage ended with an out of control fire and the deaths of those inside. | A devoted believer in the old ways, %name% desires to die a glorious warrior\'s death to take %their% place beside the gods. But slaughtering villagers like cattle won\'t get the attention of the gods, and so %they% now looks for a greater challenge. " + maleOnlyOption + " | It started with a good raid on a merchant caravan. The few guards were quickly cut down and the fleeing merchant didn\'t run fast enough - a javelin to his back attested to it. The spoils were rich, but before long there was heated argument about how they were to be shared. By evening, most of the raiders had killed each other. %name% only barely escaped and had nothing to show for %their% day but a limping leg. | But %they% always had a soft spot for women, and the constant rape and murder by %their% comrades pushed the raider away from this lifestyle. | Caught by a lord\'s guards, the raider barely escaped, instead watching from a hilltop as %their% comrades were executed. | But one village ambushed %their% party on a raid, cutting down everyone but %themselves% as %they% stole a stable horse and escaped certain doom. | While staking out in a forest, the raider\'s party was attacked by vicious beasts. %They% fed %their% own comrade to the foul things just to save %their% own neck. | But as war tears the world asunder, the raider realized there was less and less to actually pillage. | But as conflicts boil, every village %they% ran into was either dirt poor or already armed to face other fiends of the world.} {Now, %name% just wants a fresh start, even in the dour field of sellswords. | %name% can\'t be wholly trusted as a mercenary, but having been in league with brigands and raiders at the very least makes %them% fit for the work. | The %person% is not brotherly in the least, but %they% can wield a weapon like it\'s one of %their% missing fingers. | While %name%\'s past leaves a bad taste in anyone\'s mouth, there are even worse out there. | %name% is adept at killing and looting, just make sure those skills are directed toward your enemies. | While a good fighter, %name% is first and foremost loyal to loot. | %name% is here to kill things and take things. For you, this is a good thing. | %name% wears a necklace of ears about %their% neck, and another necklace adorned with those ears\' earrings. Fancy. | %name% is a strong fighter, but %they're% in good running to be the least-liked individual in your whole party. | The countryside is an alluring, green canvas upon which to build a life. Maybe the raider just wants to settle down. | Wearing clothes tracked with their previous owner\'s blood, %name% looks strikingly ready for duty. | You get the feeling that %name% is wearing clothes that someone was probably murdered in.}";
        mode = "pattern"
        en = "{Living by the shore, %name%'s life was peppered with the spice of sea raiders. As an adult, %they% joined them in the raiding. | When %their% family was slaughtered, newborn %name% was taken in by the very raiders who did it. | Born in a faraway place, %name% traveled to this land looking for towns to pillage. | A strong %person% from a remote part of the land, %name%'s presence here has been hellacious for local residents. | A raider with a strong oar-arm and an even greater axe-arm, %name% is part of the folklore that keeps kids in bed at night. | Part warrior, part criminal, %name% has made a good life as a raider. | %name% decided many years ago to take by force from the weak and feeble whatever %they% desired, and has made %their% presence known by raiding caravans and villages ever since. | A poor and starved %child% growing up, %name% took to joining robbers and cutthroats out of desperation. For the first time in %their% life %they% didn't feel hunger every night, and so %they% continued to take by force from others what %they% needed. %They% learned to fight and to kill without remorse, and before long, %they% was a monster of a %person%. | Wearing a lord's boots and a queen's torn dress as a shawl, %name%'s attire reflects %their% years of raiding well. | The threat that stirs lords in their sleep and rushes housewives beneath beds, %name% is a menacing raider. | The strong take from the weak - that is the order of things that %name% lives by.} {%They% and %their% comrades raided caravans and preyed on outlying farms, only to find themselves being attacked for spoils of war one day. A small band of orcs had spotted %name%'s camp and washed it away like a force of nature, scattering the few survivors into every which direction. %name% ran and didn't look behind. | After many years of ill-gotten gains, the %person% gave up the life after a raid on an orphanage ended with an out of control fire and the deaths of those inside. | A devoted believer in the old ways, %name% desires to die a glorious warrior's death to take %their% place beside the gods. But slaughtering villagers like cattle won't get the attention of the gods, and so %they% now looks for a greater challenge. <maleOnlyOption:str> | It started with a good raid on a merchant caravan. The few guards were quickly cut down and the fleeing merchant didn't run fast enough - a javelin to his back attested to it. The spoils were rich, but before long there was heated argument about how they were to be shared. By evening, most of the raiders had killed each other. %name% only barely escaped and had nothing to show for %their% day but a limping leg. | But %they% always had a soft spot for women, and the constant rape and murder by %their% comrades pushed the raider away from this lifestyle. | Caught by a lord's guards, the raider barely escaped, instead watching from a hilltop as %their% comrades were executed. | But one village ambushed %their% party on a raid, cutting down everyone but %themselves% as %they% stole a stable horse and escaped certain doom. | While staking out in a forest, the raider's party was attacked by vicious beasts. %They% fed %their% own comrade to the foul things just to save %their% own neck. | But as war tears the world asunder, the raider realized there was less and less to actually pillage. | But as conflicts boil, every village %they% ran into was either dirt poor or already armed to face other fiends of the world.} {Now, %name% just wants a fresh start, even in the dour field of sellswords. | %name% can't be wholly trusted as a mercenary, but having been in league with brigands and raiders at the very least makes %them% fit for the work. | The %person% is not brotherly in the least, but %they% can wield a weapon like it's one of %their% missing fingers. | While %name%'s past leaves a bad taste in anyone's mouth, there are even worse out there. | %name% is adept at killing and looting, just make sure those skills are directed toward your enemies. | While a good fighter, %name% is first and foremost loyal to loot. | %name% is here to kill things and take things. For you, this is a good thing. | %name% wears a necklace of ears about %their% neck, and another necklace adorned with those ears' earrings. Fancy. | %name% is a strong fighter, but %they're% in good running to be the least-liked individual in your whole party. | The countryside is an alluring, green canvas upon which to build a life. Maybe the raider just wants to settle down. | Wearing clothes tracked with their previous owner's blood, %name% looks strikingly ready for duty. | You get the feeling that %name% is wearing clothes that someone was probably murdered in.}"
        es = "{Al vivir en la costa, la vida de %name% estaba salpicada del sabor de los incursores marinos. Ya de adult%o%, se unió a ellos en sus incursiones. | Cuando su familia fue masacrada, %name%, recién nacid%o%, fue acogid%o% por los mismos asaltantes que lo hicieron. | Nacid%o% en un lugar lejano, %name% viajó a esta tierra en busca de pueblos que saquear. | %Un% %hombre% fuerte de un rincón remoto de estas tierras: la presencia de %name% aquí ha sido infernal para los vecinos. | %name%, asaltante de brazo fuerte para el remo y aún más fuerte para el hacha, forma parte del folclore que mantiene a los niños en la cama por la noche. | En parte guerrer%o%, en parte criminal, %name% se ha labrado una buena vida como asaltante. | %name% decidió hace muchos años arrebatar por la fuerza a los débiles e indefensos todo lo que deseara, y desde entonces ha dado a conocer su presencia asaltando caravanas y pueblos. | De niñ%o%, pobre y muert%o% de hambre, %name% se unió por pura desesperación a ladrones y degolladores. Por primera vez en su vida no pasaba hambre todas las noches, así que siguió quitándoles a los demás por la fuerza lo que necesitaba. Aprendió a luchar y a matar sin remordimientos y, en poco tiempo, se convirtió en un monstruo de %hombre%. | Con botas de señor y el vestido rasgado de una reina a modo de chal, el atuendo de %name% refleja bien sus años de saqueos. | La amenaza que desvela a los señores y hace que las amas de casa se escondan bajo la cama: %name% es %un% asaltante temible. | Los fuertes les quitan a los débiles: ese es el orden de las cosas por el que se rige %name%.} {Con sus camaradas asaltaba caravanas y caía sobre granjas apartadas, hasta que un día fueron ellos a quienes atacaron para quitarles el botín. Un pequeño grupo de orcos había descubierto el campamento de %name% y lo arrasó como una fuerza de la naturaleza, dispersando a los pocos supervivientes en todas direcciones. %name% huyó sin mirar atrás. | Tras muchos años de ganancias mal habidas, %art% %hombre% dejó esa vida después de que el asalto a un orfanato terminara en un incendio descontrolado y con la muerte de quienes estaban dentro. | Devot%o% creyente de las viejas costumbres, %name% desea morir con una muerte gloriosa en combate para ocupar su lugar junto a los dioses. Pero degollar aldeanos como si fueran ganado no atraerá la atención de los dioses, así que ahora busca un desafío mayor. <maleOnlyOption:t> | Todo empezó con un buen asalto a una caravana de mercaderes. Los pocos guardias cayeron enseguida y el mercader que huía no corrió lo bastante rápido: una jabalina en la espalda lo atestiguaba. El botín era rico, pero al poco tiempo estalló una acalorada discusión sobre cómo repartirlo. Al anochecer, la mayoría de los asaltantes se habían matado entre sí. %name% escapó por los pelos y no sacó de aquel día más que una pierna coja. | Pero siempre tuvo debilidad por las mujeres, y las constantes violaciones y asesinatos de sus camaradas acabaron apartando %al% asaltante de esa forma de vida. | Capturad%o% por los guardias de un señor, %art% asaltante escapó por poco y tuvo que contemplar desde lo alto de una colina cómo ejecutaban a sus camaradas. | Pero en una incursión, una aldea tendió una emboscada a su grupo y mató a todos menos a %el%, que robó un caballo de un establo y escapó de una muerte segura. | Mientras acechaban en un bosque, el grupo %del% asaltante fue atacado por bestias feroces. Arrojó a su propio camarada a aquellas criaturas inmundas solo para salvar el pellejo. | Pero a medida que la guerra desgarra el mundo, %art% asaltante se dio cuenta de que cada vez quedaba menos que saquear. | Pero con los conflictos en plena ebullición, cada aldea con la que se topaba era pobre de solemnidad o ya estaba armada para hacer frente a otros demonios del mundo.} {Ahora, %name% solo quiere empezar de cero, aunque sea en el sombrío oficio de mercenario. | No se puede confiar del todo en %name% como mercenari%o%, pero haber andado con bandidos y asaltantes %lo% hace, como mínimo, apt%o% para el trabajo. | %Art% %hombre% no tiene nada de fraternal, pero empuña un arma como si fuera uno de los dedos que le faltan. | Aunque el pasado de %name% deja mal sabor de boca a cualquiera, ahí fuera los hay peores. | %name% es diestr%o% matando y saqueando; solo asegúrate de que esas habilidades apunten a tus enemigos. | Aunque lucha bien, %name% es ante todo fiel al botín. | %name% está aquí para matar cosas y llevarse cosas. Para ti, eso es bueno. | %name% lleva al cuello un collar de orejas y otro adornado con los aretes de esas orejas. Muy elegante. | %name% lucha con fuerza, pero va camino de ser la persona menos querida de todo tu grupo. | El campo es un lienzo verde y tentador sobre el que construir una vida. Quizá %art% asaltante solo quiera sentar cabeza. | Con ropa manchada de la sangre de su anterior dueño, %name% parece sorprendentemente list%o% para el servicio. | Tienes la sensación de que %name% lleva una ropa con la que probablemente asesinaron a alguien.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\ratcatcher_background.nut
    // en = "Ratcatchers need to have quick reflexes to catch their prey."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% the ratcatcher came from stranger stocks, and to stranger stocks he returned. After retiring from the %companyname%, he started a ratcatching company. He was doing wonderful business until it came out that he hadn't been killing any of the rats, but instead stowing thousands of them in a storehouse just outside town. Last you heard, the man was quite content with his new and numerous friends."
    // en base_es
    // en = "You didn't think %name% would fit in with sellswords, but he proved himself capable. Unfortunately, the %companyname% fell apart and he returned to ratcatching. You got word that his body was found in a sewer utterly covered in nibbling rats. It's said that he had a smile on his face."
    // en base_es
    // context: ratcatcher_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "%name% the ratcatcher came from stranger stocks, and to stranger stocks she returned. After retiring from the %companyname%, she started a ratcatching company. She was doing wonderful business until it came out that she hadn't been killing any of the rats, but instead stowing thousands of them in a storehouse just outside town. Last you heard, the woman was quite content with her new and numerous friends."
        es = "%name%, la cazadora de ratas, provenía de un linaje extraño, y a un linaje extraño regresó. Después de retirarse de %companyname%, fundó una empresa de caza de ratas. Le iba de maravilla hasta que se descubrió que no había estado matando ninguna rata, sino guardando miles de ellas en un almacén a las afueras de la ciudad. Lo último que supiste es que la mujer estaba muy contenta con sus nuevos y numerosos amigos."
    }
    // context: ratcatcher_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "You didn't think %name% would fit in with sellswords, but she proved herself capable. Unfortunately, the %companyname% fell apart and he returned to ratcatching. You got word that her body was found in a sewer utterly covered in nibbling rats. It's said that she had a smile on her face."
        es = "No pensaste que %name% encajaría con los mercenarios, pero demostró ser capaz. Desafortunadamente, %companyname% se desmoronó y ella volvió a la caza de ratas. Te enteraste de que su cuerpo apareció en una alcantarilla completamente cubierto de ratas que lo mordisqueaban. Se dice que tenía una sonrisa en el rostro."
    }
    // context: ratcatcher_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: "así como algunos ratones" → "además de algunas ratas": el inglés dice "rats" y el chiste es que lo peludo y escurridizo ya eran ratas.
        // corrige base: "y no se refería al mercado" → "y no se refería a las del mercado" ("she didn't mean from the market": las carnes no eran del mercado).
        en = "{Catcher of rats, that's the title %name% once preferred. | With perhaps misplaced pride, %name% fashions herself as a woman of the sewers. | Bowlegged and scrawny, %name%'s career of hunting rats has seemingly turned her into one.} She grew up in %townname%, surviving {in the alleys | on rat, the fruit of the sewers | alongside the furry and scuttling, as well as some rats}. {For cheap entertainment, her father taught her the ways of snaring tiny rodents | Her fallen brother's body was eaten by rats, forging an angry future of rodent-revenge | Her mother demanded the finest meats she could find, and she didn't mean from the market}. But %townname% wears on people, and it wore on %name% like a giant, nibbling creature. {Hearing of greater rats in the world | Sensing that there must be more to life than rats | Trusting her rat-whispering skills}, %name% now seeks to {put her shriveled nose, odd gnawing habits, and quick but kind of gross hands to better use. | crush every rat, see them driven before her, and to hear the squeals of their kin. She has a thousand-yard stare and a clenched fist as she tells you this. | perhaps graduate her skills from rats to dogs and maybe humans, so she says. She doesn't appear to know what she's in for, but perhaps it is best to not tell her. | dish up some rat soup, rat salad, rat kebab, rat bread, rat stew, rat chicken, rat wine... after a while, you just stop listening.}"
        es = "{Cazadora de ratas: ese era el título que %name% prefería en otros tiempos. | Con un orgullo quizá fuera de lugar, %name% se considera una mujer de las alcantarillas. | De piernas arqueadas y escuálida, %name% parece haberse convertido en una rata tras toda una carrera cazándolas.} Creció en %townname%, sobreviviendo {en los callejones | a base de rata, la fruta de las alcantarillas | junto a los seres peludos y escurridizos, además de algunas ratas}. {Como entretenimiento barato, su padre le enseñó a atrapar pequeños roedores | Las ratas se comieron el cuerpo de su difunto hermano, lo que forjó un futuro de rabiosa venganza contra los roedores | Su madre le exigía las mejores carnes que pudiera encontrar, y no se refería a las del mercado}. Pero %townname% desgasta a la gente, y desgastó a %name% como una criatura gigante y roedora. {Al oír hablar de ratas más grandes en el mundo | Intuyendo que tiene que haber algo más en la vida que las ratas | Confiando en su don para susurrar a las ratas}, %name% busca ahora {dar mejor uso a su nariz arrugada, a sus extraños hábitos de roer y a sus manos rápidas pero algo asquerosas. | aplastar a todas las ratas, verlas huir ante ella y oír los chillidos de los suyos. Tiene la mirada perdida en la distancia y el puño apretado mientras te lo cuenta. | tal vez pasar de las ratas a los perros y quizá a los humanos, según dice. No parece saber en qué se está metiendo, pero quizá sea mejor no decírselo. | servir sopa de rata, ensalada de rata, kebab de rata, pan de rata, estofado de rata, pollo de rata, vino de rata... al cabo de un rato, simplemente dejas de escuchar.}"
    }
    // en = "\x7bCatcher of rats, that's the title %name% once preferred. | With perhaps misplaced pride, %name% fashions himself as a man of the sewers. | Bowlegged and scrawny, %name%'s career of hunting rats has seemingly turned him into one.\x7d He grew up in %townname%, surviving \x7bin the alleys | on rat, the fruit of the sewers | alongside the furry and scuttling, as well as some rats\x7d. \x7bFor cheap entertainment, his father taught him the ways of snaring tiny rodents | His fallen brother's body was eaten by rats, forging an angry future of rodent-revenge | His mother demanded the finest meats he could find, and she didn't mean from the market\x7d. But %townname% wears on people, and it wore on %name% like a giant, nibbling creature. \x7bHearing of greater rats in the world | Sensing that there must be more to life than rats | Trusting his rat-whispering skills\x7d, %name% now seeks to \x7bput his shriveled nose, odd gnawing habits, and quick but kind of gross hands to better use. | crush every rat, see them driven before him, and to hear the squeals of their kin. He has a thousand-yard stare and a clenched fist as he tells you this. | perhaps graduate his skills from rats to dogs and maybe humans, so he says. He doesn't appear to know what he's in for, but perhaps it is best to not tell him. | dish up some rat soup, rat salad, rat kebab, rat bread, rat stew, rat chicken, rat wine... after a while, you just stop listening.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\refugee_background.nut
    // en = "Refugee"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Refugees lack the conviction to fight for their homes, but they are used to long and exhausting travel by now."
    // en base_es
    // context: refugee_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "%name% the refugee proved to be a natural fighter, but eventually retired from the %companyname%. Word has it %name% returned home and is using the wealth gained in the company to help rebuild the town."
        es = "%name%, que llegó huyendo de su tierra, demostró tener un don natural para la lucha, pero acabó retirándose de %companyname%. Se dice que %name% volvió a su hogar y está usando la riqueza ganada en la compañía para ayudar a reconstruir el pueblo."
    }
    // context: refugee_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "With the downfall of the %companyname% written plainly on the wall, %name% the refugee split with the company. Using their remaining scant crowns to purchase a set of shoes and returned to a destroyed home, to try and rebuild it. While walking home, an illiterate wildman murdered %name% and ate the shoes."
        es = "Cuando la caída de %companyname% ya era evidente para cualquiera, %name%, que había llegado huyendo de su tierra, se separó de la compañía. Con las escasas coronas que le quedaban compró un par de zapatos y volvió a su hogar destruido para intentar reconstruirlo. De camino a casa, un salvaje analfabeto asesinó a %name% y se comió los zapatos."
    }
    // en = "the Refugee"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Survivor"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Runsfar"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Derelict"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Surbated"
    // en base_es
    // context: refugee_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: «ahora solo es recordado por palabra hablada» es un calco de «spoken word»; mejor «ahora solo se recuerda de boca en boca».
        // corrige base: «vidrio en los ojos» calca «glazes his eyes», que significa que la mirada se vela; «horrorífica» mejor «espantosa».
        // corrige base: «eso dice algo» calca «that's saying something», cuyo sentido es «y eso ya es decir mucho».
        // corrige base: «pero está decidido a sobrevivir» omite el «for damn sure» del inglés, lo que rebaja la crudeza; debería ser «pero, maldita sea, está decidido a sobrevivir».
        en = "{Catastrophes are cheap. | Disease, the ultimate invisible hand. | Win or lose a war, everything is as it has been.} %name% hails from a tiny village that {is now only remembered by spoken word, a generation away from being forgotten. | was destroyed, to put it succinctly. | now stands as a mere footnote, wasting little of the historian's ink. | suffered the world's wrath.} But %name% is a survivor. {%name% fled the disaster with only clothes. | With home ablaze, %name% saved what little could be saved, and fled. | After stumbling upon %their% dead family, %name% gathered what could be saved and ran. | War, famine, disease. It's all a blur now.} {%name% is merely anxious to look ahead rather than behind. | %name% carries little more than a sense of steeled determination, but that is something worth having. | A horrific history scars %name%'s body and glazes %their% eyes, but the mercenary is easily motivated to never experience that past again. | Whatever befell the %name%'s town didn't get %name% and, judging by the rumors you hear, that's saying something. | %name% isn't skilled in martial arts, but is damn sure determined to survive. | Whatever vocation %name% had in the past is now lost. Like many others, seeking mercenary work to get by in this increasingly bloody world. | One of many refugees you've seen, this victim has decided to stop running and start fighting.}"
        es = "{Las catástrofes son baratas. | La enfermedad, la mano invisible definitiva. | Ganes o pierdas una guerra, todo sigue como siempre.} %name% proviene de un pequeño pueblo que {ahora solo se recuerda de boca en boca, a una generación de caer en el olvido. | fue destruido, por decirlo sucintamente. | hoy no es más que una nota a pie de página que apenas gasta la tinta del historiador. | sufrió la ira del mundo.} Pero %name% es %un% sobreviviente. {%name% huyó del desastre con lo puesto. | Con su hogar en llamas, %name% salvó lo poco que pudo salvarse y huyó. | Tras toparse con su familia muerta, %name% reunió lo que pudo salvar y echó a correr. | Guerra, hambruna, enfermedad. Ahora todo es un borrón.} {%name% solo ansía mirar hacia adelante y no hacia atrás. | %name% lleva poco más que una férrea determinación, pero eso es algo que vale la pena tener. | Una historia espantosa ha llenado de cicatrices el cuerpo de %name% y le ha velado la mirada, pero le sobran motivos para no volver a vivir ese pasado. | Lo que asoló el pueblo de %name% no pudo con %el% y, a juzgar por los rumores que oyes, eso ya es decir mucho. | %name% no domina las artes marciales, pero, maldita sea, está decidid%o% a sobrevivir. | Sea cual fuera el oficio que %name% tuvo en el pasado, ya se ha perdido. Como tantos otros, busca trabajo de mercenario para salir adelante en este mundo cada vez más sangriento. | De entre tantos refugiados como has visto, esta víctima ha decidido dejar de huir y empezar a luchar.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\regent_in_absentia_background.nut
    // en = "Regent in Absentia"
    // en base_es
    // context: regent_in_absentia_background.o.create.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "%name% is a Regent in Absentia, choosing to spend their time with a mercenary company as opposed to in court."
        es = "%name% es Regente en Absenta y prefiere pasar el tiempo con una compañía de mercenarios antes que en la corte."
    }
    // context: regent_in_absentia_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "A noble at heart, the disowned noble%person% %name% returned to %them% family. Word has it %they% kicked in the doors and demanded a royal seat. An usurper challenged %them% in combat and, well, %name% learned a lot in %them% days with the %companyname% and %they% now sits on a very, very comfortable throne."
        es = "Noble de corazón, %art% noble desheredad%o% %name% regresó con su familia. Se dice que derribó las puertas a patadas y exigió un asiento real. Un usurpador %lo% retó a combate y, bueno, %name% aprendió mucho en sus días con %companyname%, y ahora se sienta en un trono muy, muy cómodo."
    }
    // context: regent_in_absentia_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "A %person% of nobility at heart, %name% the disowned noble%person% returned to %them% family home. Word has it an usurper arrested %them% at the gates. %Them% head currently rests on a pike with crows for a crown."
        es = "Noble de corazón, %name%, %art% noble desheredad%o%, regresó a la casa familiar. Se dice que un usurpador %lo% arrestó a las puertas. Ahora su cabeza descansa en una pica, con cuervos por corona."
    }
    // context: regent_in_absentia_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: «ya no es un desheredado por su familia real» es agramatical; debería ser «ya no está desheredado por su familia real».
        en = "{%name% is no longer disowned by %their% royal family, yet %their% allegiance is now with the %companyname%. Despite not returning home to %their% lineage, you know that deep down %they% is emboldened by the fact that %they% is back in %their% natural bloodline.}"
        es = "{%name% ya no está desheredad%o% por su familia real, pero su lealtad está ahora con %companyname%. Aunque no ha vuelto a casa con su linaje, sabes que en el fondo se siente envalentonad%o% por saberse de nuevo parte de su estirpe natural.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\retired_soldier_background.nut
    // en = "Retired Soldier"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Retired soldiers tend to have decent experience in warfare, and their resolve is not easily broken. However, their age may have taken a toll on their physical attributes."
    // en base_es
    // context: retired_soldier_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: «de toda la lucha que puede obtener» calca «as far away ... as he can get», que significa «lo más lejos posible de cualquier combate».
        en = "%name% retired again, this time from sellswording instead of soldiering. Leaving the %companyname% behind, %they% built a cabin out in the woods and enjoys the peace and quiet, staying as far away from all the fighting as %they% can get."
        es = "%name% se retiró de nuevo, esta vez del oficio de mercenario en lugar del de soldado. Dejando atrás a %companyname%, construyó una cabaña en el bosque y disfruta de la paz y la tranquilidad, lo más lejos posible de cualquier combate."
    }
    // context: retired_soldier_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "Tired of all the fighting, %name% left the quickly declining %companyname% and went out and built %themselves% a cabin in the woods. Unfortunately, vagabonds attacked. Word has it %they% was found bleeding out on the floor, surrounded by six dead men and the last man standing, a nervous, broken boy shakily waving a sword at the dying old %person%."
        es = "Cansad%o% de tanta lucha, %name% dejó a %companyname%, que decaía a toda prisa, y se construyó una cabaña en el bosque. Por desgracia, unos vagabundos atacaron. Se dice que %lo% encontraron desangrándose en el suelo, rodead%o% de seis hombres muertos y del último que quedaba en pie: un muchacho nervioso y destrozado que agitaba temblorosamente una espada ante %art% viej%o% moribund%o%."
    }
    // en = "the Oldguard"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Sergeant"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Veteran"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Soldier"
    // en base_es
    // context: retired_soldier_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "Once {a sergeant | a royal guards%person% | a dedicated soldier | a respected arms%person% | a frontliner | a soldier | a foot%person%} in the army of a local lord, %fullname% {retired from service after taking an arrow to the knee | was replaced by an aspiring youngster | was expelled after falling asleep on guard duty | retired after a long and exemplary service | was wounded in combat and forced to retire | grew weary of the battles and bloodbaths, formally ending %their% service before it ruined %their% mind | battled the ferocious orc hordes, the campaigns eventually forcing %them% into retirement}. {He locked %their% equipment in a chest along with the memories of %their% duty, intending to never pick up either one again | %They% shelved both sword and shield in %their% study as merely relics of a military past | %They% hung %their% weapons above the chimney as a silent reminder of the %person% %they% used to be | But a new chapter in %their% life was awaiting %them%, one where %they% would not need a sword to get on with %their% day | With many years of service behind %them%, %they% could finally get some peace and quiet | Absent of a military drill's barking, %their% life never felt so quiet}. {For many years %they% lived a happy life with %their% beloved wife, until she died of old age. With nothing else to turn to | Only when finding out that %their% former comrades were brutally slain in an ambush | Only when hearing rumors of a large invasion about to destroy %their% homeland, | %They% tried to live as a farmer for a while, but every day %they% missed having a good sword in hand and standing in the shieldwall. Finally, | But life outside the army, as it turned out, was not for %them%, for %they% felt idle and useless. Finally, | For a time, %they% felt at ease. But as the land was consumed by warfare, | Time spent away from war was short-lived, as the war soon came to %them%. It wasn't long until | Living out on a farm, boredom crept at %name%'s wits until, finally,} %they% picked up arms once more. Although {%their% best days are long over | not as physically fit as %they% once was | %their% constitution is not that of a young %person% anymore | %they% is not the brash young fighter %they% once was | time away from the service has dampened %their% abilities}, {%their% swordfighting skills are still enough to beat any young braggart | %they% still knows how fighting is done on the battlefield | %their% experience is second to few | %they% can rely on the combat experience of a lifetime | %they% is eager to stand amongst brothers | %they% is eager to find battle again | %their% itch to find battle is mirrored by %their% capabilities to actually fight | %they% still knows a thing or two about holding a shieldwall}."
        es = "Antaño {sargento | guardia real | soldado entregad%o% | %hombre% de armas respetad%o% | combatiente de primera línea | soldado | soldado de a pie} en el ejército de un señor local, %fullname% {se retiró del servicio después de recibir una flecha en la rodilla | fue sustituid%o% por un joven aspirante | fue expulsad%o% tras quedarse dormid%o% durante la guardia | se retiró tras un largo y ejemplar servicio | resultó herid%o% en combate y se vio obligad%o% a retirarse | se hartó de las batallas y los baños de sangre, y puso fin formalmente a su servicio antes de que le arruinara la mente | combatió contra las feroces hordas de orcos hasta que las campañas acabaron por obligar%lo% a retirarse}. {Guardó su equipo bajo llave en un arcón junto con los recuerdos de su deber, con la intención de no volver a tocar ninguno de los dos | Colocó la espada y el escudo en un estante de su estudio, como simples reliquias de un pasado militar | Colgó sus armas sobre la chimenea como recordatorio silencioso de quien había sido | Pero %lo% esperaba un nuevo capítulo de su vida, uno en el que no necesitaría una espada para salir adelante cada día | Con muchos años de servicio a sus espaldas, por fin podía disfrutar de un poco de paz y tranquilidad | Sin los gritos de la instrucción militar, su vida nunca había sido tan tranquila}. {Durante muchos años vivió feliz con su amada esposa, hasta que ella murió de vieja. Sin nada más a lo que aferrarse, | Solo al enterarse de que sus antiguos camaradas habían sido brutalmente masacrados en una emboscada, | Solo al oír rumores de una gran invasión que estaba a punto de arrasar su tierra natal, | Intentó vivir un tiempo como granjer%o%, pero cada día añoraba tener una buena espada en la mano y formar en el muro de escudos. Al final, | Pero, como se vio después, la vida fuera del ejército no era para %el%, pues se sentía ocios%o% e inútil. Al final, | Durante un tiempo se sintió en paz. Pero, a medida que la guerra devoraba la tierra, | El tiempo lejos de la guerra duró poco, pues la guerra no tardó en ir a buscar%lo%. Poco después, | Viviendo en una granja, el aburrimiento fue minando el juicio de %name% hasta que, al final,} volvió a tomar las armas. Aunque {sus mejores días quedaron muy atrás | ya no está en tan buena forma como antes | su constitución ya no es la de %un% joven | ya no es %art% joven combatiente impetuos%o% que fue | el tiempo lejos del servicio ha mermado sus capacidades}, {su destreza con la espada aún basta para vencer a cualquier joven fanfarrón | aún sabe cómo se lucha en el campo de batalla | su experiencia tiene pocos rivales | puede confiar en la experiencia de combate de toda una vida | está ansios%o% por formar de nuevo entre hermanos | ansía volver a la batalla | sus ganas de batalla están a la altura de su capacidad real para luchar | aún sabe un par de cosas sobre cómo sostener un muro de escudos}."
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\sellsword_background.nut
    // en = "Sellsword"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Sellswords are expensive, but a life of warfare has forged them into skilled fighters."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% the sellsword left the %companyname% and started his own mercenary company. As far as you know, it's a very successful venture and he often buddies up with the men of the %companyname% to work together."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% left the %companyname% and started his own competing company. The two companies clashed on opposite sides of a battle between nobles. The sellsword died when a mercenary from the %companyname% stove his head in with a hedge knight's helmet."
    // en base_es
    // context: sellsword_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: la 1.0 añade «en los contratos más lucrativamente peligrosos. El jamón y la cerveza nunca faltan alrededor de la fogata cuando ambas compañías se encuentran.», que el inglés no tiene; termina en «para trabajar juntos».
        en = "%name% the sellsword left the %companyname% and started her own mercenary company. As far as you know, it's a very successful venture and she often buddies up with the mercenaries of the %companyname% to work together."
        es = "%name%, la mercenaria, dejó a %companyname% y fundó su propia compañía de mercenarios. Hasta donde sabes, es una empresa muy próspera y a menudo se alía con los mercenarios de %companyname% para trabajar juntos."
    }
    // context: sellsword_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        // corrige base: la 1.0 añade «Sin rencores.», que el inglés no tiene, y pierde el «hedge» de «hedge knight» (caballero errante).
        en = "%name% left the %companyname% and started her own competing company. The two companies clashed on opposite sides of a battle between nobles. The sellsword died when a mercenary from the %companyname% stove her head in with a hedge knight's helmet."
        es = "%name% dejó a %companyname% y fundó su propia compañía rival. Las dos compañías se enfrentaron en bandos opuestos de una batalla entre nobles. La mercenaria murió cuando un mercenario de %companyname% le aplastó la cabeza con el yelmo de un caballero errante."
    }
    // context: sellsword_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{%fullname%'s worked as a sellsword since her father handed down his equipment. | %fullname% can't remember a time when she wasn't a sword for hire. | As a mercenary, %fullname% has never had to look long for work. | The literate talk about letting loose the dogs of war. %fullname% is one such hound. | In war, there is death and profit. %fullname% causes the former to earn the latter. | There has never been a better time for mercenaries like %name% to earn a crown or two. | After her husband ran off with her children, an angry %name% made a steady career as a nasty sellsword. | A decade ago %name% lost everything in a fire. She's been working as a sellsword ever since. | %name% always had the mind for violence and has pursued a long career as a sellsword. | Once dirt poor, %name% has earned a very tidy sum over the years as a sellsword. | %fullname% prefers to keep for herself whence she came, but her reputation as a sword for hire speaks for itself.} {Well experienced, she has traveled in the company of many outfits in her time. | Military campaigns are but notches in her belt. | From work as a lord's bodyguard to being an enforcer for a skeevy merchant, %name% has seen it all. | She once made a living off slaying the wild beasts that encroach on human settlements. | With a grim grin, she boasts she has slain all manner of living creatures. | Through plenty of use, the mercenary has learned a thing or two about weapons you didn't even know existed. | The sellsword is counting how many she has slain to this day and she appears to not be stopping any time soon. | With a sword and shield in hand, the mercenary appears to do what she does best for a living.} {The woman is no stranger to the fields of battle. | The woman is no stranger to the cruelties of war. | She is used to the harsh realities of mercenary life. | She is said to be a reliable cog in any shield wall. | Some say she can hold a battle line as well as an oak tree. | Rumors abound that the woman enjoys the sight of blood. | Without shame, she takes an uneasy pleasure in the misery of others on the battlefield. | Strangely, she seldom joins others around the campfire, instead keeping to herself. | The woman loves to tell a good tale about how she killed this thing or that. | Given a chance, the woman is quick to showcase a wide variety of fighting styles.} {As long as you have the coin, %name% is yours to command. | A true mercenary, %name% will fight anyone for the right price. | Displaying some fine sword skills, %name% says she can run any man through. | With but a hint of a nod, %name% agrees to join you if you have the crowns. | Excited for an opportunity to earn coin, %name% knocks her mug on the table.}"
        es = "{%fullname% ha trabajado como mercenaria desde que su padre le legó su equipo. | %fullname% no recuerda una época en la que no fuera una espada de alquiler. | Como mercenaria, %fullname% nunca ha tenido que buscar trabajo por mucho tiempo. | Los letrados hablan de soltar a los perros de la guerra. %fullname% es uno de esos sabuesos. | En la guerra hay muerte y beneficio. %fullname% provoca lo primero para ganar lo segundo. | Nunca ha habido mejor momento para que mercenarios como %name% se ganen una corona o dos. | Después de que su marido se fugara con sus hijos, una furiosa %name% labró una carrera estable como mercenaria despiadada. | Hace una década, %name% lo perdió todo en un incendio. Desde entonces trabaja como mercenaria. | %name% siempre tuvo inclinación por la violencia y ha seguido una larga carrera como mercenaria. | Antaño pobre de solemnidad, %name% ha ganado una suma muy considerable a lo largo de los años como mercenaria. | %fullname% prefiere guardarse de dónde viene, pero su reputación como espada de alquiler habla por sí sola.} {Con mucha experiencia, ha viajado con muchas bandas a lo largo de su vida. | Las campañas militares no son más que muescas en su cinturón. | Desde guardaespaldas de un señor hasta matona a sueldo de un mercader turbio, %name% lo ha visto todo. | En su día se ganó la vida matando a las bestias salvajes que acechan los asentamientos humanos. | Con una sonrisa sombría, presume de haber matado a toda clase de criaturas vivientes. | A base de mucho uso, la mercenaria ha aprendido un par de cosas sobre armas que ni sabías que existían. | La mercenaria lleva la cuenta de cuántos ha matado hasta hoy y no parece que vaya a parar pronto. | Con espada y escudo en mano, la mercenaria parece ganarse la vida haciendo lo que mejor sabe hacer.} {Esta mujer no es ajena a los campos de batalla. | Esta mujer no es ajena a las crueldades de la guerra. | Está acostumbrada a las duras realidades de la vida mercenaria. | Dicen que es una pieza fiable en cualquier muro de escudos. | Algunos dicen que aguanta una línea de batalla tan bien como un roble. | Abundan los rumores de que a esta mujer le gusta ver sangre. | Sin vergüenza alguna, disfruta de un modo inquietante con la desgracia ajena en el campo de batalla. | Curiosamente, rara vez se une a los demás junto a la fogata y prefiere quedarse a solas. | A esta mujer le encanta contar una buena historia sobre cómo mató esto o aquello. | En cuanto tiene ocasión, esta mujer no tarda en lucir una gran variedad de estilos de combate.} {Mientras tengas la moneda, %name% estará a tus órdenes. | Mercenaria de verdad, %name% luchará contra cualquiera por el precio justo. | Haciendo gala de un buen manejo de la espada, %name% asegura que puede atravesar a cualquier hombre. | Con apenas un asomo de asentimiento, %name% acepta unirse a ti si tienes las coronas. | Entusiasmada ante la oportunidad de ganar dinero, %name% golpea la mesa con su jarra.}"
    }
    // en = "\x7b%fullname%'s worked as a sellsword since his father handed down his equipment. | %fullname% can't remember a time when he wasn't a sword for hire. | As a mercenary, %fullname% has never had to look long for work. | The literate talk about letting loose the dogs of war. %fullname% is one such hound. | In war, there is death and profit. %fullname% causes the former to earn the latter. | There has never been a better time for mercenaries like %name% to earn a crown or two. | After his wife ran off with his children, an angry %name% made a steady career as a nasty sellsword. | A decade ago %name% lost everything in a fire. He's been working as a sellsword ever since. | %name% always had the mind for violence and has pursued a long career as a sellsword. | Once dirt poor, %name% has earned a very tidy sum over the years as a sellsword. | %fullname% prefers to keep for himself whence he came, but his reputation as a sword for hire speaks for itself.\x7d \x7bWell experienced, he has traveled in the company of many outfits in his time. | Military campaigns are but notches in his belt. | From work as a lord's bodyguard to being an enforcer for a skeevy merchant, %name% has seen it all. | He once made a living off slaying the wild beasts that encroach on human settlements. | With a grim grin, he boasts he has slain all manner of living creatures. | Through plenty of use, the mercenary has learned a thing or two about weapons you didn't even know existed. | The sellsword is counting how many he has slain to this day and he appears to not be stopping any time soon. | With a sword and shield in hand, the mercenary appears to do what he does best for a living.\x7d \x7bThe man is no stranger to the fields of battle. | The man is no stranger to the cruelties of war. | He is used to the harsh realities of mercenary life. | He is said to be a reliable cog in any shield wall. | Some say he can hold a battle line as well as an oak tree. | Rumors abound that the man enjoys the sight of blood. | Without shame, he takes an uneasy pleasure in the misery of others on the battlefield. | Strangely, he seldom joins others around the campfire, instead keeping to himself. | The man loves to tell a good tale about how he killed this thing or that. | Given a chance, the man is quick to showcase a wide variety of fighting styles.\x7d \x7bAs long as you have the coin, %name% is yours to command. | A true mercenary, %name% will fight anyone for the right price. | Displaying some fine swordsmanship, %name% says he can run any man through. | With but a hint of a nod, %name% agrees to join you if you have the crowns. | Excited for an opportunity to earn coin, %name% knocks his mug on the table.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\servant_background.nut
    // en = "Servant"
    // en base_es
    // context: servant_background.o.create.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "Servants are not used to hard labour, but do have good knowledge of more mundane activities."
        es = "Los sirvientes no están acostumbrados al trabajo duro, pero conocen bien las tareas más cotidianas."
    }
    // en = "As it turns out, %name% the servant had been stowing away every last crown he had earned with the %companyname%. When he had enough, he retired and bought himself some land and slowly worked his way up the social ladder. He died in a comfortable bed, surrounded by friends, family, and loyal servants."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% the servant grew tired of the sellsword life and left the company. He returned to serving nobility. When raiders attacked his liege's castle, the nobleman pushed the servant out the door with only a kitchen knife to defend himself with. He was found headless in a pile of broken chairs, a few dead raiders littered around him."
    // en base_es
    // context: servant_background.o.setGender.m.Name
    {
        en = "Housemaid"
        es = "Criada"
    }
    // context: servant_background.o.setGender.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "Housemaids are not used to hard labour, but do have good knowledge of more mundane activities."
        es = "Las criadas no están acostumbradas al trabajo duro, pero conocen bien las tareas más cotidianas."
    }
    // context: servant_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: «cada última corona» calca «every last crown»; en castellano es «hasta la última corona».
        en = "As it turns out, %name% the housemaids had been stowing away every last crown she had earned with the %companyname%. When she had enough, she retired and bought herself some land and slowly worked her way up the social ladder. She died in a comfortable bed, surrounded by friends, family, and loyal servants."
        es = "Resulta que %name%, la criada, había estado ahorrando hasta la última corona que ganó con %companyname%. Cuando tuvo suficiente, se retiró, se compró unas tierras y fue ascendiendo poco a poco en la escala social. Murió en una cama cómoda, rodeada de amigos, familiares y sirvientes leales."
    }
    // context: servant_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "%name% the servant grew tired of the sellsword life and left the company. She returned to serving nobility. When raiders attacked her liege's castle, the nobleman pushed the housemaid out the door with only a kitchen knife to defend herself with. She was found headless in a pile of broken chairs, a few dead raiders littered around her."
        es = "%name%, la sirvienta, se cansó de la vida de mercenaria y dejó la compañía. Volvió a servir a la nobleza. Cuando unos saqueadores atacaron el castillo de su señor, el noble empujó a la criada por la puerta con solo un cuchillo de cocina para defenderse. La encontraron decapitada en un montón de sillas rotas, con unos cuantos saqueadores muertos a su alrededor."
    }
    // context: servant_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: la 1.0 reutiliza aquí la versión sureña, pero el inglés del trasfondo norteño dice «lord», «brigands» y «wild boar»; debe ser «señor decadente», «bandidos» y «jabalí salvaje», no «visir», «nómadas» ni «hiena».
        // corrige base: «se fue en serio» calca «left in earnest», que significa que se marchó sin perder tiempo.
        en = "{Life is difficult. Moreso for some than others. | Some women can fall from grace. Other women have nowhere to fall to, having been born already on the ground. | If life is a throw of dice, maybe some are fools to be women rather than mice.} %name% {was a servant to a decadent lord. | served an abusive family where the kids played with fire. | was kidnapped by brigands and forced to serve their every. Last. Need. | worked feverishly for mad men who looked far too long at the stars.}  She rarely made a mistake about her place in the world. One day, though, her masters {beat her unconscious. When she awoke, she did so in the bed of a benevolent doctor who refused to return her to her 'employers'. Instead, %name% was free to go and her masters were told she had died. | set her free, no questions asked. Not one to dally on ceremony, %name% left in earnest. | invited her to a party. Believing she was a guest, she showed up in her finest attire - a shirt with hemmed sleeves and a billowy dress that hid her skeletal frame well. Unfortunately, she was but a show for the party - they gave her a wooden shield and sword, threw her into an arena with a wild boar, and took bets as they watched the horrific spectacle. She barely escaped the 'festivities'.} {%name% has since sworn to never 'serve' someone again. | The woman, though now free of her duties, still bears a great deal of humiliation and pain from her long, hard life.}"
        es = "{La vida es difícil. Más para algunos que para otros. | Algunas mujeres pueden caer en desgracia. Otras mujeres no tienen a dónde caer, pues ya nacieron en el suelo. | Si la vida es una tirada de dados, tal vez algunas sean tontas por ser mujeres en lugar de ratones.} %name% {fue sirvienta de un señor decadente. | sirvió a una familia abusiva donde los niños jugaban con fuego. | fue secuestrada por bandidos y obligada a satisfacer todas sus. Últimas. Necesidades. | trabajó febrilmente para locos que pasaban demasiado tiempo mirando las estrellas.} Rara vez se equivocaba acerca de su lugar en el mundo. Sin embargo, un día, sus amos {la golpearon hasta dejarla inconsciente. Cuando despertó, lo hizo en la cama de un médico benévolo que se negó a devolverla a sus 'empleadores'. En su lugar, %name% quedó libre y a sus amos se les dijo que había muerto. | la liberaron sin hacer preguntas. Poco dada a las ceremonias, %name% se marchó sin perder tiempo. | la invitaron a una fiesta. Creyendo que era una invitada, se presentó con su mejor atuendo: una camisa con mangas rematadas y un vestido vaporoso que ocultaba bien su cuerpo esquelético. Por desgracia, solo era el espectáculo de la fiesta: le dieron un escudo y una espada de madera, la arrojaron a un ruedo con un jabalí salvaje y apostaron mientras contemplaban el horrible espectáculo. A duras penas logró escapar de la 'festividad'.} {Desde entonces, %name% ha jurado no volver a 'servir' a nadie. | Esta mujer, aunque ya libre de sus deberes, todavía arrastra mucha humillación y dolor de su larga y dura vida.}"
    }
    // en = "\x7bLife is difficult. Moreso for some than others. | Some men can fall from grace. Other men have nowhere to fall to, having been born already on the ground. | If life is a throw of dice, maybe some are fools to be men rather than mice.\x7d %name% \x7bwas a servant to a decadent lord. | served an abusive family where the kids played with fire. | was kidnapped by brigands and forced to serve their every. Last. Need. | worked feverishly for mad men who looked far too long at the stars.\x7d  He rarely made a mistake about his place in the world. One day, though, his masters \x7bbeat him unconscious. When he awoke, he did so in the bed of a benevolent doctor who refused to return him to his 'employers'. Instead, %name% was free to go and his masters were told he had died. | set him free, no questions asked. Not one to dally on ceremony, %name% left in earnest. | invited him to a party. Believing he was a guest, he showed up in his finest attire - a shirt with hemmed sleeves and a billowy set of pantaloons that hid his skeletal frame well. Unfortunately, he was but a show for the party - they gave him a wooden shield and sword, threw him into an arena with a wild boar, and took bets as they watched the horrific spectacle. He barely escaped the 'festivities'.\x7d \x7b%name% has since sworn to never 'serve' someone again. | The man, though now free of his duties, still bears a great deal of humiliation and pain from his long, hard life.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\servant_southern_background.nut
    // context: servant_southern_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: «se fue en serio» calca «left in earnest», que significa que se marchó sin perder tiempo.
        en = "{Life is difficult. Moreso for some than others. | Some women can fall from grace. Other women have nowhere to fall to, having been born already on the ground. | If life is a throw of dice, maybe some are fools to be women rather than mice.} %name% {was a servant to a decadent vizier. | served an abusive family where the kids played with fire. | was kidnapped by nomads and forced to serve their every. Last. Need. | worked feverishly for mad men who looked far too long at the stars.}  She rarely made a mistake about her place in the world. One day, though, her masters {beat her unconscious. When she awoke, she did so in the bed of a benevolent doctor who refused to return her to her 'employers'. Instead, %name% was free to go and her masters were told she had died. | set her free, no questions asked. Not one to dally on ceremony, %name% left in earnest. | invited her to a party. Believing she was a guest, she showed up in her finest attire - a shirt with hemmed sleeves and a billowy dress that hid her skeletal frame well. Unfortunately, she was but a show for the party - they gave her a wooden shield and sword, threw her into an arena with a wild hyena, and took bets as they watched the horrific spectacle. She barely escaped the 'festivities'.} {%name% has since sworn to never 'serve' someone again. | The woman, though now free of her duties, still bears a great deal of humiliation and pain from her long, hard life.}"
        es = "{La vida es difícil. Más para algunos que para otros. | Algunas mujeres pueden caer en desgracia. Otras mujeres no tienen a dónde caer, pues ya nacieron en el suelo. | Si la vida es una tirada de dados, tal vez algunas sean tontas por ser mujeres en lugar de ratones.} %name% {fue sirvienta de un visir decadente. | sirvió a una familia abusiva donde los niños jugaban con fuego. | fue secuestrada por nómadas y obligada a satisfacer todas sus. Últimas. Necesidades. | trabajó febrilmente para locos que pasaban demasiado tiempo mirando las estrellas.} Rara vez se equivocaba acerca de su lugar en el mundo. Sin embargo, un día, sus amos {la golpearon hasta dejarla inconsciente. Cuando despertó, lo hizo en la cama de un médico benévolo que se negó a devolverla a sus 'empleadores'. En su lugar, %name% quedó libre y a sus amos se les dijo que había muerto. | la liberaron sin hacer preguntas. Poco dada a las ceremonias, %name% se marchó sin perder tiempo. | la invitaron a una fiesta. Creyendo que era una invitada, se presentó con su mejor atuendo: una camisa con mangas rematadas y un vestido vaporoso que ocultaba bien su cuerpo esquelético. Por desgracia, solo era el espectáculo de la fiesta: le dieron un escudo y una espada de madera, la arrojaron a un ruedo con una hiena salvaje y apostaron mientras contemplaban el horrible espectáculo. A duras penas logró escapar de la 'festividad'.} {Desde entonces, %name% ha jurado no volver a 'servir' a nadie. | Esta mujer, aunque ya libre de sus deberes, todavía arrastra mucha humillación y dolor de su larga y dura vida.}"
    }
    // en = "\x7bLife is difficult. Moreso for some than others. | Some men can fall from grace. Other men have nowhere to fall to, having been born already on the ground. | If life is a throw of dice, maybe some are fools to be men rather than mice.\x7d %name% \x7bwas a servant to a decadent vizier. | served an abusive family where the kids played with fire. | was kidnapped by nomads and forced to serve their every. Last. Need. | worked feverishly for mad men who looked far too long at the stars.\x7d  He rarely made a mistake about his place in the world. One day, though, his masters \x7bbeat him unconscious. When he awoke, he did so in the bed of a benevolent doctor who refused to return him to his 'employers'. Instead, %name% was free to go and his masters were told he had died. | set him free, no questions asked. Not one to dally on ceremony, %name% left in earnest. | invited him to a party. Believing he was a guest, he showed up in his finest attire - a shirt with hemmed sleeves and a billowy set of pantaloons that hid his skeletal frame well. Unfortunately, he was but a show for the party - they gave him a wooden shield and sword, threw him into an arena with a wild hyena, and took bets as they watched the horrific spectacle. He barely escaped the 'festivities'.\x7d \x7b%name% has since sworn to never 'serve' someone again. | The man, though now free of his duties, still bears a great deal of humiliation and pain from his long, hard life.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\shepherd_background.nut
    // en = "Shepherds are used to physical labor and known to keep the occasional wolf at bay with a sling."
    // en base_es
    // en = "It was unusual that a shepherd such as %name% ever found his way into a company of sellswords, but he did prove himself an able warrior. With injuries mounting, he eventually retired, returning to a meadow, staff in hand, and herding sheep until his final, peaceful days."
    // en base_es
    // en = "You'd think a shepherd would have no place in the company of sellsword and, eventually, %name% agreed. He left the %companyname% not long after you and last you heard he was back to tending his sheep. While most men left the company in poor spirits, %name%'s injuries did not bring down his docile lifestyle of staring at fluffy white critters about as dangerous as a bad dream."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Shepherd"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Humble"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Peaceful"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Goatman"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Hoofmind"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Sheep"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7b%name% was just a simple shepherd from a simple town, spending many years tending to his flock. | A lovely place like %townname% deserved a lovely shepherd like %name%. | %name% inherited his flock the same day he buried his father. | As a child, %name% stumbled upon a dead shepherd and the listless flock beside him. The boy took up the shepherd's staff and continued his work for many years. | More colorblind than a dog, %name% always enjoyed the company of color-friendly sheep. | When %name% fell from a tower, a flock of sheep broke his fall. He vowed to repay their sacrifice by being the safest shepherd in the land. | %name% found profit in bandying sheep about from one town to the next, selling their coats to tailors and skins to tanners. | Tending sheep was the easiest job %name% could find. | As harmless as the sheep he tends, %name% took to shepherding to find peace in the cruel world. | Never one to find good company amongst humans, %name% preferred the somber sapience of sheep. | Bullied as a child, %name% found peace in tending flocks of sheep. | The playfully obedient sheep of %name%'s life gave him the peace and calm from an otherwise rough upbringing. | Once mistaken for a \x7bprophet | new messiah\x7d, %name% escaped the \x7breligious hordes | angry inquisitors\x7d by disappearing into the vocation sheep shepherding. | Watching \x7bsheep | white blobs of wool\x7d munch on grass all day sounds boring, but to %name% it was bliss. | Enthralled by a sheep herding competition, %name% took to shepherding as a surprisingly competitive vocation. | Always a soft, kind boy, shepherding just made sense to the likes of %name%. | Escaping his abusive \x7bmother | father | sisters | brothers | uncle | aunt\x7d, %name% took the tranquility of being a shepherd.\x7d \x7bMixed up in a religious conflict between gods followers and cultists, his flock suffered the wrath of those looking for both scapegoats and sacrifices. | Once fending off \x7bbrigands | wolves\x7d with his walking stick, the shepherd wondered if maybe he was more physically capable than he once thought. | As time passed, the man felt \x7bas though his vocation had passed him by. | like his heart just wasn't in it anymore.\x7d \x7bHe mournfully retired | He hung up his shepherding stick\x7d and sought out other work. | Feeling as though he was seeing the world's beauty but not experiencing it in full, the man decided to abandon shepherding. | When hulking, furry beasts slaughtered his flock, the shepherd was left looking for vengeance. | Sadly, the man's sole companion, a shepherding dog, was killed by \x7bbrigands | orcs | wolves\x7d, leaving the peaceful man looking for revenge. | Caught in a loan shark's schemes, though, the shepherd suddenly needed more coin than his flock of sheep could ever provide. | However, the loneliness of his life finally got the shepherd. | But long days and nights by himself wore on the shepherd as they would any man. | But he could not escape the masculinity his father expected of him, and one day put down his walking stick to seek out a manlier vocation. | But one day, textiling while tending, he led every last sheep over a cliff. | But on a rainy afternoon he took one baaa too many: he had to do something beyond just stare at sheep all day. | One morning he awoke covered in sheep's blood, entrails, and bloody, entrails-laden wool. Wolves howled merrily in the distance. As it turned out, he had counted one too many sheep that night. | Unfortunately, rumors of what he did in the privacy of his flock were too embarrassing to face and he had to flee to greener, more accepting pastures. | Sadly, brigands drunk on violence stumbled upon his flock. Bessie, Little Ada, and even the newborn Goatsieg were bloodily dispatched.\x7d \x7bWhile stopping into town to think things over, %name% stumbled upon a call for mercenaries. With nothing to lose, he is ready to sign up. | The land had no place for a peaceful shepherd. It was time to move on to a new life. | A tiny, blood-rusted bell clings below %name%' neck. It is a relic of another life, and perhaps the sign of a new one. | He swears to still hear the bleating of his flock. For some reason, this does not inspire much confidence in his fighting skills. | Although peaceful as could be, without a flock the man is lost. | While hardly a fighter, the man knows how to keep a tight formation. | %name% knows the stars surprisingly well and can locate a sound in the darkness like a blind dog sniffing a treat. | Walking so much has given %name% sturdy legs, but the most combat experience he has is with a stick. | The world doesn't usually turn to shepherds in its time of need, but this is one very needy world at the moment. | Staring at the shepherd, you wonder just how bad things have gotten for such a man to be standing where he is. | %name% carries almost all weapons like they're walking sticks, and he has a bad habit of whacking the legs of others to move them along. | %name%'s humility is a welcome respite from the usual gungho brethren that become sellswords. | %name% looks like he wouldn't hurt a fly, but with good training you can see to it that he'll hurt a lot more than that. | %name% doesn't carry the murderous conviction of other sellswords, but like any man he can be trained up in all the right ways. | Some of the %companyname%'s men are little better than sheep. Maybe %name% has a place here after all.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\shepherd_southern_background.nut
    // en = "\x7b%name% was just a simple shepherd from a simple town, spending many years tending to his flock. | A lovely place like %townname% deserved a lovely shepherd like %name%. | %name% inherited his flock the same day he buried his father. | As a child, %name% stumbled upon a dead shepherd and the listless flock beside him. The boy took up the shepherd's staff and continued his work for many years. | More colorblind than a dog, %name% always enjoyed the company of color-friendly sheep. | When %name% fell from a tower, a flock of sheep broke his fall. He vowed to repay their sacrifice by being the safest shepherd in the land. | %name% found profit in bandying sheep about from one town to the next, selling their coats to tailors and skins to tanners. | Tending sheep was the easiest job %name% could find. | As harmless as the sheep he tends, %name% took to shepherding to find peace in the cruel world. | Never one to find good company amongst humans, %name% preferred the somber sapience of sheep. | Bullied as a child, %name% found peace in tending flocks of sheep. | The playfully obedient sheep of %name%'s life gave him the peace and calm from an otherwise rough upbringing. | Once mistaken for a \x7bprophet | new messiah\x7d, %name% escaped the \x7breligious hordes | angry inquisitors\x7d by disappearing into the vocation sheep shepherding. | Watching \x7bsheep | white blobs of wool\x7d munch on grass all day sounds boring, but to %name% it was bliss. | Enthralled by a sheep herding competition, %name% took to shepherding as a surprisingly competitive vocation. | Always a soft, kind boy, shepherding just made sense to the likes of %name%. | Escaping his abusive \x7bmother | father | sisters | brothers | uncle | aunt\x7d, %name% took the tranquility of being a shepherd.\x7d \x7bMixed up in a religious conflict between gods followers and cultists, his flock suffered the wrath of those looking for both scapegoats and sacrifices. | Once fending off \x7bbrigands | wolves\x7d with his walking stick, the shepherd wondered if maybe he was more physically capable than he once thought. | As time passed, the man felt \x7bas though his vocation had passed him by. | like his heart just wasn't in it anymore.\x7d \x7bHe mournfully retired | He hung up his shepherding stick\x7d and sought out other work. | Feeling as though he was seeing the world's beauty but not experiencing it in full, the man decided to abandon shepherding. | When hulking, furry beasts slaughtered his flock, the shepherd was left looking for vengeance. | Sadly, the man's sole companion, a shepherding dog, was killed by \x7bbrigands | orcs | wolves\x7d, leaving the peaceful man looking for revenge. | Caught in a loan shark's schemes, though, the shepherd suddenly needed more coin than his flock of sheep could ever provide. | However, the loneliness of his life finally got the shepherd. | But long days and nights by himself wore on the shepherd as they would any man. | But he could not escape the masculinity his father expected of him, and one day put down his walking stick to seek out a manlier vocation. | But one day, textiling while tending, he led every last sheep over a cliff. | But on a rainy afternoon he took one baaa too many: he had to do something beyond just stare at sheep all day. | Unfortunately, rumors of what he did in the privacy of his flock were too embarrassing to face and he had to flee to greener, more accepting pastures. | Sadly, nomads drunk on violence stumbled upon his flock. Bessie, Little Ada, and even the newborn Goatsieg were bloodily dispatched.\x7d \x7bWhile stopping into town to think things over, %name% stumbled upon a call for mercenaries. With nothing to lose, he is ready to sign up. | The land had no place for a peaceful shepherd. It was time to move on to a new life. | A tiny, blood-rusted bell clings below %name%' neck. It is a relic of another life, and perhaps the sign of a new one. | He swears to still hear the bleating of his flock. For some reason, this does not inspire much confidence in his fighting skills. | Although peaceful as could be, without a flock the man is lost. | While hardly a fighter, the man knows how to keep a tight formation. | %name% knows the stars surprisingly well and can locate a sound in the darkness like a blind dog sniffing a treat. | Walking so much has given %name% sturdy legs, but the most combat experience he has is with a stick. | The world doesn't usually turn to shepherds in its time of need, but this is one very needy world at the moment. | Staring at the shepherd, you wonder just how bad things have gotten for such a man to be standing where he is. | %name% carries almost all weapons like they're walking sticks, and he has a bad habit of whacking the legs of others to move them along. | %name%'s humility is a welcome respite from the usual gungho brethren that become sellswords. | %name% looks like he wouldn't hurt a fly, but with good training you can see to it that he'll hurt a lot more than that. | %name% doesn't carry the murderous conviction of other sellswords, but like any man he can be trained up in all the right ways. | Some of the %companyname%'s men are little better than sheep. Maybe %name% has a place here after all.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\slave_background.nut
    // en = "The indebted are a caste of de-facto slaves in the city states, and as such are not hired, but bought, and receive no daily wage."
    // en base_es
    // context: slave_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "%name% the indebted has had a rough life and you've both contributed to that and helped alleviate it in some way. You found %them% as a slave in the south, far from family and home. You 'hired' %them% essentially for free and worked %them% as an enslaved sellsword. After you left the %companyname%, %their% name was removed from the ledger of indebted and %they% was for all intents and purposes a free %person%. %They% stayed with the company and has been rising through its ranks ever since. You stand at an odd relation to the %person%. He's never thanked you, nor has %they% expressed ill."
        es = "%name%, %art% endeudad%o%, ha tenido una vida dura, y tú has contribuido a ello y a la vez has ayudado a aliviarla en cierto modo. %Lo% encontraste como esclav%o% en el sur, lejos de su familia y su hogar. %Lo% 'contrataste' prácticamente gratis y %lo% hiciste trabajar como mercenari%o% esclavizad%o%. Después de que dejaras a %companyname%, su nombre se borró del registro de endeudados y, a todos los efectos, pasó a ser %un% %hombre% libre. Se quedó en la compañía y desde entonces no ha dejado de ascender en sus filas. Tu relación con %el% es extraña. Nunca te ha dado las gracias, pero tampoco te ha deseado ningún mal."
    }
    // context: slave_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "With your retiring from the unsuccessful %companyname%, %name% the indebted from the north carried on with the company for a time. You got wind that the mercenary band ran into financial troubles and was selling off '%person% and material' to make ends meet. It seems %name%'s time with the company presumably ended sometime there, and %their% time as a slave started again."
        es = "Cuando te retiraste de %companyname% tras su fracaso, %name%, %art% endeudad%o% del norte, siguió un tiempo con la compañía. Te llegaron rumores de que la banda de mercenarios tenía problemas económicos y estaba vendiendo 'personal y material' para llegar a fin de mes. Parece que la etapa de %name% en la compañía terminó probablemente por entonces, y su vida de esclav%o% volvió a empezar."
    }
    // en = "the Enslaved"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Captive"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Pale"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Prisoner"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Kidnapped"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Unlucky"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Indebted"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Unfree"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Restrained"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Shackled"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Bound"
    // en base_es
    // en = "No morale check triggered for non-indebted allies upon dying"
    // en base_es
    // context: slave_background.o.getTooltip.ret.extend().text
    {
        en = "Will not take part in most events and can not be converted to a cultist"
        es = "No participará en la mayoría de los eventos y no puede convertirse en cultista"
    }
    // context: slave_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{You can tell %name% is a northerner simply by appearance. And %their% servitude in the south has come by way of being indebted to the Gilder whom %they% has transgressed with %their% faith in the heretical old gods. | %name% bears the features of a northerner, easily capturing the eye of passing men or women. It also happened to catch the attention of a priest who claimed the northerner was indebted to the Gilder and promptly sold the interloper into servitude. | A northerner, %name% was once a soldier sent south on patrol. Lost in the desert, %their% troop slowly dwindled until %they% was the last survivor. Manhunters caught %them% and brought %them% back from the brink, and of course sold %them% into servitude once %their% healed body was worth something. | Despite being a northerner and thus easily spotted, %name% unwisely sought the criminal life and was caught thieving pomegranates from a Vizier's garden. %they%'s lucky to have %their% head, but now serves as a commodity of labor on the slave markets.}"
        es = "{Basta con ver a %name% para saber que es del norte. Y su servidumbre en el sur se debe a que está en deuda con el Dorado, a quien ofendió con su fe en los heréticos viejos dioses. | %name% tiene los rasgos de la gente del norte, que atraen con facilidad la mirada de los hombres y mujeres que pasan. También llamaron la atención de un sacerdote, que afirmó que %art% norteñ%o% estaba en deuda con el Dorado y no tardó en vender %al% intrus%o% como esclav%o%. | Natural del norte, %name% fue en su día soldado, enviad%o% al sur de patrulla. Perdida en el desierto, su tropa fue menguando poco a poco hasta que solo quedó %el%. Unos Cazahombres %lo% capturaron y %lo% sacaron del borde de la muerte, y, por supuesto, %lo% vendieron como esclav%o% en cuanto su cuerpo curado valió algo. | Pese a ser del norte y, por tanto, fácil de reconocer, %name% se lanzó imprudentemente a la vida criminal y %lo% atraparon robando granadas del jardín de un visir. Tiene suerte de conservar la cabeza, pero ahora es mano de obra en venta en los mercados de esclavos.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\slave_barbarian_background.nut
    // en = "the Barbarian"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Northman"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Unruly"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\slave_southern_background.nut
    // en = "You purchased %name% as an indebted for almost no gold and continued to pay him a 'slave's wage' for his stay as a sellsword. He did make himself an effective fighter, no doubt believing it was better to be paid nothing and fight to stay alive than be paid nothing and give up and rot. After your departure, you heard that the %companyname% traveled south on a campaign and the indebted got a good chance to exact a fair bit of revenge on a number of enemies in his past. Thankfully, he does not consider you one such person despite having kept him enslaved."
    // en base_es
    // en = "You purchased %name% as an indebted and after your retiring, he went on with the %companyname%. Word of the mercenary band's problems have trickled in, but nothing about the indebted's current situation. Knowing how this world works, he has either been put into the vanguard as fodder or perhaps even been sold off to recoup profits. Either way, the world isn't easy on a sellsword, and it isn't easy on an indebted, and the man is unfortunately both."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Criminal"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Obedient"
    // en base_es
    // context: slave_southern_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{Much of the southern city states float atop the expendable bodies of prisoners of war, criminals, and indebted, throngs of people who have slighted the Gilder or His followers and must 'earn' salvation through hard work. %name% is one such unfortunate soul.} {Like a shocking many, %name% was not always a hunted woman. She worked as a traveling merchant until nomads ambushed her caravan. The nomads took her to a Vizier, pretending the woman a criminal, and sold her as a hunted woman. | Spotted for her beauty, %name% was kidnapped off the streets of %randomcitystate% and sold straight to a manipulative Vizier. She does not speak much of what all happened, but there is a sense manual labor was not her sole duty. | So great the religious transgressions of her predecessors, %name% was born into an indebted family, and it is uncertain how far back into her ancestry you must go before a truly free woman would be found. | Desperate to save her family from generational debt, %name% sold herself into indentured servitude to ensure her children have a life to live for themselves. | %name% swears she is from the north, but the deserts of the south have left her darkly tanned and, frankly, you've not much reason to believe the words of a former prisoner of war no matter where she's from. | A once sea-farer, %name% spent years traveling from harbor to harbor to drive the goods of opulent merchants. Those who gave her to you stated she has a criminal past in piracy. | %name% was accused of ravishing an old man and was given the option of execution or lifelong servitude. | Caught stealing from a fruit stall, %name% was pressed into lifelong servitude. | Fornications with 'non-men' led to %name%'s submission to servitude per the rules of the city-state in which she broke the laws. It was either that or become a eunuch, and you can hardly blame her for choosing the hard labor in this case.} {The hardships of her life, rather quaintly, may serve as an excellent cast from which to mold a proper mercenary. | Her servitude no doubt made the woman formidable in appearance, though it may be hard to say where her mind is at being what is essence an indentured sellsword. | Slaves for warriors are a usual sight in the southern cities and %name% might serve as a useful, albeit enslaved, sellsword yet. | You hope %name% could make a sound sellsword, but you have the feeling her primary allegiance is to that which any woman wishes to taste: freedom.}"
        es = "{Buena parte de las ciudades-estado del sur flota sobre los cuerpos prescindibles de prisioneros de guerra, criminales y endeudados, multitudes de personas que han ofendido al Dorado o a Sus seguidores y deben 'ganarse' la salvación con trabajo duro. %name% es una de esas almas desdichadas.} {Como tantísimas otras, %name% no siempre fue una mujer perseguida. Trabajaba como mercader ambulante hasta que unos nómadas emboscaron su caravana. Los nómadas la llevaron ante un visir, haciéndola pasar por criminal, y la vendieron como mujer perseguida. | Señalada por su belleza, %name% fue secuestrada en las calles de %randomcitystate% y vendida directamente a un visir manipulador. No habla mucho de todo lo que ocurrió, pero se intuye que el trabajo manual no era su única tarea. | Tan graves fueron las transgresiones religiosas de sus antepasados que %name% nació en una familia endeudada, y no se sabe cuánto habría que remontarse en su linaje para encontrar a una mujer verdaderamente libre. | Desesperada por librar a su familia de una deuda que pasa de generación en generación, %name% se vendió como sierva por contrato para asegurar que sus hijos tuvieran una vida propia. | %name% jura que es del norte, pero los desiertos del sur la han dejado muy morena y, francamente, no tienes muchos motivos para creer la palabra de una antigua prisionera de guerra, sea de donde sea. | Antigua navegante, %name% pasó años viajando de puerto en puerto transportando las mercancías de opulentos mercaderes. Quienes te la entregaron aseguraron que tiene un pasado criminal como pirata. | %name% fue acusada de violar a un anciano y le dieron a elegir entre la ejecución o la servidumbre de por vida. | Sorprendida robando en un puesto de fruta, %name% fue condenada a servidumbre de por vida. | Sus fornicaciones con 'no hombres' llevaron a %name% a la servidumbre, según las normas de la ciudad-estado cuyas leyes infringió. Era eso o convertirse en eunuco, y difícilmente puedes reprocharle que eligiera los trabajos forzados en este caso.} {Las penurias de su vida, curiosamente, podrían servir de molde excelente para forjar a una auténtica mercenaria. | Sin duda, la servidumbre le ha dado a esta mujer un aspecto formidable, aunque es difícil saber qué pasa por su cabeza siendo lo que en esencia es una mercenaria esclavizada. | Los esclavos guerreros son algo habitual en las ciudades del sur, y %name% aún podría servir como mercenaria útil, aunque esclavizada. | Esperas que %name% pueda ser una buena mercenaria, pero tienes la sensación de que su principal lealtad es a aquello que toda mujer desea probar: la libertad.}"
    }
    // en = "\x7bMuch of the southern city states float atop the expendable bodies of prisoners of war, criminals, and indebted, throngs of people who have slighted the Gilder or His followers and must 'earn' salvation through hard work. %name% is one such unfortunate soul.\x7d \x7bLike a shocking many, %name% was not always a hunted man. He worked as a traveling merchant until nomads ambushed his caravan. The nomads took him to a Vizier, pretending the man a criminal, and sold him as a hunted man. | Spotted for his handsomeness, %name% was kidnapped off the streets of %randomcitystate% and sold straight to a manipulative Vizier. He does not speak much of what all happened, but there is a sense manual labor was not his sole duty. | So great the religious transgressions of his predecessors, %name% was born into an indebted family, and it is uncertain how far back into his ancestry you must go before a truly free man would be found. | Desperate to save his family from generational debt, %name% sold himself into indentured servitude to ensure his wife and children have a life to live for themselves. | %name% swears he is from the north, but the deserts of the south have left him darkly tanned and, frankly, you've not much reason to believe the words of a former prisoner of war no matter where he's from. | A once sea-farer, %name% spent years as an oarmen traveling from harbor to harbor to drive the goods of opulent merchants. Those who gave him to you stated he has a criminal past in piracy. | %name% was accused of ravishing an old woman and was given the option of execution or lifelong servitude. | Caught stealing from a fruit stall, %name% was pressed into lifelong servitude. | Fornications with 'non-women' led to %name%'s submission to servitude per the rules of the city-state in which he broke the laws. It was either that or become a eunuch, and you can hardly blame him for choosing the hard labor in this case.\x7d \x7bThe hardships of his life, rather quaintly, may serve as an excellent cast from which to mold a proper mercenary. | His servitude no doubt made the man formidable in appearance, though it may be hard to say where his mind is at being what is essence an indentured sellsword. | Slaves for warriors are a usual sight in the southern cities and %name% might serve as a useful, albeit enslaved, sellsword yet. | You hope %name% could make a sound sellsword, but you have the feeling his primary allegiance is to that which any man wishes to taste: freedom.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // context: slave_southern_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "You purchased %name% as an indebted for almost no gold and continued to pay her a 'slave's wage' for her stay as a sellsword. She did make herself an effective fighter, no doubt believing it was better to be paid nothing and fight to stay alive than be paid nothing and give up and rot. After your departure, you heard that the %companyname% traveled south on a campaign and the indebted got a good chance to exact a fair bit of revenge on a number of enemies in her past. Thankfully, she does not consider you one such person despite having kept her enslaved."
        es = "Adquiriste a %name% como endeudada por casi nada de oro y seguiste pagándole un 'salario de esclava' durante su estancia como mercenaria. Se convirtió en una luchadora eficaz, convencida sin duda de que era mejor no cobrar nada y luchar por seguir con vida que no cobrar nada, rendirse y pudrirse. Tras tu marcha, te enteraste de que %companyname% viajó al sur en campaña y la endeudada tuvo buena ocasión de cobrarse una buena dosis de venganza contra varios enemigos de su pasado. Por suerte, no te considera una de esas personas pese a haberla mantenido esclavizada."
    }
    // context: slave_southern_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        // corrige base: «este hombre era ambas cosas» pone en pasado lo que el inglés dice en presente («the man is unfortunately both»); debería ser «es».
        en = "You purchased %name% as an indebted and after your retiring, she went on with the %companyname%. Word of the mercenary band's problems have trickled in, but nothing about the indebted's current situation. Knowing how this world works, she has either been put into the vanguard as fodder or perhaps even been sold off to recoup profits. Either way, the world isn't easy on a sellsword, and it isn't easy on an indebted, and the woman is unfortunately both."
        es = "Adquiriste a %name% como endeudada y, después de tu retiro, siguió con %companyname%. Han llegado rumores de los problemas de la banda de mercenarios, pero nada sobre la situación actual de la endeudada. Sabiendo cómo funciona este mundo, o bien la han puesto en la vanguardia como carne de cañón, o quizá incluso la han vendido para recuperar ganancias. Sea como sea, el mundo no es fácil para una mercenaria, ni lo es para una endeudada, y por desgracia esta mujer es ambas cosas."
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\squire_background.nut
    // en = "Squires usually have received some training in warfare, and often have a high resolve to excel in what they do."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% the squire eventually left the %companyname%. You've heard that he's since been knighted. No doubt he is sitting happy as a plum wherever he is."
    // en base_es
    // en = "The squire, %name%, eventually departed the %companyname%. He intended to return home and become knighted, fulfilling his lifelong dream. Cruel politics got in the way and not only was he not knighted, he was stripped of his squire duties. Word has it he hanged himself from a barn's rafters."
    // en base_es
    // context: squire_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "%name% the squire eventually left the %companyname%. You've heard that she's since been knighted. No doubt she is sitting happy as a plum wherever she is."
        es = "%name%, la escudera, acabó dejando a %companyname%. Has oído que desde entonces ha sido nombrada caballero. Sin duda, está sentada feliz como una ciruela dondequiera que esté."
    }
    // context: squire_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "The squire, %name%, eventually departed the %companyname%. She intended to return home and become knighted, fulfilling her lifelong dream. Cruel politics got in the way and not only was she not knighted, she was stripped of her squire duties. Word has it she hanged herself from a barn's rafters."
        es = "La escudera, %name%, acabó marchándose de %companyname%. Tenía la intención de volver a casa y ser nombrada caballero, cumpliendo el sueño de toda su vida. La cruel política se interpuso en su camino: no solo no fue nombrada caballero, sino que además la despojaron de sus deberes de escudera. Se dice que se ahorcó de las vigas de un granero."
    }
    // context: squire_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: errata «desafiear» (desafiar); además «para desafiear en un duelo a su señor» añade «a su señor», que el inglés no tiene («came to %townname% for a duel»).
        // corrige base: «caballero carmesí» y luego «caballero rojo» para el mismo «red knight»; mejor unificar en «caballero rojo».
        // corrige base: «hombres justos como %name%» añade «justos», que el inglés no tiene; y sobra la coma tras «%name%,» en la primera variante.
        en = "{A young squire, %name% dutifully accompanied her knight to many battles. | Squire to a harsh knight, %name% spent her days running errands for her lordship. | Although a squire, %name%'s life largely meant guarding prisoners of war, much to her chagrin. | Squire to a knight, sure, but %name% mostly cleaned latrines, fed dogs, and got far too much use out of a shinebox.} {One night, strange, shuffling men silhouetted the moonlit horizon. Alarm bells met their moans and an hour later half of %townname% lay in ruin. | While traveling, brigands attacked her lordship's wagon-train. Swords were drawn, heads were halved, and when it was all said and done the squire had failed: everyone she was supposed to protect lay dead. | But one evening a horde of ferocious, furred creatures came down upon her lord's keep. In desperation, %name% let a group of prisoners free, hoping they would aid her in combat. Instead, they slew her lordship and ran off into the night. The squire, bravely, managed to survive, a dozen husky corpses at her feet, but the battle left her alone and without purpose. | Angered by a horrible crime in %townname%, she took matters into her own hands, personally slaying the criminal. A just act, but also an improper one. The young squire was banished for her insubordination. | When a devilish red knight came to %townname% for a duel, %name%'s knight proved far too sick to fight. After downing a mug of liquid confidence, %name% donned her lordship's armor and faced the red knight herself. With a sword slash so fast it rang the very air, %name% slew her opponent down.} {Now there was only one task left for her - to attain knighthood. | Now the squire seeks the company of good folk with which to again prove herself worthy of being a knight. | As war ravages the land, there is now plenty of opportunity to put her skills to use. | Though a bit too earnest, there is no doubt the world needs women like %name%.}"
        es = "{Joven escudera, %name% acompañó con diligencia a su caballero en muchas batallas. | Escudera de un caballero severo, %name% pasaba los días haciendo recados para su señoría. | Aunque era escudera, la vida de %name% consistía sobre todo en custodiar prisioneros de guerra, para su disgusto. | Escudera de un caballero, sí, pero %name% sobre todo limpiaba letrinas, daba de comer a los perros y le daba demasiado uso a una caja de lustrar.} {Una noche, unas siluetas extrañas que arrastraban los pies se recortaron en el horizonte iluminado por la luna. Las campanas de alarma respondieron a sus gemidos y, una hora después, la mitad de %townname% yacía en ruinas. | Durante un viaje, unos bandidos atacaron el convoy de su señoría. Se desenvainaron espadas, se partieron cabezas y, cuando todo terminó, la escudera había fracasado: todos a quienes debía proteger yacían muertos. | Pero una noche, una horda de feroces criaturas peludas cayó sobre la fortaleza de su señor. Desesperada, %name% liberó a un grupo de prisioneros con la esperanza de que la ayudaran en el combate. En cambio, mataron a su señoría y huyeron en la noche. La escudera, con valentía, logró sobrevivir, con una docena de cadáveres robustos a sus pies, pero la batalla la dejó sola y sin propósito. | Indignada por un crimen horrible en %townname%, se tomó la justicia por su mano y mató personalmente al criminal. Un acto justo, pero también improcedente. La joven escudera fue desterrada por su insubordinación. | Cuando un diabólico caballero rojo llegó a %townname% en busca de un duelo, el caballero de %name% resultó estar demasiado enfermo para luchar. Tras beberse una jarra de confianza líquida, %name% se puso la armadura de su señoría y se enfrentó ella misma al caballero rojo. Con un tajo tan rápido que hizo vibrar el mismo aire, %name% abatió a su oponente.} {Ahora solo le quedaba una tarea: obtener la investidura de caballero. | Ahora la escudera busca la compañía de buena gente con la que demostrar de nuevo que es digna de ser caballero. | Mientras la guerra asola la tierra, hay muchas oportunidades de poner a prueba su destreza. | Aunque es demasiado sincera, no cabe duda de que el mundo necesita mujeres como %name%.}"
    }
    // context: squire_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: errata «desafiear» (desafiar); además «para desafiear en un duelo a su señor» añade «a su señor», que el inglés no tiene («came to %townname% for a duel»).
        // corrige base: «caballero carmesí» y luego «caballero rojo» para el mismo «red knight»; mejor unificar en «caballero rojo».
        // corrige base: «hombres justos como %name%» añade «justos», que el inglés no tiene; y sobra la coma tras «%name%,» en la primera variante.
        en = "{A young squire, %name% dutifully accompanied his knight to many battles. | Squire to a harsh knight, %name% spent his days running errands for his lordship. | Although a squire, %name%'s life largely meant guarding prisoners of war, much to his chagrin. | Squire to a knight, sure, but %name% mostly cleaned latrines, fed dogs, and got far too much use out of a shinebox.} {One night, strange, shuffling men silhouetted the moonlit horizon. Alarm bells met their moans and an hour later half of %townname% lay in ruin. | While traveling, brigands attacked his lordship's wagon-train. Swords were drawn, heads were halved, and when it was all said and done the squire had failed: everyone he was supposed to protect lay dead. | But one evening a horde of ferocious, furred creatures came down upon his lord's keep. In desperation, %name% let a group of prisoners free, hoping they would aid him in combat. Instead, they slew his lordship and ran off into the night. The squire, bravely, managed to survive, a dozen husky corpses at his feet, but the battle left him alone and without purpose. | Angered by a horrible crime in %townname%, he took matters into his own hands, personally slaying the criminal. A just act, but also an improper one. The young squire was banished for his insubordination. | When a devilish red knight came to %townname% for a duel, %name%'s knight proved far too sick to fight. After downing a mug of liquid confidence, %name% donned his lordship's armor and faced the red knight himself. With a sword slash so fast it rang the very air, %name% slew his opponent down.} {Now there was only one task left for him - to attain knighthood. | Now the squire seeks the company of good folk with which to again prove himself worthy of being a knight. | As war ravages the land, there is now plenty of opportunity to put his skills to use. | Though a bit too earnest, there is no doubt the world needs men like %name%.}"
        es = "{Joven escudero, %name% acompañó con diligencia a su caballero en muchas batallas. | Escudero de un caballero severo, %name% pasaba los días haciendo recados para su señoría. | Aunque era escudero, la vida de %name% consistía sobre todo en custodiar prisioneros de guerra, para su disgusto. | Escudero de un caballero, sí, pero %name% sobre todo limpiaba letrinas, daba de comer a los perros y le daba demasiado uso a una caja de lustrar.} {Una noche, unas siluetas extrañas que arrastraban los pies se recortaron en el horizonte iluminado por la luna. Las campanas de alarma respondieron a sus gemidos y, una hora después, la mitad de %townname% yacía en ruinas. | Durante un viaje, unos bandidos atacaron el convoy de su señoría. Se desenvainaron espadas, se partieron cabezas y, cuando todo terminó, el escudero había fracasado: todos a quienes debía proteger yacían muertos. | Pero una noche, una horda de feroces criaturas peludas cayó sobre la fortaleza de su señor. Desesperado, %name% liberó a un grupo de prisioneros con la esperanza de que lo ayudaran en el combate. En cambio, mataron a su señoría y huyeron en la noche. El escudero, con valentía, logró sobrevivir, con una docena de cadáveres robustos a sus pies, pero la batalla lo dejó solo y sin propósito. | Indignado por un crimen horrible en %townname%, se tomó la justicia por su mano y mató personalmente al criminal. Un acto justo, pero también improcedente. El joven escudero fue desterrado por su insubordinación. | Cuando un diabólico caballero rojo llegó a %townname% en busca de un duelo, el caballero de %name% resultó estar demasiado enfermo para luchar. Tras beberse una jarra de confianza líquida, %name% se puso la armadura de su señoría y se enfrentó él mismo al caballero rojo. Con un tajo tan rápido que hizo vibrar el mismo aire, %name% abatió a su oponente.} {Ahora solo le quedaba una tarea: obtener la investidura de caballero. | Ahora el escudero busca la compañía de buena gente con la que demostrar de nuevo que es digno de ser caballero. | Mientras la guerra asola la tierra, hay muchas oportunidades de poner a prueba su destreza. | Aunque es demasiado sincero, no cabe duda de que el mundo necesita hombres como %name%.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\swordmaster_background.nut
    // context: swordmaster_background.o.create.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "A swordmaster excels in melee combat like no other, but may be vulnerable at range. Age may have taken a toll on %their% physical attributes and may continue to do so. Swordmasters fight smart and conserve their strength which allows them to have a reduced impact on initiative due to fatigue."
        es = "%Un% maestr%o% espadachín destaca como nadie en el combate cuerpo a cuerpo, pero puede ser vulnerable a distancia. La edad puede haber hecho mella en sus atributos físicos y puede seguir haciéndolo. Los maestros espadachines luchan con inteligencia y ahorran fuerzas, por lo que la Fatiga reduce menos su Iniciativa."
    }
    // context: swordmaster_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: la 1.0 añade «valiente», «recientemente acusado de traición» y «en el arte de la esgrima», que el inglés no tiene («secretly training a nobleman's daughter»).
        en = "The finest swordsman you'd ever seen, %name% the old swordmaster was a natural addition to the %companyname%. But a %person% can't fight forever. Despite the company's growing success, it was becoming readily obvious that the swordmaster just could not physically do it anymore. %They% retired to a nice plot of land and is enjoying some time to %themselves%. Or so you thought. You went out to go see the %person% and found %them% secretly training a nobleman's daughter. You promised to keep it a secret."
        es = "La mejor espada que hayas visto jamás, %name%, %art% viej%o% maestr%o% espadachín, fue una incorporación natural a %companyname%. Pero nadie puede luchar para siempre. A pesar del creciente éxito de la compañía, resultaba cada vez más evidente que %art% maestr%o% espadachín ya no podía con ello físicamente. Se retiró a una bonita parcela de tierra y está disfrutando de un tiempo para sí. O eso creías. Fuiste a ver%lo% y %lo% encontraste entrenando en secreto a la hija de un noble. Prometiste guardar el secreto."
    }
    // context: swordmaster_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "A shame that %name% the swordmaster had to spend %their% twilight years in a declining mercenary company. %They% retired, stating %they% just could not physically do it anymore. You think %they% was just letting the %companyname% down easy, because a week later %they% slew ten would-be brigands on the side of a road without breaking a sweat. Last you heard, %they% was training ungrateful princes in the art of swordfighting."
        es = "Es una pena que %name%, %art% maestr%o% espadachín, tuviera que pasar el ocaso de su vida en una compañía de mercenarios en declive. Se retiró alegando que físicamente ya no podía más. Crees que solo intentaba que %companyname% no se lo tomara a mal, porque una semana después mató a diez aspirantes a bandido al borde de un camino sin despeinarse. Lo último que supiste es que estaba enseñando el arte de la esgrima a príncipes desagradecidos."
    }
    // en = "the Legend"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Old Guard"
    // en base_es
    // context: swordmaster_background.o.getTooltip.ret.push().text
    {
        en = "At all times your Initiative is reduced only by [color=%negative%]50%[/color] of your accumulated Fatigue, instead of all of it. Stacks with [color=%perk%]Relentless[/color]"
        es = "En todo momento, tu Iniciativa solo se reduce en un [color=%positive%]50%[/color] de tu Fatiga acumulada, en lugar de en su totalidad. Se acumula con [color=%perk%]Implacable[/color]"
    }
    // context: swordmaster_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{%name% fights like a fish practices swimming. | %name% isn't just a %person%'s handle, it's a myth. A name used in place of words like war, combat, and death. | To say, 'You move like %name%' is, perhaps, the greatest honor a man can bestow upon a fellow warrior. | %name% is considered to be one of the most dangerous swordsmen to have ever walked the earth.} {Much of %their% life is founded in myth: stories like how %they% dismantled a realm by challenging a king and all %their% guardsmen to a duel - and besting them with one hand. | Supposedly, %they% fought twenty men in %their% own garden, slowly picking and pruning %their% tomatoes with the same blade %they% was using to kill. | Some say %they% was left to sea for three-hundred days and there %they% learned - balancing on a piece of flotsam - how to move, how to fight, and how to survive. | A story goes that %their% family was murdered and %they% knew not by whom. Wanting to be ready if %they% came across those responsible, %they% taught %themselves% to be good enough with a blade to kill anyone. | Raised by a one-armed father, %they% first learned how to fight with limitations. By the time %they% started using both hands %they% could already kill anybody with just one.} {Unfortunately, time and age have withered %name% into a shell of %their% former self. | During the orc invasions, %name% managed to kill a dozen greenskins singlehandedly. Sadly, an impossible feat does not come without a price: %their% sword-hand lost three fingers and %their% lead foot's achilles was severed. | Sadly, a horde of drunks fell upon %their% home, each hoping to become infamous by killing the famous swordsman. %They% slew them all, but not before taking irreversible injuries. | Legend has it that %they% quarreled with a foul beast of monstrous proportions. %They% waves the notion away with a fingerless hand and a scarred wink. | While teaching royalty how to fight, a coup that swept the entire realm had %them% running for %their% life. | Hired to teach noble heirs fighting skills, it wasn't long until %they% was embroiled in a web of intrigue and backstabbing, and had to leave as long as %they% still could.} {Now the old swordsman just looks to spend the rest of %their% fighting knowledge on the field. | While %they%'s lost %their% edge, the %person% is still plenty dangerous and some say %they're% looking to find a student before %they% dies. | A master in the martial arts %they% may be, every movement %they% makes is echoed by the cracking of old bones. | Depressed and without purpose, %name% now finds meaning in simply blending in with the very men %they% used to teach. | The %person% makes it impossible to get through %their% defense, countering everything offered, but %they% no longer has the jump in %their% step to attack back. Admirable, but sad. | Given a sword, the old guard spins and twirls it in an impressive demonstration. When %they% plants it in the ground, %they% leans on the pommel to catch %their% breath. Not so impressive. | The %person% has been robbed of %their% athleticism, but %their% knowledge has turned swordfighting into mathematics.}"
        es = "{%name% lucha con la misma naturalidad con la que nada un pez. | %name% no es solo el nombre de una persona, es un mito. Un nombre que se usa en lugar de palabras como guerra, combate y muerte. | Decir 'Te mueves como %name%' es, quizá, el mayor honor que un hombre puede conceder a otro guerrero. | %name% está considerad%o% entre los espadachines más peligrosos que jamás hayan pisado la tierra.} {Buena parte de su vida se basa en mitos: historias como la de cómo desmanteló un reino desafiando a duelo a un rey y a todos sus guardias... y venciéndolos con una sola mano. | Supuestamente, luchó contra veinte hombres en su propio huerto, recogiendo y podando tranquilamente sus tomates con la misma hoja con la que mataba. | Algunos dicen que pasó trescientos días a la deriva en el mar y que allí aprendió, manteniendo el equilibrio sobre unos restos flotantes, a moverse, a luchar y a sobrevivir. | Cuenta una historia que asesinaron a su familia sin que supiera quién lo hizo. Queriendo estar preparad%o% por si se topaba con los responsables, aprendió por su cuenta a manejar la espada lo bastante bien como para matar a cualquiera. | Criad%o% por un padre manco, primero aprendió a luchar con limitaciones. Para cuando empezó a usar ambas manos, ya podía matar a cualquiera con una sola.} {Por desgracia, el tiempo y la edad han marchitado a %name% hasta dejar%lo% en una sombra de lo que fue. | Durante las invasiones orcas, %name% logró matar sin ayuda a una docena de pieles verdes. Por desgracia, una hazaña imposible no sale gratis: su mano de la espada perdió tres dedos y le cortaron el tendón de Aquiles del pie adelantado. | Por desgracia, una horda de borrachos cayó sobre su casa, cada uno con la esperanza de hacerse un nombre matando a una leyenda de la espada. Los mató a todos, pero no sin sufrir heridas irreversibles. | Cuenta la leyenda que se enfrentó a una bestia inmunda de proporciones monstruosas. Descarta la idea con un gesto de su mano sin dedos y un guiño lleno de cicatrices. | Mientras enseñaba a luchar a la realeza, un golpe de Estado que barrió todo el reino %lo% obligó a huir para salvar la vida. | Contratad%o% para enseñar a luchar a herederos nobles, no tardó en verse envuelt%o% en una red de intrigas y puñaladas por la espalda, y tuvo que marcharse mientras aún podía.} {Ahora la vieja espada solo busca gastar en el campo de batalla lo que le queda de su saber marcial. | Aunque ha perdido filo, sigue siendo muy peligros%o%, y algunos dicen que busca un discípulo antes de morir. | Puede que sea maestr%o% en las artes marciales, pero cada movimiento que hace va acompañado del crujido de huesos viejos. | Deprimid%o% y sin propósito, %name% encuentra ahora sentido en confundirse sin más entre los mismos hombres a los que antes enseñaba. | Es imposible atravesar su defensa, pues responde a todo lo que se le lanza, pero ya no tiene la agilidad necesaria para contraatacar. Admirable, pero triste. | Con una espada en la mano, la vieja gloria la hace girar y voltear en una demostración impresionante. Cuando la clava en el suelo, se apoya en el pomo para recuperar el aliento. No tan impresionante. | Le han robado la agilidad física, pero su saber ha convertido la esgrima en matemáticas.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\tailor_background.nut
    // en = "Tailor"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Tailors are not used to hard physical labor."
    // en base_es
    // en = "What was a tailor doing in a mercenary company? A good question, but %name% certainly answered it well by killing so many enemies they could've made an epic tapestry out of story. After a few good years in the company, he eventually left to start up a business creating clothes for nobility. His name is world-renowned, well, the known-world-renowned, and he gets so much business he's making a very different killing these days."
    // en base_es
    // en = "A tailor at heart, it didn't take much to compel %name% to bail from the quickly sinking company. He left to go start a business, but was kidnapped along the way by a group of brigands. When they threatened to kill him, he pretended to be a simple and weak tailor and showed his talents in creating clothes. Impressed, the raggedly dressed outlaws took him into their band. A few days later they were all dead and this 'meek' man walked out of their camp with a bit of red on him. He started his business a week later and is doing well to this day."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Tailor"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Particular"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Fine"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Silkworm"
    // en base_es
    // context: tailor_background.o.setGender.m.Name
    {
        en = "Seamstress"
        es = "Costurera"
    }
    // context: tailor_background.o.setGender.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "Seamstresses are not used to hard physical labor."
        es = "Las costureras no están acostumbradas al trabajo físico duro."
    }
    // context: tailor_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: «mundialmente conocido, bueno, conocido en todo el mundo» repite lo mismo y pierde el chiste de «the known-world-renowned» (en todo el mundo conocido).
        // corrige base: «está teniendo un éxito muy diferente» pierde el juego de palabras de «making a very different killing» (forrarse / matar).
        en = "What was a Seamstress doing in a mercenary company? A good question, but %name% certainly answered it well by killing so many enemies they could've made an epic tapestry out of story. After a few good years in the company, she eventually left to start up a business creating clothes for nobility. Her name is world-renowned, well, the known-world-renowned, and she gets so much business she's making a very different killing these days."
        es = "¿Qué hacía una costurera en una compañía de mercenarios? Buena pregunta, pero %name% la respondió con creces matando a tantos enemigos que con su historia podría haberse tejido un tapiz épico. Tras unos buenos años en la compañía, acabó marchándose para montar un negocio de ropa para la nobleza. Su nombre es famoso en todo el mundo, bueno, en todo el mundo conocido, y tiene tanta clientela que estos días arrasa de una forma muy distinta."
    }
    // context: tailor_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "A tailor at heart, it didn't take much to compel %name% to bail from the quickly sinking company. She left to go start a business, but was kidnapped along the way by a group of brigands. When they threatened to kill her, she pretended to be a simple and weak tailor and showed her talents in creating clothes. Impressed, the raggedly dressed outlaws took her into their band. A few days later they were all dead and this 'meek' woman walked out of their camp with a bit of red on her. She started her business a week later and is doing well to this day."
        es = "Sastra de corazón, no hizo falta mucho para convencer a %name% de abandonar la compañía, que se hundía a toda prisa. Se marchó para montar un negocio, pero por el camino la secuestró un grupo de bandidos. Cuando amenazaron con matarla, fingió ser una sastra simple y débil y les mostró su talento para confeccionar ropa. Impresionados, los forajidos harapientos la aceptaron en su banda. Unos días después estaban todos muertos y aquella mujer 'mansa' salió de su campamento con algo de rojo encima. Abrió su negocio una semana después y le va bien hasta el día de hoy."
    }
    // context: tailor_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{%name% was always curious about fabrics, seeing more science in a linen cloth than {a diviner would in the sands of the desert. | a haruspex would in a toad's entrails. | an alchemist would in a mortar and pestle.} | %name% was always an odd girl growing up, fancying a good silk waistcoat instead of the boy beneath it. | Daughter to a {milling mother | fine lady | baroness | farmhand}, %name%'s turn toward fashioning clothes was a surprise to all. | While %name%'s sisters fancied being warriors and heroes, %name% thought of herself as a future dresser of kings. | %name% spent much of her youth in the company of boys, but not for the reasons one might think. | %name% always fancied animals, particularly how they would look as a good coat or scarf. | As tunics and shirts grew popular, %name% turned to seamstressing to make a crown or two. | With a surge in pantaloons popularity, %name% went from being a tanner to a seamstress to make more money. | %name% hails from a faraway land where how a man dresses is more important than how he fights. | Seamstressing is the science of colors and fabrics, by which standards %name% is renowned. | Good with measuring and calculating, %name% turned her mathematical prowess to seamstressing to earn as much as she could. | %name%'s career in seamstressing started when her mother pushed her into the vocation to dodge a passing noble's attentions. | %name% took up seamstressing to honor her father, a tailor who was killed by an unhappy customer. | Widowed by war, %name%'s mother taught her how to put her hands to better use in seamstressing instead of killing.} {When raiders attacked her home, %name% dressed everyone up in clever disguises. The town was destroyed, but not a soul was lost. | She spent many years dressing royalty until a fashion faux pas led her being exiled. | Unfortunately, a woman fancying a good fabric, as %name% is wont to do, left the seamstress ostracized from many a village. | She tried to make her break in the big cities, but sadly she just could not compete with the other seamstresses. | When a lord organized an army, %name% handled the clothes, giving the soldiers proper uniforms. | But a fierce competition between seamstresses led to a linen-wrapped deadman and %name% coincidentally leaving her shop behind. | Sadly, robbers ransacked her shop and, with the wars going on, it would be impossible to restock. | But when she sheared a sheep that did not belong to her, %name% was kicked out of town. | She once choked out a would-be thief with a cord of measuring wire. So she says, anyway. | But dressing unlikeable and unfriendly nobility eventually {bored her. | wore on her.} | Once tasked with making a tunic embroidered with epic feats, %name% wondered what the outside world was really like. | Designing a dress adorned with {epic quests | epic feats}, %name% wondered if maybe she should be the one they wove stories about.} Now the seamstress looks for a new life, no matter where it takes her. {Maybe she can dress the unit well, or something. | She's particular and peculiar, peppering everyone with clothing criticisms. | She's no natural soldier, but she appraises a man's attire as if he's about to go to war with it. | The way she measures and calculates for dressing, it's too bad %name% wasn't a siege engineer. | While hardly a soldier, %name%'s earnest love for seamstressing is to be admired. | %name%'s knowledge of various cloths is seriously impressive. | A bit on the nimby-pimbly side, %name% has the footwork of a swordfighter, but the swordfighting of a soft breeze. | %name% would seem very out of place in a suit of armor, but boy is she going to need one. | As it turns out, %name% can in fact make a silk purse out of a sow's ear. | Don't let her vocation fool you, %name% is more deft with her hands than some {cardsharks | jugglers | pickpockets}. | Seamstresses don't seem fit for combat, but then again neither do most of the men you run across these days. | A seamstress seems ill-fit for combat, yet for some reason you find the finest soldiers in the strangest of places. | With an eye {for calculations | for measuring}, %name% is a lot smarter than she lets on at first glance.}"
        es = "{%name% siempre sintió curiosidad por las telas y veía más ciencia en un paño de lino que {un adivino en las arenas del desierto. | un arúspice en las entrañas de un sapo. | un alquimista en un mortero.} | De niña, %name% siempre fue una chica rara, que se fijaba más en un buen chaleco de seda que en el muchacho que lo llevaba. | Hija de {una madre molinera | una dama distinguida | una baronesa | una jornalera}, el giro de %name% hacia la confección de ropa sorprendió a todos. | Mientras las hermanas de %name% soñaban con ser guerreras y heroínas, %name% se imaginaba como futura modista de reyes. | %name% pasó gran parte de su juventud en compañía de chicos, pero no por las razones que uno pensaría. | A %name% siempre le gustaron los animales, sobre todo imaginar cómo quedarían convertidos en un buen abrigo o una bufanda. | Cuando las túnicas y las camisas se pusieron de moda, %name% se dedicó a la costura para ganarse una corona o dos. | Con el auge de los pantalones bombachos, %name% pasó de curtidora a costurera para ganar más dinero. | %name% procede de una tierra lejana donde cómo viste un hombre importa más que cómo lucha. | La costura es la ciencia de los colores y las telas, y en ella %name% goza de renombre. | Hábil midiendo y calculando, %name% puso su destreza matemática al servicio de la costura para ganar todo lo que pudiera. | La carrera de costurera de %name% empezó cuando su madre la empujó al oficio para librarla de las atenciones de un noble de paso. | %name% se hizo costurera para honrar a su padre, un sastre al que mató un cliente descontento. | Viuda por la guerra, la madre de %name% le enseñó a dar a sus manos mejor uso en la costura que matando.} {Cuando unos saqueadores atacaron su pueblo, %name% vistió a todos con ingeniosos disfraces. El pueblo fue destruido, pero no se perdió ni un alma. | Pasó muchos años vistiendo a la realeza hasta que un desliz de moda le valió el exilio. | Por desgracia, que una mujer se aficionara a las buenas telas, como suele hacer %name%, hizo que la costurera fuera marginada en más de un pueblo. | Intentó abrirse camino en las grandes ciudades, pero, por desgracia, no pudo competir con las demás costureras. | Cuando un señor organizó un ejército, %name% se encargó de la ropa y dio a los soldados uniformes como es debido. | Pero una feroz competencia entre costureras terminó con un muerto envuelto en lino y, casualmente, con %name% abandonando su taller. | Por desgracia, unos ladrones saquearon su taller y, con las guerras en curso, sería imposible reabastecerse. | Pero cuando esquiló una oveja que no era suya, %name% fue expulsada del pueblo. | Una vez estranguló a un aspirante a ladrón con un cordón de medir. O eso dice ella, al menos. | Pero vestir a una nobleza antipática y desagradable acabó por {aburrirla. | agotarla.} | Cuando le encargaron una túnica bordada con hazañas épicas, %name% se preguntó cómo sería de verdad el mundo exterior. | Mientras diseñaba un vestido adornado con {gestas épicas | hazañas épicas}, %name% se preguntó si no debería ser ella la protagonista de las historias que se tejían.} Ahora la costurera busca una nueva vida, la lleve adonde la lleve. {Quizá pueda vestir bien a la tropa, o algo así. | Es quisquillosa y peculiar, y acribilla a todo el mundo con críticas sobre su ropa. | No es una soldado nata, pero examina el atuendo de un hombre como si estuviera a punto de ir a la guerra con él. | Con lo que mide y calcula para vestir, es una lástima que %name% no fuera ingeniera de asedio. | Aunque apenas es soldado, hay que admirar el sincero amor de %name% por la costura. | Lo que sabe %name% sobre distintas telas es verdaderamente impresionante. | Algo remilgada, %name% tiene el juego de pies de una esgrimista, pero el manejo de la espada de una suave brisa. | %name% parecería muy fuera de lugar con una armadura, pero vaya si le va a hacer falta una. | Resulta que %name% sí puede sacar un bolso de seda de una oreja de cerda. | Que su oficio no te engañe: %name% es más hábil con las manos que algunos {tahúres | malabaristas | carteristas}. | Las costureras no parecen hechas para el combate, aunque, pensándolo bien, tampoco la mayoría de los hombres con los que te cruzas estos días. | Una costurera parece poco apta para el combate, pero por algún motivo los mejores soldados aparecen en los lugares más insospechados. | Con buen ojo {para los cálculos | para las medidas}, %name% es mucho más lista de lo que aparenta a primera vista.}"
    }
    // en = "\x7b%name% was always curious about fabrics, seeing more science in a linen cloth than \x7ba diviner would in the sands of the desert. | a haruspex would in a toad's entrails. | an alchemist would in a mortar and pestle.\x7d | %name% was always an odd boy growing up, fancying a good silk dress instead of the girl beneath it. | Son to a \x7bmining father | squire | knight | farmhand\x7d, %name%'s turn toward fashioning clothes was a surprise to all. | While %name%'s sisters fancied being warriors and heroes, %name% thought of himself as a future dresser of kings. | %name% spent much of his youth in the company of girls, but not for the reasons one might think. | %name% always fancied animals, particularly how they would look as a good coat or scarf. | As tunics and shirts grew popular, %name% turned to tailoring to make a crown or two. | With a surge in pantaloons popularity, %name% went from being a tanner to a tailor to make more money. | %name% hails from a faraway land where how a man dresses is more important than how he fights. | Tailoring is the science of colors and fabrics, by which standards %name% is renowned. | Good with measuring and calculating, %name% turned his mathematical prowess to tailoring to earn as much as he could. | %name%'s career in tailoring started when his mother pushed him into the vocation to dodge a passing noble's conscription. | %name% took up tailoring to honor his father, a tailor who was killed by an unhappy customer. | Widowed by war, %name%'s mother taught him how to put his hands to better use in tailoring instead of killing.\x7d \x7bWhen raiders attacked his home, %name% dressed everyone up in clever disguises. The town was destroyed, but not a soul was lost. | He spent many years dressing royalty until a fashion faux pas led his being exiled. | Unfortunately, a man fancying a good fabric, as %name% is wont to do, left the tailor ostracized from many a village. | He tried to make his break in the big cities, but sadly he just could not compete with the other tailors. | When a lord organized an army, %name% handled the clothes, giving the soldiers proper uniforms. | But a fierce competition between tailors led to a linen-wrapped deadman and %name% coincidentally leaving his shop behind. | Sadly, robbers ransacked his shop and, with the wars going on, it would be impossible to restock. | But when he sheared a sheep that did not belong to him, %name% was kicked out of town. | He once choked out a would-be thief with a cord of measuring wire. So he says, anyway. | But dressing unlikeable and unfriendly nobility eventually \x7bbored him. | wore on him.\x7d | Once tasked with making a tunic embroidered with epic feats, %name% wondered what the outside world was really like. | Designing a dress adorned with \x7bepic quests | epic feats\x7d, %name% wondered if maybe he should be the one they wove stories about.\x7d Now the tailor looks for a new life, no matter where it takes him. \x7bMaybe he can dress the unit well, or something. | He's particular and peculiar, peppering everyone with clothing criticisms. | He's no natural soldier, but he appraises a man's attire as if he's about to go to war with it. | The way he measures and calculates for dressing, it's too bad %name% wasn't a siege engineer. | While hardly a soldier, %name%'s earnest love for tailoring is to be admired. | %name%'s knowledge of various cloths is seriously impressive. | A bit on the nimby-pimby side, %name% has the footwork of a swordfighter, but the swordfighting of a soft breeze. | %name% would seem very out of place in a suit of armor, but boy is he going to need one. | As it turns out, %name% can in fact make a silk purse out of a sow's ear. | Don't let his vocation fool you, %name% is more deft with his hands than some \x7bcardsharks | jugglers | pickpockets\x7d. | Tailors don't seem fit for combat, but then again neither do most of the men you run across these days. | A tailor seems ill-fit for combat, yet for some reason you find the finest soldiers in the strangest of places. | With an eye \x7bfor calculations | for measuring\x7d, %name% is a lot smarter than he lets on at first glance.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\tailor_southern_background.nut
    // context: tailor_southern_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: «mundialmente conocido, bueno, conocido en todo el mundo» repite la idea y pierde el chiste de «known-world-renowned» (en todo el mundo conocido); «teniendo un éxito muy diferente» pierde el juego de «making a killing» (matar / forrarse), que «arrasa» conserva
        en = "What was a Seamstress doing in a mercenary company? A good question, but %name% certainly answered it well by killing so many enemies they could've made an epic tapestry out of story. After a few good years in the company, she eventually left to start up a business creating clothes for southern nobility. Her name is world-renowned, well, the known-world-renowned, and she gets so much business she's making a very different killing these days."
        es = "¿Qué hacía una costurera en una compañía de mercenarios? Buena pregunta, pero %name% sin duda la respondió bien matando a tantos enemigos que con su historia podría haberse tejido un tapiz épico. Tras unos buenos años en la compañía, acabó marchándose para montar un negocio de ropa para la nobleza del sur. Su nombre es conocido en todo el mundo, bueno, en todo el mundo conocido, y tiene tanta clientela que estos días arrasa de una manera muy distinta."
    }
    // context: tailor_southern_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "A tailor at heart, it didn't take much to compel %name% to bail from the quickly sinking company. She left to go start a business, but was kidnapped along the way by a group of nomads. When they threatened to kill her, she pretended to be a simple and weak tailor and showed her talents in creating clothes. Impressed, the raggedly dressed outlaws took her into their band. A few days later they were all dead and this 'meek' woman walked out of their camp with a bit of red on her. She started her business a week later and is doing well to this day."
        es = "Costurera de corazón, a %name% no le costó mucho decidirse a abandonar una compañía que se hundía a toda prisa. Se marchó para montar un negocio, pero por el camino la secuestró un grupo de nómadas. Cuando amenazaron con matarla, fingió ser una simple y débil costurera y les mostró su talento para confeccionar ropa. Impresionados, los forajidos harapientos la aceptaron en su banda. Unos días después estaban todos muertos y esta mujer tan 'mansa' salió de su campamento con algo de rojo encima. Abrió su negocio una semana más tarde y le va bien hasta el día de hoy."
    }
    // context: tailor_southern_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{%name% was always curious about fabrics, seeing more science in a linen cloth than {a diviner would in the sands of the desert. | a haruspex would in a toad's entrails. | an alchemist would in a mortar and pestle.} | %name% was always an odd girl growing up, fancying a good silk waistcoat instead of the boy beneath it. | Daughter to a {butcher | soldier}, %name%'s turn toward fashioning clothes was a surprise to all. | While %name%'s sisters fancied being warriors and heroes, %name% thought of herself as a future dresser of viziers. | %name% spent much of her youth in the company of boys, but not for the reasons one might think. | %name% always fancied animals, particularly how they would look as a good coat or scarf. | As tunics and shirts grew popular, %name% turned to seamstressing to make a crown or two. | With a surge in pantaloons popularity, %name% went from being a tanner to a seamstress to make more money. | Seamstressing is the science of colors and fabrics, by which standards %name% is renowned. | Good with measuring and calculating, %name% turned her mathematical prowess to seamstressing to earn as much as she could. | %name% took up seamstressing to honor her father, a tailor who was killed by an unhappy customer. | Widowed by war, %name%'s mother taught her how to put her hands to better use in seamstressing instead of killing.} {When nomads attacked her home, %name% dressed everyone up in clever disguises. The town was destroyed, but not a soul was lost. | She spent many years dressing royalty until a fashion faux pas led her being exiled. | Unfortunately, a woman fancying a good fabric, as %name% is wont to do, left the seamstress ostracized from many a village. | She tried to make her break in the city, but sadly she just could not compete with the other seamstresses. | When a vizier organized an army, %name% handled the clothes, giving the conscripts proper uniforms. | But a fierce competition between seamstresses led to a linen-wrapped deadman and %name% coincidentally leaving her shop behind. | She once choked out a would-be thief with a cord of measuring wire. So she says, anyway. | Once tasked with making a tunic embroidered with epic feats, %name% wondered what the outside world was really like. | Designing a dress adorned with {epic quests | epic feats}, %name% wondered if maybe she should be the one they wove stories about.} Now the seamstress looks for a new life, no matter where it takes her. {Maybe she can dress the unit well, or something. | She's particular and peculiar, peppering everyone with clothing criticisms. | She's no natural soldier, but she appraises a man's attire as if he's about to go to war with it. | The way she measures and calculates for dressing, it's too bad %name% wasn't a siege engineer. | While hardly a soldier, %name%'s earnest love for seamstressing is to be admired. | %name%'s knowledge of various cloths is seriously impressive. | A bit on the nimby-pimbly side, %name% has the footwork of a swordfighter, but the swordfighting of a soft breeze. | %name% would seem very out of place in a suit of armor, but boy is she going to need one. | As it turns out, %name% can in fact make a silk purse out of a sow's ear. | Don't let her vocation fool you, %name% is more deft with her hands than some {cardsharks | jugglers | pickpockets}. | Seamstresses don't seem fit for combat, but then again neither do most of the men you run across these days. | A seamstress seems ill-fit for combat, yet for some reason you find the finest soldiers in the strangest of places. | With an eye {for calculations | for measuring}, %name% is a lot smarter than she lets on at first glance.}"
        es = "{%name% siempre sintió curiosidad por las telas y veía más ciencia en un paño de lino que {un adivino en las arenas del desierto. | un arúspice en las entrañas de un sapo. | un alquimista en un mortero.} | De pequeña, %name% siempre fue una chica rara: le gustaba más un buen chaleco de seda que el muchacho que lo llevaba. | Hija de un {carnicero | soldado}, que %name% acabara confeccionando ropa sorprendió a todos. | Mientras las hermanas de %name% soñaban con ser guerreras y heroínas, %name% se imaginaba como futura modista de visires. | %name% pasó buena parte de su juventud rodeada de chicos, pero no por los motivos que uno pensaría. | A %name% siempre le gustaron los animales, sobre todo imaginar cómo quedarían convertidos en un buen abrigo o una bufanda. | Cuando las túnicas y las camisas se pusieron de moda, %name% se dedicó a la costura para ganarse alguna corona. | Con el auge de los pantalones bombachos, %name% pasó de curtidora a costurera para ganar más dinero. | La costura es la ciencia de los colores y las telas, y en ella %name% goza de renombre. | Buena para medir y calcular, %name% puso su talento para los números al servicio de la costura para ganar todo lo posible. | %name% se dedicó a la costura para honrar a su padre, un sastre al que mató un cliente descontento. | Viuda por la guerra, la madre de %name% le enseñó a dar a sus manos un mejor uso con la costura en lugar de matar.} {Cuando unos nómadas atacaron su hogar, %name% vistió a todos con ingeniosos disfraces. El pueblo quedó arrasado, pero no se perdió ni una sola alma. | Pasó muchos años vistiendo a la realeza hasta que un desliz de moda la llevó al exilio. | Por desgracia, que una mujer se pierda por una buena tela, como suele hacer %name%, le valió a la costurera el rechazo de más de una aldea. | Intentó abrirse paso en la ciudad, pero por desgracia no pudo competir con las demás costureras. | Cuando un visir reunió un ejército, %name% se encargó de la ropa y dio a los reclutas uniformes como es debido. | Pero una feroz rivalidad entre costureras acabó con un muerto envuelto en lino y con %name%, casualmente, abandonando su taller. | Una vez estranguló a un aspirante a ladrón con una cinta de medir. O eso dice ella, al menos. | Cuando le encargaron una túnica bordada con hazañas épicas, %name% se preguntó cómo sería de verdad el mundo exterior. | Mientras diseñaba un vestido adornado con {gestas épicas | hazañas épicas}, %name% se preguntó si no debería ser ella la protagonista de las historias que se tejen.} Ahora la costurera busca una nueva vida, la lleve donde la lleve. {Quizá pueda vestir bien a la tropa, o algo así. | Es exigente y peculiar, y acribilla a todo el mundo con críticas sobre su ropa. | No es una soldado nata, pero examina el atuendo de un hombre como si estuviera a punto de ir a la guerra con él. | Con lo que mide y calcula para vestir a la gente, es una lástima que %name% no fuera ingeniera de asedio. | Aunque de soldado tiene poco, el amor sincero de %name% por la costura es digno de admiración. | Lo que sabe %name% de telas es realmente impresionante. | Algo blandengue, %name% tiene el juego de pies de una espadachina, pero el manejo de la espada de una suave brisa. | %name% parecería muy fuera de lugar dentro de una armadura, pero vaya si va a necesitar una. | Resulta que %name% sí es capaz de sacar un bolso de seda de una oreja de cerda. | Que su oficio no te engañe: %name% es más hábil con las manos que algunos {tahúres | malabaristas | carteristas}. | Las costureras no parecen aptas para el combate, pero tampoco lo parece la mayoría de los hombres con los que te cruzas estos días. | Una costurera parece poco apta para el combate, pero, por algún motivo, los mejores soldados aparecen en los lugares más extraños. | Con buen ojo {para los cálculos | para las medidas}, %name% es mucho más lista de lo que aparenta a primera vista.}"
    }
    // en = "\x7b%name% was always curious about fabrics, seeing more science in a linen cloth than \x7ba diviner would in the sands of the desert. | a haruspex would in a toad's entrails. | an alchemist would in a mortar and pestle.\x7d | %name% was always an odd boy growing up, fancying a good silk dress instead of the girl beneath it. | Son to a \x7bbutcher | soldier\x7d, %name%'s turn toward fashioning clothes was a surprise to all. | While %name%'s brothers fancied being warriors and heroes, %name% thought of himself as a future dresser of viziers. | %name% spent much of his youth in the company of girls, but not for the reasons one might think. | %name% always fancied animals, particularly how they would look as a good coat or scarf. | As tunics and shirts grew popular, %name% turned to tailoring to make a crown or two. | With a surge in pantaloons popularity, %name% went from being a tanner to a tailor to make more money. | Tailoring is the science of colors and fabrics, by which standards %name% is renowned. | Good with measuring and calculating, %name% turned his mathematical prowess to tailoring to earn as much as he could. | %name% took up tailoring to honor his father, a tailor who was killed by an unhappy customer. | Widowed by war, %name%'s mother taught him how to put his hands to better use in tailoring instead of killing.\x7d \x7bWhen nomads attacked his home, %name% dressed everyone up in clever disguises. The town was destroyed, but not a soul was lost. | He spent many years dressing royalty until a fashion faux pas led his being exiled. | Unfortunately, a man fancying a good fabric, as %name% is wont to do, left the tailor ostracized from many a village. | He tried to make his break in the city, but sadly he just could not compete with the other tailors. | When a vizier organized an army, %name% handled the clothes, giving the conscripts proper uniforms. | But a fierce competition between tailors led to a linen-wrapped deadman and %name% coincidentally leaving his shop behind. | He once choked out a would-be thief with a cord of measuring wire. So he says, anyway. | Once tasked with making a tunic embroidered with epic feats, %name% wondered what the outside world was really like. | Designing a dress adorned with \x7bepic quests | epic feats\x7d, %name% wondered if maybe he should be the one they wove stories about.\x7d Now the tailor looks for a new life, no matter where it takes him. \x7bMaybe he can dress the unit well, or something. | He's particular and peculiar, peppering everyone with clothing criticisms. | He's no natural soldier, but he appraises a man's attire as if he's about to go to war with it. | The way he measures and calculates for dressing, it's too bad %name% wasn't a siege engineer. | While hardly a soldier, %name%'s earnest love for tailoring is to be admired. | %name%'s knowledge of various cloths is seriously impressive. | A bit on the nimby-pimby side, %name% has the footwork of a swordfighter, but the swordfighting of a soft breeze. | %name% would seem very out of place in a suit of armor, but boy is he going to need one. | As it turns out, %name% can in fact make a silk purse out of a sow's ear. | Don't let his vocation fool you, %name% is more deft with his hands than some \x7bcardsharks | jugglers | pickpockets\x7d. | Tailors don't seem fit for combat, but then again neither do most of the men you run across these days. | A tailor seems ill-fit for combat, yet for some reason you find the finest soldiers in the strangest of places. | With an eye \x7bfor calculations | for measuring\x7d, %name% is a lot smarter than he lets on at first glance.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\thief_background.nut
    // en = "A good thief will have quick reflexes and the ability to evade any captors."
    // en base_es
    // context: thief_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        // corrige base: «despiadado» no está en el inglés; «bóvedas» por «vaults» es la bóveda arquitectónica, aquí son cámaras del tesoro
        en = "%name% the thief retired from fighting and disappeared off the map. You haven't heard word of the %person% since, but there are rumors that a certain nobleman had one of his vaults completely drained in a perfectly executed heist."
        es = "%name%, siempre amig%o% de lo ajeno, se retiró de la lucha y desapareció del mapa. No has vuelto a saber nada de %el% desde entonces, pero corren rumores de que a cierto noble le vaciaron por completo una de sus cámaras del tesoro en un golpe ejecutado a la perfección."
    }
    // context: thief_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "%name% the thief read the lines being drawn in the sands and retired from the %companyname% while %they% still could. %They% took what money %they% had made and threw together a crew of thieves and brigands. Last you heard, %they% pulled off a perfect heist only for one of %their% partners to stab %them% in the back and take off with all the goods."
        es = "%name%, siempre amig%o% de lo ajeno, vio por dónde soplaba el viento y se retiró de %companyname% mientras aún podía. Con el dinero que había ganado reunió una banda de ladrones y bandidos. Lo último que supiste es que dio un golpe perfecto, solo para que uno de sus socios %lo% apuñalara por la espalda y se largara con todo el botín."
    }
    // en = "the Cutpurse"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Snake"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Burglar"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Snatcher"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Black Cat"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Prince"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Quickfingers"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Thief"
    // en base_es
    // context: thief_background.o.setGender.m.Name
    {
        en = "Pickpocket"
        es = "Carterista"
    }
    // context: thief_background.o.setGender.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "A good pickpocket will have quick reflexes and the ability to evade any captors."
        es = "Un buen carterista tiene reflejos rápidos y sabe zafarse de quien intente atraparlo."
    }
    // context: thief_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{Raised by thieves on a diet of honeymilk and stolen gold, %name% started life off on the wrong foot. | Raised by a drunken father and an ill mother, %name% was parented straight into a life of thievery. | Born as the sixth-child of an already impoverished family, the budding thief %name% first learned the craft by stealing the last bits of dinner. | Growing up in a family servant to a rich noble, the eventual-thief %name% spent many years staring at royal opulence - and stealing from it. | Taken in by a local orphanage, it wasn't long for %name% to start taking abuse from the lowly orphans. %They% fell back on thieving to survive. | Orphaned, %name% grew up as a street urchin, %their% days governed by cutting purses and picking pockets. | While never particularly in need of money, %name%'s jealousy over material things led %them% to thieving. | The profligacy of the rich amidst crowds of poor always rubbed %name% the wrong way. So %they% stole from them both and gave to %themselves%. | %name%'s father taught %them% all there was to know about stealing including, unfortunately, how to backstab. | The church steals with a silver plate. The lords do it with the taxman. So %name% figured why can't %they% do it with %their% own two hands? | Impoverished while growing up, %name% took to stealing bread. Well-fed, %they% soon took to stealing crowns.} {After years of successful stealing, one mistake landed %name% in a dungeon. Thankfully, years of stealing also meant years of lockpicking and %they% didn't spend long. | But when %they% was caught trying to steal a temple's chalice, a talk with a priest convinced %name% to perhaps take a different path. | Unfortunately, a smash-and-grab at a local store ended with %name% being caught red-handed. %They% was soon profiled on posters everywhere, making %their% work difficult. | Daring to cut the purse of a fat trader, %name% soon found %themselves% nursing a hand absent of a few fingers. %They% really liked those fingers, too. | %name%'s thievery eventually placed %them% at the head of an entire guild. But after a dozen failed assassination attempts, the thief realized there was nobody to trust in %their% line of work. | Partnering up with a beautiful woman, %name% managed to steal from everybody. Too bad the woman stole from %them%, in the end. | Trying to sell some goods, a trusted fence turned out to be a traitorous informant. One bad pillory experience later and the thief was exiled from %randomtown%. | It was the perfect heist. That's all that is said about it. Now, %name% just needs to lay low. | Tortured by a rival gang, %they% came to miss a number of teeth, fingernails, and any drive to return to thieving. | %Their% time as a thief came to an end when, arrested, %they% spent five days pilloried during tomato season. | Naturally, it wasn't long until %they% went to prison. %They% doesn't speak of %their% time there, but it is obvious %they% wishes to never return. | But one day %they% learned there are much better ways to spin a blade for a coin than petty thievery. | But %their% half-brother was captured by a local gang, forcing the thief to find new ways to pay the hefty ransom. | But life as a brigand is not easy. Arrested for eating a chicken that was not %theirs%, the %person% forfeited two fingers and any will to keep thieving. | After a heist went south, the %person% fingered all %their% former partners to save %their% own hide. Now %they% can never go back to thieving.} {For all you know %name% is just using sellswords to hide behind. Regardless of %their% reasons, %they're% still going to have to earn %their% pay. | You recognize %name% from some posters.  Well, a %person% who has gotten this far without being caught must have some value. | With one hand, %name% twirls a blade between %their% fingers. With the other, %they% snags your purse. Impressive. Now give it back. | Years of thieving have made %name% adept at escaping trouble. | %name% has the skills to be a good mercenary, just be sure to watch your purse while around %them%. | You can't trust a %person% like %name%, but that attribute has plenty of company anyway. | Supposedly, somebody once shot an arrow at %name%. They missed, but the thief kept the feathers. | %name%'s effort to join sellswords better not be a scheme to steal from your coffers. | Wanted posters say %name% is considered 'armed and dangerous'. Perfect. | There are plenty of lawmen looking for %name%. Maybe you can get them to join, too.}"
        es = "{Criad%o% por ladrones con una dieta de leche con miel y oro robado, %name% empezó la vida con el pie izquierdo. | Criad%o% por un padre borracho y una madre enferma, %name% fue educad%o% directamente para una vida de robos. | Sext%o% hij%o% de una familia ya empobrecida, %name% aprendió el oficio robando las últimas sobras de la cena. | Criad%o% en una familia al servicio de un noble rico, %name% pasó muchos años contemplando el lujo señorial... y, con el tiempo, robándole. | Acogid%o% por un orfanato local, %name% no tardó en sufrir los abusos de los huérfanos más miserables. Recurrió al robo para sobrevivir. | Huérfan%o%, %name% creció como %un% pilluel%o% de la calle, con los días dedicados a cortar bolsas y vaciar bolsillos. | Aunque nunca le hizo especial falta el dinero, la envidia que sentía %name% por las cosas materiales %lo% llevó al robo. | El derroche de los ricos en medio de multitudes de pobres siempre le sentó mal a %name%. Así que robó a unos y a otros y se lo dio a sí mism%o%. | El padre de %name% le enseñó todo lo que había que saber sobre el robo, incluido, por desgracia, cómo apuñalar por la espalda. | La iglesia roba con la bandeja de plata. Los señores, con el recaudador. Así que %name% pensó: ¿por qué no hacerlo con sus propias manos? | Pobre de niñ%o%, %name% se dedicó a robar pan. Ya bien alimentad%o%, pronto pasó a robar coronas.} {Tras años de robos con éxito, un solo error llevó a %name% a una mazmorra. Por suerte, años de robos también significaban años forzando cerraduras, y no pasó allí mucho tiempo. | Pero cuando %lo% pillaron intentando robar el cáliz de un templo, una charla con un sacerdote convenció a %name% de que quizá debía tomar otro camino. | Por desgracia, un robo relámpago en una tienda local terminó con %name% atrapad%o% con las manos en la masa. Pronto su cara apareció en carteles por todas partes, lo que le complicó el trabajo. | Por atreverse a cortar la bolsa de un comerciante gordo, %name% pronto se encontró curándose una mano a la que le faltaban algunos dedos. Y eso que les tenía mucho cariño a esos dedos. | Sus robos acabaron poniendo a %name% al frente de todo un gremio. Pero tras una docena de intentos de asesinato fallidos, se dio cuenta de que en su oficio no se podía confiar en nadie. | Asociándose con una mujer hermosa, %name% logró robar a todo el mundo. Lástima que, al final, la mujer también le robara a %el%. | Al intentar vender una mercancía, un perista de confianza resultó ser un soplón traidor. Tras un mal trago en la picota, acabó desterrad%o% de %randomtown%. | Fue el golpe perfecto. Es todo lo que se dice al respecto. Ahora, %name% solo necesita pasar desapercibid%o%. | Torturad%o% por una banda rival, se quedó sin unos cuantos dientes, sin varias uñas y sin ninguna gana de volver a robar. | Su carrera en el robo terminó cuando, tras ser detenid%o%, pasó cinco días en la picota en plena temporada de tomates. | Naturalmente, no tardó en ir a la cárcel. No habla de su paso por allí, pero es evidente que no desea volver jamás. | Pero un día descubrió que hay formas mucho mejores de ganarse una moneda con una hoja que el robo de poca monta. | Pero una banda local capturó a su medio hermano, y tuvo que buscar nuevas formas de pagar el elevado rescate. | Pero la vida fuera de la ley no es fácil. Detenid%o% por comerse un pollo que no era suyo, perdió dos dedos y cualquier deseo de seguir robando. | Después de un golpe que salió mal, delató a todos sus antiguos socios para salvar el pellejo. Ahora no puede volver a robar nunca más.} {Por lo que sabes, %name% solo quiere esconderse detrás de los mercenarios. Sean cuales sean sus motivos, tendrá que ganarse la paga igualmente. | Reconoces a %name% de unos carteles. Bueno, %un% %hombre% que ha llegado tan lejos sin que %lo% atrapen debe de valer algo. | Con una mano, %name% hace girar una hoja entre los dedos. Con la otra, te birla la bolsa. Impresionante. Ahora devuélvela. | Años de robos han hecho de %name% %un% expert%o% en librarse de los problemas. | %name% tiene madera de mercenari%o%; eso sí, vigila tu bolsa cuando estés cerca de %el%. | No puedes fiarte de %un% %hombre% como %name%, pero esa cualidad ya está bien representada en la compañía. | Al parecer, una vez alguien disparó una flecha a %name%. Falló, pero la víctima se quedó con las plumas. | Más vale que el empeño de %name% en unirse a los mercenarios no sea una maniobra para robar de tus arcas. | Los carteles de búsqueda dicen que se considera a %name% 'armad%o% y peligros%o%'. Perfecto. | Hay muchos agentes de la ley buscando a %name%. Quizá también consigas que se unan.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\thief_southern_background.nut
    // context: thief_southern_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: «un cercano vendedor de bienes» no traduce «a trusted fence» (un perista de confianza); «llegó a extrañar» malinterpreta «came to miss» (se quedó sin); sobran las comillas añadidas a «Realmente», «Fue el robo perfecto» e «Impresionante... Ahora devuélvela»; «Una mala experiencia en el cepo más tarde» y «su línea de trabajo» son calcos
        en = "{Raised by thieves on a diet of honeymilk and stolen gold, %name% started life off on the wrong foot. | Raised by a drunken father and an ill mother, %name% was parented straight into a life of thievery. | Born as the sixth-child of an already impoverished family, the budding thief %name% first learned the craft by stealing the last bits of dinner. | Growing up in a family servant to a rich merchant, the eventual-thief %name% spent many years staring at decadent opulence - and stealing from it. | Taken in by a local orphanage, it wasn't long for %name% to start taking abuse from the lowly orphans. She fell back on thieving to survive. | Orphaned, %name% grew up as a street urchin, his days governed by cutting purses and picking pockets. | While never particularly in need of money, %name%'s jealousy over material things led her to thieving. | The profligacy of the rich amidst crowds of poor always rubbed %name% the wrong way. So she stole from them both and gave to herself. | %name%'s father taught her all there was to know about stealing including, unfortunately, how to backstab. | The church steals with a silver plate. The lords do it with the taxman. So %name% figured why can't she do it with her own two hands? | Impoverished while growing up, %name% took to stealing bread. Well-fed, she soon took to stealing crowns.} {After years of successful stealing, one mistake landed %name% in a dungeon. Thankfully, years of stealing also meant years of lockpicking and she didn't spend long. | But when she was caught trying to steal a temple's chalice, a talk with a monk convinced %name% to perhaps take a different path. | Unfortunately, a smash-and-grab at a local store ended with %name% being caught red-handed. She was soon profiled on posters everywhere, making her work difficult. | Daring to cut the purse of a fat trader, %name% soon found herself nursing a hand absent of a few fingers. She really liked those fingers, too. | %name%'s thievery eventually placed her at the head of an entire guild. But after a dozen failed assassination attempts, the thief realized there was nobody to trust in her line of work. | Partnering up with a beautiful woman, %name% managed to steal from everybody. Too bad the woman stole from her, in the end. | Trying to sell some goods, a trusted fence turned out to be a traitorous informant. One bad pillory experience later and the thief was exiled from %randomtown%. | It was the perfect heist. That's all that is said about it. Now, %name% just needs to lay low. | Tortured by a rival gang, she came to miss a number of teeth, fingernails, and any drive to return to thieving. | Her time as a thief came to an end when, arrested, she spent five days pilloried during tomato season. | Naturally, it wasn't long until she went to prison. She doesn't speak of her time there, but it is obvious she wishes to never return. | But one day she learned there are much better ways to spin a blade for a coin than petty thievery. | But her half-brother was captured by a local gang, forcing the thief to find new ways to pay the hefty ransom. | But life as a brigand is not easy. Arrested for eating a chicken that was not hers, the man forfeited two fingers and any will to keep thieving. | After a heist went south, the woman fingered all her former partners to save her own hide. Now she can never go back to thieving.} {For all you know %name% is just using sellswords to hide behind. Regardless of her reasons, she's still going to have to earn her pay. | You recognize %name% from some posters.  Well, a woman who has gotten this far without being caught must have some value. | With one hand, %name% twirls a blade between her fingers. With the other, she snags your purse. Impressive. Now give it back. | Years of thieving have made %name% adept at escaping trouble. | %name% has the skills to be a good mercenary, just be sure to watch your purse while around her. | You can't trust a woman like %name%, but that attribute has plenty of company anyway. | Supposedly, somebody once shot an arrow at %name%. They missed, but the thief kept the feathers. | %name%'s effort to join sellswords better not be a scheme to steal from your coffers. | Wanted posters say %name% is considered 'armed and dangerous'. Perfect. | There are plenty of lawmen looking for %name%. Maybe you can get them to join, too.}"
        es = "{Criada por ladrones con una dieta de leche con miel y oro robado, %name% empezó la vida con el pie izquierdo. | Criada por un padre borracho y una madre enferma, %name% fue educada directamente para una vida de robos. | Sexta hija de una familia ya empobrecida, la joven ladrona %name% aprendió el oficio robando las últimas sobras de la cena. | Criada en una familia al servicio de un rico mercader, la futura ladrona %name% pasó muchos años contemplando un lujo decadente... y robándole. | Acogida por un orfanato local, %name% no tardó en sufrir los abusos de los huérfanos más miserables. Recurrió al robo para sobrevivir. | Huérfana, %name% creció como una pilluela de la calle, con los días dedicados a cortar bolsas y vaciar bolsillos. | Aunque nunca le hizo especial falta el dinero, la envidia que sentía %name% por las cosas materiales la llevó al robo. | El derroche de los ricos en medio de multitudes de pobres siempre le sentó mal a %name%. Así que robó a unos y a otros y se lo dio a sí misma. | El padre de %name% le enseñó todo lo que había que saber sobre el robo, incluido, por desgracia, cómo apuñalar por la espalda. | La iglesia roba con la bandeja de plata. Los señores, con el recaudador. Así que %name% pensó: ¿por qué no puede hacerlo ella con sus propias manos? | Pobre de niña, %name% se dedicó a robar pan. Ya bien alimentada, pronto pasó a robar coronas.} {Tras años de robos con éxito, un solo error llevó a %name% a una mazmorra. Por suerte, años de robos también significaban años forzando cerraduras, y no pasó allí mucho tiempo. | Pero cuando la pillaron intentando robar el cáliz de un templo, una charla con un monje convenció a %name% de que quizá debía tomar otro camino. | Por desgracia, un robo relámpago en una tienda local terminó con %name% atrapada con las manos en la masa. Pronto su cara apareció en carteles por todas partes, lo que le complicó el trabajo. | Por atreverse a cortar la bolsa de un comerciante gordo, %name% pronto se encontró curándose una mano a la que le faltaban algunos dedos. Y eso que les tenía mucho cariño a esos dedos. | Sus robos acabaron poniendo a %name% al frente de todo un gremio. Pero tras una docena de intentos de asesinato fallidos, la ladrona se dio cuenta de que en su oficio no se podía confiar en nadie. | Asociándose con una mujer hermosa, %name% logró robar a todo el mundo. Lástima que, al final, la mujer también le robara a ella. | Al intentar vender una mercancía, un perista de confianza resultó ser un soplón traidor. Tras un mal trago en la picota, la ladrona acabó desterrada de %randomtown%. | Fue el golpe perfecto. Es todo lo que se dice al respecto. Ahora, %name% solo necesita pasar desapercibida. | Torturada por una banda rival, se quedó sin unos cuantos dientes, sin varias uñas y sin ninguna gana de volver a robar. | Su carrera de ladrona terminó cuando, tras ser detenida, pasó cinco días en la picota en plena temporada de tomates. | Naturalmente, no tardó en ir a la cárcel. No habla de su paso por allí, pero es evidente que no desea volver jamás. | Pero un día descubrió que hay formas mucho mejores de ganarse una moneda con una hoja que el robo de poca monta. | Pero una banda local capturó a su medio hermano, y la ladrona tuvo que buscar nuevas formas de pagar el elevado rescate. | Pero la vida de bandida no es fácil. Detenida por comerse un pollo que no era suyo, perdió dos dedos y cualquier deseo de seguir robando. | Después de un golpe que salió mal, la mujer delató a todos sus antiguos socios para salvar el pellejo. Ahora no puede volver a robar nunca más.} {Por lo que sabes, %name% solo quiere esconderse detrás de los mercenarios. Sean cuales sean sus motivos, tendrá que ganarse la paga igualmente. | Reconoces a %name% de unos carteles. Bueno, una mujer que ha llegado tan lejos sin que la atrapen debe de valer algo. | Con una mano, %name% hace girar una hoja entre los dedos. Con la otra, te birla la bolsa. Impresionante. Ahora devuélvela. | Años de robos han hecho de %name% una experta en librarse de los problemas. | %name% tiene madera de mercenaria; eso sí, vigila tu bolsa cuando estés cerca de ella. | No puedes fiarte de una mujer como %name%, pero esa cualidad ya está bien representada en la compañía. | Al parecer, una vez alguien disparó una flecha a %name%. Falló, pero la ladrona se quedó con las plumas. | Más vale que el empeño de %name% en unirse a los mercenarios no sea una maniobra para robar de tus arcas. | Los carteles de búsqueda dicen que se considera a %name% 'armada y peligrosa'. Perfecto. | Hay muchos agentes de la ley buscando a %name%. Quizá también consigas que se unan.}"
    }
    // context: thief_southern_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: «un cercano vendedor de bienes» no traduce «a trusted fence» (un perista de confianza); «llegó a extrañar» malinterpreta «came to miss» (se quedó sin); sobran las comillas añadidas a «Realmente», «Fue el robo perfecto» e «Impresionante... Ahora devuélvela»; «Una mala experiencia en el cepo más tarde» y «su línea de trabajo» son calcos
        en = "{Raised by thieves on a diet of honeymilk and stolen gold, %name% started life off on the wrong foot. | Raised by a drunken father and an ill mother, %name% was parented straight into a life of thievery. | Born as the sixth-child of an already impoverished family, the budding thief %name% first learned the craft by stealing the last bits of dinner. | Growing up in a family servant to a rich merchant, the eventual-thief %name% spent many years staring at decadent opulence - and stealing from it. | Taken in by a local orphanage, it wasn't long for %name% to start taking abuse from the lowly orphans. %name% fell back on thieving to survive. | Orphaned, %name% grew up as a street urchin, days governed by cutting purses and picking pockets. | While never particularly in need of money, %name%'s jealousy over material things led him to thieving. | The profligacy of the rich amidst crowds of poor always rubbed %name% the wrong way. So %name% stole from them both and gave to one's self. | %name%'s father taught all there was to know about stealing including, unfortunately, how to backstab. | The church steals with a silver plate. The lords do it with the taxman. So %name% figured why not do it with your own two hands? | Impoverished while growing up, %name% took to stealing bread. Well-fed, he soon took to stealing crowns.} {After years of successful stealing, one mistake landed %name% in a dungeon. Thankfully, years of stealing also meant years of lockpicking and he didn't spend long. | But when he was caught trying to steal a temple's chalice, a talk with a monk convinced %name% to perhaps take a different path. | Unfortunately, a smash-and-grab at a local store ended with %name% being caught red-handed. He was soon profiled on posters everywhere, making his work difficult. | Daring to cut the purse of a fat trader, %name% soon found himself nursing a hand absent of a few fingers. He really liked those fingers, too. | %name%'s thievery eventually placed him at the head of an entire guild. But after a dozen failed assassination attempts, the thief realized there was nobody to trust in his line of work. | Partnering up with a beautiful woman, %name% managed to steal from everybody. Too bad the woman stole from him, in the end. | Trying to sell some goods, a trusted fence turned out to be a traitorous informant. One bad pillory experience later and the thief was exiled from %randomtown%. | It was the perfect heist. That's all that is said about it. Now, %name% just needs to lay low. | Tortured by a rival gang, he came to miss a number of teeth, fingernails, and any drive to return to thieving. | His time as a thief came to an end when, arrested, he spent five days pilloried during tomato season. | Naturally, it wasn't long until he went to prison. He doesn't speak of his time there, but it is obvious he wishes to never return. | But one day he learned there are much better ways to spin a blade for a coin than petty thievery. | But his half-brother was captured by a local gang, forcing the thief to find new ways to pay the hefty ransom. | But life as a brigand is not easy. Arrested for eating a chicken that was not his, the man forfeited two fingers and any will to keep thieving. | After a heist went south, the man fingered all his former partners to save his own hide. Now he can never go back to thieving.} {For all you know %name% is just using sellswords to hide behind. Regardless of his reasons, he's still going to have to earn his pay. | You recognize %name% from some posters.  Well, a man who has gotten this far without being caught must have some value. | With one hand, %name% twirls a blade between his fingers. With the other, he snags your purse. Impressive. Now give it back. | Years of thieving have made %name% adept at escaping trouble. | %name% has the skills to be a good mercenary, just be sure to watch your purse while around him. | You can't trust a man like %name%, but that attribute has plenty of company anyway. | Supposedly, somebody once shot an arrow at %name%. They missed, but the thief kept the feathers. | %name%'s effort to join sellswords better not be a scheme to steal from your coffers. | Wanted posters say %name% is considered 'armed and dangerous'. Perfect. | There are plenty of lawmen looking for %name%. Maybe you can get them to join, too.}"
        es = "{Criado por ladrones con una dieta de leche con miel y oro robado, %name% empezó la vida con el pie izquierdo. | Criado por un padre borracho y una madre enferma, %name% fue educado directamente para una vida de robos. | Sexto hijo de una familia ya empobrecida, el joven ladrón %name% aprendió el oficio robando las últimas sobras de la cena. | Criado en una familia al servicio de un rico mercader, el futuro ladrón %name% pasó muchos años contemplando un lujo decadente... y robándole. | Acogido por un orfanato local, %name% no tardó en sufrir los abusos de los huérfanos más miserables. %name% recurrió al robo para sobrevivir. | Huérfano, %name% creció como un pilluelo de la calle, con los días dedicados a cortar bolsas y vaciar bolsillos. | Aunque nunca le hizo especial falta el dinero, la envidia que sentía %name% por las cosas materiales lo llevó al robo. | El derroche de los ricos en medio de multitudes de pobres siempre le sentó mal a %name%. Así que %name% robó a unos y a otros y se lo dio a sí mismo. | El padre de %name% le enseñó todo lo que había que saber sobre el robo, incluido, por desgracia, cómo apuñalar por la espalda. | La iglesia roba con la bandeja de plata. Los señores, con el recaudador. Así que %name% pensó: ¿por qué no hacerlo con tus propias manos? | Pobre de niño, %name% se dedicó a robar pan. Ya bien alimentado, pronto pasó a robar coronas.} {Tras años de robos con éxito, un solo error llevó a %name% a una mazmorra. Por suerte, años de robos también significaban años forzando cerraduras, y no pasó allí mucho tiempo. | Pero cuando lo pillaron intentando robar el cáliz de un templo, una charla con un monje convenció a %name% de que quizá debía tomar otro camino. | Por desgracia, un robo relámpago en una tienda local terminó con %name% atrapado con las manos en la masa. Pronto su cara apareció en carteles por todas partes, lo que le complicó el trabajo. | Por atreverse a cortar la bolsa de un comerciante gordo, %name% pronto se encontró curándose una mano a la que le faltaban algunos dedos. Y eso que les tenía mucho cariño a esos dedos. | Sus robos acabaron poniendo a %name% al frente de todo un gremio. Pero tras una docena de intentos de asesinato fallidos, el ladrón se dio cuenta de que en su oficio no se podía confiar en nadie. | Asociándose con una mujer hermosa, %name% logró robar a todo el mundo. Lástima que, al final, la mujer también le robara a él. | Al intentar vender una mercancía, un perista de confianza resultó ser un soplón traidor. Tras un mal trago en la picota, el ladrón acabó desterrado de %randomtown%. | Fue el golpe perfecto. Es todo lo que se dice al respecto. Ahora, %name% solo necesita pasar desapercibido. | Torturado por una banda rival, se quedó sin unos cuantos dientes, sin varias uñas y sin ninguna gana de volver a robar. | Su carrera de ladrón terminó cuando, tras ser detenido, pasó cinco días en la picota en plena temporada de tomates. | Naturalmente, no tardó en ir a la cárcel. No habla de su paso por allí, pero es evidente que no desea volver jamás. | Pero un día descubrió que hay formas mucho mejores de ganarse una moneda con una hoja que el robo de poca monta. | Pero una banda local capturó a su medio hermano, y el ladrón tuvo que buscar nuevas formas de pagar el elevado rescate. | Pero la vida de bandido no es fácil. Detenido por comerse un pollo que no era suyo, el hombre perdió dos dedos y cualquier deseo de seguir robando. | Después de un golpe que salió mal, el hombre delató a todos sus antiguos socios para salvar el pellejo. Ahora no puede volver a robar nunca más.} {Por lo que sabes, %name% solo quiere esconderse detrás de los mercenarios. Sean cuales sean sus motivos, tendrá que ganarse la paga igualmente. | Reconoces a %name% de unos carteles. Bueno, un hombre que ha llegado tan lejos sin que lo atrapen debe de valer algo. | Con una mano, %name% hace girar una hoja entre los dedos. Con la otra, te birla la bolsa. Impresionante. Ahora devuélvela. | Años de robos han hecho de %name% un experto en librarse de los problemas. | %name% tiene madera de mercenario; eso sí, vigila tu bolsa cuando estés cerca de él. | No puedes fiarte de un hombre como %name%, pero esa cualidad ya está bien representada en la compañía. | Al parecer, una vez alguien disparó una flecha a %name%. Falló, pero el ladrón se quedó con las plumas. | Más vale que el empeño de %name% en unirse a los mercenarios no sea una maniobra para robar de tus arcas. | Los carteles de búsqueda dicen que se considera a %name% 'armado y peligroso'. Perfecto. | Hay muchos agentes de la ley buscando a %name%. Quizá también consigas que se unan.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\vagabond_background.nut
    // en = "Vagabonds are used to long travels, but don't excel in anything in particular."
    // en base_es
    // en = "Some men were just intended to wander. While his time with the %companyname% went well, %name% the vagabond eventually departed with the company and set off on the roads once more. You've no idea where he's gone, you just know all he's interested in is going."
    // en base_es
    // en = "As the company fell apart, it's little surprise that a vagabond like %name% chose to leave it behind and return to the roads. Unfortunately, with the world in such a dire state, it did not take long for him to find trouble. His body was found hanging outside a small farming village. A sign nailed to his chest read: 'No Free Rangers'."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Vagabond"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Threefeet"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Bindlestiff"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Tatterdemalion"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Traveller"
    // en base_es
    // en = "\x7bPushed out of his town by war, %name% wanders the world as a vagabond. | Lazy and unmotivated, %name% one day put all three of his belongings into a knapsack and hit the road. | Never a strong learner in school, %name% dropped out to wander the earth. | %name% did not have the business acumen to protect his inheritance from debtors, lawmen, and other maleficent men. Now he wanders with the last of his crowns jangling in a pocket. | Life on the road has taught %name% to be a jack of all trades, and a master of none - except walking, of course. | Not quite one for the city, and not quite one for the wild, %name% spends his purposeless days traveling between both. | During his drinking days, %name% managed to gamble away a small fortune. Now homeless, he simply wanders. | When his wife was murdered while he was away, %name% refused to sleep in the house. The man walks the earth, trying to forget the memory. | His son murdered five others. In shame, %name% abandoned his hometown to walk the earth and forget his failures as a father.\x7d \x7bBut when a gang of thieves took all he had - including his shoes - he knew he needed yet another change. | But when he came to a literal fork in the road, the man realized he hadn't eaten in some time. His stomach demanded a change in scenery - and diet. | Sadly, the world is not a pleasant place for those who nobody would miss. He was harassed and bullied every day. | After one particularly harsh day trudging through mud, he realized there was no life to be had in walking around. | Strangely, one day he came across his long-forgotten brother he-never-had who said there was plenty of walking to be done for a mercenary outfit - and they'd pay him to do it, too! | Like any good, impulsive man, he flipped a coin on whether or not to try his hand at mercenary work.\x7d \x7bHe's not particularly good at anything, but %name% has seen and done a lot, and that's worth at least something. | Mucking about this violent land and surviving with all his limbs is a lot more than some folks can say. | A mercenary band would be but another adventure for a vagabond like %name%. One hopes he survives to write about it. | Through his travels his only weapon was a walking stick. Let's see how he does with something a smidge sharper. | A thief, a scoundrel, a baker, a tailor, %name%'s done it all. Too bad he was never good at any of those things. Maybe it'll be different this time. | The world has been harsh to %name% for many years now. That isn't going to change, but at least he will be with brothers now.\x7d"
    // en base_es
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\wildman_background.nut
    // en = "Wildmen are used to the hard life of the wild where only the strong prevail. They are less used to the life of cities, where the astute and deceitful rule."
    // en base_es
    // en = "While the %companyname% visited a town for rest and recuperation, a local princess took a shine to %name% the wildman. He was 'purchased' for a large sum of gold and given to the noblewoman. You went and visited the man recently. For dinner, he sat at a kingly table, grinning goofily and mimicking the nobles around him as best he could. His new and inexplicable wife adored him, and him her. When you said your goodbyes, he offered you a heavy golden crown off the top of his head. It weighed heavy with traditions and ancient histories. You said it'd be best if he kept it. The wildman shrugged and walked off, spinning the circlet around a finger."
    // en base_es
    // en = "%name% the wildman stayed with the fragmenting %companyname% for a time and then, just like that, he was gone. The company went out looking for him in a forest, eventually finding some sort of crude note: an enormous pile of crowns next to a dirt-drawing of the %companyname% and some of its members, all of them being hugged by a big, literal stick figure with a goofy smile on its face. There was also an offering of a dead, half-eaten rabbit."
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Savage"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Outcast"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Wildman"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Feral"
    // en base_es
    // en = "the Wild"
    // en base_es
    // context: wildman_background.o.getTooltip.ret.push().text
    {
        en = "[color=%negative%]-15%[/color] Experience Gain"
        es = "[color=%negative%]-15%[/color] de experiencia obtenida"
    }
    // context: wildman_background.o.setGender.m.Name
    {
        en = "Wildwoman"
        es = "Salvaje"
    }
    // context: wildman_background.o.setGender.m.BackgroundDescription
    {
        en = "Wildwomen are used to the hard life of the wild where only the strong prevail. They are less used to the life of cities, where the astute and deceitful rule."
        es = "Las mujeres salvajes están acostumbradas a la dura vida en la naturaleza, donde solo prevalecen los fuertes. Lo están menos a la vida de las ciudades, donde mandan los astutos y los embusteros."
    }
    // context: wildman_background.o.setGender.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "While the %companyname% visited a town for rest and recuperation, a local prince took a shine to %name% the wildwoman. She was 'purchased' for a large sum of gold and given to the nobleman. You went and visited the woman recently. For dinner, she sat at a kingly table, grinning goofily and mimicking the nobles around her as best she could. Her new and inexplicable husband adored her, and her him. When you said your goodbyes, she offered you a heavy golden crown off the top of her head. It weighed heavy with traditions and ancient histories. You said it'd be best if she kept it. The wildwoman shrugged and walked off, spinning the circlet around a finger."
        es = "Mientras %companyname% visitaba una ciudad para descansar y recuperarse, un príncipe local se encaprichó de %name%, la mujer salvaje. Fue 'comprada' por una gran suma de oro y entregada al noble. Hace poco fuiste a visitarla. En la cena, se sentó a una mesa digna de un rey, sonriendo como una boba e imitando lo mejor que podía a los nobles que la rodeaban. Su nuevo e inexplicable marido la adoraba, y ella a él. Cuando te despediste, te ofreció una pesada corona de oro que llevaba en la cabeza. Pesaba con el lastre de tradiciones e historias antiguas. Le dijiste que sería mejor que la conservara. La mujer salvaje se encogió de hombros y se alejó, haciendo girar la diadema en un dedo."
    }
    // context: wildman_background.o.setGender.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "%name% the wildwoman stayed with the fragmenting %companyname% for a time and then, just like that, she was gone. The company went out looking for her in a forest, eventually finding some sort of crude note: an enormous pile of crowns next to a dirt-drawing of the %companyname% and some of its members, all of them being hugged by a big, literal stick figure with a goofy smile on its face. There was also an offering of a dead, half-eaten rabbit."
        es = "%name%, la mujer salvaje, se quedó un tiempo con %companyname% mientras se desmoronaba y luego, sin más, desapareció. La compañía salió a buscarla a un bosque y acabó encontrando una especie de nota tosca: un enorme montón de coronas junto a un dibujo en la tierra de %companyname% y algunos de sus miembros, todos abrazados por una figura grande hecha literalmente de palitos, con una sonrisa boba en la cara. También había una ofrenda: un conejo muerto y medio comido."
    }
    // context: wildman_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        // corrige base: «que lo persiguieron en los bosques» invierte «chased him into the forests» (lo empujaron hasta los bosques); «Juzgando por» es calco de «A juzgar por»; «algunas monedas» por «a few crowns» (coronas); «ha estado luchando con ferocidad» pierde «something fierce» (contra algo feroz)
        en = "{For some, the wild is a refuge. | It is said that %person% is born with the wilderness in %them%, and that %they% does wrong by turning %their% back on it. | Civilization is a stain, one prolonged arming of every next-generation to better battle the ultimate enemy: Mother Nature herself. | In a time of war, it's not surprising that many once again seek refuge in the wild. | Some people flee from town to town. Others stop in between, disappearing into the tranquil forests.} {%name% once found a safe register amongst the trees, but that time is over. | Once a mysterious figure to hunters - the famed masskewatsthat - %name% now returns to civilization for reasons unknown. | %name%'s got the hands of a blacksmith, but the hygiene of a pigsty. | Maybe it was spurned love, or maybe just war, but %name% has spent the last decade far from the rest of mankind. | Possibly a poacher who settled where %they% hunted, %name%'s lived amongst the trees for untold years. | With cleverly stitched garb, %name%'s atavistic appearance perhaps belies a past as a tailor or tanner.} {There is an obvious language barrier with the wildman, but for some reason %they% seems very willing to fight. Let's hope %their% newfound 'calling' doesn't have a darker purpose behind it. | Colorful and permanent ritual rites circle about %their% body. When asked why %they% wishes to join a band of mercenaries, %they% hoots and, with a crooked finger, replicates one of %their% fleshen arts across the sky. | Wounds, old and fresh, dot %their% already mottled body. And they are not superficial - this %person% had been fighting something fierce in the wild. | One has to wonder if the calamities which chased %them% into the forests have come to chase %them% back out. | Judging by %their% wild grunting, it's doubtful %they%'s here to rejoin civilization. | Years as a recluse haven't made the %person% forget what a few crowns can get you. The question is, why did %they% come back? | He has the strength to wrestle a boar - and %their% many scars makes you wonder if perhaps %they% did.}"
        es = "{Para algunos, lo salvaje es un refugio. | Se dice que uno nace con lo salvaje dentro y que hace mal en darle la espalda. | La civilización es una mancha, un largo adiestramiento de cada nueva generación para luchar mejor contra el enemigo definitivo: la propia Madre Naturaleza. | En tiempos de guerra, no es de extrañar que muchos vuelvan a buscar refugio en lo salvaje. | Algunas personas huyen de pueblo en pueblo. Otras se quedan a medio camino y desaparecen en la quietud de los bosques.} {%name% encontró una vez un refugio seguro entre los árboles, pero ese tiempo ha terminado. | En otro tiempo una figura misteriosa para los cazadores, %art% famos%o% masskewatsthat, %name% vuelve ahora a la civilización por razones desconocidas. | %name% tiene las manos de un herrero, pero la higiene de una pocilga. | Tal vez fue un amor despechado, o tal vez solo la guerra, pero %name% ha pasado la última década lejos del resto de la humanidad. | Quizá se dedicaba a la caza furtiva y se asentó donde cazaba; %name% ha vivido entre los árboles durante incontables años. | Con ropas ingeniosamente cosidas, la apariencia atávica de %name% quizá oculte un pasado en la sastrería o la curtiduría.} {Hay una evidente barrera idiomática con %art% salvaje, pero por alguna razón parece muy dispuest%o% a luchar. Esperemos que su recién descubierta 'vocación' no tenga detrás un propósito más oscuro. | Coloridos ritos permanentes le recorren el cuerpo. Cuando se le pregunta por qué quiere unirse a una banda de mercenarios, ulula y, con un dedo torcido, reproduce en el cielo uno de los dibujos de su piel. | Heridas, viejas y recientes, salpican su cuerpo ya de por sí moteado. Y no son superficiales: %ese% %hombre% ha estado luchando contra algo feroz en la espesura. | Uno no puede evitar preguntarse si las calamidades que %lo% empujaron a los bosques han venido ahora a sacar%lo% de ellos. | A juzgar por sus gruñidos salvajes, es dudoso que esté aquí para volver a la civilización. | Años de reclusión no le han hecho olvidar lo que se consigue con unas cuantas coronas. La pregunta es: ¿por qué ha vuelto? | Tiene fuerza para luchar con un jabalí, y sus muchas cicatrices te hacen preguntarte si no lo habrá hecho.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\backgrounds\witchhunter_background.nut
    // en = "Witchhunter"
    // en base_es
    // en = "Witchhunters tend to have some martial experience, and their resolve often remains unbroken even in the face of unspeakable horror."
    // en base_es
    // context: witchhunter_background.o.create.m.GoodEnding
    {
        en = "%name% the witchhunter eventually heard word of evil spreading in northern villages. %They% departed the %companyname% and has been burning those horrid witches at the stake ever since."
        es = "%name%, que se dedicaba a cazar brujas, acabó oyendo hablar de un mal que se propagaba por los pueblos del norte. Dejó %companyname% y desde entonces quema en la hoguera a esas horribles brujas."
    }
    // context: witchhunter_background.o.create.m.BadEnding
    {
        en = "Word of evil spreading in the north drew %name% the witchhunter from the company. %They% departed with stakes, vials of strange liquids, and a lot of kindling. A month later a peasant found %them% wandering the northern wastes with %their% eyes gouged out and %their% mouth sewn shut. %They% had a strange symbol ironed into %their% chest and when the peasant touched it both %people% exploded."
        es = "Los rumores de un mal que se propagaba por el norte apartaron de la compañía a %name%, que se dedicaba a cazar brujas. Partió con estacas, frascos de líquidos extraños y mucha yesca. Un mes después, un campesino %lo% encontró vagando por los páramos del norte con los ojos arrancados y la boca cosida. Tenía un extraño símbolo marcado a fuego en el pecho y, cuando el campesino lo tocó, ambos estallaron."
    }
    // context: witchhunter_background.o.getTooltip.ret.push().text
    {
        en = "[color=%positive%]+20[/color] Resolve at morale checks against fear, panic or mind control effects. Also knows how to craft wooden stakes for use against vampires."
        es = "[color=%positive%]+20[/color] de Resolución en las tiradas de moral contra efectos de miedo, pánico o control mental. Además, sabe fabricar estacas de madera para usarlas contra los vampiros."
    }
    // context: witchhunter_background.o.onBuildDescription
    {
        en = "{%name% appeared one day in %townname%, some say upon request {of the local council | of a local priest}. | %name% has a reputation of showing up where things out of the ordinary happen and being out and about at the darkest part of the night. | Being a quiet and grim %person%, %name% has the tendency to make other people feel uncomfortable around %them%, even afraid. | The name of %name% is known in many a village, for %they% has travelled the land to wherever %their% talents are needed the most.} {A Witchhunter %they% calls %themselves%. With %their% assortment of exotic tools %they% has a great deal of experience in getting people to confess in agony their sinful liaisons with demons and devils under terrible torture. | %They% refers to %themselves% as a Witchhunter, but only superstitious fools would believe this and fall for %their% preposterous tales. | A Witchhunter %they% calls %randomname%, and %they% claims to have seen horrors from beyond that would drive a lesser mind insane. | After %their% arrival in %townname%, rumors spread that %they% was on the hunt for devil worshippers and creatures of the night, but no one knew what the real purpose of %their% visit was. | In %townname% %they% killed an elderly woman and was thrown into the dungeon. As it turned out, the woman was responsible for the abduction and death of 3 infants, and so %they% was set free again. | For nights on end %they% sat in %townname%'s pub, silently studying every patron like a bird of prey circling above, %their% crossbow never far away. It didn't sit well with the residents but they didn't dare approach %them%.} {By now most of the local folks want %name% to be gone rather sooner than later and would happily see %them% join a travelling mercenary company. | It seems that whatever %their% mission was is now accomplished and so %name% offers %their% service as a mercenary. | It is somewhat obvious that %name% is not easily scared and %they% also knows how to handle a crossbow. Nobody was therefore surprised as %they% approached a mercenary company that was hiring. | Now, a mercenary company would be just the tool %they% needed to fulfill %their% personal quest against the evil from the world beyond. | Most people would be glad to get rid of %them%.}"
        es = "{%name% apareció un día en %townname%, según dicen a petición {del consejo local | de un sacerdote local}. | %name% tiene fama de presentarse allí donde ocurren cosas fuera de lo común y de andar por ahí en lo más oscuro de la noche. | Como %un% %hombre% callad%o% y sombrí%o%, %name% tiende a incomodar a quienes %lo% rodean, e incluso a darles miedo. | El nombre de %name% es conocido en muchas aldeas, pues ha recorrido estas tierras allí donde más se necesitaban sus talentos.} {Dice dedicarse a cazar brujas. Con su surtido de herramientas exóticas, tiene mucha experiencia en hacer que la gente confiese entre terribles tormentos sus pecaminosos tratos con demonios y diablos. | Asegura que caza brujas, pero solo unos necios supersticiosos se lo creerían y caerían en sus disparatadas historias. | Según %randomname%, se dedica a cazar brujas, y asegura haber visto horrores del más allá que volverían loca a una mente más débil. | Tras su llegada a %townname%, corrió el rumor de que andaba a la caza de adoradores del diablo y criaturas de la noche, pero nadie sabía cuál era el verdadero propósito de su visita. | En %townname% mató a una anciana y acabó en la mazmorra. Resultó que la mujer era responsable del secuestro y la muerte de 3 bebés, así que %lo% pusieron de nuevo en libertad. | Noche tras noche se sentaba en la taberna de %townname%, estudiando en silencio a cada parroquiano como un ave de presa que vuela en círculos, con la ballesta siempre a mano. A los vecinos no les gustaba, pero no se atrevían a acercarse a %el%.} {A estas alturas, casi todos los lugareños quieren que %name% se marche cuanto antes y estarían encantados de ver%lo% unirse a una compañía de mercenarios itinerante. | Parece que, fuera cual fuera su misión, ya la ha cumplido, así que %name% ofrece sus servicios como mercenari%o%. | Es bastante evidente que %name% no se asusta con facilidad y que sabe manejar una ballesta. Por eso a nadie le sorprendió que se acercara a una compañía de mercenarios que buscaba gente. | Ahora, una compañía de mercenarios sería justo la herramienta que necesita para cumplir su cruzada personal contra el mal del mundo de más allá. | La mayoría de la gente estaría encantada de librarse de %el%.}"
    }
    // FILE: mod_legends\hooks\skills\effects\afraid_effect.nut
