    }
    // FILE: scripts\events\events\legends\legend_lose_fear_nobles_event.nut
    // context: legend_lose_fear_nobles_event.create.m.Screens.push().Text
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_26.png[/img]{%fearful% is staring at a pauldron they keep turning over and over in their hands. Dented and bloodstained, it nevertheless appears to be a fine piece, inlaid with gold filigree and a noble sigil. A war trophy. Catching your gaze, they laugh and toss the piece to you.%SPEECH_ON%You can have it Cap. You know, all my life I've been afraid of these posh farks in their shiny plate, yet it turns out they bleed red, same as you and me. 'Aint nothing special about 'em at all.%SPEECH_OFF%}"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_26.png[/img]{%fearful% contempla una hombrera a la que no deja de dar vueltas entre las manos. Abollada y manchada de sangre, aun así parece una pieza de calidad, con filigrana de oro incrustada y un blasón noble. Un trofeo de guerra. Al notar tu mirada, se ríe y te lanza la pieza.%SPEECH_ON%Quédatela, capi. ¿Sabes? Toda la vida he tenido miedo de esos señoritos de mierda con sus placas relucientes, y resulta que sangran rojo, igual que tú y que yo. No tienen nada de especial.%SPEECH_OFF%}"
    }
    // context: legend_lose_fear_nobles_event.create.m.Screens.push().Options.Text
    {
        en = "How the mighty doth fall."
        es = "¡Cómo han caído los poderosos!"
    }
    // context: legend_lose_fear_nobles_event.create.m.Screens.push().start.List.push().text
    {
        // text = _event.m.Casualty.getName() + " no longer fears nobles"
        mode = "pattern"
        en = "<name:str> no longer fears nobles"
        es = "<name> ya no teme a los nobles"
    }
    // en = "fearful"
    // FILE: scripts\events\events\legends\legend_missed_opportunity_event.nut
    // context: legend_missed_opportunity_event.create.m.Title
    {
        en = "A Missed Opportunity"
        es = "Una oportunidad perdida"
    }
    // context: legend_missed_opportunity_event.create.m.Screens.push().Text
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_71.png[/img]{A sudden, chilling sensation washes over you, like a thread of destiny snapping cleanly in the dark.\n\nThe familiar sights and sounds of the town vanish in an instant. In their place, a grand thoroughfare materializes, teeming with vividly-cloaked nobility, armored guards wearing suits of segmented iron, shackled slaves, and wealthy merchants - all draped in strange finery, going about their daily routines.\n\nFor a fleeting second you feel at peace, only to be choked out by an overwhelming feeling of foreboding. You nervously look around searching the crowds for the familiar faces of your mercenaries, but they are nowhere to be seen.\n\nYou close your eyes.\n\nWhen you open them again, the street is once again dull and ordinary. The only thing left of the witnessed grandiosity is a frustrating feeling of a missed opportunity. }"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_71.png[/img]{Te invade una sensación repentina y escalofriante, como si un hilo del destino se partiera limpiamente en la oscuridad.\n\nLas imágenes y los sonidos familiares del pueblo se desvanecen en un instante. En su lugar se materializa una gran avenida, rebosante de nobles con capas de vivos colores, guardias acorazados con armaduras de hierro segmentado, esclavos encadenados y ricos mercaderes, todos ataviados con extrañas galas y ocupados en sus quehaceres cotidianos.\n\nDurante un fugaz instante sientes paz, pero enseguida te ahoga un abrumador presentimiento funesto. Miras nerviosamente a tu alrededor, buscando entre la multitud las caras conocidas de tus mercenarios, pero no hay ni rastro de ellos.\n\nCierras los ojos.\n\nCuando vuelves a abrirlos, la calle vuelve a ser gris y corriente. Lo único que queda de la grandiosidad presenciada es la frustrante sensación de haber perdido una oportunidad. }"
    }
    // context: legend_missed_opportunity_event.create.m.Screens.push().Options.Text
    {
        en = "Damn. I was sure something important was about to happen."
        es = "Maldita sea. Habría jurado que estaba a punto de pasar algo importante."
    }
    // FILE: scripts\events\events\legends\legend_muladi_trials1_event.nut
    // context: legend_muladi_trials1_event.create.m.Title
    {
        en = "Whilst in the City..."
        es = "Estando en la ciudad..."
    }
    // context: legend_muladi_trials1_event.create.m.Screens.push().Text
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_163.png[/img]{Perusing the exotic and aggressively colourful bazaars of %CityName%, your attention is drawn to one of the city's many snaking alleyways. In the gloom of a dusty dead end, the familiar sound of violence beckons you to the creeping maw of the passageway. Under a barrage of kicks and clubs and curses is none other than %brother%, the company's wayfaring muladi. A shout and brandishing of steel scares the attackers away, scurrying away into crevices and around blind corners where you imagine the labyrinth of alleys and hidden paths stretches on for untold miles. Sputtering dust, blood, and what looks like a tooth, %brother% tries to rise to %their_brother% feet, but crumples back down under the stress of the beating they'd just suffered. Kneeling to check their wounds aren't too severe, your own bones ache having witnessed only the end of what seems a most savage beatdown.%SPEECH_ON%Ah, shit. Hey, captain. Fancy meeting you in such a classy side of town. You just missed my good friends I'm afraid.%SPEECH_OFF%Indeed. You remark it seemed the attackers showed no signs of stopping their mauling until your interference, to which %brother% chuckles and confirms your musing. Your inspection reveals %brother%'s injuries are grizzly, but not life threatening; while they won't be dancing any time soon, you suspect they can follow you back to camp. You ask them what the hells happened.%SPEECH_ON%As I say, just catching up with old friends- we go way back.%SPEECH_OFF%A frown and demanding gaze makes it clear you aren't taking that for an answer. Slinging %their_brother% arm over your shoulder and hauling their weight into your side, %brother% braces against you and manages to stand, albeit like some caricature of a %person_muladi% with pudding for bones. They match your frown, and say %they_brother%'ll tell you when you get back to camp, preferably after taking something stiff for the pain which you can almost feel radiating off %them_brother%. Fair enough. Hobbling your way through the market and the arteries of the city, you make sure to stick to the most open streets, though even there the many people of the city spit at and curse the half-corpse clinging to you. Even a throng of indebted pause their labour to gawk at the pariah before them, their eyes betraying a mix of both desperate sadness and disgust as you both limp past.}"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_163.png[/img]{Mientras recorres los exóticos y chillones bazares de %CityName%, uno de los muchos callejones serpenteantes de la ciudad te llama la atención. En la penumbra de un polvoriento callejón sin salida, el familiar sonido de la violencia te atrae hacia las fauces del pasaje. Bajo una lluvia de patadas, porrazos y maldiciones está nada menos que %brother%, %art_muladi% muladí trotamundos de la compañía. Un grito y un destello de acero bastan para espantar a los agresores, que huyen a rastras por grietas y esquinas ciegas, donde imaginas que el laberinto de callejas y pasadizos ocultos se extiende por leguas incontables. Escupiendo polvo, sangre y lo que parece un diente, %brother% intenta ponerse en pie, pero vuelve a desplomarse, vencid%o_muladi% por la paliza que acaba de recibir. Te arrodillas para comprobar que sus heridas no son demasiado graves, y te duelen los huesos solo de haber presenciado el final de lo que parece una paliza de lo más salvaje.%SPEECH_ON%Ah, mierda. Hola, capitán. Qué casualidad encontrarte en un barrio tan elegante. Me temo que acabas de perderte a mis buenos amigos.%SPEECH_OFF%Desde luego. Comentas que parecía que los agresores no tenían ninguna intención de dejar de moler%lo_muladi% a golpes hasta que interviniste, y %brother% suelta una risita y te da la razón. Al examinar%lo_muladi% ves que las heridas de %brother% son feas, pero no ponen en peligro su vida; aunque no va a bailar en una temporada, sospechas que puede seguirte hasta el campamento. Le preguntas qué demonios ha pasado.%SPEECH_ON%Lo que te digo: me estaba poniendo al día con unos viejos amigos. Nos conocemos desde hace mucho.%SPEECH_OFF%Con el ceño fruncido y una mirada exigente dejas claro que no te vale esa respuesta. Pasándote el brazo por encima del hombro y cargando su peso sobre tu costado, %brother% se apoya en ti y consigue ponerse en pie, aunque como una caricatura de %hombre_muladi% con los huesos de gelatina. Frunce el ceño como tú y dice que te lo contará cuando vuelvan al campamento, a ser posible después de tomarse algo fuerte para el dolor, que casi puedes sentir irradiando de %el_muladi%. Es razonable. Mientras avanzan cojeando por el mercado y las arterias de la ciudad, te aseguras de ir por las calles más despejadas, aunque incluso allí la multitud escupe y maldice al medio cadáver que se aferra a ti. Hasta un tropel de endeudados interrumpe su trabajo para mirar boquiabierto %al_muladi% paria que tienen delante, con una mirada que delata una mezcla de tristeza desesperada y asco al ver cómo pasan cojeando.}"
    }
    // context: legend_muladi_trials1_event.create.m.Screens.push().Options.Text
    {
        en = "So much for southern hospitality..."
        es = "Y luego hablan de la hospitalidad sureña..."
    }
    // context: legend_muladi_trials1_event.create.m.Screens.push().Title
    {
        en = "Back at camp..."
        es = "De vuelta en el campamento..."
    }
    // context: legend_muladi_trials1_event.create.m.Screens.push().Text
    {
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_05.png[/img]{Stumbling your way back to camp, a few of the company rise and meet you with visible concern for the battered muladi clinging to your frame. Crashing into a cot, %muladi% lets out a noise not unlike a draught animal's death rattle. After dispersing the onlookers and sourcing some suitably strong liquid medicine, you sit beside the battered wayfarer and ask what really happened. They take a swig of drink, sigh, and look towards the city's gleaming walls and banners.%SPEECH_ON%I've been here many times, captain. Sometimes as a sellsword, other times a merchant of foreign goods. I've solved problems, started others; helped folks, hurt some. I have spent a veritable lifetime learning the many dialects of the tribes, the endless protocol of city life, the patterns of fashion, trade, politics. What drives the people who call this land home, and the plights of those who don	 but are otherwise stuck here. All of it, and yet what am I to the peoples of these lands?%SPEECH_OFF%You shrug. A damn good speaker despite the recent punishment, that's for sure. %They_brother% let out a sharp and markedly venomous word you don't understand, undoubtedly of the local tongue.%SPEECH_ON%'Outsider'. It's the closest single word I can think of in our speech. But it's closer to 'one without home', or 'forever wanderer'. They see not a person of the south, nor do they even regard me as a northerner. I am neither from the north or the south, the city or the tribes, and for this, they both fear and are disgusted by me. Those men back there-  my 'good friends'- they took issue with my lifestyle- called me a charlatan and mongrel, which of course they have for years. But today they said they would no longer tolerate me, if in fact they ever did; they planned to make a pulped example of me, to warn others who they claimed threatened their order of being. Of course, I've heard this before in many cities, from many people, but I think were it not for you, they would have followed through on their mission.%SPEECH_OFF%For a moment, you sit in silence, looking to the ground with your arms bowed between your knees. You have no doubt the muladi has suffered and battled with these thoughts long before joining the company, and unfortunately the life of a sellsword has offered no peace from it. While many within your ranks know their origins, their lives or callings back home, or the lands they consider familiar enough to one day become home, you know the pain %muladi% bears. You open your mouth to speak, but %muladi% stops you.%SPEECH_ON%It's quite alright, captain, you don't need to say anything. I've had such beatings before, and these thoughts are almost as old and good friends as the ruffians from that alleyway. I think I just needed to speak it, put it out in the open air for once.%SPEECH_OFF%You nod, and think to pat %muladi%'s shoulder, though their current state makes you reconsider. You leave the skin of booze with them, and rise to find someone to properly dress %their_brother% wounds.}"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_05.png[/img]{Cuando llegas a trompicones al campamento, algunos miembros de la compañía se levantan y salen a tu encuentro, visiblemente preocupados por el estado en que llega tu muladí, que se aferra a ti. Al desplomarse en un catre, %muladi% suelta un ruido no muy distinto del estertor de un animal de tiro. Tras dispersar a los curiosos y conseguir una medicina líquida convenientemente fuerte, te sientas junto a tu trotamundos de cuerpo maltrecho y le preguntas qué pasó en realidad. Da un trago, suspira y mira hacia las relucientes murallas y estandartes de la ciudad.%SPEECH_ON%He estado aquí muchas veces, capitán. Unas veces vendiendo mi espada, otras como mercader de productos extranjeros. He resuelto problemas y he causado otros; he ayudado a gente y he hecho daño a alguna. Me he pasado toda una vida aprendiendo los muchos dialectos de las tribus, el protocolo interminable de la vida en la ciudad, los vaivenes de la moda, el comercio y la política. Qué mueve a la gente que llama hogar a esta tierra, y las penurias de quienes no lo hacen pero aun así están atrapados aquí. Todo eso, ¿y qué soy yo para los pueblos de estas tierras?%SPEECH_OFF%Te encoges de hombros. Desde luego, tiene un pico de oro pese a la paliza reciente. Suelta una palabra cortante y claramente venenosa que no entiendes, sin duda de la lengua local.%SPEECH_ON%«Forastero». Es la palabra más parecida que se me ocurre en nuestra lengua. Pero se acerca más a «quien no tiene hogar» o «quien vaga eternamente». No ven en mí a una persona del sur, y ni siquiera me consideran del norte. No soy del norte ni del sur, ni de la ciudad ni de las tribus, y por eso me temen y les doy asco. Esos hombres de antes, mis «buenos amigos», tenían algo en contra de mi forma de vida: me llamaron farsante y chucho, como llevan haciendo años, claro. Pero hoy dijeron que ya no me tolerarían más, si es que alguna vez lo hicieron; pensaban hacerme papilla para dar ejemplo y advertir a otros que, según ellos, amenazan su orden de las cosas. Claro que ya he oído esto antes en muchas ciudades, de boca de mucha gente, pero creo que, de no ser por ti, habrían cumplido su propósito.%SPEECH_OFF%Durante un momento te quedas en silencio, con la vista en el suelo y los brazos colgando entre las rodillas. No te cabe duda de que tu muladí ha sufrido y ha lidiado con estos pensamientos mucho antes de unirse a la compañía, y por desgracia la vida de mercenario no le ha dado tregua. Mientras que muchos en tus filas conocen sus orígenes, su vida o su vocación allá en casa, o las tierras que les resultan lo bastante familiares como para llegar a ser un día su hogar, tú conoces el dolor que carga %muladi%. Abres la boca para hablar, pero %muladi% te detiene.%SPEECH_ON%No pasa nada, capitán, no hace falta que digas nada. Ya me han dado palizas así antes, y estos pensamientos son casi tan viejos y buenos amigos como los matones de ese callejón. Creo que solo necesitaba decirlo, sacarlo al aire libre por una vez.%SPEECH_OFF%Asientes y piensas en darle una palmada en el hombro a %muladi%, aunque su estado actual te hace pensártelo mejor. Le dejas el odre de licor y te levantas a buscar a alguien que le cure las heridas como es debido.}"
    }
    // context: legend_muladi_trials1_event.create.m.Screens.push().Options.Text
    {
        en = "Get well soon, %muladi%."
        es = "Mejórate pronto, %muladi%."
    }
    // context: legend_muladi_trials1_event.create.m.Screens.push().start.List.extend().::Legends.EventList.changeMood()
    {
        en = "Was battered and alienated by southerners"
        es = "Recibió una paliza y el rechazo de los sureños"
    }
    // context: legend_muladi_trials1_event.onPrepareVariables._vars.push()
    // en = "muladi"  // nombre de variable del evento, no se muestra
    // FILE: scripts\events\events\legends\legend_muladi_trials2_event.nut
    // context: legend_muladi_trials2_event.create.m.Title
    {
        // this.m.Title = "On the outskirts of %settlement%...";
        mode = "pattern"
        en = "On the outskirts of %settlement%..."
        es = "En las afueras de %settlement%..."
    }
    // context: legend_muladi_trials2_event.create.m.Screens.push().Text
    {
        // Text = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_141.png[/img]{Walking the sodden fields of %settlement%, you spy a number of your men up ahead running towards something. Following them round the back of a barn, you\'re met with a cluster of mercenaries, farmhands, and in the middle in a heap on the floor, %muladi% the muladi. You can feel the tension as the company quickly backs up the muladi, barking threats and demands, though the peasants offer firm verbal resistance. You push through to see a swelling puddle of blood and %muladi% curled into a fetal ball, holding their hands to their body. Across, peasants brace with farming tools as makeshift weapons of war, striking a most embarrassing defensive formation against the presence of your men. %SPEECH_ON%They farkin\' jumped %them_mualdi%, captain! Ran \'em through with a pitchfork for nothing!%SPEECH_OFF%One of the peasants produces said pitchfork, blood dripping from one of its rusted metal points. They brandish it against you and the others, declaring they\'ll run you through as well if you interfere.%SPEECH_ON%This freak has humiliated us, us good normal folk! They\'ve been living as one of them southern nomad bastards, the same ones who steal our cattle, our food, our children! Now they think they can slink back here and pretend they\'re like us and not some thieving brigand!%SPEECH_OFF%Their fervour and certainty in your brother\'s perceived crime is only tempered when you draw your sword and posture up against this peasant, who by now is shaking and looking to their peers for support. While you know little of your muladi\'s past, the fact stands that a mob of rabble just tried to murder them in an ambush. You have no doubt your company would make a short and brutal example of the now shaking assailants, but such a massacre would certainly harm any goodwill with the locals. Glancing back, you see %muladi% clutching their wound and groaning, as well as the rage in the company\'s eyes for such a slight. The men crave that one command that would sate their anger and promise them justice. With a sigh, you order the company...}",
        mode = "pattern"
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_141.png[/img]{Walking the sodden fields of %settlement%, you spy a number of your men up ahead running towards something. Following them round the back of a barn, you're met with a cluster of mercenaries, farmhands, and in the middle in a heap on the floor, %muladi% the muladi. You can feel the tension as the company quickly backs up the muladi, barking threats and demands, though the peasants offer firm verbal resistance. You push through to see a swelling puddle of blood and %muladi% curled into a fetal ball, holding their hands to their body. Across, peasants brace with farming tools as makeshift weapons of war, striking a most embarrassing defensive formation against the presence of your men. %SPEECH_ON%They farkin' jumped %them_mualdi%, captain! Ran 'em through with a pitchfork for nothing!%SPEECH_OFF%One of the peasants produces said pitchfork, blood dripping from one of its rusted metal points. They brandish it against you and the others, declaring they'll run you through as well if you interfere.%SPEECH_ON%This freak has humiliated us, us good normal folk! They've been living as one of them southern nomad bastards, the same ones who steal our cattle, our food, our children! Now they think they can slink back here and pretend they're like us and not some thieving brigand!%SPEECH_OFF%Their fervour and certainty in your brother's perceived crime is only tempered when you draw your sword and posture up against this peasant, who by now is shaking and looking to their peers for support. While you know little of your muladi's past, the fact stands that a mob of rabble just tried to murder them in an ambush. You have no doubt your company would make a short and brutal example of the now shaking assailants, but such a massacre would certainly harm any goodwill with the locals. Glancing back, you see %muladi% clutching their wound and groaning, as well as the rage in the company's eyes for such a slight. The men crave that one command that would sate their anger and promise them justice. With a sigh, you order the company...}"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_141.png[/img]{Mientras caminas por los campos empapados de %settlement%, ves más adelante a varios de tus hombres corriendo hacia algo. Los sigues hasta la parte trasera de un granero y te encuentras con un corrillo de mercenarios y peones, y en medio, en el suelo, a %muladi%, tu muladí. Se nota la tensión mientras la compañía sale enseguida en su defensa, soltando amenazas y exigencias, aunque los campesinos replican con firmeza. Te abres paso y ves un charco de sangre cada vez mayor y a %muladi% en posición fetal, con las manos apretadas contra el cuerpo. Enfrente, los campesinos se aprestan con aperos de labranza a modo de armas improvisadas, en una formación defensiva de lo más bochornosa ante tus hombres. %SPEECH_ON%¡Le han saltado encima los muy cabrones, capitán! ¡Le han clavado una horca por nada!%SPEECH_OFF%Uno de los campesinos enseña la horca en cuestión, con sangre goteando de una de sus púas de metal oxidado. La blande contra ti y los demás, y declara que también a ustedes los ensartará si se meten.%SPEECH_ON%¡Este engendro nos ha humillado, a nosotros, gente buena y normal! ¡Ha estado viviendo como esos bastardos nómadas del sur, los mismos que nos roban el ganado, la comida y los hijos! ¡Y ahora se cree que puede volver aquí a escondidas y fingir que es de los nuestros y no una rata salteadora!%SPEECH_OFF%Su fervor y su certeza sobre el supuesto crimen de uno de los tuyos solo se templan cuando desenvainas la espada y te plantas ante ese campesino, que ya tiembla y busca apoyo en sus compañeros. Aunque sabes poco del pasado de tu muladí, lo cierto es que una turba de chusma acaba de intentar quitarle la vida en una emboscada. No te cabe duda de que tu compañía daría un escarmiento rápido y brutal a los agresores, que ahora tiemblan, pero semejante masacre sin duda arruinaría cualquier buena relación con los lugareños. Al mirar atrás, ves a %muladi% apretándose la herida y gimiendo, y también la rabia en los ojos de la compañía ante semejante afrenta. Los hombres ansían esa única orden que saciaría su ira y les prometería justicia. Con un suspiro, ordenas a la compañía...}"
    }
    // en = "Kill them all!"
    // en base_es
    // context: legend_muladi_trials2_event.create.m.Screens.push().Options.Text
    {
        en = "{Blast it! Grab %muladi% and let's go!}"
        es = "{¡Maldita sea! ¡Recojan a %muladi% y vámonos!}"
    }
    // context: legend_muladi_trials2_event.create.m.Screens.push().Title
    {
        en = "After the massacre..."
        es = "Tras la masacre..."
    }
    // context: legend_muladi_trials2_event.create.m.Screens.push().Text
    {
        // Text = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_22.png[/img]{The words had hardly left your mouth before the men descend upon the murderous rabble like waves on rocks. Desperate screams of terror are met with ferocious roars of vengeance and bloodlust as the company gores the peasants before you. One peasant lets out a shrill screech, cut short as their head is swiftly liberated of its body. Another turns to run, but is planted into the very earth they worked with a hideous crunch, as though an unhold had fell onto a stack of bramble. The pitchfork wielding peasant is soundly disembowelled with their own implement as the rest of the company wraps up their bloody work. In only seconds, this mass of men had been turned into a scene of carnage and brutality signed by your company. Whether justified or not, the people of %settlement% will no doubt remember this.\nTurning your attention to your skewered muladi, you order some of the company to check their wounds and patch %them_muladi% up. While certainly gruesome, the pitchfork thankfully wasn\'t lethal, and %muladi% quickly has their wound plugged and bandaged by some of the more healing-inclined men. The contrast between the delicate care taken for your injured man and the barbarous scene around them stirs something within you, and you crouch to speak to the now responsive muladi. They shake their head and glance around as you ask how they\'re feeling.%SPEECH_ON%Like shit, to be honest, captain. I\'ve known some of those farmers for years, before my travels. Played horseshoes with some, drank with others. Some of them were right bastards, but I never thought they\'d do this.%SPEECH_OFF%%They_muladi% gesture to their wound and rise to their feet with your help and a few other brothers to support them. Standing over some of the freshly made bodies, they frown and wipe something from their face before continuing.%SPEECH_ON%They poked fun at first. My trips to the south were a fun topic of ribbing, of me \'sampling the flavours\' of those lands. Nevermind the struggles, the beatings I suffered, the people I hurt. They just saw what they wanted to see of me, whatever made them feel better about their lives wasted toiling on the same soil year by year. Later it turned to suspicion of the new clothes I wore, the accent I picked up, the trinkets I brought back. I suppose this was their breaking point- and mine.%SPEECH_OFF%They survey the peasant with the pitchfork embedded in their stomach, spit on them, then turn back to the company. A bolt of pain sends them doubling over, another punishment from %their_muladi% now dead attacker. Your men support %them_muladi% as they begin their walk back to camp, bloodied and sapped of spirit. Looking back to the corpses, %muladi% sounds off their last defiance to those who estranged %them_muladi% for who they dared to be.%SPEECH_ON%Rot, you bastards.%SPEECH_OFF%}",
        mode = "pattern"
        en = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_22.png[/img]{The words had hardly left your mouth before the men descend upon the murderous rabble like waves on rocks. Desperate screams of terror are met with ferocious roars of vengeance and bloodlust as the company gores the peasants before you. One peasant lets out a shrill screech, cut short as their head is swiftly liberated of its body. Another turns to run, but is planted into the very earth they worked with a hideous crunch, as though an unhold had fell onto a stack of bramble. The pitchfork wielding peasant is soundly disembowelled with their own implement as the rest of the company wraps up their bloody work. In only seconds, this mass of men had been turned into a scene of carnage and brutality signed by your company. Whether justified or not, the people of %settlement% will no doubt remember this.\nTurning your attention to your skewered muladi, you order some of the company to check their wounds and patch %them_muladi% up. While certainly gruesome, the pitchfork thankfully wasn't lethal, and %muladi% quickly has their wound plugged and bandaged by some of the more healing-inclined men. The contrast between the delicate care taken for your injured man and the barbarous scene around them stirs something within you, and you crouch to speak to the now responsive muladi. They shake their head and glance around as you ask how they're feeling.%SPEECH_ON%Like shit, to be honest, captain. I've known some of those farmers for years, before my travels. Played horseshoes with some, drank with others. Some of them were right bastards, but I never thought they'd do this.%SPEECH_OFF%%They_muladi% gesture to their wound and rise to their feet with your help and a few other brothers to support them. Standing over some of the freshly made bodies, they frown and wipe something from their face before continuing.%SPEECH_ON%They poked fun at first. My trips to the south were a fun topic of ribbing, of me 'sampling the flavours' of those lands. Nevermind the struggles, the beatings I suffered, the people I hurt. They just saw what they wanted to see of me, whatever made them feel better about their lives wasted toiling on the same soil year by year. Later it turned to suspicion of the new clothes I wore, the accent I picked up, the trinkets I brought back. I suppose this was their breaking point- and mine.%SPEECH_OFF%They survey the peasant with the pitchfork embedded in their stomach, spit on them, then turn back to the company. A bolt of pain sends them doubling over, another punishment from %their_muladi% now dead attacker. Your men support %them_muladi% as they begin their walk back to camp, bloodied and sapped of spirit. Looking back to the corpses, %muladi% sounds off their last defiance to those who estranged %them_muladi% for who they dared to be.%SPEECH_ON%Rot, you bastards.%SPEECH_OFF%}"
        es = "[img]gfx/ui/events/event_22.png[/img]{Apenas has terminado de hablar cuando los hombres caen sobre la chusma asesina como olas contra las rocas. A los desesperados gritos de terror responden feroces rugidos de venganza y sed de sangre mientras la compañía destroza a los campesinos ante tus ojos. Uno de ellos suelta un chillido agudo que se corta en seco cuando su cabeza queda rápidamente liberada de su cuerpo. Otro se da la vuelta para huir, pero acaba hundido en la misma tierra que labraba con un crujido espantoso, como si un unhold hubiera caído sobre un montón de zarzas. El campesino de la horca acaba bien destripado con su propia herramienta mientras el resto de la compañía remata su sangrienta faena. En apenas unos segundos, aquel grupo de hombres se ha convertido en una escena de carnicería y brutalidad con la firma de tu compañía. Justificado o no, la gente de %settlement% sin duda lo recordará.\nTe centras en tu muladí ensartad%o_muladi% y ordenas a algunos miembros de la compañía que le examinen las heridas y %lo_muladi% remienden. Aunque la herida de horca es espantosa, por suerte no es mortal, y algunos de los hombres más mañosos con la medicina enseguida le taponan y le vendan la herida a %muladi%. El contraste entre los delicados cuidados que recibe tu muladí herid%o_muladi% y la escena bárbara a su alrededor remueve algo en tu interior, y te agachas para hablar con %art_muladi% muladí, que ya responde. Niega con la cabeza y mira a su alrededor cuando le preguntas cómo se encuentra.%SPEECH_ON%Como una mierda, para serte sincer%o_muladi%, capitán. A algunos de esos granjeros los conozco desde hace años, desde antes de mis viajes. Con unos jugaba a la herradura, con otros bebía. Algunos eran unos cabrones de cuidado, pero nunca pensé que harían esto.%SPEECH_OFF%Señala la herida y se pone en pie con tu ayuda y la de otros cuantos hermanos que %lo_muladi% sostienen. De pie junto a algunos de los cadáveres recién hechos, frunce el ceño y se limpia algo de la cara antes de continuar.%SPEECH_ON%Al principio se burlaban. Mis viajes al sur eran un tema divertido para pincharme, que si me iba a «probar los sabores» de aquellas tierras. Daban igual las penurias, las palizas que sufrí, la gente a la que hice daño. Solo veían en mí lo que querían ver, lo que les hiciera sentirse mejor con sus vidas desperdiciadas deslomándose en la misma tierra año tras año. Luego se volvió desconfianza por la ropa nueva que llevaba, el acento que se me pegó, las baratijas que traía. Supongo que este ha sido su límite... y el mío.%SPEECH_OFF%Contempla al campesino con la horca clavada en el estómago, le escupe y luego se vuelve hacia la compañía. Una punzada de dolor %lo_muladi% dobla en dos, otro castigo de su agresor, ya muerto. Tus hombres %lo_muladi% sostienen mientras emprende el camino de vuelta al campamento, ensangrentad%o_muladi% y sin ánimo. Volviendo la vista hacia los cadáveres, %muladi% lanza un último desafío a quienes %lo_muladi% repudiaron por atreverse a ser quien es.%SPEECH_ON%Púdranse, cabrones.%SPEECH_OFF%}"
    }
    // context: legend_muladi_trials2_event.create.m.Screens.push().Options.Text
    {
        en = "Life can be a fickle thing."
